WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.769
Joe: From calorie count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.771
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.540
between McDonald's in Japan and the US.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.275
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:12.879
Hey, guys, Joe from "Food Wars."

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.381
We're doing a new season.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:16.416
We're comparing the US to Japan.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.817
In order to do that, I
want to introduce you

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:21.087
to cohost and my man in Japan, George.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.555
Hello, guys. I'm George.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.925
I'm from Japan, and I like McDonald's.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:34.634
So, in Japan, our McDonald's
sodas come in three sizes.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.302
This is small.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.704
Small.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.306
And this is Japan's medium.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.574
Medium.

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.377
And this one is Japan's large.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.678
Large.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.483
In Japan, our chicken McNuggets

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.686
come in five and 15 pieces.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.954
Our chicken McNuggets come in

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.889
four,

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:56.890
six,

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:57.724
10,

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:58.558
20,

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.493
or 40 piece.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.895
Look at all those nuggets.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:05.832
Oh.

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.500
They've been sitting for a while.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.170
Japan McDonald's fries
come in three sizes,

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.505
small, medium, and large.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.774
In the US, you can get
your fries in four sizes,

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:18.178
kids, small, medium, and large.

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.915
Look at this little guy.
Look at this little guy.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.817
George: So, this is large fries,

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.018
and I'm going to weigh them.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:29.189
Joe: We are going to also
weigh a large McDonald's fry.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.256
Wow!

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.659
OK, so, so far our larges are the same.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:33.860
Yeah, wow. That worked perfectly,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.795
that thing I just did
there. Great job, Joe.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.297
Go home.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.132
Go!

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.501
Joe: Now let's measure
the medium. Why not?

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.238
Our mediums are smaller.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.474
Huh. Interesting.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:50.043
So, this is a Japanese Big Mac.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.344
Ta-da!
[trumpets playing]

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.280
Oh!

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.249
So, this is a Japanese Big Mac.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.584
Joe: This is an American Big Mac,

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.385
and we're going to weigh it as well.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:02.222
Oh, we've got a heftier
Big Mac here in the US.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.523
That's more like it.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.391
So, in Japan, the Big Mac value set,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:09.629
which is a Big Mac and medium
fries and a medium drink,

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:14.200
comes out to 690 yen, or $6.21.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:18.004
In the US, that same meal costs $8.54,

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:22.375
or 948.46 Japanese yen.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:27.113
That's a 37.52% increase
in price in the US.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.281
What the heck?

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.752
So, here is everything you can only get

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.020
at Japan's McDonald's

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.822
you cannot get in the US.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.458
And this is everything you
can get at a US McDonald's

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.993
that you cannot get in Japan.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:43.930
So, we are going to start
with waffle cones, right here.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.732
So, we got plain.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:48.835
So, plain means it's,
like, rich milk taste.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.905
And next one is strawberry.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:54.274
Strawberry. Personally, I like this.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.342
Our next one is

00:02:56.342 --> 00:03:00.180
chocolate and almond, right there.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.247
Mm.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.515
It's not melting.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:04.250
Good job, buddy.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.886
So, here we've got McFloats.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.122
So, McFloats means there is soda,

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.424
and on top of that, there is ice cream.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.859
That's it. That's it.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.395
And this is McFloats melon.

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:20.133
Ooh!

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.701
[laughs]

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.403
It's too sweet.

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.671
This is grape.

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.439
Coffee McFloats.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.709
Mm.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:30.843
And the last one,

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.646
we've got Coke McFloats.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:36.849
Mm.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:41.254
Oh, Joe, you definitely try this.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.655
Yes, absolutely.

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:43.756
I'm trying that when I go to Japan.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.724
That looks real good.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:45.725
Let me think here.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.026
Hang on a second.

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:48.461
[metal clanging]

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.295
OK.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.466
We do not have McFloats here in the US,

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:54.901
so I'm going to make my own.

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:55.735
On the way over here,

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.337
I was looking for grape soda.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.771
It's actually harder
to find than I thought.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.573
Fanta's not very popular
in the United States.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.342
But we got this.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:06.279
This is Midnight Grape
Kickstart Mountain Dew.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:07.380
It's grape.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.252
Haha! Left over from
the Ben &amp; Jerry's shoot.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.420
This stuff is frozen. There we go.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.658
[electric zapping]

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:22.428
Yeah. I'm into this.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.430
These would do well in the US.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.633
Our cold drinks, a little bit different.

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:28.468
We have two exclusive slushies

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.769
that you can't get in Japan.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.970
One is a pink lemonade.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.705
Strawberry watermelon.

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.140
Yeah, dude.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.241
That looks real good.

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:38.044
Yes, they do have McFlurries
and ice cream in Japan,

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:41.080
but one McFlurry you can
get in the US is this one.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.649
It's an M&amp;M's McFlurry.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:45.551
Sorry, it's since melted,

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.288
but it's like those mini M&amp;M's.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.256
I went to one of the few
McDonald's in the country

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.824
where the ice cream machine was working.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.860
Hot caramel sundae,

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.296
and the classic

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.097
fudge sundae.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:01.434
George: So, let's go with
soft drinks, right here.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.136
Fanta grape,

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:06.105
and here is Fanta melon.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:10.243
And this one is Japanese vegetable juice.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.544
And there is,

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:14.547
I guess, more than 20
or 30 vegetables in it.

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:17.417
And it's good for health, for sure.

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.288
Aah.

00:05:22.288 --> 00:05:24.590
[water running]
[chimes sound]

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.292
Mm.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:29.862
We've got Qoo white grape.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:30.897
Sokenbicha.

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:33.733
Sokenbicha is like a Japanese blended tea.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:34.867
It's healthy.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:38.271
And Japanese people drink
this on a daily basis.

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:39.138
So, next one,

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:42.775
we've got Earl Grey iced tea.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.577
Let me show you.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:47.146
Wait, there is something.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.582
[beep]

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.017
There's a mosquito.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:55.054
I have to make a complaint,
Japan McDonald's!

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:00.059
Next one, we've got

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.594
oolong tea.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.796
So, this is not actually Japanese tea.

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:05.331
It's a Chinese tea

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:07.100
that's good for health as well.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.836
For health, we do have

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.838
a mango pineapple smoothie

00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:14.407
and a banana strawberry smoothie.

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:16.175
Smoothies have fruit in it, right?

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:18.911
Oh, yeah.

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:22.248
I can just feel the nutrients
coursing through my veins!

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:27.987
So, let's start with this Hawaiian menu.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:29.422
This is limited.

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:32.792
This one right here is Cheese Loco Moco.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.794
Ooh, it's messy.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.899
It's a demi-glace sauce. Man.

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:41.634
And it's also got

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:43.936
round egg, right there,

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:47.240
beef patty, and some cheese.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.008
I'm hungry, actually.

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:52.678
Mm!

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:57.550
Oh, this is good!

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.551
Oh!

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.054
[laughs]

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:03.423
This is [speaks Japanese],

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:06.893
which means really, really delicious.

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:09.862
All right, so, next one,
we've got garlic shrimp,

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:12.999
and it's also got interesting bun.

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.234
There is sesame on there.

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:17.670
And deep-fried shrimp.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.540
Hawaiian barbecue potato and beef.

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.543
Demi-glace sauce again.

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:24.644
It's gonna be good.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.916
This is called barbecue burger, right?

00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:31.951
But I don't taste barbecue at all.

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:32.952
All right, so, next one,

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:35.321
we've got Hawaiian pancake

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:38.191
with triple berry sauce.

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:39.692
Two pancakes.

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.562
Hello!

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:45.765
Mm, smells so sweet. Ooh.

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:46.866
Let's go.

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:51.537
Ooh.

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.444
Too sweet.

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:01.013
McFizz blue Hawaii.

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:02.448
Wow.

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:05.451
It has bright blue color.

00:08:05.451 --> 00:08:08.888
This is McFizz cassis and orange.

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:13.493
I would get this. I would get this.

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:16.295
So, congratulations,

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:18.197
this is the worst.

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:21.868
OK. Breakfast time.

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:24.770
This is a breakfast burrito.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:25.938
Ugh.

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:30.343
Neon-yellow egg, Mexican-style salsa.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:33.713
Not to be confused with,
what, Canadian salsa?

00:08:33.713 --> 00:08:34.714
This is actually the same burrito

00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:37.316
from the US-UK thing we
shot over a year ago. So.

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:39.685
Let's go on to these
breakfast sandwiches here.

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:41.654
Japan does have the McGriddles,

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:43.055
which are a favorite of mine,

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:45.625
so unfortunately we will not
be talking about those today.

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:46.759
Sad face.

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:48.327
I love you, McGriddles.

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:49.762
So, what they don't have,

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:51.531
and also the UK did not have,

00:08:51.531 --> 00:08:54.100
were our breakfast biscuit sandwiches.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.935
I don't know how to describe a biscuit,

00:08:55.935 --> 00:08:58.938
other than it's dry,

00:08:58.938 --> 00:09:00.206
it's baked.

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:01.841
Maybe they're made with cornmeal?

00:09:01.841 --> 00:09:02.708
According to the internet,

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.977
this is not a scone, so there you go.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.913
Sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:09:06.913 --> 00:09:08.414
Our egg is like

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:12.451
this fluffy, folded scrambled-egg egg.

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:13.953
So theirs are, like, sunny-side up?

00:09:13.953 --> 00:09:14.987
Ours are scrambled.

00:09:14.987 --> 00:09:16.656
I can tell this was folded over.

00:09:16.656 --> 00:09:18.257
You can see the fold lines there.

00:09:18.257 --> 00:09:19.859
This is how we do it in the US.

00:09:19.859 --> 00:09:21.027
Bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:23.062
Is there a better breakfast
combination in the world?

00:09:23.062 --> 00:09:24.063
I don't think there is.

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.932
Then they just have a sausage,

00:09:25.932 --> 00:09:26.832
no egg, no cheese,

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:28.834
just sausage and biscuit.

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:30.403
We have regular-sized hotcakes,

00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:33.306
and we have a hotcake-and-sausage combo.

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:36.475
And, of course, comes with syrup

00:09:36.475 --> 00:09:38.778
and butter.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.982
Very natural pose.

00:09:42.982 --> 00:09:44.984
Very natural feeling right now.

00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:49.088
♪ Always up for a pour, yes! ♪

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:52.592
Breakfast is served.

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:53.492
Oatmeal.

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:55.194
On the side, to be mixed in,

00:09:55.194 --> 00:09:56.495
cranberries and raisins

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:57.830
and

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:58.664
diced --

00:09:58.664 --> 00:09:59.498
oh!

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:02.535
Diced apples.

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:03.736
[slurps]

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:07.273
And here we've got Mega Muffin.

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:08.674
Pork patties.

00:10:08.674 --> 00:10:10.743
That's huge one.

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:12.578
Mini pancakes.

00:10:12.578 --> 00:10:13.846
Oh, cute.

00:10:13.846 --> 00:10:16.582
It comes with apple cream sauce.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.219
Ooh.

00:10:21.621 --> 00:10:24.323
Ooh, this is perfect for breakfast.

00:10:24.323 --> 00:10:25.658
I would get it.

00:10:25.658 --> 00:10:28.527
Bacon egg McSandwich.

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:31.097
So, it's got bacon

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:32.565
and round egg

00:10:32.565 --> 00:10:34.233
and cheddar cheese.

00:10:34.233 --> 00:10:35.301
That's it.

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:37.670
And you might be surprised,

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:39.772
we've got Filet-O-Fish.

00:10:39.772 --> 00:10:41.874
Ta-da!

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:44.510
So, Filet-O-Fish is on the breakfast menu.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.545
I guess Japanese people tend to

00:10:46.545 --> 00:10:48.748
eat fish for breakfast.

00:10:48.748 --> 00:10:50.282
Three exclusive burgers here in the US

00:10:50.282 --> 00:10:53.586
are variations on the
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:10:53.586 --> 00:10:55.388
Yes, we've all seen "Pulp Fiction,"

00:10:55.388 --> 00:10:57.289
we know about the whole
Quarter Pounder thing.

00:10:57.289 --> 00:10:58.791
Does not exist outside of the US,

00:10:58.791 --> 00:10:59.659
I don't think.

00:10:59.659 --> 00:11:01.127
So, probably why they don't have

00:11:01.127 --> 00:11:02.928
Quarter Pounders in Japan.

00:11:02.928 --> 00:11:04.930
The classic Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:05.931
Look at this guy.

00:11:05.931 --> 00:11:09.335
I mean, this was maybe my
go-to one for a decade.

00:11:09.335 --> 00:11:12.104
The Quarter Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:13.372
I don't know.

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:15.141
I feel like this is
pretty close to a Whopper.

00:11:15.141 --> 00:11:16.409
I'm not a big Whopper guy,

00:11:16.409 --> 00:11:17.610
but there you go,

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.046
a deluxe Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:11:20.046 --> 00:11:21.814
The double Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:11:21.814 --> 00:11:23.916
Look at the size of this thing!

00:11:23.916 --> 00:11:26.385
Yes, sir.

00:11:26.385 --> 00:11:28.954
Japan's exclusive burgers.

00:11:28.954 --> 00:11:30.723
Teriyaki McBurger,

00:11:30.723 --> 00:11:34.026
which is my most favorite one.

00:11:34.026 --> 00:11:37.396
My body is made of McTeriyaki burger.

00:11:39.865 --> 00:11:42.702
[angelic singing]

00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:47.373
So, it's got mayo right there,

00:11:47.373 --> 00:11:49.175
and lettuce, pork patties,

00:11:49.175 --> 00:11:51.410
dip it into delicious teriyaki sauce,

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:54.613
and it's covering whole
pork patties perfectly.

00:11:54.613 --> 00:11:58.551
Joe, when you come to
Japan, please try this.

00:11:58.551 --> 00:12:01.220
You will thank me later.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:02.955
Everything that they have

00:12:02.955 --> 00:12:05.691
looks so good and sounds so good.

00:12:05.691 --> 00:12:07.827
Man, when I go to Tokyo,

00:12:07.827 --> 00:12:09.829
first stop, I'm going to McDonald's.

00:12:09.829 --> 00:12:12.698
Sushi, ramen, get it out of my face.

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:14.266
I want the teriyaki burger.

00:12:14.266 --> 00:12:16.135
That's the first thing I'm
getting when I get there.

00:12:17.136 --> 00:12:18.370
Mm!

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.439
I'm getting full, actually.

00:12:20.439 --> 00:12:21.407
[laughs]

00:12:23.209 --> 00:12:25.144
Slow down, George. We got
a lot of food to cover.

00:12:29.014 --> 00:12:32.585
[dance music]

00:12:32.585 --> 00:12:34.420
All right, so we've got

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:37.223
bacon lettuce burger right here.

00:12:37.223 --> 00:12:38.691
It looks sad.

00:12:40.192 --> 00:12:42.128
Egg cheeseburger,

00:12:42.128 --> 00:12:45.030
but we also call it Eguchi.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:48.501
Eguchi is an abbreviation
for egg cheeseburger.

00:12:48.501 --> 00:12:51.237
Japanese people love abbreviation.

00:12:51.237 --> 00:12:55.040
It's got ketchup and pickle, round egg,

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.810
and cheddar cheese and beef patties.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:58.677
Next one.

00:12:58.677 --> 00:13:00.813
Spicy beef burger.

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:02.314
Ooh, look at this!

00:13:02.314 --> 00:13:03.716
Oh, it looks so spicy!

00:13:03.716 --> 00:13:05.885
It has spicy mayo or something like that.

00:13:05.885 --> 00:13:10.356
So, here we've got Samurai Mac.

00:13:10.356 --> 00:13:11.957
Samurai!

00:13:11.957 --> 00:13:13.793
Samurai Mac?

00:13:13.793 --> 00:13:16.595
Yo, that sounds awesome.

00:13:16.595 --> 00:13:17.863
And this blue one

00:13:17.863 --> 00:13:21.767
is called roasted soy
sauce double thick beef.

00:13:21.767 --> 00:13:24.470
We've got roasted soy sauce

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:26.539
bacon tomato thick beef.

00:13:26.539 --> 00:13:28.307
So if you want a little bit more, like,

00:13:28.307 --> 00:13:30.709
healthy veggies,

00:13:30.709 --> 00:13:31.844
go for it.

00:13:31.844 --> 00:13:33.179
Uh, yeah, George, I don't know if that

00:13:33.179 --> 00:13:34.380
makes that much healthier there

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:37.082
'cause it also has twice
as much meat and cheese.

00:13:37.082 --> 00:13:38.884
If you're looking to be healthy
at a McDonald's in Japan,

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:40.586
I'd stick with the vegetable juice.

00:13:40.586 --> 00:13:43.489
And this one right here is called

00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:45.491
Teriyaki chicken Filet-O.

00:13:45.491 --> 00:13:48.093
Wow. So much sauce.

00:13:48.093 --> 00:13:51.130
So, next one, we've got ebi Filet-O.

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:52.198
Ebi means shrimp,

00:13:52.198 --> 00:13:54.400
so it's a shrimp Filet-O.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:56.769
Oh, yeah. It's got aurora sauce.

00:13:56.769 --> 00:14:00.706
Aurora sauce is like
ketchup and mayonnaise.

00:14:00.706 --> 00:14:02.641
So, it's got a lot of shrimp in there.

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:06.212
Mm!

00:14:06.212 --> 00:14:08.314
So good. So good.

00:14:08.314 --> 00:14:09.548
In the US, we have about

00:14:09.548 --> 00:14:13.352
four exclusive chicken
sandwiches specifically.

00:14:13.352 --> 00:14:14.520
I didn't see this on the menu,

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:17.423
but apparently you guys
don't have a McChicken,

00:14:17.423 --> 00:14:20.726
which is just chicken sandwich.

00:14:20.726 --> 00:14:23.362
Regular bun, mayo,

00:14:23.362 --> 00:14:24.163
chicken.

00:14:25.331 --> 00:14:26.298
Yeah.

00:14:26.298 --> 00:14:27.566
We also have,

00:14:27.566 --> 00:14:30.302
check this out, spicy McChicken.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.171
So pretty much the same McChicken,

00:14:32.171 --> 00:14:33.372
but they put spicy coating

00:14:33.372 --> 00:14:35.441
on the breading on the chicken.

00:14:35.441 --> 00:14:38.344
Every fast-food chain in America right now

00:14:38.344 --> 00:14:39.211
is having what we're calling

00:14:39.211 --> 00:14:40.946
the fried-chicken-sandwich wars.

00:14:40.946 --> 00:14:44.416
Popeyes, Burger King,
of course McDonald's,

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:46.552
all of them are at this arms race

00:14:46.552 --> 00:14:47.820
to have the best chicken sandwich.

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.855
I think 'cause Chick-fil-A
has edged everyone out.

00:14:49.855 --> 00:14:53.092
These are the three that
are currently available.

00:14:53.092 --> 00:14:54.727
I don't know for how long.

00:14:54.727 --> 00:14:56.161
You have the crispy chicken sandwich.

00:14:56.161 --> 00:14:58.364
I think it's a brioche bun,

00:14:58.364 --> 00:15:01.734
pickles, and no sauce,
which I think is strange.

00:15:01.734 --> 00:15:02.902
So, like, the whole flavor

00:15:02.902 --> 00:15:04.637
is just the chicken.

00:15:04.637 --> 00:15:07.539
Spicy chicken sandwich.

00:15:07.539 --> 00:15:08.641
Same deal,

00:15:08.641 --> 00:15:12.912
but, of course, spicy sauce.

00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:16.081
And the spicy chicken deluxe,

00:15:16.081 --> 00:15:17.750
which, to George's point,

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.184
has more vegetables on it.

00:15:19.184 --> 00:15:22.021
You know, to be healthier.

00:15:22.021 --> 00:15:24.390
OK, so when it comes to side menus,

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:28.127
we've got Shaka Shaka Chicken,

00:15:28.127 --> 00:15:29.495
and we have

00:15:29.495 --> 00:15:30.629
two fla --
[thunder rumbles]

00:15:30.629 --> 00:15:31.463
oh!

00:15:31.463 --> 00:15:32.831
Two flavors.

00:15:32.831 --> 00:15:36.468
Can you hear that?
Thunder, thunder, thunder!

00:15:36.468 --> 00:15:38.771
'Cause it's rainy season in Japan.

00:15:38.771 --> 00:15:41.740
It's the sunny season here
in Southern California.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:44.343
And here is red pepper.

00:15:44.343 --> 00:15:46.578
And this one is cheddar cheese.

00:15:46.578 --> 00:15:49.748
[thundering]

00:15:49.748 --> 00:15:51.583
Thunder, stop!

00:15:51.583 --> 00:15:52.885
So, all you have to do is just

00:15:52.885 --> 00:15:55.087
put the powder into the bag

00:15:55.087 --> 00:15:56.889
and shake it.

00:15:56.889 --> 00:15:59.658
[paper rattling]

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.729
And the powder should be covering

00:16:03.729 --> 00:16:05.731
the whole Shaka Chicken.
[thundering]

00:16:05.731 --> 00:16:07.833
Ooh, big one!

00:16:07.833 --> 00:16:09.134
Like this.

00:16:13.639 --> 00:16:16.008
This I've seen before. This I want.

00:16:16.008 --> 00:16:18.210
That's the thing I want the
most at a Japanese McDonald's.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.446
US McDonald's, we have the bags,

00:16:20.446 --> 00:16:22.047
we have the chicken.

00:16:22.047 --> 00:16:25.250
Just get the spice packets. Throw it in.

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.886
George: We've got side salad,

00:16:27.886 --> 00:16:32.024
and it comes with this
roasted sesame dressing.

00:16:32.024 --> 00:16:33.359
Let's go!

00:16:33.359 --> 00:16:35.828
Ooh.

00:16:35.828 --> 00:16:37.029
That was cool.

00:16:37.029 --> 00:16:38.464
Now put it all in the garbage.

00:16:38.464 --> 00:16:41.367
We've got edamame and corn.

00:16:42.234 --> 00:16:43.669
Yogurt,

00:16:43.669 --> 00:16:46.271
and there's cow,

00:16:46.271 --> 00:16:47.373
cow.

00:16:47.373 --> 00:16:48.741
Exclusive sauces.

00:16:48.741 --> 00:16:50.376
It's sauce talk time.

00:16:50.376 --> 00:16:51.910
Sauce Talk.

00:16:51.910 --> 00:16:54.513
We have sweet 'n sour sauce.

00:16:54.513 --> 00:16:56.015
They gave me

00:16:56.015 --> 00:16:57.616
hot mustard.

00:16:57.616 --> 00:16:59.318
This was supposed to be honey mustard.

00:16:59.318 --> 00:17:00.486
You guys have hot mustard?

00:17:00.486 --> 00:17:01.887
I know you don't have honey mustard.

00:17:01.887 --> 00:17:03.655
Of course, ranch.

00:17:04.757 --> 00:17:07.893
Ooh, spicy Buffalo.

00:17:07.893 --> 00:17:08.994
Now, these might be promotions

00:17:08.994 --> 00:17:12.698
'cause of that singing group BTS,

00:17:12.698 --> 00:17:14.833
but we have right now a

00:17:14.833 --> 00:17:17.536
Cajun sauce and a sweet chili sauce.

00:17:17.536 --> 00:17:21.006
This sauce is fantastic.

00:17:21.006 --> 00:17:23.075
This is the sauce. This
has to stay on the menu.

00:17:23.075 --> 00:17:25.577
So, these two are new ones.

00:17:25.577 --> 00:17:28.080
This one right here is

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.182
soy sauce, best sauce.

00:17:32.985 --> 00:17:35.120
Man. This is fantastic!

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.121
Good job!

00:17:36.121 --> 00:17:38.057
Very good taste.

00:17:38.057 --> 00:17:40.559
So, this one right here is called

00:17:40.559 --> 00:17:42.194
Louisiana hot sauce.

00:17:42.194 --> 00:17:45.764
Ooh, it does look like very spicy one.

00:17:49.701 --> 00:17:51.637
This is not spicy at all.

00:17:51.637 --> 00:17:55.474
Actually, we were supposed
to have bai burger options,

00:17:55.474 --> 00:17:58.677
but unfortunately you can
only get them from 5:30 p.m.

00:17:58.677 --> 00:18:01.113
But let me explain what bai burger is.

00:18:01.113 --> 00:18:04.083
Bai simply means double in Japanese.

00:18:04.083 --> 00:18:06.118
So if you order a normal Big Mac,

00:18:06.118 --> 00:18:07.920
it has two beef patties, right?

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:10.222
But if you order bai Big Mac,

00:18:10.222 --> 00:18:11.723
it has four beef patties.

00:18:11.723 --> 00:18:14.660
But not only Big Mac, but all burgers

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.929
adopts the bai burger options.

00:18:16.929 --> 00:18:17.763
That's funny.

00:18:17.763 --> 00:18:19.698
You can only get double
the meat after 5:30,

00:18:19.698 --> 00:18:20.666
that's really funny.

00:18:20.666 --> 00:18:23.402
That would not stand
in this country at all.

00:18:23.402 --> 00:18:25.571
People would lose their minds.

00:18:25.571 --> 00:18:27.773
Four patties?

00:18:27.773 --> 00:18:29.308
On a Big Mac?

00:18:29.308 --> 00:18:30.642
So after shooting this video,

00:18:30.642 --> 00:18:33.011
I'm going to order bai Big Mac.

00:18:33.011 --> 00:18:35.581
And then bye-bye, health.

00:18:35.581 --> 00:18:37.349
You ain't gotta tell me, George!

00:18:37.349 --> 00:18:38.484
Bye, health!

00:18:41.553 --> 00:18:42.788
All right, here are all the ingredients

00:18:42.788 --> 00:18:44.423
for a US Big Mac.

00:18:44.423 --> 00:18:45.257
Oh, God.

00:18:45.257 --> 00:18:46.492
The bun. It has:

00:18:46.492 --> 00:18:47.993
enriched flour, which is wheat flour,

00:18:47.993 --> 00:18:50.462
[fast-forwarding]

00:18:50.462 --> 00:18:52.831
vinegar, and contains wheat.

00:18:52.831 --> 00:18:53.899
On to the beef patty.

00:18:53.899 --> 00:18:57.002
100% pure USDA inspected beef,

00:18:57.002 --> 00:18:58.904
no fillers, no extenders!

00:18:58.904 --> 00:19:00.472
Prepared on the grill with seasoning,

00:19:00.472 --> 00:19:01.840
salt and black pepper.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.542
There you go. There you go.

00:19:03.542 --> 00:19:05.010
Try the lettuce ingredients,

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:06.044
lettuce.

00:19:06.044 --> 00:19:07.045
Nice.

00:19:07.045 --> 00:19:08.814
The Big Mac sauce ingredients.

00:19:08.814 --> 00:19:10.215
Soybean oil,

00:19:10.215 --> 00:19:12.951
[fast-forwarding]

00:19:12.951 --> 00:19:16.488
extractives of paprika, soy lecithin.

00:19:16.488 --> 00:19:17.356
[burps]

00:19:17.356 --> 00:19:18.991
The pickle slice ingredients.

00:19:18.991 --> 00:19:20.859
Cucumbers, water, distilled vinegar,

00:19:20.859 --> 00:19:23.495
salt, calcium chloride, alum,

00:19:23.495 --> 00:19:25.531
potassium sorbate as a preservative,

00:19:25.531 --> 00:19:27.533
natural flavors, polysorbate 80,

00:19:27.533 --> 00:19:29.668
extractives of turmeric for color.

00:19:29.668 --> 00:19:30.769
Onion ingredients.

00:19:30.769 --> 00:19:31.603
Onions.

00:19:31.603 --> 00:19:32.638
There you go.

00:19:32.638 --> 00:19:34.206
A few things I want to note.

00:19:34.206 --> 00:19:37.042
Alum is used to dissolve steel.

00:19:37.042 --> 00:19:41.113
Polysorbate 80 has been linked
to colon cancer in mice.

00:19:41.113 --> 00:19:42.481
Cue the dancing mice.

00:19:42.481 --> 00:19:46.251
[dance music]

00:19:46.251 --> 00:19:49.121
And caramel color is on
California's list of chemicals

00:19:49.121 --> 00:19:52.357
that may cause cancer and
reproductive toxicity,

00:19:52.357 --> 00:19:53.525
good God.

00:19:53.525 --> 00:19:54.526
Counterpoint.

00:19:54.526 --> 00:19:56.228
They all taste fantastic.

00:19:56.228 --> 00:19:58.530
So, McDonald's Japan doesn't disclose

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:00.566
their ingredients in the Big Mac.

00:20:00.566 --> 00:20:04.870
However, they do tell us where
the ingredients come from.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:06.772
If you order a Big Mac in Japan,

00:20:06.772 --> 00:20:10.642
you'll eat beef from
Australia or New Zealand;

00:20:10.642 --> 00:20:14.146
buns made from wheat
imported from the USA,

00:20:14.146 --> 00:20:16.348
Canada, and Australia;

00:20:16.348 --> 00:20:19.751
and pickles made from
cucumbers grown in Turkey,

00:20:19.751 --> 00:20:21.987
Sri Lanka, or India;

00:20:21.987 --> 00:20:25.557
onions grown in the USA or India;

00:20:25.557 --> 00:20:28.160
sliced cheddar cheese made in New Zealand,

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:31.463
Australia, the USA, or Japan;

00:20:31.463 --> 00:20:33.532
and lettuce grown in Japan,

00:20:33.532 --> 00:20:37.236
Taiwan, the USA, or Malaysia.

00:20:37.236 --> 00:20:40.272
The only ingredients that come from Japan

00:20:40.272 --> 00:20:42.574
are the cheese and the lettuce.

00:20:42.574 --> 00:20:45.777
And even then, McDonald's
still imports some lettuce

00:20:45.777 --> 00:20:48.013
and cheese from other countries.

00:20:48.013 --> 00:20:50.949
So this is a very international burger.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:53.151
Thank you, world!

00:20:56.288 --> 00:20:59.858
In Japan, our Big Mac is 525 calories

00:20:59.858 --> 00:21:02.427
and 28.3 grams of fat

00:21:02.427 --> 00:21:05.964
and 1,007 milligrams of sodium

00:21:05.964 --> 00:21:09.101
and 41.8 grams of carbs

00:21:09.101 --> 00:21:11.703
and 26 grams of protein.

00:21:11.703 --> 00:21:15.140
In the US, our Big Mac is 550 calories,

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:16.174
30 grams of fat,

00:21:16.174 --> 00:21:18.410
1,010 milligrams of sodium,

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:19.745
45 grams of carbs,

00:21:19.745 --> 00:21:22.314
and 25 grams of protein.

00:21:22.314 --> 00:21:23.849
So the US has a slight increase

00:21:23.849 --> 00:21:26.118
on everything except protein.

00:21:26.118 --> 00:21:28.487
So, in Japan, our five-piece nuggets

00:21:28.487 --> 00:21:30.656
is 270 calories

00:21:30.656 --> 00:21:33.325
and 17.2 grams of fat

00:21:33.325 --> 00:21:36.228
and 506 milligrams of sodium

00:21:36.228 --> 00:21:39.131
and 13.1 grams of carbs

00:21:39.131 --> 00:21:42.167
and 15.8 grams of protein.

00:21:42.167 --> 00:21:45.170
Broken down, each nugget is 54 calories.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:46.705
We don't have a five-piece here in the US,

00:21:46.705 --> 00:21:48.106
but we do have this, a 10-piece.

00:21:48.106 --> 00:21:49.741
Let's get those stats on the screen.

00:21:49.741 --> 00:21:51.276
Go ahead and divide everything by two,

00:21:51.276 --> 00:21:54.112
and, yes, now we have the
stats for a five-piece.

00:21:54.112 --> 00:21:55.147
Pretty smart, eh?

00:21:55.147 --> 00:21:57.716
If we want to divide all
that by, I think, five,

00:21:57.716 --> 00:22:00.385
you'll get the stats for one nugget.

00:22:00.385 --> 00:22:02.621
[sighs] This is so exhausting.

00:22:02.621 --> 00:22:04.756
In Japan, if you order a Big Mac meal

00:22:04.756 --> 00:22:08.193
with large fries and a
medium chocolate shake,

00:22:08.193 --> 00:22:11.897
the grand total will be 1,405 calories.

00:22:11.897 --> 00:22:13.899
And in the US, adding medium fries

00:22:13.899 --> 00:22:15.867
and a medium chocolate shake to a Big Mac,

00:22:15.867 --> 00:22:19.237
the grand total is 1,660 calories.

00:22:19.237 --> 00:22:23.742
And that is a calorie increase of 18.14%.

00:22:23.742 --> 00:22:25.510
If you're wondering why
we're using a large fry

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:27.112
but a medium chocolate shake,

00:22:27.112 --> 00:22:28.480
it turns out that in Japan,

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:31.049
you can't get a large chocolate shake.

00:22:31.049 --> 00:22:32.751
They'll only sell it to you in medium.

00:22:32.751 --> 00:22:33.785
I'm assuming because they don't want you

00:22:33.785 --> 00:22:35.854
eating that much ice cream.

00:22:35.987 --> 00:22:38.090
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:40.025
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:22:40.025 --> 00:22:42.794
between KFC in Japan and the US.

00:22:42.794 --> 00:22:45.030
This is "Food Wars."

00:22:46.932 --> 00:22:48.834
So, the fries at the KFC in Japan

00:22:48.834 --> 00:22:50.569
come in three sizes.

00:22:50.569 --> 00:22:52.037
So this is small.

00:22:53.171 --> 00:22:55.807
George: Next one is
Joe: And back again!

00:22:55.807 --> 00:22:57.743
George: Large.
Joe: The large.

00:22:57.743 --> 00:23:01.146
Then we got a box.

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:07.953
Now let's weigh our largest fries.

00:23:09.388 --> 00:23:11.456
Ooh, ooh, ooh!

00:23:11.456 --> 00:23:13.392
[Joe laughs]

00:23:13.392 --> 00:23:14.292
George: We can do it!

00:23:15.961 --> 00:23:16.828
I'm shook!

00:23:16.828 --> 00:23:19.030
As the kids say. By that information.

00:23:19.030 --> 00:23:21.566
I want to say, though,
that theirs is a box.

00:23:21.566 --> 00:23:23.769
That thing is, like, made to be eaten

00:23:23.769 --> 00:23:25.303
by more than one person, I'm assuming.

00:23:25.303 --> 00:23:26.405
But this, clearly,

00:23:26.405 --> 00:23:27.939
this is for a person. So.

00:23:27.939 --> 00:23:30.442
So, in Japan, we have three drink sizes.

00:23:30.442 --> 00:23:32.077
So we have a small.

00:23:32.077 --> 00:23:33.311
In the US, our drinks come

00:23:33.311 --> 00:23:35.447
in medium.
George: A medium.

00:23:35.447 --> 00:23:37.449
Then we got a large.

00:23:37.449 --> 00:23:38.817
And large.

00:23:40.585 --> 00:23:42.754
So, in Japan, KFC doesn't disclose

00:23:42.754 --> 00:23:45.624
how much liquid is in each of the sizes.

00:23:45.624 --> 00:23:46.591
Why?

00:23:46.591 --> 00:23:48.927
So I will help you, KFC.

00:23:48.927 --> 00:23:51.263
We will measure the cups right now.

00:23:51.263 --> 00:23:52.330
Let's go.

00:23:59.070 --> 00:24:01.106
So now let's measure our large,

00:24:01.106 --> 00:24:02.340
and just to make sure it's accurate,

00:24:02.340 --> 00:24:03.975
we didn't clean the measuring cup.

00:24:10.081 --> 00:24:10.916
Go home.

00:24:14.653 --> 00:24:16.121
So, at the KFC in Japan,

00:24:16.121 --> 00:24:18.857
you can order your chicken pieces in

00:24:18.857 --> 00:24:19.724
one piece,

00:24:19.724 --> 00:24:20.625
two pieces,

00:24:20.625 --> 00:24:22.761
three pieces,

00:24:22.761 --> 00:24:24.429
four pieces,

00:24:24.429 --> 00:24:26.364
and six pieces,

00:24:28.099 --> 00:24:30.302
and eight pieces,

00:24:32.637 --> 00:24:34.906
and 10 pieces,

00:24:35.841 --> 00:24:38.743
and 12 pieces.

00:24:40.579 --> 00:24:41.680
KFC in the US,

00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:43.181
our chicken portion sizes

00:24:43.181 --> 00:24:45.317
start as a two-piece combo.

00:24:45.317 --> 00:24:47.185
By the way, come on, guys.

00:24:47.185 --> 00:24:49.087
This isn't whatever
this is supposed to be.

00:24:49.087 --> 00:24:51.223
Then the three-piece
right in front of me here.

00:24:51.223 --> 00:24:52.390
And that's the exact opposite.

00:24:52.390 --> 00:24:53.825
I went extra crispy for this.

00:24:53.825 --> 00:24:55.894
Look at the size of these chicken pieces!

00:24:55.894 --> 00:24:57.829
Yes, yes to these.

00:24:57.829 --> 00:24:59.397
And the four-piece.

00:24:59.397 --> 00:25:00.632
This is somewhere in the middle.

00:25:00.632 --> 00:25:02.133
Each combo comes with a biscuit,

00:25:02.133 --> 00:25:03.201
your choice of potato,

00:25:03.201 --> 00:25:05.871
either fries or mashed with gravy,

00:25:05.871 --> 00:25:07.973
and all of them come with a medium drink.

00:25:07.973 --> 00:25:09.174
But we don't stop there.

00:25:09.174 --> 00:25:10.509
We go now to buckets,

00:25:10.509 --> 00:25:12.544
where you can get an eight-piece bucket,

00:25:12.544 --> 00:25:13.912
12-piece bucket,

00:25:13.912 --> 00:25:15.514
or a 16-piece bucket.

00:25:17.916 --> 00:25:19.351
So, now we are going to weigh

00:25:19.351 --> 00:25:20.986
our eight-piece chicken

00:25:20.986 --> 00:25:23.655
to compare the weights in each country.

00:25:23.655 --> 00:25:26.391
Joe: Ooh, ooh, oh!

00:25:26.391 --> 00:25:30.161
Oh, this is the — ugh!

00:25:30.161 --> 00:25:31.763
Yo!

00:25:31.763 --> 00:25:32.764
It's pretty close!

00:25:32.764 --> 00:25:35.066
Considering all the variables of

00:25:35.066 --> 00:25:36.768
size of chicken,

00:25:36.768 --> 00:25:39.271
bone density, batter.

00:25:39.271 --> 00:25:40.639
I don't know what I'm talking about,

00:25:40.639 --> 00:25:42.340
but that's surprisingly close.

00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:45.143
So, in Japan, a two-piece
of original chicken,

00:25:45.143 --> 00:25:47.012
which are breasts and wing

00:25:47.012 --> 00:25:49.614
and small fries and a medium drink,

00:25:49.614 --> 00:25:53.852
costs 800 yen, or $7.27.

00:25:53.852 --> 00:25:54.686
So, in Japan,

00:25:54.686 --> 00:25:58.189
actually KFC is considered
a little bit more expensive

00:25:58.189 --> 00:26:01.092
compared to other fast-food
chains, like McDonald's.

00:26:01.092 --> 00:26:04.362
So it's a classic fast food in Japan.

00:26:04.362 --> 00:26:07.866
That same meal is about $8.99,

00:26:07.866 --> 00:26:11.736
or in Japanese yen, 992.27.

00:26:11.736 --> 00:26:15.307
So that's about a 24%
cost increase in the US.

00:26:15.307 --> 00:26:18.043
So, in Japan, to make chicken at KFC,

00:26:18.043 --> 00:26:21.513
you must be certified
as a chicken specialist,

00:26:21.513 --> 00:26:23.915
and certification takes three months,

00:26:23.915 --> 00:26:27.552
and your knowledge and
skills are tested every year.

00:26:27.552 --> 00:26:28.987
All right, so let's take

00:26:28.987 --> 00:26:31.489
the chicken-specialist test right now.

00:26:31.489 --> 00:26:32.691
All right, George, let's do this.

00:26:32.691 --> 00:26:33.625
No. 1.

00:26:33.625 --> 00:26:36.761
"For the original chicken,
100% domestic ... "

00:26:36.761 --> 00:26:38.663
That's kind of a bummer.

00:26:38.663 --> 00:26:39.731
Hmm.

00:26:39.731 --> 00:26:41.399
I'm just gonna — yeah. Ba ba de ba ba ba.

00:26:41.399 --> 00:26:42.534
Animal fat or vegetable oil ...

00:26:42.534 --> 00:26:44.536
Fried with a lighter weight.

00:26:44.536 --> 00:26:47.806
With a lighter weight than —
these got hard fast.

00:26:47.806 --> 00:26:50.442
Beep, beep, beep, beep, beep ...

00:26:50.442 --> 00:26:51.676
I am in over my head on this one.

00:26:51.676 --> 00:26:53.244
I don't even know what that means.

00:26:53.244 --> 00:26:54.346
All right, so just now

00:26:54.346 --> 00:26:56.548
I've got all of the five answers,

00:26:56.548 --> 00:26:58.950
so let's check answers.

00:26:58.950 --> 00:27:01.453
Gold chicken certification.

00:27:01.453 --> 00:27:02.754
Gold!

00:27:02.754 --> 00:27:04.756
[applause]

00:27:04.756 --> 00:27:05.590
Oof!

00:27:05.590 --> 00:27:07.225
Says "Not KFC material,"

00:27:07.225 --> 00:27:10.161
and it's a picture of Colonel
Sanders giving me the finger.

00:27:10.161 --> 00:27:12.130
So I'm gonna assume I did not pass it.

00:27:12.130 --> 00:27:14.899
But anyway, I've got gold.

00:27:14.899 --> 00:27:16.835
I'm the champion!

00:27:16.835 --> 00:27:17.936
I am very surprised by that.

00:27:17.936 --> 00:27:19.638
I think I could work for KFC.

00:27:19.638 --> 00:27:22.807
I mean, I kind of look like
Colonel Sanders, right?

00:27:22.807 --> 00:27:24.509
Look at this guy.

00:27:24.509 --> 00:27:26.244
I'm a younger Colonel Sanders.

00:27:26.244 --> 00:27:27.779
KFC is doing any sort of

00:27:27.779 --> 00:27:31.349
"The Adventures of Young
Colonel Sanders" ad campaign.

00:27:31.349 --> 00:27:33.151
Is this a face that can sell chicken?

00:27:33.151 --> 00:27:35.086
Yeah! Haven't you guys
ever read the secret?

00:27:35.086 --> 00:27:36.321
I'm putting the energy that I want

00:27:36.321 --> 00:27:38.256
out into the universe,
and it comes back to me.

00:27:38.256 --> 00:27:39.557
Conner: Manifesting.

00:27:39.557 --> 00:27:41.292
It's called manifesting.

00:27:43.094 --> 00:27:45.163
So, here is everything you can only find

00:27:45.163 --> 00:27:47.399
on the menu at the KFC in Japan,

00:27:47.399 --> 00:27:48.933
but not in the US.

00:27:48.933 --> 00:27:51.269
And here is everything
you can find on the menu

00:27:51.269 --> 00:27:53.738
at a US KFC you cannot get in Japan.

00:27:53.738 --> 00:27:57.308
Here, we've got KFC biscuits.

00:27:57.308 --> 00:27:58.309
Both places have biscuits,

00:27:58.309 --> 00:27:59.711
but their biscuit has a hole in it.

00:27:59.711 --> 00:28:01.312
And it looks a lot fluffier. Right?

00:28:01.312 --> 00:28:02.480
Our biscuit, on the other hand,

00:28:02.480 --> 00:28:04.449
is just this Southern style.

00:28:04.449 --> 00:28:05.684
Not exactly a scone,

00:28:05.684 --> 00:28:07.285
but kind of looks like
one from a distance.

00:28:07.285 --> 00:28:09.320
Dry cornmeal biscuit.

00:28:09.320 --> 00:28:12.791
It comes with honey maple KFC.

00:28:12.791 --> 00:28:16.227
George: Ahh.
Joe: Oh, ho ho ho ho!

00:28:16.227 --> 00:28:17.328
Yeah.

00:28:19.964 --> 00:28:20.932
This is good.

00:28:20.932 --> 00:28:23.702
The maple is a little bit sweet for me.

00:28:23.702 --> 00:28:24.703
Mac and cheese.

00:28:24.703 --> 00:28:26.805
I can't believe you guys do
not have macaroni and cheese.

00:28:26.805 --> 00:28:28.640
Mwah. Love mac and cheese.

00:28:28.640 --> 00:28:30.175
Mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:28:30.175 --> 00:28:31.309
You don't have that in Japan?

00:28:31.309 --> 00:28:32.143
Guys.

00:28:32.143 --> 00:28:32.977
Guys!

00:28:32.977 --> 00:28:35.914
Demand this from your Japanese KFC.

00:28:35.914 --> 00:28:37.415
You want the mashed potatoes and gravy.

00:28:37.415 --> 00:28:40.518
So, we also have dip packs.

00:28:40.518 --> 00:28:42.353
Ooh.

00:28:42.353 --> 00:28:44.889
So, it's got Colonel Crispy,

00:28:44.889 --> 00:28:46.958
and some nuggets,

00:28:46.958 --> 00:28:49.427
and boneless Kentucky,

00:28:49.427 --> 00:28:51.863
and some original chicken.

00:28:51.863 --> 00:28:53.431
So this dip pack,

00:28:53.431 --> 00:28:54.966
it comes with this fries

00:28:54.966 --> 00:28:56.301
and also

00:28:56.301 --> 00:28:59.704
these three dipping sauces.

00:28:59.704 --> 00:29:02.307
And now for the quickest Sauce Talk ever.

00:29:02.307 --> 00:29:03.208
Sauce Talk.

00:29:03.208 --> 00:29:04.109
KFC sauce.

00:29:07.445 --> 00:29:10.181
I think the KFC sauce is
like a brown mustard mayo.

00:29:10.181 --> 00:29:11.783
Yeah, that sauce is good.

00:29:11.783 --> 00:29:13.952
So, we've got

00:29:13.952 --> 00:29:14.919
barbecue sauce

00:29:14.919 --> 00:29:17.055
and mustard,

00:29:17.055 --> 00:29:20.458
and this pink one is called mentaiko mayo.

00:29:20.458 --> 00:29:23.428
Mentaiko means it's spicy cod roe,

00:29:23.428 --> 00:29:26.164
and it's very popular at KFC in Japan.

00:29:26.164 --> 00:29:27.265
This is actually great.

00:29:27.265 --> 00:29:28.933
I'll dip this.

00:29:28.933 --> 00:29:29.768
Mm!

00:29:32.537 --> 00:29:35.106
It tastes fantastic.

00:29:35.106 --> 00:29:36.975
Winner!

00:29:36.975 --> 00:29:39.711
So, if you want to have
a little bigger one,

00:29:39.711 --> 00:29:41.846
you can order dip barrel.

00:29:41.846 --> 00:29:44.449
I mean, it's double
amount of this dip pack,

00:29:44.449 --> 00:29:45.850
so it's going to be very big.

00:29:45.850 --> 00:29:48.353
So, this one right here is called

00:29:48.353 --> 00:29:50.488
four-piece red hot chicken box,

00:29:50.488 --> 00:29:54.025
and it comes with a pie and fry,

00:29:54.025 --> 00:29:56.728
and a medium drink.

00:29:56.728 --> 00:29:59.898
And actually we have other box options,

00:29:59.898 --> 00:30:03.601
like four-piece half hot
and half original box.

00:30:03.601 --> 00:30:05.937
And it comes with fries as well.

00:30:05.937 --> 00:30:10.275
And six-piece half hot
and half original box.

00:30:10.275 --> 00:30:11.843
It comes with fries again.

00:30:13.778 --> 00:30:16.414
So, in Japan, we have tori no hi pack.

00:30:16.414 --> 00:30:18.183
That means chicken day.

00:30:18.183 --> 00:30:21.386
It's on every 28th of the month.

00:30:21.386 --> 00:30:24.055
And two stands for ni,

00:30:24.055 --> 00:30:27.025
and eight stands for wa.

00:30:27.025 --> 00:30:28.827
And it becomes niwa,

00:30:28.827 --> 00:30:32.197
and niwa is synonmous with niwatori.

00:30:32.197 --> 00:30:34.465
Niwatori means chicken.

00:30:34.465 --> 00:30:37.168
So that's why it's called chicken day.

00:30:37.168 --> 00:30:42.140
KFC in America has extra-crispy chicken.

00:30:42.140 --> 00:30:43.441
This is the best type of chicken.

00:30:43.441 --> 00:30:44.309
I mean, look at this.

00:30:44.309 --> 00:30:45.577
I don't know what they do to this,

00:30:45.577 --> 00:30:47.812
but the skin is practically falling off.

00:30:47.812 --> 00:30:50.181
It is so crispy and so delicious.

00:30:50.181 --> 00:30:52.016
I love extra crispy so much.

00:30:52.016 --> 00:30:53.651
I got this little guy.

00:30:53.651 --> 00:30:55.053
The Chicken Little. Look at this guy.

00:30:55.053 --> 00:30:56.454
Eh? Look at this little guy.

00:30:56.454 --> 00:30:58.356
Comes with pickles, mayo.

00:30:58.356 --> 00:30:59.991
The pot pie that they have here,

00:30:59.991 --> 00:31:02.961
they're not kidding when they
say "pie" in the pot pie.

00:31:02.961 --> 00:31:03.928
Look how thick this is!

00:31:03.928 --> 00:31:05.797
Speaking of big dishes of stuff,

00:31:05.797 --> 00:31:07.332
the Famous Bowl.

00:31:07.332 --> 00:31:10.668
Once upon a time, a KFC employee was like,

00:31:10.668 --> 00:31:13.938
I'm gonna put everything into
one dish and call it a day.

00:31:13.938 --> 00:31:16.074
And ta-da, the Famous Bowl was born.

00:31:16.074 --> 00:31:18.309
This has to be, like, 3 pounds.

00:31:18.309 --> 00:31:20.445
All right, so here we've got

00:31:20.445 --> 00:31:22.647
two special twisters.

00:31:22.647 --> 00:31:25.116
So this one right here is called

00:31:25.116 --> 00:31:27.051
pepper mayonnaise twister.

00:31:27.051 --> 00:31:29.687
Ooh! It looks great.

00:31:32.857 --> 00:31:35.059
[applause]

00:31:35.059 --> 00:31:36.761
9 out of 10.

00:31:36.761 --> 00:31:38.730
KFC, thank you!

00:31:38.730 --> 00:31:40.732
Thank you for making me happy.

00:31:40.732 --> 00:31:42.267
So, next, we've got,

00:31:42.267 --> 00:31:43.134
ooh!

00:31:43.134 --> 00:31:45.136
Teriyaki twister.

00:31:45.136 --> 00:31:46.604
Should be great.

00:31:46.604 --> 00:31:47.872
It's kind of gross.

00:31:47.872 --> 00:31:49.107
[laughs]

00:31:49.107 --> 00:31:51.976
It's got mayo and Colonel Crispy,

00:31:51.976 --> 00:31:53.177
some veggies,

00:31:53.177 --> 00:31:56.514
and I hope this is teriyaki sauce.

00:31:56.514 --> 00:31:57.615
Itadakimasu!

00:32:01.119 --> 00:32:04.889
Mm. Mm! Mm!

00:32:04.889 --> 00:32:09.627
It looks gross, but it tastes incredible.

00:32:09.627 --> 00:32:13.364
10 out of 10. Congratulations.

00:32:13.364 --> 00:32:14.799
Oishii!

00:32:14.799 --> 00:32:16.200
It means delicious!

00:32:16.200 --> 00:32:17.936
Look how tiny those twisters are.

00:32:17.936 --> 00:32:20.505
I could eat, like, three
of those easily. Easily!

00:32:20.505 --> 00:32:22.840
All right, so we have nuggets.

00:32:22.840 --> 00:32:25.410
We have three pieces,

00:32:25.410 --> 00:32:27.045
five pieces,

00:32:27.045 --> 00:32:30.381
and they come with only ketchup.

00:32:30.381 --> 00:32:32.617
Also at a US KFC that
you can't get in Japan

00:32:32.617 --> 00:32:33.584
are wings.

00:32:33.584 --> 00:32:35.186
You can get wings at the KFC

00:32:35.186 --> 00:32:39.424
in units of six, 12, 24 or 48.

00:32:39.424 --> 00:32:42.460
I believe the three wing
flavors that I got here are

00:32:42.460 --> 00:32:43.861
standard Buffalo,

00:32:43.861 --> 00:32:45.997
the honey barbecue,

00:32:45.997 --> 00:32:47.899
and if you're a total wuss,

00:32:47.899 --> 00:32:49.133
unsauced?

00:32:49.133 --> 00:32:50.468
What's wrong with you?

00:32:50.468 --> 00:32:51.769
Yeah. Very sketchy.

00:32:51.769 --> 00:32:54.906
You can also get them, in a limited time,

00:32:54.906 --> 00:32:56.441
Nashville hot sauce.

00:32:56.441 --> 00:33:00.111
Now we have special sandwiches.

00:33:00.111 --> 00:33:01.612
This one right here is called

00:33:01.612 --> 00:33:04.315
Japanese-style chicken katsu sandwich.

00:33:04.315 --> 00:33:06.184
So let's take a look inside.

00:33:06.184 --> 00:33:07.285
So, it's got mayo,

00:33:07.285 --> 00:33:08.987
and it's got cabbage,

00:33:08.987 --> 00:33:11.289
and chicken katsu right there.

00:33:11.289 --> 00:33:12.390
Itadakimasu!

00:33:14.492 --> 00:33:15.960
Mm.

00:33:15.960 --> 00:33:16.794
Oh!

00:33:16.794 --> 00:33:19.697
This sauce is soy-sauce-based sauce,

00:33:19.697 --> 00:33:20.965
and it's a little bit sweet.

00:33:20.965 --> 00:33:23.901
And this mayo is also
great with this sauce.

00:33:23.901 --> 00:33:25.803
This looks really small,

00:33:25.803 --> 00:33:28.773
but it has huge amount of chicken.

00:33:28.773 --> 00:33:31.309
So if you eat this, you're gonna be full.

00:33:32.210 --> 00:33:36.047
And next one, we've got chicken fillet.

00:33:36.047 --> 00:33:38.649
Wow. This is also huge.

00:33:38.649 --> 00:33:40.718
All right, so this one right here

00:33:40.718 --> 00:33:43.855
is called black hot sandwich.

00:33:43.855 --> 00:33:45.590
Ooh!

00:33:45.590 --> 00:33:48.092
Look at this. It's, like, pepper mayo?

00:33:48.092 --> 00:33:50.328
I just tasted this pepper mayo,

00:33:50.328 --> 00:33:53.297
but it has a little, like, spiciness.

00:33:53.297 --> 00:33:55.199
Ooh, ho ho.

00:33:55.199 --> 00:33:57.835
Oh, man. It's too strong.

00:33:57.835 --> 00:34:00.071
I wouldn't get it. Be careful.

00:34:00.071 --> 00:34:03.608
Now, of course, the US
has a chicken sandwich.

00:34:03.608 --> 00:34:05.443
But our chicken sandwich
and their chicken sandwich,

00:34:05.443 --> 00:34:06.944
as you can see, is way different.

00:34:06.944 --> 00:34:09.614
You can also get it spicy or classic.

00:34:09.614 --> 00:34:10.448
This is a classic.

00:34:10.448 --> 00:34:11.983
All right, so this one right here

00:34:11.983 --> 00:34:14.352
is called Colonel Crispy.

00:34:14.352 --> 00:34:15.653
Is it only in Japan?

00:34:15.653 --> 00:34:17.655
I cannot confirm the difference between

00:34:17.655 --> 00:34:20.391
a Colonel Crispy and a KFC chicken tender.

00:34:20.391 --> 00:34:22.660
They call their tenders Colonel Crispies,

00:34:22.660 --> 00:34:26.097
and we call our Colonel
Crispies chicken tenders.

00:34:26.097 --> 00:34:28.733
It's been a while since
I ordered this one,

00:34:28.733 --> 00:34:31.569
but it still has crispy bits.

00:34:32.970 --> 00:34:33.805
Good job.

00:34:33.805 --> 00:34:38.376
Japanese KFC's technology,
state of the art.

00:34:38.376 --> 00:34:41.379
We currently have a Nashville hot chicken

00:34:41.379 --> 00:34:42.380
and hot tenders.

00:34:42.380 --> 00:34:43.581
I went ahead with the tenders.

00:34:43.581 --> 00:34:44.415
I've just been informed

00:34:44.415 --> 00:34:45.917
this was a big TikTok thing for a minute.

00:34:45.917 --> 00:34:47.351
Something about biting
it and crunching it.

00:34:47.351 --> 00:34:48.453
I don't know anything about that.

00:34:48.453 --> 00:34:49.787
I can say just by holding this,

00:34:49.787 --> 00:34:51.522
there's no way these are crispy.

00:34:51.522 --> 00:34:52.356
[crunching]

00:34:53.691 --> 00:34:54.926
Was not that spicy.

00:34:54.926 --> 00:34:55.860
That's kind of spicy.

00:34:55.860 --> 00:34:57.228
I do like this a lot.

00:35:00.298 --> 00:35:01.899
I can't stop eating it.

00:35:01.899 --> 00:35:04.469
Ooh. That heat's catching up with me.

00:35:04.469 --> 00:35:06.003
Slow burn. Slow build on the heat.

00:35:06.003 --> 00:35:09.173
So, here we've got
Japanese exclusive drinks.

00:35:09.173 --> 00:35:12.009
This one right here is

00:35:12.009 --> 00:35:12.977
water,

00:35:13.978 --> 00:35:18.349
but it comes with this Assam tea pack.

00:35:19.217 --> 00:35:22.253
It's supposed to be hot, but it's cold.

00:35:22.253 --> 00:35:24.856
And next one, we've got coffee.

00:35:24.856 --> 00:35:27.024
So, this one right here is

00:35:27.024 --> 00:35:29.060
roasted rich coffee.

00:35:29.060 --> 00:35:30.061
Itadakimasu.

00:35:32.530 --> 00:35:36.067
It's a little bit better
than the normal coffee.

00:35:36.067 --> 00:35:40.004
And here we've got Earl Grey iced tea.

00:35:40.004 --> 00:35:41.205
It's not sweet at all.

00:35:41.205 --> 00:35:44.142
And next one is melon soda.

00:35:44.142 --> 00:35:46.410
It has bright green color.

00:35:51.048 --> 00:35:52.950
Horrible. It's too sweet.

00:35:52.950 --> 00:35:55.353
Here is ginger ale.

00:35:55.353 --> 00:35:56.387
Nothing special.

00:35:56.387 --> 00:35:57.855
And the last one,

00:35:57.855 --> 00:36:00.358
it's Nacchan refreshing orange.

00:36:00.358 --> 00:36:02.293
Fountain drinks. There's
a few that we can get

00:36:02.293 --> 00:36:04.795
that you guys cannot over there in Japan.

00:36:04.795 --> 00:36:07.565
The first one is a beverage that

00:36:07.565 --> 00:36:11.469
I have yet to meet one
human being who enjoys it.

00:36:11.469 --> 00:36:13.137
Of course, I'm talking about Sierra Mist.

00:36:13.137 --> 00:36:14.906
Maybe grossest soda ever.

00:36:16.807 --> 00:36:18.442
Oh, it's so bad.

00:36:18.442 --> 00:36:20.711
Another drink that you can get at KFC

00:36:20.711 --> 00:36:21.946
that you can't get at Japan,

00:36:21.946 --> 00:36:22.947
and here it is right here,

00:36:22.947 --> 00:36:24.215
Mountain Dew's great.

00:36:24.215 --> 00:36:25.983
When I was in college, I
worked at a pizza place.

00:36:25.983 --> 00:36:27.852
I drank so much Mountain Dew, I threw up.

00:36:27.852 --> 00:36:28.853
And now I'm drinking Mountain Dew.

00:36:28.853 --> 00:36:29.954
Let's see if I can do it again.

00:36:29.954 --> 00:36:33.424
My favorite beverage,
Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning.

00:36:34.926 --> 00:36:36.194
So good. So good.

00:36:36.194 --> 00:36:39.530
So, drinks are just
normal, nothing special,

00:36:39.530 --> 00:36:41.866
but chickens are

00:36:41.866 --> 00:36:43.701
finger-licking good.

00:36:44.769 --> 00:36:46.070
Desserts at a US KFC,

00:36:46.070 --> 00:36:48.039
you can get this chocolate chip cookie.

00:36:48.039 --> 00:36:49.941
Recognize that guy?

00:36:49.941 --> 00:36:51.776
I just look just like this guy.

00:36:51.776 --> 00:36:53.711
And, finally,

00:36:53.711 --> 00:36:55.246
a chocolate chip cake.

00:36:57.381 --> 00:36:59.784
So, let's talk about Christmas in Japan.

00:36:59.784 --> 00:37:03.521
So Christmas is one of the
biggest events in Japan,

00:37:03.521 --> 00:37:07.792
even though about 1% of
Japanese people are Christians.

00:37:07.792 --> 00:37:11.596
We just enter Christmas
as just a fun event.

00:37:11.596 --> 00:37:14.465
And as for KFC for Christmas in Japan,

00:37:14.465 --> 00:37:16.934
back in 1970s,

00:37:16.934 --> 00:37:18.836
Japan KFC launched

00:37:18.836 --> 00:37:22.607
a hugely successful advertising campaign

00:37:22.607 --> 00:37:24.575
called Kentakki ni wa Kurisumasu.

00:37:24.575 --> 00:37:27.078
That's Kentucky for Christmas.

00:37:27.078 --> 00:37:30.181
And with that strong marketing campaign,

00:37:30.181 --> 00:37:31.616
it became so popular

00:37:31.616 --> 00:37:34.485
to have KFC for Christmas in Japan.

00:37:34.485 --> 00:37:38.556
And now about 3.6
million Japanese families

00:37:38.556 --> 00:37:40.258
eat KFC for Christmas.

00:37:40.258 --> 00:37:42.727
And talking about my personal experiences,

00:37:42.727 --> 00:37:44.262
yes, when I was young,

00:37:44.262 --> 00:37:47.598
I would eat KFC for
Christmas with my family.

00:37:47.598 --> 00:37:50.101
But when you started dating, you know,

00:37:50.101 --> 00:37:52.303
Christmas makes the transformation

00:37:52.303 --> 00:37:56.173
from a family event to couple's event.

00:37:56.173 --> 00:37:58.109
And I'm looking for the one

00:37:58.109 --> 00:38:01.212
who can enjoy KFC for Christmas with me.

00:38:03.147 --> 00:38:05.983
So, in Japan, one drumstick of ori —

00:38:05.983 --> 00:38:07.385
ooh!

00:38:07.385 --> 00:38:11.088
So, in Japan, one drumstick
of original chicken,

00:38:11.088 --> 00:38:14.725
on average, has 237 calories.

00:38:14.725 --> 00:38:17.261
Chicken's looking a
little limp there, George.

00:38:17.261 --> 00:38:21.465
In the US, one stiff
drumstick of original recipe

00:38:21.465 --> 00:38:22.933
is 130 calories.

00:38:22.933 --> 00:38:25.336
But according to KFC's US site,

00:38:25.336 --> 00:38:27.338
that's for a 53-gram piece.

00:38:27.338 --> 00:38:29.940
Now, adjusting for the 87-gram piece,

00:38:29.940 --> 00:38:31.008
like that of Japan,

00:38:31.008 --> 00:38:33.678
the calories go up to 210.

00:38:33.678 --> 00:38:35.079
Does that make sense? Great.

00:38:35.079 --> 00:38:37.581
Now, take this bad boy
and make him extra crispy?

00:38:37.581 --> 00:38:40.117
You got 270 calories.

00:38:40.117 --> 00:38:43.587
So, in Japan, a two-piece
of original chickens

00:38:43.587 --> 00:38:45.790
and a small fry and a medium drink

00:38:45.790 --> 00:38:49.560
is roughly 717 calories.

00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:52.596
A US two-piece, individual
fry, and medium drink

00:38:52.596 --> 00:38:55.466
comes out to be 990 calories.

00:38:55.466 --> 00:38:56.801
So a lot more.

00:38:56.801 --> 00:38:58.936
It's too many calories.

00:38:58.936 --> 00:39:00.705
Mm.

00:39:00.705 --> 00:39:02.173
Not enough calories, if you ask me.

00:39:02.173 --> 00:39:04.442
But finger-licking good.

00:39:04.442 --> 00:39:05.943
I think KFC got to George.

00:39:05.943 --> 00:39:07.411
He keeps dropping that slogan.

00:39:07.411 --> 00:39:08.279
Are they paying George?

00:39:08.279 --> 00:39:10.848
I think George is getting some
money on the side from KFC.

00:39:10.848 --> 00:39:11.682
Oh, my God.

00:39:11.682 --> 00:39:13.217
If George turns out to be Colonel Sanders,

00:39:13.217 --> 00:39:14.585
I will lose my mind.

00:39:16.153 --> 00:39:19.557
So, KFC in Japan doesn't
disclose their ingredients.

00:39:19.557 --> 00:39:22.259
So we emailed their customer support,

00:39:22.259 --> 00:39:24.328
and this is what they told us.

00:39:26.530 --> 00:39:27.365
And in the US,

00:39:27.365 --> 00:39:29.400
our original-recipe
chicken ingredients are:

00:39:29.400 --> 00:39:30.735
first, with the fresh chicken,

00:39:30.735 --> 00:39:33.671
it is marinated with
salt, sodium phosphate,

00:39:33.671 --> 00:39:35.206
and monosodium glutamate.

00:39:35.206 --> 00:39:36.040
On to the breading,

00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:37.775
it's breaded with wheat flour,

00:39:37.775 --> 00:39:39.043
tricalcium phosphate,

00:39:39.043 --> 00:39:40.111
maltodextrin,

00:39:40.111 --> 00:39:41.011
triglycerides,

00:39:41.011 --> 00:39:42.146
natural flavor,

00:39:42.146 --> 00:39:45.850
Colonel's secret original
recipe seasoning.

00:39:45.850 --> 00:39:50.121
They also said our fries are
made of potatoes, obviously,

00:39:50.121 --> 00:39:51.789
and vegetable oil and fat.

00:39:51.789 --> 00:39:54.291
The batter is made of rice flour,

00:39:54.291 --> 00:39:55.393
vegetable starch,

00:39:55.393 --> 00:39:57.061
and dextrose.

00:39:57.061 --> 00:39:57.895
And our fries,

00:39:57.895 --> 00:39:59.230
which contain sea salt,

00:39:59.230 --> 00:40:00.498
monosodium glutamate,

00:40:00.498 --> 00:40:01.766
tricalcium phosphate,

00:40:01.766 --> 00:40:03.267
hydrolyzed soy protein,

00:40:03.267 --> 00:40:04.702
potassium chloride,

00:40:04.702 --> 00:40:06.137
potatoes, that's good,

00:40:06.137 --> 00:40:07.671
degermed yellow cornmeal,

00:40:07.671 --> 00:40:11.108
disodium dihydrogen pyrophosphate,

00:40:11.108 --> 00:40:13.010
to maintain natural color.

00:40:13.010 --> 00:40:13.978
What's more natural

00:40:13.978 --> 00:40:16.280
than disodium dihydrogen pyrophosphate?

00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:17.548
Rolls off the tongue.

00:40:17.548 --> 00:40:19.083
And one thing I have to say

00:40:19.083 --> 00:40:21.552
is that our fries are imported

00:40:21.552 --> 00:40:23.821
from both America and Belgium.

00:40:23.821 --> 00:40:26.524
And some of the Belgian fries

00:40:26.524 --> 00:40:29.326
are made with potatoes from France.

00:40:29.326 --> 00:40:33.964
So our fries are truly, truly French.

00:40:33.964 --> 00:40:35.099
Bonjour!

00:40:35.099 --> 00:40:39.303
In the US, we have four chicken shapes.

00:40:39.303 --> 00:40:42.206
In Japan, we have five chicken shapes.

00:40:42.206 --> 00:40:43.207
Let me explain.

00:40:43.207 --> 00:40:45.409
So, we have this one.

00:40:45.409 --> 00:40:46.811
It's called kiru.

00:40:46.811 --> 00:40:51.682
Kiru is like chicken's breast, right here.

00:40:53.350 --> 00:40:54.351
[laughing]

00:40:54.351 --> 00:40:57.455
I'm gonna say chicken's chest.

00:40:57.455 --> 00:40:58.556
Breasts ...

00:40:58.556 --> 00:41:00.124
[laughing]

00:41:03.227 --> 00:41:07.331
Kiru is like chicken's chest, right there.

00:41:07.331 --> 00:41:08.599
The first one is the breast.

00:41:08.599 --> 00:41:10.267
This is the big piece of
chicken your dad gets.

00:41:10.267 --> 00:41:12.736
And also we got wing.

00:41:12.736 --> 00:41:15.806
It's a, as you know, chicken wing.

00:41:15.806 --> 00:41:17.475
This is supposed to be a wing.

00:41:17.475 --> 00:41:19.710
This is laughably small.

00:41:19.710 --> 00:41:21.645
And we've got this one.

00:41:21.645 --> 00:41:22.947
It's called rib.

00:41:22.947 --> 00:41:23.881
Chickens have ribs?

00:41:23.881 --> 00:41:28.185
So, rib is, like, under
the chest, right here.

00:41:28.185 --> 00:41:30.187
And we got this one, thigh.

00:41:30.187 --> 00:41:32.289
Thigh is, like, chicken's lower back.

00:41:33.224 --> 00:41:36.961
And the next piece is this,
which I think is the thigh.

00:41:36.961 --> 00:41:38.762
And, of course,

00:41:38.762 --> 00:41:40.631
the next piece, everyone knows the drum.

00:41:40.631 --> 00:41:42.032
And this is a chicken's leg.

00:41:43.033 --> 00:41:44.835
Joe: From calorie count to portion sizes,

00:41:44.835 --> 00:41:46.637
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:41:46.637 --> 00:41:49.540
between Starbucks in Japan and the US.

00:41:49.540 --> 00:41:51.208
This is "Food Wars."

00:41:56.080 --> 00:41:59.683
In Japan, our hot coffee
comes in four sizes.

00:41:59.683 --> 00:42:00.885
Short.

00:42:00.885 --> 00:42:02.219
Short.

00:42:02.219 --> 00:42:03.521
Tall.

00:42:03.521 --> 00:42:05.155
Tall.

00:42:05.155 --> 00:42:06.423
Grande.

00:42:06.423 --> 00:42:08.092
The grande.

00:42:08.092 --> 00:42:09.627
And venti.

00:42:09.627 --> 00:42:12.329
And, of course, the venti.

00:42:12.329 --> 00:42:13.531
Mm!

00:42:17.701 --> 00:42:20.704
Starbucks episode. I'm
taking a sip of everything.

00:42:20.704 --> 00:42:24.875
In Japan, our iced coffee
comes in four sizes.

00:42:24.875 --> 00:42:25.709
Short.

00:42:25.709 --> 00:42:28.012
So, we start with the tall.

00:42:28.012 --> 00:42:29.113
Tall.

00:42:30.247 --> 00:42:32.349
Too good. And ...

00:42:32.349 --> 00:42:33.183
Grande.

00:42:33.183 --> 00:42:34.518
Grande, mm.

00:42:34.518 --> 00:42:35.753
And venti.

00:42:35.753 --> 00:42:37.788
Now, when we get to the iced venti size,

00:42:37.788 --> 00:42:39.323
it gets a little bit different.

00:42:39.323 --> 00:42:41.692
So, our iced venti ain't 20;

00:42:41.692 --> 00:42:43.727
it's 24 ounces.

00:42:43.727 --> 00:42:46.430
And then we have a bigger size,

00:42:46.430 --> 00:42:50.501
the trenta, which is 30 fluid ounces.

00:42:50.501 --> 00:42:52.269
For your iced-coffee aficionados

00:42:52.269 --> 00:42:53.737
who also hate your bladder,

00:42:53.737 --> 00:42:55.205
this is the one for you.

00:42:55.205 --> 00:42:58.609
So, in Japan, we have this
handy coffee traveler.

00:42:58.609 --> 00:43:00.778
It's 12 cups of coffee.

00:43:00.778 --> 00:43:05.215
So you just take this off
and set the cup right here.

00:43:09.820 --> 00:43:10.988
Itadakimasu!

00:43:13.691 --> 00:43:15.225
Muy bien!

00:43:15.225 --> 00:43:16.493
[sighs]

00:43:16.493 --> 00:43:17.728
I'm disappointed.

00:43:17.728 --> 00:43:20.798
Because our coffee traveler box is this.

00:43:20.798 --> 00:43:22.466
It's 96 fluid ounces.

00:43:23.734 --> 00:43:26.136
So this peels off, which is nice.

00:43:26.136 --> 00:43:28.238
Theirs is funner than ours.

00:43:28.238 --> 00:43:30.908
I like that one. Like, this is like ...

00:43:32.343 --> 00:43:33.911
[cardboard scraping]

00:43:33.911 --> 00:43:36.113
We got this boring box. Look at this.

00:43:37.648 --> 00:43:40.050
Ugh! It's like a caveman.

00:43:42.886 --> 00:43:45.122
So, here is everything

00:43:45.122 --> 00:43:46.757
you can only find on the menu

00:43:46.757 --> 00:43:48.592
at Starbucks in Japan.

00:43:48.592 --> 00:43:50.894
And here is everything you can get

00:43:50.894 --> 00:43:53.897
at a US Starbucks you cannot get in Japan.

00:43:53.897 --> 00:43:56.100
Holy [beep].

00:43:56.100 --> 00:43:57.401
A bit of clarification:

00:43:57.401 --> 00:43:59.737
We know that Starbucks will
customize drink orders,

00:43:59.737 --> 00:44:01.205
and there's thousands of variations

00:44:01.205 --> 00:44:02.706
of special secret menu items.

00:44:02.706 --> 00:44:04.041
Plus, now, thanks to TikTok,

00:44:04.041 --> 00:44:05.175
there are endless new drinks.

00:44:05.175 --> 00:44:08.078
So these are things on the
official Starbucks menu

00:44:08.078 --> 00:44:09.780
in Japan and the US.

00:44:09.780 --> 00:44:13.984
So, Japan Starbucks updates
their menu very often.

00:44:13.984 --> 00:44:16.887
So by the time this video is released,

00:44:16.887 --> 00:44:18.989
they might not be available.

00:44:18.989 --> 00:44:20.391
Gomenasai.

00:44:20.391 --> 00:44:21.492
Sorry.

00:44:21.492 --> 00:44:24.762
This one is called Go peach Frappuccino.

00:44:25.729 --> 00:44:26.964
Mm!

00:44:26.964 --> 00:44:29.233
I really love peach,

00:44:29.233 --> 00:44:30.501
and this is good.

00:44:30.501 --> 00:44:32.603
7 out of 10.

00:44:32.603 --> 00:44:33.937
Nice!

00:44:33.937 --> 00:44:36.106
Go pineapple Frappuccino.

00:44:36.106 --> 00:44:39.410
Pink frozen lemonade and passion tea.

00:44:41.945 --> 00:44:43.447
It's a little bit sour.

00:44:43.447 --> 00:44:45.783
Yuzu citrus and tea.

00:44:46.617 --> 00:44:48.285
It's the worst.

00:44:48.285 --> 00:44:49.887
What happened to you?

00:44:49.887 --> 00:44:51.989
1 out of 10.

00:44:51.989 --> 00:44:54.024
Hojicha classic latte.

00:44:54.024 --> 00:44:57.594
So, hojicha is roasted Japanese green tea

00:44:57.594 --> 00:45:01.699
that originated in Kyoto 100 years ago.

00:45:02.633 --> 00:45:04.635
This is good!

00:45:04.635 --> 00:45:05.836
Fantastic!

00:45:05.836 --> 00:45:09.073
I'll give this 9 out of 10.

00:45:09.073 --> 00:45:11.408
Chai chocolate Frappuccino.

00:45:16.680 --> 00:45:17.514
What?

00:45:19.316 --> 00:45:22.853
[laughs] Too sweet!

00:45:22.853 --> 00:45:24.788
Espresso affogato.

00:45:24.788 --> 00:45:27.091
So, affogato is the process

00:45:27.091 --> 00:45:30.561
of pouring espresso shot onto ice cream.

00:45:31.729 --> 00:45:33.697
[in Japanese] Mixing, mixing.

00:45:33.697 --> 00:45:35.365
Clip: I don't know about
y'all, but this s--- --

00:45:35.365 --> 00:45:36.734
[gags]

00:45:36.734 --> 00:45:38.736
Again, it's too sweet.

00:45:38.736 --> 00:45:43.006
We've got dark mocha chip cream.

00:45:43.006 --> 00:45:46.043
I'm so sorry. I spilled most of it.

00:45:46.043 --> 00:45:47.311
The last one,

00:45:47.311 --> 00:45:50.647
we've got mango passion tea.

00:45:50.647 --> 00:45:54.885
And as you can imagine,
this has strong mango taste.

00:45:54.885 --> 00:45:56.220
[clapboard snaps]

00:45:56.220 --> 00:45:57.321
Ugh!

00:45:57.321 --> 00:45:59.323
I feel like I'm hitting a wall here, guys.

00:45:59.323 --> 00:46:01.024
And you know what would help that?

00:46:02.526 --> 00:46:05.195
The US does not have as many exclusives

00:46:05.195 --> 00:46:07.498
as they do in Japan, at
least not as frequently,

00:46:07.498 --> 00:46:09.266
but at the time of the shooting this,

00:46:09.266 --> 00:46:10.334
it is the fall.

00:46:10.334 --> 00:46:12.870
And you know what that
means, Starbucks USA fans.

00:46:12.870 --> 00:46:15.472
Pumpkin spice latte.

00:46:15.472 --> 00:46:19.176
Every fall, the entire
country loses their mind,

00:46:19.176 --> 00:46:20.811
and they go buy pumpkins,

00:46:20.811 --> 00:46:22.012
and they get themselves this,

00:46:22.012 --> 00:46:23.213
which is pretty much a latte

00:46:23.213 --> 00:46:25.249
that tastes like pumpkin pie.

00:46:26.583 --> 00:46:29.720
And as basic as it is, it is pretty good.

00:46:29.720 --> 00:46:32.723
Starbucks has decided to
introduce a new fall beverage

00:46:32.723 --> 00:46:34.424
to their lineup, and that is this:

00:46:34.424 --> 00:46:37.427
the apple crisp macchiato.

00:46:37.427 --> 00:46:38.529
Let's check it out.

00:46:40.831 --> 00:46:42.032
What is this?

00:46:42.032 --> 00:46:44.334
Oh, man, that's terrible!

00:46:44.334 --> 00:46:45.803
What's wrong with you guys?

00:46:45.803 --> 00:46:46.770
You thought this could compete

00:46:46.770 --> 00:46:48.238
with the pumpkin spice latte?

00:46:48.238 --> 00:46:49.072
Not at all.

00:46:49.072 --> 00:46:52.075
[echoing] Does it sound like
I'm, like, losing my mind?

00:46:52.075 --> 00:46:55.112
'Cause I'm, like, really
keyed up right now.

00:46:55.112 --> 00:46:55.946
I'm going to do my best

00:46:55.946 --> 00:46:57.948
to pretend like I'm not unhinged.

00:46:57.948 --> 00:47:01.385
Starbucks in the US, is this -- [laughs]

00:47:01.385 --> 00:47:02.386
Moving on.

00:47:02.386 --> 00:47:03.453
Flat white.

00:47:04.421 --> 00:47:07.858
What is a flat white?
This is a flat white.

00:47:07.858 --> 00:47:09.660
♪ Frappuccinos! ♪

00:47:09.660 --> 00:47:12.329
Strawberry funnel cake Frappuccino.

00:47:12.329 --> 00:47:13.964
[sighs]

00:47:13.964 --> 00:47:15.532
That is really sweet.

00:47:16.600 --> 00:47:17.835
Whoo!

00:47:17.835 --> 00:47:20.103
On a scale of 1 to 10, that gets, like,

00:47:20.103 --> 00:47:22.139
10 yos!

00:47:22.139 --> 00:47:23.674
Joe's yos. That's how I'm rating them.

00:47:23.674 --> 00:47:26.043
I cannot imagine any time
of the day wanting that.

00:47:26.043 --> 00:47:27.911
A WTMOC. What is that?

00:47:30.514 --> 00:47:31.915
Eight yos.

00:47:31.915 --> 00:47:33.750
Chai creme.

00:47:33.750 --> 00:47:35.352
Oh, God, come on.

00:47:35.352 --> 00:47:37.454
The caramel ribbon crunch.

00:47:38.956 --> 00:47:40.924
Yeah, it's still really bad.

00:47:40.924 --> 00:47:43.060
Java chip Frappuccino.

00:47:44.795 --> 00:47:45.796
Nope!

00:47:45.796 --> 00:47:47.965
Last one. Thank you, God!

00:47:47.965 --> 00:47:52.970
Double chocolaty chip creme Frappuccino.

00:47:54.271 --> 00:47:55.372
Shh!

00:47:57.474 --> 00:47:59.810
That's not nearly as
chocolaty as the other one.

00:47:59.810 --> 00:48:00.811
That's, like, less chocolaty,

00:48:00.811 --> 00:48:02.045
and there's "double" in the title.

00:48:02.045 --> 00:48:05.449
And we also got limited tea.

00:48:05.449 --> 00:48:08.452
This one is called Youthberry.

00:48:08.452 --> 00:48:11.355
So, Youthberry is citrus white tea,

00:48:11.355 --> 00:48:14.758
featuring mango, pineapple, and acai.

00:48:14.758 --> 00:48:17.127
Wow! So it should be healthy.

00:48:17.127 --> 00:48:20.931
And next one, we have roasted green tea.

00:48:20.931 --> 00:48:23.066
We drink this on a daily basis

00:48:23.066 --> 00:48:26.403
with breakfast, lunch, dinner,

00:48:26.403 --> 00:48:28.071
anytime you want.

00:48:28.071 --> 00:48:29.973
It's our go-to drink.

00:48:29.973 --> 00:48:32.776
Also in the US, you can
get iced black teas.

00:48:32.776 --> 00:48:34.912
Can't get those in
Japan. I don't know why.

00:48:34.912 --> 00:48:36.513
You can get these varieties.

00:48:36.513 --> 00:48:39.917
An iced royal English breakfast tea latte.

00:48:39.917 --> 00:48:41.585
Tea sucks,

00:48:41.585 --> 00:48:43.754
so I have very low expectations for this.

00:48:45.322 --> 00:48:46.356
Expectations met!

00:48:46.356 --> 00:48:47.557
The next one you have here

00:48:47.557 --> 00:48:49.559
is an iced London fog tea.

00:48:49.559 --> 00:48:51.194
I don't know what makes it foggy.

00:48:52.262 --> 00:48:53.096
I don't know.

00:48:53.096 --> 00:48:55.465
And you can also get an
iced matcha lemonade.

00:48:55.465 --> 00:48:57.401
Other iced black teas I
could not get my hands on

00:48:57.401 --> 00:48:59.169
is the iced guava black tea

00:48:59.169 --> 00:49:00.837
and the iced peach green tea.

00:49:00.837 --> 00:49:02.072
Ooh, I bet that peach one's pretty good.

00:49:02.072 --> 00:49:03.674
Cold brews and nitro cold brews.

00:49:03.674 --> 00:49:07.577
You can get yourself a
nitro cold brew right here,

00:49:07.577 --> 00:49:11.915
and also a salted caramel cream cold brew.

00:49:14.151 --> 00:49:16.286
Vanilla sweet cream cold brew.

00:49:16.286 --> 00:49:17.955
When I said I was taking
a sip of every one,

00:49:17.955 --> 00:49:19.356
I'm taking a sip of every one.

00:49:19.356 --> 00:49:22.292
I'm, like, caffeine drunk.

00:49:22.292 --> 00:49:23.961
I bet that was good four hours ago.

00:49:23.961 --> 00:49:26.763
You can get yourself an
iced shaken espresso,

00:49:26.763 --> 00:49:27.798
is that what it says?

00:49:29.032 --> 00:49:30.600
[meter busts]

00:49:33.337 --> 00:49:35.639
[dance music]

00:49:37.407 --> 00:49:40.277
[echoing] Does it sound like
I'm, like, losing my mind?

00:49:45.949 --> 00:49:46.783
All right.

00:49:46.783 --> 00:49:50.053
The honey almond milk flat white.

00:49:54.558 --> 00:49:57.627
So terrible. It tastes plasticky.

00:49:57.627 --> 00:50:01.798
Ta-da! So, here is Starbucks Origami.

00:50:01.798 --> 00:50:05.902
Starbucks Origami is
one-cup drip-coffee system.

00:50:05.902 --> 00:50:08.605
So, it's got six origamis.

00:50:10.273 --> 00:50:12.776
And this is what it looks like.

00:50:12.776 --> 00:50:15.579
You unfold it like this.

00:50:15.579 --> 00:50:17.948
So, you just put this over a cup,

00:50:17.948 --> 00:50:20.817
and let's add some hot water.

00:50:20.817 --> 00:50:24.221
Easy-peasy, Japanese-y.

00:50:24.221 --> 00:50:26.590
And Starbucks coffee is served.

00:50:28.025 --> 00:50:31.028
Refreshers!

00:50:31.028 --> 00:50:33.663
♪ Refreshers! ♪

00:50:33.663 --> 00:50:35.165
What are Refreshers, you ask?

00:50:35.165 --> 00:50:37.467
I'm not quite sure. They look like juice.

00:50:37.467 --> 00:50:39.202
Oh, there's, like,
stuff floating in these!

00:50:39.202 --> 00:50:40.404
Fruit and stuff.

00:50:40.404 --> 00:50:42.305
Kiwi starfish.

00:50:42.305 --> 00:50:44.207
No, starfruit.

00:50:44.207 --> 00:50:45.876
That would be weird if
there were starfish in this.

00:50:47.244 --> 00:50:49.513
These were a good idea.
Good call, Starbucks.

00:50:49.513 --> 00:50:51.148
Ooh, mango dragon fruit.

00:50:51.148 --> 00:50:52.182
Here we go.

00:50:53.750 --> 00:50:54.885
Mm!

00:50:54.885 --> 00:50:57.054
Blended strawberry lemonade.

00:50:57.054 --> 00:50:57.888
Very good.

00:50:57.888 --> 00:51:00.490
And this was the strawberry
acai lemonade Refresher.

00:51:01.425 --> 00:51:02.292
Not as good.

00:51:02.292 --> 00:51:03.894
Iced pineapple matcha.

00:51:03.894 --> 00:51:04.995
I don't want this at all.

00:51:05.896 --> 00:51:07.130
[laughs]

00:51:07.130 --> 00:51:09.733
[whimpers]

00:51:09.733 --> 00:51:11.301
Mm-mm.

00:51:11.301 --> 00:51:13.570
So, here is all the food

00:51:13.570 --> 00:51:16.339
you can only get at Starbucks in Japan.

00:51:16.339 --> 00:51:18.475
So many!

00:51:18.475 --> 00:51:20.110
Here's the exclusive food
you can get in the US

00:51:20.110 --> 00:51:21.278
you can't get in Japan.

00:51:22.412 --> 00:51:23.847
Breakfast sandwiches, I'm going in.

00:51:23.847 --> 00:51:25.816
Turkey bacon sandwich.

00:51:25.816 --> 00:51:29.386
Double-smoked bacon, cheddar,
and egg, I think? Yes.

00:51:29.386 --> 00:51:31.955
Impossible breakfast sandwich.

00:51:31.955 --> 00:51:33.523
Sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:51:33.523 --> 00:51:37.561
Classic spinach feta wrap.

00:51:37.561 --> 00:51:39.062
Oh, yeah.

00:51:39.062 --> 00:51:42.399
This is the bacon Gouda sandwich.

00:51:42.399 --> 00:51:45.402
You can get yourself an avocado spread.

00:51:45.402 --> 00:51:47.037
These little guys are egg bites.

00:51:47.037 --> 00:51:48.038
Bacon and Gruyère.

00:51:48.038 --> 00:51:50.373
Egg white, roasted red pepper.

00:51:50.373 --> 00:51:52.442
Also, these, that I bet are not any good.

00:51:52.442 --> 00:51:56.113
The kale and portobello
mushroom egg bites. No, thanks!

00:51:56.113 --> 00:51:57.314
Now moving on to bagels.

00:51:57.314 --> 00:51:59.683
So, what they were able to give me was

00:51:59.683 --> 00:52:00.884
cinnamon raisin.

00:52:00.884 --> 00:52:02.285
Plain bagel.

00:52:02.285 --> 00:52:04.588
You can also get cheese,
onion, and garlic bagels,

00:52:04.588 --> 00:52:07.524
