Ah, yes. Venti mocha.

00:58:57.066 --> 00:58:58.701
Adult hot chocolate.

00:58:58.701 --> 00:59:01.571
This is a venti caramel Frappuccino.

00:59:01.571 --> 00:59:06.175
In Japan, ours has 487 calories.

00:59:06.175 --> 00:59:07.911
It looks really bad,

00:59:07.911 --> 00:59:12.282
so I'm going to put whipped cream.

00:59:16.853 --> 00:59:20.256
Ah! [laughs]

00:59:26.796 --> 00:59:29.766
Ooh!

00:59:29.766 --> 00:59:30.767
Itadakimasu!

00:59:33.336 --> 00:59:35.004
Ah!

00:59:35.004 --> 00:59:36.205
Hey, George, your whipped cream's

00:59:36.205 --> 00:59:37.640
looking a little wimpy there, buddy.

00:59:37.640 --> 00:59:39.108
You gotta do it how we do it in the USA.

00:59:39.108 --> 00:59:40.543
Check this out.

00:59:40.543 --> 00:59:42.512
Boom!

00:59:42.512 --> 00:59:43.947
Take that, environment.

00:59:43.947 --> 00:59:46.316
In the US, ours has less calories,

00:59:46.316 --> 00:59:48.384
only 470.

00:59:48.384 --> 00:59:50.053
I brought reusable straws.

00:59:51.955 --> 00:59:54.190
I don't get it. This is so bad.

00:59:54.190 --> 00:59:55.558
What about the cost?

00:59:55.558 --> 00:59:59.529
This venti Frappuccino is 627 yen,

00:59:59.529 --> 01:00:03.266
or $5.69.

01:00:03.266 --> 01:00:05.635
Can you put the price down, please?

01:00:05.635 --> 01:00:09.005
In the US, a caramel Frappuccino is $5.45,

01:00:09.005 --> 01:00:11.140
which is around 600 Japanese yen.

01:00:11.140 --> 01:00:12.909
It's kind of close, but you must consider

01:00:12.909 --> 01:00:15.578
that a US venti is 4 fluid ounces bigger.

01:00:15.578 --> 01:00:17.480
So let's do that math.

01:00:17.480 --> 01:00:20.016
Looks like it's a bit cheaper in the US.

01:00:20.016 --> 01:00:23.653
So, here is my favorite Frappuccino.

01:00:23.653 --> 01:00:26.255
This is called matcha Frappuccino.

01:00:26.255 --> 01:00:28.625
Do you have this in the US?

01:00:28.625 --> 01:00:29.926
Yes, George, we do in fact

01:00:29.926 --> 01:00:32.228
have the matcha Frappuccino
here in the US, too.

01:00:32.228 --> 01:00:34.097
I don't recall putting that in the script,

01:00:34.097 --> 01:00:36.199
so I think you pulled a fast one

01:00:36.199 --> 01:00:37.800
and got us to buy you a Frappuccino,

01:00:37.800 --> 01:00:40.169
so, enjoy.

01:00:40.169 --> 01:00:41.337
Itadakimasu!

01:00:43.606 --> 01:00:44.874
[laughs]

01:00:44.874 --> 01:00:47.010
This is delicious.

01:00:47.010 --> 01:00:48.277
Excelente!

01:00:51.214 --> 01:00:55.485
Japan Starbucks doesn't
disclose their ingredients,

01:00:55.485 --> 01:00:59.389
so we emailed their customer support.

01:00:59.389 --> 01:01:04.193
But, as of today, they
haven't gotten back to us.

01:01:04.193 --> 01:01:06.763
What are you doing, Starbucks?

01:01:06.763 --> 01:01:09.232
You know, just respond to George!

01:01:09.232 --> 01:01:11.367
So, here is what we do know:

01:01:11.367 --> 01:01:14.337
Our cappuccino is made of espresso,

01:01:14.337 --> 01:01:17.640
steamed milk, and foamed milk.

01:01:17.640 --> 01:01:20.276
In the US, our cappuccino
is made up of milk

01:01:20.276 --> 01:01:21.644
and brewed espresso.

01:01:21.644 --> 01:01:22.812
Not a lot of info in this section,

01:01:22.812 --> 01:01:23.713
gonna be honest with you.

01:01:23.713 --> 01:01:24.580
It's not a lot.

01:01:24.580 --> 01:01:27.283
We don't appreciate being
left on read, Starbucks.

01:01:27.283 --> 01:01:30.553
Our caramel Frappuccino
is made of blended ice

01:01:30.553 --> 01:01:32.822
with milk, whipped cream,

01:01:32.822 --> 01:01:35.525
real caramel, and espresso.

01:01:37.493 --> 01:01:40.530
Ugh! It tastes the way
perfume smells, you know?

01:01:40.530 --> 01:01:42.498
In the US, our caramel Frappuccino

01:01:42.498 --> 01:01:44.734
is made up of ice, milk,

01:01:44.734 --> 01:01:46.202
carrageenan? I don't know.

01:01:46.202 --> 01:01:48.504
Vanilla syrup, coffee, obviously,

01:01:48.504 --> 01:01:51.374
and the caramel syrup is
made up of sugar, water,

01:01:51.374 --> 01:01:53.142
natural flavor, citric acid,

01:01:53.142 --> 01:01:53.976
pota,

01:01:53.976 --> 01:01:54.811
potassium,

01:01:54.811 --> 01:01:55.745
potassium sorbate,

01:01:55.745 --> 01:01:57.580
salt, mono- and diglycerides,

01:01:57.580 --> 01:02:00.483
soy lecithin, and sulfites.

01:02:00.483 --> 01:02:02.985
A Japanese caramel macchiato contains

01:02:02.985 --> 01:02:05.855
vanilla syrup, milk, espresso,

01:02:05.855 --> 01:02:08.624
and original caramel sauce.

01:02:08.624 --> 01:02:11.194
And ours in the US contains
milk, brewed espresso,

01:02:11.194 --> 01:02:13.029
vanilla syrup, which is
made of sugar, water,

01:02:13.029 --> 01:02:15.531
natural flavors, potassium sorbate,

01:02:15.531 --> 01:02:17.633
citric acid, corn syrup, butter,

01:02:17.633 --> 01:02:19.736
cream, salt, mono- and diglycerides,

01:02:19.736 --> 01:02:22.238
soy lecithin, and sulfites.

01:02:22.638 --> 01:02:24.774
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:02:24.774 --> 01:02:26.743
we wanted to find out all the differences

01:02:26.743 --> 01:02:29.545
between Pizza Hut in Japan and the US.

01:02:29.545 --> 01:02:31.380
This is "Food Wars."

01:02:33.449 --> 01:02:37.086
In Japan, a Pizza Hut
pizza comes in three sizes.

01:02:37.086 --> 01:02:40.289
The smallest comes in a My Box order

01:02:40.289 --> 01:02:43.760
and is approximately 15 centimeters.

01:02:45.194 --> 01:02:48.631
Our small can only be made
on a gluten-free crust.

01:02:48.631 --> 01:02:49.632
Check it out.

01:02:49.632 --> 01:02:50.666
Looks like something you would get

01:02:50.666 --> 01:02:52.001
at your high-school cafeteria.

01:02:52.001 --> 01:02:55.805
And it measures 10 inches,
or 25.4 centimeters.

01:02:55.805 --> 01:02:58.241
Our next size up is a medium,

01:02:58.241 --> 01:03:00.777
which is 26 centimeters.

01:03:02.178 --> 01:03:03.446
I'm gonna take this little guy.

01:03:06.048 --> 01:03:07.784
This pizza is so good, dude.

01:03:10.920 --> 01:03:13.923
And our large pizza is 14 inches,

01:03:13.923 --> 01:03:17.293
or 35.5 centimeters.

01:03:19.362 --> 01:03:22.865
This My Box pizza deal includes fries

01:03:22.865 --> 01:03:26.335
and chicken nuggets for 1,080 yen,

01:03:26.335 --> 01:03:28.638
or add a Basque cheesecake

01:03:28.638 --> 01:03:31.974
for 1,290 yen,

01:03:31.974 --> 01:03:35.178
or get three My Boxes

01:03:35.178 --> 01:03:37.680
for 3,000 yen,

01:03:37.680 --> 01:03:40.183
and you can get a free side menu item,

01:03:40.183 --> 01:03:43.719
like 1.5 liters of Coca-Cola.

01:03:43.719 --> 01:03:46.622
Also, for those wanting a little alcohol,

01:03:46.622 --> 01:03:48.424
you can get a My Box deal

01:03:48.424 --> 01:03:52.862
with an alcoholic beverage for 1,100 yen.

01:03:52.862 --> 01:03:55.531
It's called Being Tipsy set.

01:03:56.966 --> 01:03:59.468
Ah, tipsy.

01:04:03.272 --> 01:04:05.341
Now I'm going to the boxes, baby!

01:04:05.341 --> 01:04:07.376
Our next size up is a $13 dinner box.

01:04:07.376 --> 01:04:09.545
It is a medium one-topping pizza,

01:04:09.545 --> 01:04:12.014
breadsticks, and cinnamon sticks.

01:04:12.014 --> 01:04:13.549
This is the best idea.

01:04:13.549 --> 01:04:14.650
If I had to go into an office,

01:04:14.650 --> 01:04:15.751
this would be my briefcase.

01:04:15.751 --> 01:04:18.054
This is what I would
take to work every day.

01:04:18.054 --> 01:04:19.288
Now, you're probably thinking,

01:04:19.288 --> 01:04:21.724
"Oh, Joe, I want more food in a box."

01:04:21.724 --> 01:04:22.859
Well, Pizza Hut of course

01:04:22.859 --> 01:04:25.528
has you covered with the big dinner box.

01:04:25.528 --> 01:04:27.196
Ah-hem.

01:04:27.196 --> 01:04:29.599
Oh, it is the big dinner box!

01:04:29.599 --> 01:04:31.834
This is [grunts]

01:04:31.834 --> 01:04:34.804
two one-topping pizzas
with wings or breadsticks.

01:04:34.804 --> 01:04:35.738
That's what I got, of course.

01:04:35.738 --> 01:04:37.406
You can also get pasta and breadsticks.

01:04:37.406 --> 01:04:39.642
You can also get Quepapas and breadsticks,

01:04:39.642 --> 01:04:41.277
or just a third pizza,

01:04:41.277 --> 01:04:44.447
all for $23.99 to $24.99.

01:04:44.447 --> 01:04:45.281
Man.

01:04:45.281 --> 01:04:47.149
Dinner is served.

01:04:47.149 --> 01:04:51.020
You can get chicken on
the bone in two pieces,

01:04:51.020 --> 01:04:53.823
four pieces, and eight pieces.

01:04:53.823 --> 01:04:56.125
That's really cute, Japan. Two wings.

01:04:56.125 --> 01:04:59.795
In the US, our wing orders start at six,

01:04:59.795 --> 01:05:00.630
12,

01:05:00.630 --> 01:05:01.464
18,

01:05:01.464 --> 01:05:03.966
and the biggest order you can get, 36.

01:05:09.138 --> 01:05:10.806
Wow, that's the hottest?

01:05:10.806 --> 01:05:14.110
WingStreet, you gotta hire a spice expert,

01:05:14.110 --> 01:05:15.745
because this is nothing, dude.

01:05:15.745 --> 01:05:17.813
I've had spicier LaCroixes.

01:05:18.948 --> 01:05:21.851
Here is a Japan large basic pizza.

01:05:21.851 --> 01:05:24.387
We call our cheese pizza basic,

01:05:24.387 --> 01:05:27.123
and it is 2,030 yen.

01:05:27.123 --> 01:05:30.693
or $18.39 US.

01:05:30.693 --> 01:05:32.795
And it has a surface area of

01:05:32.795 --> 01:05:37.333
754.77 square centimeters.

01:05:37.333 --> 01:05:40.636
So that is about $0.024,

01:05:40.636 --> 01:05:45.308
or 2.63 yen per square centimeter.

01:05:45.308 --> 01:05:48.444
The US large cheese pizza is $13.99,

01:05:48.444 --> 01:05:51.347
or 1,544 Japanese yen.

01:05:51.347 --> 01:05:55.184
It has a surface area of
989.9 square centimeters,

01:05:55.184 --> 01:05:59.322
which breaks down to $0.014

01:05:59.322 --> 01:06:01.457
per square centimeter,

01:06:01.457 --> 01:06:04.794
or 1.54 Japanese yen.

01:06:04.794 --> 01:06:06.095
Much cheaper here in the US.

01:06:06.095 --> 01:06:09.098
So, here are two large basic pizzas.

01:06:09.098 --> 01:06:12.101
This one right here is hand-tossed dough,

01:06:12.101 --> 01:06:14.904
and this one right here is a pan pizza.

01:06:14.904 --> 01:06:17.006
Here are two large US cheese pizzas.

01:06:17.006 --> 01:06:18.441
One of them has the pan crust,

01:06:18.441 --> 01:06:20.443
and one of them has the hand-tossed crust.

01:06:20.443 --> 01:06:23.813
Both are the same size and the same price.

01:06:23.813 --> 01:06:25.614
We want to find out which gives you

01:06:25.614 --> 01:06:28.351
more pizza for your money.

01:06:28.351 --> 01:06:31.287
Let's weigh a slice of each and compare.

01:06:31.287 --> 01:06:32.121
George: Go!

01:06:34.256 --> 01:06:35.825
So, winner is:

01:06:35.825 --> 01:06:37.860
ta-da!

01:06:37.860 --> 01:06:39.962
Hand-tossed dough.

01:06:39.962 --> 01:06:40.930
Oh, wow.

01:06:40.930 --> 01:06:41.831
That's, like,

01:06:41.831 --> 01:06:43.666
that's crazy, how good I did just there.

01:06:43.666 --> 01:06:44.700
Look at that.

01:06:48.070 --> 01:06:50.673
Same price, 25% more pizza.

01:06:52.675 --> 01:06:54.510
Look at these!

01:06:54.510 --> 01:06:56.612
Here's everything you can get

01:06:56.612 --> 01:07:00.416
at the Japanese Pizza Hut
you cannot get in the US.

01:07:00.416 --> 01:07:02.451
And here is everything you
can get at a US Pizza Hut

01:07:02.451 --> 01:07:03.919
you can't get in Japan.

01:07:03.919 --> 01:07:06.555
Japan-exclusive pizzas!

01:07:06.555 --> 01:07:07.456
OK!

01:07:07.456 --> 01:07:10.092
So, I got everything on here

01:07:10.092 --> 01:07:11.861
in half and half

01:07:11.861 --> 01:07:16.399
and in medium size on hand-tossed crust.

01:07:16.399 --> 01:07:18.467
All right, so let's start with this one.

01:07:18.467 --> 01:07:21.237
So I got this toku-uma bulgogi.

01:07:21.237 --> 01:07:24.173
Toku-uma means special delicious.

01:07:24.173 --> 01:07:27.243
So it's special delicious bulgogi.

01:07:27.243 --> 01:07:31.047
And this one is menta potemayo bacon.

01:07:31.047 --> 01:07:34.050
Menta means spicy cod roe,

01:07:34.050 --> 01:07:35.851
and it looks good.

01:07:35.851 --> 01:07:37.553
So, next one we've got

01:07:37.553 --> 01:07:41.190
double shrimp with special lobster sauce,

01:07:41.190 --> 01:07:44.293
and this one is grand barbecue.

01:07:44.293 --> 01:07:45.928
Asparagus bacon.

01:07:45.928 --> 01:07:49.031
And this one is potato sausage mayo.

01:07:49.031 --> 01:07:52.601
Next one, we've got crumbling

01:07:52.601 --> 01:07:54.570
pulled pork,

01:07:54.570 --> 01:07:58.407
and next one, spicy pulled pork.

01:07:58.407 --> 01:08:01.577
Selected cheese and thick-cut Iberico.

01:08:01.577 --> 01:08:04.080
And this one is Super Supreme.

01:08:04.080 --> 01:08:05.915
Mexican Kara Peno.

01:08:05.915 --> 01:08:07.983
Kara means it's spicy,

01:08:07.983 --> 01:08:10.586
so spicy jalapeño on there.

01:08:10.586 --> 01:08:14.390
And next one is snappy potato sausage.

01:08:14.390 --> 01:08:17.860
And this one is green
and yellow veggie pizza.

01:08:17.860 --> 01:08:20.496
Shrimp mayo mentai seafood.

01:08:20.496 --> 01:08:24.633
And this one is addictive
anchovy and black olive.

01:08:24.633 --> 01:08:26.569
First exclusive-US-pizza pizzas.

01:08:26.569 --> 01:08:29.205
This one right here, it
is the meat lover's pizza.

01:08:29.205 --> 01:08:30.272
Look at this thing!

01:08:30.272 --> 01:08:31.207
Can you see that?

01:08:31.207 --> 01:08:36.078
This thing is pepperoni,
Italian sausage, ham,

01:08:36.078 --> 01:08:39.181
bacon, seasoned pork, and beef.

01:08:39.181 --> 01:08:41.117
That's every meat in the store, I think.

01:08:41.117 --> 01:08:45.688
This one right here is the
Hawaiian chicken pizza.

01:08:45.688 --> 01:08:49.258
This looks like one bite
would send me to my grave.

01:08:49.258 --> 01:08:51.827
This at least has a vegetable on it.

01:08:53.429 --> 01:08:55.264
I think green peppers were a mistake.

01:08:55.264 --> 01:08:56.232
This one right here,

01:08:56.232 --> 01:08:59.001
chicken bacon Parmesan.

01:08:59.001 --> 01:09:02.738
Chicken, bacon, tomatoes,
and a Parmesan crust.

01:09:02.738 --> 01:09:05.307
Oh, yeah, dude. Look at the crust on this.

01:09:05.307 --> 01:09:06.976
They bake the cheese right into the crust.

01:09:06.976 --> 01:09:08.744
I just love that Pizza Hut's like,

01:09:08.744 --> 01:09:11.013
"We gotta cover every
surface with cheese."

01:09:11.013 --> 01:09:12.982
God forbid you would take a bite

01:09:12.982 --> 01:09:14.517
of something that doesn't
have cheese in it.

01:09:14.517 --> 01:09:16.352
In Japan, you can get a pizza

01:09:16.352 --> 01:09:18.821
with four different topping areas

01:09:18.821 --> 01:09:20.890
called the Four Series.

01:09:20.890 --> 01:09:23.425
So let's start with this one.

01:09:23.425 --> 01:09:25.594
It's called Gochiso Four.

01:09:25.594 --> 01:09:27.530
Gochiso means feast.

01:09:30.432 --> 01:09:34.069
And next one, we've
got Bulgogi Festa Four.

01:09:36.405 --> 01:09:38.707
So, let's move on to the next one.

01:09:38.707 --> 01:09:41.277
We've got Lovers Four.

01:09:41.277 --> 01:09:42.578
Lovers!

01:09:45.314 --> 01:09:46.515
What?

01:09:46.515 --> 01:09:48.184
Is this for this beef?

01:09:48.184 --> 01:09:50.319
It's gonna be horrible.

01:09:50.319 --> 01:09:53.722
And this one is called Kodawari Four.

01:09:53.722 --> 01:09:55.724
Kodawari means authentic.

01:09:58.160 --> 01:10:02.698
And this one in front of
me is Gourmet Mania Four.

01:10:05.000 --> 01:10:07.703
What did I do to you, Pizza Hut?

01:10:07.703 --> 01:10:09.138
It's burned!

01:10:09.138 --> 01:10:10.706
Look at this!

01:10:10.706 --> 01:10:11.707
All right, next one.

01:10:14.176 --> 01:10:17.546
And the last one is Classic Four.

01:10:17.546 --> 01:10:18.714
This is classic.

01:10:21.383 --> 01:10:22.651
Deluxe!

01:10:22.651 --> 01:10:24.053
This one right here,

01:10:24.053 --> 01:10:25.788
the backyard barbecue pizza.

01:10:25.788 --> 01:10:28.157
Barbecue sauce instead
of pizza sauce I think.

01:10:28.157 --> 01:10:31.160
And it comes with a
barbecue honey. Shall I?

01:10:31.160 --> 01:10:32.561
I think I shall.

01:10:32.561 --> 01:10:34.597
Oh, yeah, I think I'm gonna like this.

01:10:36.699 --> 01:10:38.867
Don't sleep on the Pizza
Hut honey barbecue.

01:10:38.867 --> 01:10:39.868
This is really good.

01:10:39.868 --> 01:10:42.438
I think this is Buffalo chicken pizza.

01:10:42.438 --> 01:10:44.473
Tangy Buffalo sauce.

01:10:47.343 --> 01:10:48.510
Exact opposite problem.

01:10:48.510 --> 01:10:49.478
I think the sauce ruins this.

01:10:49.478 --> 01:10:51.013
Too strong. Skip the sauce.

01:10:51.013 --> 01:10:54.984
So, this one right here
is a Japan-only pizza.

01:10:54.984 --> 01:10:57.319
So this is a pizza with a

01:10:57.319 --> 01:10:58.354
boom!

01:10:58.354 --> 01:10:59.888
Sausage crust

01:10:59.888 --> 01:11:03.192
with bulgogi, teriyaki chicken,

01:11:03.192 --> 01:11:07.563
Camembert cheese, Gouda
cheese, green chili sauce,

01:11:07.563 --> 01:11:10.699
shrimp, squid, tuna mayo,

01:11:10.699 --> 01:11:12.901
broccoli, corn,

01:11:12.901 --> 01:11:16.138
basil sauce, and anchovies.

01:11:16.138 --> 01:11:17.072
Too much.

01:11:17.072 --> 01:11:18.641
But let's give it a try.

01:11:18.641 --> 01:11:20.109
Look at this.

01:11:21.543 --> 01:11:23.112
Just too much.

01:11:23.112 --> 01:11:24.179
Itadakimasu.

01:11:27.349 --> 01:11:28.584
Mm.

01:11:29.785 --> 01:11:31.754
It's disgusting.

01:11:31.754 --> 01:11:35.391
In the first place, I hate anchovies.

01:11:35.391 --> 01:11:38.160
Don't put anchovies!

01:11:38.160 --> 01:11:40.095
It's just

01:11:40.095 --> 01:11:41.030
mazui!

01:11:41.030 --> 01:11:42.631
I picked out that pizza for you, George.

01:11:42.631 --> 01:11:44.833
Sorry, my man. Gotta do it for the show.

01:11:44.833 --> 01:11:46.235
Here is a USA-only pizza.

01:11:46.235 --> 01:11:49.104
It is a pizza with toppings
and sauces and cheeses

01:11:49.104 --> 01:11:51.240
you can only get in the
US and not in Japan.

01:11:51.240 --> 01:11:52.941
First, we have the gluten-free crust.

01:11:52.941 --> 01:11:55.110
Remember that really sad-looking crust?

01:11:55.110 --> 01:11:56.679
We can have a creamy garlic Parmesan,

01:11:56.679 --> 01:11:58.414
barbecue, or Buffalo sauce as a base.

01:11:58.414 --> 01:12:00.549
I went with the creamy garlic Parmesan.

01:12:00.549 --> 01:12:03.285
Got meatballs, banana peppers,

01:12:03.285 --> 01:12:04.553
and for the crust,

01:12:04.553 --> 01:12:06.255
pretty sure I went the garlic Parmesan.

01:12:18.200 --> 01:12:19.702
It's not awful.

01:12:19.702 --> 01:12:22.104
When you order food and
you're, like, really hungry,

01:12:22.104 --> 01:12:24.173
so something sounds like
it's gonna be really good,

01:12:24.173 --> 01:12:25.274
but then when you start
eating it, you're like,

01:12:25.274 --> 01:12:26.475
"Oh, I think I screwed up."

01:12:26.475 --> 01:12:27.743
This is definitely like ...

01:12:27.743 --> 01:12:29.078
skip this.

01:12:29.078 --> 01:12:29.912
[thud]

01:12:29.912 --> 01:12:33.248
So, here we've got
Japan's exclusive sides.

01:12:33.248 --> 01:12:35.117
We've got chicken nuggets,

01:12:35.117 --> 01:12:36.852
and this is four pieces,

01:12:36.852 --> 01:12:38.120
eight pieces,

01:12:38.120 --> 01:12:39.388
16 pieces.

01:12:39.388 --> 01:12:42.925
And we also have plain
flavor and spicy flavor.

01:12:42.925 --> 01:12:43.992
Let's try this.

01:12:45.928 --> 01:12:48.063
Plain!

01:12:48.063 --> 01:12:49.998
This is plain.

01:12:49.998 --> 01:12:51.467
Everything is plain!

01:12:52.434 --> 01:12:53.469
I want spicy!

01:12:53.469 --> 01:12:56.004
Where is spicy nuggets?

01:12:56.004 --> 01:12:59.408
And next one, we've
got honey cheese balls.

01:12:59.408 --> 01:13:03.512
So cheese balls there,
and we've got honey syrup.

01:13:03.512 --> 01:13:07.683
So, next one, we've got
Japanese-style tatsuta chicken.

01:13:07.683 --> 01:13:11.120
So this chicken is marinated in soy sauce

01:13:11.120 --> 01:13:14.790
and rolled in potato starch
instead of wheat flour

01:13:14.790 --> 01:13:16.492
and deep-fried.

01:13:16.492 --> 01:13:18.794
Let's talk about US-exclusive sides.

01:13:18.794 --> 01:13:20.696
Can't get these in Japan.

01:13:20.696 --> 01:13:22.865
Pizza Hut also got pasta.

01:13:22.865 --> 01:13:24.566
Referred to at one point as Pasta Hut.

01:13:24.566 --> 01:13:28.370
You can get two of these baked
pastas at our Pizza Huts.

01:13:28.370 --> 01:13:30.339
One is the Tusca --

01:13:30.339 --> 01:13:31.240
Tuscani --

01:13:32.374 --> 01:13:34.076
What? What'd I say?

01:13:35.277 --> 01:13:36.278
Fine.

01:13:36.278 --> 01:13:38.514
No, Tuscany is T U S C A N Y.

01:13:38.514 --> 01:13:42.184
They spell this one with T U S C A N I.

01:13:42.184 --> 01:13:44.620
No, come on. I'm looking
it up. Keep rolling.

01:13:44.620 --> 01:13:45.621
Ad: Now at Pizza Hut,

01:13:45.621 --> 01:13:47.556
get a family-size Tuscani pasta

01:13:47.556 --> 01:13:50.959
for just 12 bucks.
Joe: Ha-ha! Tuscani!

01:13:50.959 --> 01:13:53.028
In your face!

01:13:53.028 --> 01:13:56.098
Just an absolute abuse of Italian culture.

01:13:56.098 --> 01:13:59.034
Here is the Tuscani chicken Alfredo pasta

01:13:59.034 --> 01:14:01.537
and the Tuscani meaty marinara pasta.

01:14:01.537 --> 01:14:03.572
If I can't put a fine enough point on it,

01:14:03.572 --> 01:14:04.907
I do not want to eat this at all.

01:14:04.907 --> 01:14:06.275
This looks like a TV dinner.

01:14:06.275 --> 01:14:07.976
Like, this is what you
eat in your apartment

01:14:07.976 --> 01:14:09.244
sitting on a folding chair,

01:14:09.244 --> 01:14:10.746
one light bulb hanging from the ceiling,

01:14:10.746 --> 01:14:12.114
eating this just right out of the oven,

01:14:12.114 --> 01:14:13.115
staring at a wall,

01:14:13.115 --> 01:14:15.184
looking at, like, cockroaches
running up and down.

01:14:15.184 --> 01:14:16.985
Your one window has a
view of a brick wall.

01:14:16.985 --> 01:14:18.954
The calendar on the wall
is from three years ago.

01:14:18.954 --> 01:14:21.323
♪ Nobody wants this! ♪

01:14:21.323 --> 01:14:22.491
Quepapas.

01:14:22.491 --> 01:14:24.259
What are Quepapas, you ask?

01:14:24.259 --> 01:14:25.227
I don't know.

01:14:27.463 --> 01:14:29.198
They got jalapeños and stuff in them.

01:14:29.198 --> 01:14:31.600
So they're kind of like spicy tater tots.

01:14:31.600 --> 01:14:35.237
These to me are quintessential
Pizza Hut sides.

01:14:35.237 --> 01:14:37.506
We got breadsticks, and
we got cheese sticks.

01:14:37.506 --> 01:14:39.208
They both come with the marinara sauce.

01:14:39.208 --> 01:14:41.243
We also have a marinara sauce
that you guys don't have.

01:14:41.243 --> 01:14:44.246
Vroom, vroom, vroom!

01:14:44.246 --> 01:14:45.781
Sauce Talk.

01:14:45.781 --> 01:14:48.884
So, here is extra sauces.

01:14:48.884 --> 01:14:49.985
So, if you want,

01:14:49.985 --> 01:14:53.856
you can get green chili
sauce or honey syrup.

01:14:53.856 --> 01:14:56.425
So, the WingStreet wings
you can get at Pizza Hut

01:14:56.425 --> 01:14:59.428
also come in exclusive flavors
you can't get in Japan.

01:14:59.428 --> 01:15:00.696
Here are all the sauces.

01:15:04.800 --> 01:15:06.235
Spicy garlic is really good.

01:15:06.235 --> 01:15:07.903
Joe's sauce seal of approval.

01:15:07.903 --> 01:15:09.671
Teriyaki, this seems like a no-brainer,

01:15:09.671 --> 01:15:11.440
but we're not gonna leave it to chance.

01:15:14.510 --> 01:15:15.577
No!

01:15:15.577 --> 01:15:16.712
Ugh!

01:15:16.712 --> 01:15:18.480
I stand corrected. This is terrible.

01:15:18.480 --> 01:15:19.548
Doesn't pass.

01:15:19.548 --> 01:15:20.816
Garlic Parmesan.

01:15:20.816 --> 01:15:23.285
Oh, look, there's Parmesan on top of it.

01:15:23.285 --> 01:15:26.655
Oh, yeah!

01:15:30.659 --> 01:15:32.160
That might be the best one.

01:15:32.160 --> 01:15:34.029
Lemon pepper dry rub.

01:15:34.029 --> 01:15:36.331
Why do I have to apply it?

01:15:40.202 --> 01:15:41.303
Yeah, not into that, man.

01:15:41.303 --> 01:15:42.137
I don't get it.

01:15:42.137 --> 01:15:43.338
I don't know what Drake's
going on about, man.

01:15:43.338 --> 01:15:44.406
The lemon pepper is not very good.

01:15:44.406 --> 01:15:45.707
Crucify me, internet!

01:15:45.707 --> 01:15:47.809
I don't like lemon pepper dry rub wings!

01:15:47.809 --> 01:15:49.411
Should I be -- I think maybe
I should be rubbing it,

01:15:49.411 --> 01:15:51.580
that's what I'm doing wrong.

01:15:51.580 --> 01:15:52.814
Is that too much?

01:15:57.219 --> 01:15:58.020
Whoops.

01:15:58.020 --> 01:15:59.988
Yep, you were right. Too much.

01:15:59.988 --> 01:16:00.856
But it's good.

01:16:00.856 --> 01:16:02.357
Also, sauces, real quick,

01:16:02.357 --> 01:16:03.692
we got blue cheese.

01:16:03.692 --> 01:16:05.127
We got ranch.

01:16:05.127 --> 01:16:08.397
So, here is Japan's exclusive desserts.

01:16:08.397 --> 01:16:11.199
Here we've got Basque cheesecake.

01:16:11.199 --> 01:16:15.103
We've got Lady Borden vanilla ice cream.

01:16:15.103 --> 01:16:16.305
And last one,

01:16:16.305 --> 01:16:19.474
we've got Lady Borden chocolate ice cream.

01:16:19.474 --> 01:16:20.309
Desserts?

01:16:20.309 --> 01:16:21.143
We got 'em.

01:16:21.143 --> 01:16:23.211
In the US, you can get yourself this,

01:16:23.211 --> 01:16:26.715
a set of six Cinnabon cinnamon rolls.

01:16:26.715 --> 01:16:30.152
This is the triple-chocolate brownie.

01:16:30.152 --> 01:16:31.687
I'm starting to lose it, guys.

01:16:31.687 --> 01:16:33.322
All that pizza, it just hit me.

01:16:33.322 --> 01:16:35.891
This right here is the
ultimate chocolate chip cookie.

01:16:35.891 --> 01:16:36.925
This is pretty funny.

01:16:36.925 --> 01:16:38.393
They should cut this like a pizza.

01:16:38.393 --> 01:16:39.528
Cinnamon sticks.

01:16:39.528 --> 01:16:40.929
They also come with a thing of icing.

01:16:41.763 --> 01:16:43.498
Gonna be my obituary photo.

01:16:48.170 --> 01:16:49.805
I can't believe how good that is.

01:16:49.805 --> 01:16:50.639
This is the Cinnabon thing.

01:16:50.639 --> 01:16:52.107
I want to try it now,
since I had it before.

01:16:52.107 --> 01:16:53.141
I want to see how it compares to that.

01:16:55.277 --> 01:16:57.312
Cinnabon is still better.

01:16:57.312 --> 01:17:01.383
In Japan, our fountain drinks
are Coca-Cola products.

01:17:01.383 --> 01:17:03.819
In the US, our soft
drinks are Pepsi products.

01:17:03.819 --> 01:17:05.387
You know what that means.

01:17:05.387 --> 01:17:07.823
This is "Soda Wars."

01:17:07.823 --> 01:17:10.826
In Japan, we have Coke,

01:17:10.826 --> 01:17:12.294
Coke Zero,

01:17:12.294 --> 01:17:13.929
and Fanta grape,

01:17:13.929 --> 01:17:15.430
and green tea,

01:17:15.430 --> 01:17:17.332
and Qoo.

01:17:17.332 --> 01:17:18.767
Qoo orange juice.

01:17:18.767 --> 01:17:20.168
Look at this face.

01:17:25.674 --> 01:17:27.476
Qoo!

01:17:27.476 --> 01:17:30.679
It has light orange taste.

01:17:30.679 --> 01:17:32.614
Classic Pepsi,

01:17:32.614 --> 01:17:33.715
cherry Pepsi,

01:17:33.715 --> 01:17:35.117
diet Pepsi,

01:17:35.117 --> 01:17:35.984
orange ...

01:17:35.984 --> 01:17:37.252
Crush right? Yeah, Orange Crush.

01:17:37.252 --> 01:17:38.086
Mountain Dew,

01:17:38.086 --> 01:17:39.855
and, of course, Sierra Mist.

01:17:39.855 --> 01:17:43.158
Which is like Mountain
Dew, only so much worse.

01:17:44.426 --> 01:17:45.260
[thud]

01:17:46.662 --> 01:17:48.397
So, a full pizza

01:17:48.397 --> 01:17:51.933
is 2,256 calories.

01:17:51.933 --> 01:17:54.870
112.8%

01:17:54.870 --> 01:17:57.205
of your daily recommended value.

01:17:57.205 --> 01:17:59.174
Too many calories!

01:17:59.174 --> 01:18:00.442
Ah!

01:18:01.710 --> 01:18:04.079
In the US, our large cheese pan pizza

01:18:04.079 --> 01:18:04.913
has eight slices,

01:18:04.913 --> 01:18:07.082
and each slice is 360 calories.

01:18:07.082 --> 01:18:10.752
So for the total pizza,
that's 2,880 calories.

01:18:10.752 --> 01:18:13.922
That's 144% of your daily calories.

01:18:13.922 --> 01:18:15.557
And both the fat and the sodium

01:18:15.557 --> 01:18:18.160
are each over 200% of
your daily allowance.

01:18:18.160 --> 01:18:20.896
Japan's large Pepperoni Supreme

01:18:20.896 --> 01:18:22.631
with plump bread crust

01:18:22.631 --> 01:18:25.867
is 228 calories per slice,

01:18:25.867 --> 01:18:29.871
or 2,736 calories

01:18:29.871 --> 01:18:31.773
for the entire thing,

01:18:31.773 --> 01:18:35.444
which is 136.8%

01:18:35.444 --> 01:18:37.045
of your daily calories.

01:18:37.045 --> 01:18:38.947
Even more calories!

01:18:38.947 --> 01:18:40.982
Ah!

01:18:40.982 --> 01:18:44.519
This is a large US pepperoni
with the pan crust.

01:18:44.519 --> 01:18:46.188
Man, that's a thick guy!

01:18:46.188 --> 01:18:48.490
One slice, 370 calories.

01:18:48.490 --> 01:18:52.127
So that makes the whole
pizza 2,930 calories,

01:18:52.127 --> 01:18:56.064
and that has 146.5% of
your daily allowance.

01:18:56.064 --> 01:18:57.866
Now, I would like to point out

01:18:57.866 --> 01:18:59.534
that the large pepperoni pizza

01:18:59.534 --> 01:19:03.672
is the most popular Pizza
Hut pizza in the US,

01:19:03.672 --> 01:19:05.407
but not in Japan.

01:19:05.407 --> 01:19:08.744
Online, it ranks about
the 14th most popular.

01:19:08.744 --> 01:19:12.047
In Japan, one of the pizzas we enjoy

01:19:12.047 --> 01:19:14.983
is the seafood mix.

01:19:14.983 --> 01:19:17.819
It's one of Pizza Hut's best sellers

01:19:17.819 --> 01:19:20.188
for over 20 years.

01:19:20.188 --> 01:19:21.156
Wow.

01:19:21.156 --> 01:19:23.458
So, Japan's most calorific pizza

01:19:23.458 --> 01:19:26.695
is the large toku-uma bulgogi.

01:19:26.695 --> 01:19:30.665
And I forgot to order
large toku-uma bulgogi!

01:19:30.665 --> 01:19:31.733
Sorry about that.

01:19:31.733 --> 01:19:34.936
But this one is toku-uma bulgogi.

01:19:34.936 --> 01:19:36.238
And this one is smaller,

01:19:36.238 --> 01:19:40.842
but large slice pizza is 285 calories,

01:19:40.842 --> 01:19:44.780
which makes the entire large
pizza on plump bread crust

01:19:44.780 --> 01:19:47.883
3,420 calories.

01:19:47.883 --> 01:19:51.353
3,420 calories!

01:19:53.522 --> 01:19:55.190
Yabai!

01:19:55.190 --> 01:19:56.024
And in the US,

01:19:56.024 --> 01:19:58.460
our most calorific pizza
is the meat lover's.

01:19:58.460 --> 01:20:01.196
I also was supposed to get
the large. This is a medium.

01:20:01.196 --> 01:20:02.097
If someone in graphics

01:20:02.097 --> 01:20:03.698
could just make this pizza much bigger

01:20:03.698 --> 01:20:05.033
or me much smaller.

01:20:05.033 --> 01:20:08.837
One slice is 470 calories,
making the total pizza,

01:20:08.837 --> 01:20:10.505
which should be eight slices,

01:20:10.505 --> 01:20:12.874
3,760 calories.

01:20:12.874 --> 01:20:14.643
That's more than double your daily fat

01:20:14.643 --> 01:20:17.112
and triple your daily sodium.

01:20:17.112 --> 01:20:18.814
I am a glutton for punishment,

01:20:18.814 --> 01:20:20.415
but I'm not going to bite into this pizza.

01:20:20.415 --> 01:20:22.250
It looks like a nightmare.

01:20:24.152 --> 01:20:25.954
There's a few ingredients to watch out for

01:20:25.954 --> 01:20:27.522
at the Pizza Huts in the US.

01:20:27.522 --> 01:20:30.425
One is an ingredient found
in our salad croutons.

01:20:30.425 --> 01:20:31.393
It is called

01:20:31.393 --> 01:20:33.395
azodicarbonamidates.

01:20:33.395 --> 01:20:34.229
[beep]

01:20:34.229 --> 01:20:35.063
Azo --

01:20:35.063 --> 01:20:35.897
[beep]

01:20:35.897 --> 01:20:38.066
Azodicarbonmidee.

01:20:38.066 --> 01:20:38.900
[beep]

01:20:38.900 --> 01:20:40.068
Or ADA.

01:20:40.068 --> 01:20:41.403
It is a substance used for making

01:20:41.403 --> 01:20:43.672
vinyl foam plastics for
things like yoga mats.

01:20:43.672 --> 01:20:45.106
And it's also in our croutons.

01:20:45.106 --> 01:20:46.341
I'm not quite sure why.

01:20:46.341 --> 01:20:47.442
The use of this additive,

01:20:47.442 --> 01:20:48.276
surprisingly enough,

01:20:48.276 --> 01:20:49.678
is not permitted in Japan.

01:20:49.678 --> 01:20:50.679
What?

01:20:50.679 --> 01:20:52.714
That's just horrible!

01:20:52.714 --> 01:20:56.484
Both yoga mats and salads
have a connection to health.

01:20:56.484 --> 01:21:01.323
But US salad croutons
have actually plastic.

01:21:01.323 --> 01:21:03.191
Yoga-mat plastic.

01:21:03.191 --> 01:21:05.260
How ironic.

01:21:05.260 --> 01:21:07.295
Also in the US you're going
to want to watch out for

01:21:07.295 --> 01:21:09.931
Yellow No. 5 aka tartrazine,

01:21:09.931 --> 01:21:13.168
which appears in these
Cinnabon mini rolls.

01:21:13.168 --> 01:21:14.536
Oops, already ate one.

01:21:14.536 --> 01:21:16.037
According to the European Union,

01:21:16.037 --> 01:21:17.439
this chemical, quote,

01:21:17.439 --> 01:21:19.341
"May have an adverse effect on activity

01:21:19.341 --> 01:21:21.676
and attention in children," end quote.

01:21:21.676 --> 01:21:23.211
It is banned in the EU.

01:21:23.211 --> 01:21:24.713
It's not banned here in America.

01:21:24.713 --> 01:21:26.481
And it is at least not allowed

01:21:26.481 --> 01:21:28.250
at any of the Pizza Huts in Japan.

01:21:28.250 --> 01:21:30.485
You can totally get this here in America.

01:21:30.485 --> 01:21:33.521
Let's get some deficit on that attention.

01:21:33.521 --> 01:21:34.589
"May have adverse effect

01:21:34.589 --> 01:21:35.824
on activity and attention in children,"

01:21:35.824 --> 01:21:37.058
I mean, it's having a horrible effect

01:21:37.058 --> 01:21:38.760
on my attention as an adult.

01:21:38.760 --> 01:21:39.628
[laughs]

01:21:39.628 --> 01:21:40.695
I stopped paying attention to

01:21:40.695 --> 01:21:42.831
what was coming out of
my mouth moments ago. So.

01:21:42.831 --> 01:21:44.666
The Dew got Yellow No. 5 as well.

01:21:44.666 --> 01:21:48.870
The Orange Crush has Yellow
No. 6 and Red No. 40.

01:21:48.870 --> 01:21:50.605
Wonder if those are bad too.

01:21:50.605 --> 01:21:52.240
All the color things are bad.

01:21:52.240 --> 01:21:55.277
I have to say, this is also terrible.

01:21:55.277 --> 01:21:58.179
Why the hell American fast-food chains

01:21:58.179 --> 01:22:02.017
put harmful chemicals into their foods?

01:22:02.017 --> 01:22:03.985
Do they make their food

01:22:03.985 --> 01:22:06.688
in a chemistry laboratory or something?

01:22:06.688 --> 01:22:08.189
Use the kitchen.

01:22:08.957 --> 01:22:11.059
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:22:11.059 --> 01:22:13.128
we wanted to find out
the biggest differences

01:22:13.128 --> 01:22:15.764
between Subway in Japan and the US.

01:22:15.764 --> 01:22:17.699
This is "Food Wars."

01:22:22.170 --> 01:22:25.307
In Japan, our sandwiches
come in three sizes.

01:22:25.307 --> 01:22:27.876
This one is regular,

01:22:27.876 --> 01:22:31.579
and here we've got foot-long sub,

01:22:31.579 --> 01:22:36.184
and this one right here is party tray.

01:22:36.184 --> 01:22:37.986
This is party tray A,

01:22:37.986 --> 01:22:40.322
which is three regular sandwiches

01:22:40.322 --> 01:22:42.424
cut into 12 pieces,

01:22:42.424 --> 01:22:44.960
or we can also get a party tray

01:22:44.960 --> 01:22:47.395
that's three foot-long subs.

01:22:47.395 --> 01:22:48.830
In the US, you have three sizes:

01:22:48.830 --> 01:22:52.100
6-inch, foot-long, and the party tray.

01:22:52.100 --> 01:22:54.836
This is five foot-longs
cut into three sections,

01:22:54.836 --> 01:22:56.938
giving us 15 sandwiches.

01:22:56.938 --> 01:22:58.540
Not enough party in that party platter?

01:22:58.540 --> 01:22:59.574
Subway's got you covered.

01:22:59.574 --> 01:23:03.812
Here in the US, you can
also get a 3-foot party sub.

01:23:04.713 --> 01:23:07.048
Whoa!

01:23:07.048 --> 01:23:07.882
Yes.

01:23:07.882 --> 01:23:09.484
♪ Yes! ♪

01:23:09.484 --> 01:23:11.920
Time to give this sandwich an exam.

01:23:11.920 --> 01:23:12.988
Dude, are you kidding me?

01:23:12.988 --> 01:23:14.155
Look at this.

01:23:14.155 --> 01:23:18.159
I'm seeing ham. I'm seeing
turkey. I'm seeing cheese.

01:23:18.159 --> 01:23:21.029
And also we have a giant sub.

01:23:21.029 --> 01:23:22.797
Let me show you.

01:23:22.797 --> 01:23:25.300
[grunts]

01:23:28.269 --> 01:23:29.404
I got this.

01:23:31.673 --> 01:23:33.541
And this is what it looks like.

01:23:34.676 --> 01:23:36.578
This is too big.

01:23:40.648 --> 01:23:44.152
In Japan, our fountain
drinks come in three sizes.

01:23:44.152 --> 01:23:46.488
This one is small,

01:23:46.488 --> 01:23:49.124
and medium,

01:23:49.124 --> 01:23:53.461
and large.

01:23:53.461 --> 01:23:56.197
Here in the US Subway, the
website says there's a small,

01:23:56.197 --> 01:23:58.299
but I talked to the Subway manager,

01:23:58.299 --> 01:24:00.235
and they assured me
they don't have a small,

01:24:00.235 --> 01:24:03.238
so apparently our fountain
drinks are just two sizes.

01:24:03.238 --> 01:24:07.142
Medium, which makes no sense
'cause there's no small,

01:24:07.142 --> 01:24:08.410
and large.

01:24:12.914 --> 01:24:15.917
At Subway, I had to fill up, myself,

01:24:15.917 --> 01:24:17.819
the fountain drinks, which
of course I don't mind.

01:24:17.819 --> 01:24:21.122
So any inaccuracies rest on my shoulders

01:24:21.122 --> 01:24:22.123
and my shoulders alone.

01:24:27.195 --> 01:24:28.029
Ooh!

01:24:29.364 --> 01:24:30.865
40 what? Not even close.

01:24:30.865 --> 01:24:32.801
And that was like, I
filled this up to the brim.

01:24:32.801 --> 01:24:36.037
I'm looking through this,
and I'm seeing 33, maybe.

01:24:36.037 --> 01:24:38.006
We'll be generous. We'll give them 34.

01:24:38.006 --> 01:24:39.874
They still missed it by 6.

01:24:39.874 --> 01:24:42.143
6 fluid ounces you guys
are skimping on us?

01:24:43.244 --> 01:24:44.412
You get a good shot of that.

01:24:44.412 --> 01:24:47.315
Is that really 6 missing ounces?

01:24:47.315 --> 01:24:50.151
Do we think that's 6 ounces
of fluid we're missing there?

01:24:50.151 --> 01:24:51.786
You better believe I'm on
a high horse right now.

01:24:51.786 --> 01:24:53.354
This is infuriating!

01:24:53.354 --> 01:24:55.256
I'm really hungry, that has
a lot to do with it too.

01:24:55.256 --> 01:24:57.258
On the surface, both countries'
sandwiches look the same,

01:24:57.258 --> 01:24:58.827
but we wanted to get a closer look.

01:24:58.827 --> 01:25:02.297
Here we have a foot-long on
white turkey with lettuce,

01:25:02.297 --> 01:25:04.432
tomato, black olives, and onions.

01:25:04.432 --> 01:25:06.067
All right, I have got the same one,

01:25:06.067 --> 01:25:07.769
so I'm going to weigh this.

01:25:08.670 --> 01:25:10.371
Joe: Wow, so pretty close.

01:25:10.371 --> 01:25:13.108
Scientific accuracy is really
important in "Food Wars," so.

01:25:15.710 --> 01:25:18.947
George: Now let's open it
up and see what's inside.

01:25:18.947 --> 01:25:21.249
Joe: Huh, only a 10-gram difference,

01:25:21.249 --> 01:25:24.719
but ours had a lot more turkey
and a lot less vegetables.

01:25:24.719 --> 01:25:26.354
Hm.

01:25:29.958 --> 01:25:33.061
So, here are all the Subway menu items

01:25:33.061 --> 01:25:36.364
you can get in Japan but not in the US.

01:25:36.364 --> 01:25:39.200
And here is everything
you can get at US Subway

01:25:39.200 --> 01:25:40.735
you cannot get in Japan.

01:25:40.735 --> 01:25:44.539
So, let's start with new
exclusive sandwiches.

01:25:44.539 --> 01:25:47.609
So, here we've got
tandoori chicken sandwich.

01:25:50.712 --> 01:25:52.313
Mm!

01:25:52.313 --> 01:25:55.216
The chicken itself is tender.

01:25:55.216 --> 01:25:56.684
9 out of 10.

01:25:56.684 --> 01:25:57.619
Congrats.

01:25:58.586 --> 01:26:03.558
So, next one, we've got tokumori
tandoori chicken sandwich.

01:26:03.558 --> 01:26:05.693
Tokumori means extra large,

01:26:05.693 --> 01:26:08.897
so extra-large tandoori chicken sandwich.

01:26:08.897 --> 01:26:12.100
We've got spicy egg shrimp.

01:26:12.100 --> 01:26:14.202
So, next one, we've got

01:26:14.202 --> 01:26:17.639
chōkatsu chicken and cheese sandwich.

01:26:19.307 --> 01:26:20.675
This is not good.

01:26:22.010 --> 01:26:24.012
It doesn't have any taste.

01:26:24.012 --> 01:26:25.713
Man, what the fudge?

01:26:25.713 --> 01:26:28.216
So, first thing, I have this
huge pile of sandwiches here.

01:26:28.216 --> 01:26:29.851
I'll just try and do some hits.

01:26:29.851 --> 01:26:32.954
Here is, of course, steak and cheese.

01:26:32.954 --> 01:26:35.523
Buffalo chicken.

01:26:35.523 --> 01:26:36.357
Yeah, I don't know.

01:26:36.357 --> 01:26:37.859
Maybe it's 'cause they put
all the veggies on here too.

01:26:37.859 --> 01:26:40.328
They kind of just did the standard ones.

01:26:40.328 --> 01:26:41.362
I don't think this looks very good.

01:26:41.362 --> 01:26:43.097
Ooh, the Cali turkey.

01:26:43.097 --> 01:26:44.432
Looks like there's spinach on here.

01:26:44.432 --> 01:26:46.534
Oh, and bacon! Yeah, OK.

01:26:49.537 --> 01:26:50.371
Not bad.

01:26:50.371 --> 01:26:51.806
They ruined it with the cucumbers.

01:26:51.806 --> 01:26:53.541
The cold cut combo.

01:26:53.541 --> 01:26:55.543
This is, like, the sandwich, right?

01:26:55.543 --> 01:26:57.645
If we were playing "Family Feud"

01:26:57.645 --> 01:27:00.882
and the category was Subway sandwiches,

01:27:00.882 --> 01:27:03.484
I feel like the cold cut
combo would be No. 1, right?

01:27:03.484 --> 01:27:05.820
Ooh, the Baja steak, everybody!

01:27:05.820 --> 01:27:08.323
Straight from Baja California.

01:27:08.323 --> 01:27:11.926
You know their blast, now try their steak.

01:27:11.926 --> 01:27:14.996
Everyone in the room
just groaned. [laughs]

01:27:14.996 --> 01:27:16.397
[sighs]

01:27:16.397 --> 01:27:18.666
I have to know, how far is
that bathroom from here?

01:27:21.703 --> 01:27:23.171
They really load it with the vegetables.

01:27:23.171 --> 01:27:27.175
Again, why would you want all
these gross veggies on ... ?

01:27:27.175 --> 01:27:28.943
I want the meatball, and I
want the sauce and the cheese.

01:27:28.943 --> 01:27:31.179
I don't want cucumbers.

01:27:31.179 --> 01:27:33.181
My meatball sandwich is ruined!

01:27:33.181 --> 01:27:34.616
I'm sneaking a meatball.

01:27:37.585 --> 01:27:39.621
Mm, mm, mm, mm.

01:27:39.621 --> 01:27:41.222
Yeah, the Italian BMT.

01:27:41.222 --> 01:27:44.092
Come on, this is, like,
the most popular one.

01:27:44.092 --> 01:27:45.860
See, you got the meat there.
Nice-looking meat, right?

01:27:45.860 --> 01:27:46.961
Nice-looking meat?

01:27:46.961 --> 01:27:49.897
Then you lift up the meat, boo!

01:27:49.897 --> 01:27:51.766
Boo!

01:27:51.766 --> 01:27:54.002
Who ruined this sandwich with vegetables?

01:27:54.002 --> 01:27:55.603
It is the spicy Italian.

01:27:57.205 --> 01:27:58.239
Looks a lot like the BMT.

01:27:58.239 --> 01:27:59.974
But yeah, dude, in Subway's defense,

01:27:59.974 --> 01:28:01.809
these sandwiches were made,

01:28:01.809 --> 01:28:03.745
what, three hours ago at this point?

01:28:03.745 --> 01:28:08.216
So, here are Japan's
exclusive regular menu items.

01:28:08.216 --> 01:28:12.820
So let's start with this
pizza bacon Italiana.

01:28:12.820 --> 01:28:14.355
Itadakimasu!

01:28:15.857 --> 01:28:19.694
I will rate this 7 out of 10.

01:28:19.694 --> 01:28:22.196
Molto bene!

01:28:22.196 --> 01:28:26.801
So, next one, we've got
prosciutto mascarpone.

01:28:26.801 --> 01:28:28.936
Shrimp avocado.

01:28:28.936 --> 01:28:31.873
And I love avocado.

01:28:31.873 --> 01:28:36.678
Next, we've got turkey, bacon, egg.

01:28:36.678 --> 01:28:37.912
Turkey;

01:28:37.912 --> 01:28:41.115
as you can see, bacon, right here;

01:28:41.115 --> 01:28:43.418
and egg paste.

01:28:47.422 --> 01:28:48.923
It's not that great.

01:28:48.923 --> 01:28:53.227
And next, we've got
chili chicken sandwich.

01:28:55.496 --> 01:28:58.966
This is terrible.

01:28:58.966 --> 01:29:01.836
Subway, how dare you?

01:29:01.836 --> 01:29:03.471
[crying]

01:29:03.471 --> 01:29:07.809
OK, I'm getting full,
but let's keep going.

01:29:07.809 --> 01:29:12.180
Here we've got avocado vegetables.

01:29:12.180 --> 01:29:13.981
Mm!

01:29:13.981 --> 01:29:16.884
Next, we've got egg sandwich.

01:29:17.785 --> 01:29:20.655
All right, one thing I
have to mention is that

01:29:20.655 --> 01:29:23.624
most of these sandwiches can be a salad.

01:29:23.624 --> 01:29:26.094
So if you like salad, go ahead.

01:29:26.094 --> 01:29:29.864
But Joe wouldn't get this for sure.

01:29:29.864 --> 01:29:31.933
What, did Subway get a
panini press or something?

01:29:31.933 --> 01:29:33.267
Like, look at these. They
just took these sandwiches

01:29:33.267 --> 01:29:34.569
and grilled them or whatever.

01:29:34.569 --> 01:29:37.772
OK, this one right here is the BMT.

01:29:37.772 --> 01:29:39.841
So, I'm just guessing for the melts,

01:29:39.841 --> 01:29:41.175
they do it on the white bread,

01:29:41.175 --> 01:29:42.043
and they add a bunch of cheese,

01:29:42.043 --> 01:29:43.378
and they just grill it, right?

01:29:43.378 --> 01:29:44.345
I mean, I can't even open this.

01:29:44.345 --> 01:29:46.013
Like, it's locked.

01:29:46.013 --> 01:29:47.515
Buffalo chicken melt.

01:29:47.515 --> 01:29:48.783
Maybe there's less vegetables in it,

01:29:48.783 --> 01:29:50.618
so maybe I do want this
and I don't realize it.

01:29:50.618 --> 01:29:52.286
Steak and cheese.

01:29:52.286 --> 01:29:53.788
A Philly cheesesteak, right?

01:29:53.788 --> 01:29:55.123
Blech. I know this one.

01:29:55.123 --> 01:29:56.824
I know this one!

01:29:56.824 --> 01:29:58.826
Tuna melt.

01:29:58.826 --> 01:30:00.395
Turkey melt. Yeah, I guess.

01:30:00.395 --> 01:30:01.462
I mean, I gotta say, like,

01:30:01.462 --> 01:30:02.597
I haven't tasted them,

01:30:02.597 --> 01:30:03.965
but the effort in these are just like,

01:30:03.965 --> 01:30:04.799
what are you guys doing?

01:30:04.799 --> 01:30:07.769
I mean, they just, like, flattened them.

01:30:07.769 --> 01:30:09.303
Ham melt.

01:30:09.303 --> 01:30:10.505
What's SP again?

01:30:10.505 --> 01:30:11.939
Producer: Spicy Italian.

01:30:11.939 --> 01:30:15.209
It should be SI, but
it's SP for spicy, right?

01:30:15.209 --> 01:30:16.611
That's why I'm like, "Wait a second,

01:30:16.611 --> 01:30:19.013
is this the spaghetti one
we've been talking about?"

01:30:19.013 --> 01:30:20.448
Meatball melt. What'd they do?

01:30:20.448 --> 01:30:22.583
They flattened the
meatballs in there, right?

01:30:22.583 --> 01:30:23.651
Oh, f---.

01:30:23.651 --> 01:30:25.353
I mean, it's better.
Less vegetables, right?

01:30:25.353 --> 01:30:27.722
This is the chicken bacon melt.

01:30:29.123 --> 01:30:32.660
So, this is the Japan Only sandwich.

01:30:32.660 --> 01:30:36.230
Everything on here, you
can't get in the US.

01:30:36.230 --> 01:30:40.468
It's a 6-inch on sesame
bread with tandoori chicken,

01:30:40.468 --> 01:30:44.839
mascarpone, cream cheese,
egg salad, shrimp,

01:30:44.839 --> 01:30:48.876
chili sauce, and wasabi soy sauce.

01:30:48.876 --> 01:30:51.312
This is a mystery sandwich.

01:30:51.312 --> 01:30:52.380
Itadakimasu.

01:30:56.317 --> 01:30:58.619
I said wasabi soy sauce, right?

01:30:58.619 --> 01:31:01.022
I got wasabi attack.

01:31:01.022 --> 01:31:02.824
It's hurting me.

01:31:02.824 --> 01:31:07.228
It's got too many flavors,
and it makes me confused.

01:31:07.228 --> 01:31:09.063
This here is the USA Only sandwich,

01:31:09.063 --> 01:31:11.065
a sandwich comprised of only ingredients

01:31:11.065 --> 01:31:13.201
you can get in the United
States and not in Japan.

01:31:13.201 --> 01:31:15.703
So, I started with the
jalapeño cheese bread.

01:31:15.703 --> 01:31:17.772
It has meatballs, American cheese,

01:31:17.772 --> 01:31:20.107
pepper jack cheese, provolone cheese,

01:31:20.107 --> 01:31:22.076
banana peppers, good God!

01:31:22.076 --> 01:31:25.947
Spinach, ranch, sriracha, and pepperoni.

01:31:25.947 --> 01:31:26.848
[sighs]

01:31:26.848 --> 01:31:27.815
Here we go.

01:31:31.085 --> 01:31:32.753
That's actually pretty good.

01:31:32.753 --> 01:31:33.588
I really like this.

01:31:33.588 --> 01:31:35.289
Dude, that's good.

01:31:35.289 --> 01:31:37.225
It's not too spicy. The
jalapeño bread's really good.

01:31:37.225 --> 01:31:39.927
The meatballs and the pepperoni
work really well together.

01:31:39.927 --> 01:31:40.895
I gotta say, the banana peppers

01:31:40.895 --> 01:31:41.729
are actually welcome in this.

01:31:41.729 --> 01:31:43.164
It kind of makes it a little sweeter.

01:31:43.164 --> 01:31:45.566
I'm gonna take another bite. Yeah!

01:31:45.566 --> 01:31:47.602
Subway, put this on your menu.

01:31:47.602 --> 01:31:48.870
This is really good.

01:31:48.870 --> 01:31:51.205
I challenge you, all the
viewers in the United States,

01:31:51.205 --> 01:31:52.874
start ordering this sandwich.

01:31:52.874 --> 01:31:54.041
Let's put the pressure on Subway

01:31:54.041 --> 01:31:56.110
to make this a featured sandwich.

01:31:56.110 --> 01:31:57.311
This is good!

01:31:57.311 --> 01:31:58.145
Mm!

01:31:58.145 --> 01:32:01.282
So, here we've got snack sandwiches.

01:32:01.282 --> 01:32:04.952
This one right here is anko sandwich.

01:32:04.952 --> 01:32:08.923
And anko is a staple of
traditional Japanese sweets.

01:32:08.923 --> 01:32:13.127
The taste can be enjoyed
alone or as a complement

01:32:13.127 --> 01:32:16.464
to other Japanese flavors, such as matcha.

01:32:16.464 --> 01:32:18.466
And here we've got

01:32:18.466 --> 01:32:21.636
anko and mascarpone.

01:32:21.636 --> 01:32:22.970
I have an announcement to make.

01:32:22.970 --> 01:32:24.472
Subway has breakfast.

01:32:24.472 --> 01:32:26.107
I'm just as surprised as all of you.

01:32:26.107 --> 01:32:28.409
Specifically, they have
four breakfast sandwiches

01:32:28.409 --> 01:32:29.243
here in the US.

01:32:29.243 --> 01:32:30.645
A bacon, egg, and cheese;

01:32:30.645 --> 01:32:32.847
a Black Forest ham, egg, and cheese;

01:32:32.847 --> 01:32:33.714
egg and cheese;

01:32:33.714 --> 01:32:35.216
and steak, egg, and cheese.

01:32:35.216 --> 01:32:36.517
I don't know which one is which.

01:32:36.517 --> 01:32:39.453
I think this is the
steak, egg, and cheese.

01:32:39.453 --> 01:32:41.222
Oh, it's flatbread too,
so I can kind of --

01:32:41.222 --> 01:32:42.557
[laughs]

01:32:42.557 --> 01:32:44.525
This looks like a cartoon!

01:32:44.525 --> 01:32:45.793
Look at this!

01:32:47.094 --> 01:32:49.030
Look at the eggs.

01:32:49.030 --> 01:32:50.865
Are you kidding me with this?

01:32:50.865 --> 01:32:51.933
At a Subway in the US,

01:32:51.933 --> 01:32:53.668
you can get just about any one

01:32:53.668 --> 01:32:55.570
of their sandwiches as a protein bowl.

01:32:55.570 --> 01:32:56.537
From what I can tell,

01:32:56.537 --> 01:32:58.606
that's their way of calling this a salad.

01:32:58.606 --> 01:33:00.942
So, you know my feelings on salad.

01:33:00.942 --> 01:33:01.842
I hate them.

01:33:01.842 --> 01:33:02.810
Just an example, though,

01:33:02.810 --> 01:33:04.912
we got what looks to be a turkey one.

01:33:04.912 --> 01:33:06.447
Everything that comes on a sandwich,

01:33:06.447 --> 01:33:08.616
but just instead of bread, it's a bowl.

01:33:08.616 --> 01:33:10.885
Then once you're done you
can throw it in the ocean.

01:33:10.885 --> 01:33:12.286
Kill a sea turtle.

01:33:12.286 --> 01:33:13.521
Who cares? Why?

01:33:13.521 --> 01:33:14.989
It's a waste. It's an absolute waste.

01:33:14.989 --> 01:33:16.557
Just eat a sandwich like a normal person.

01:33:16.557 --> 01:33:18.326
There's nothing wrong with bread.

01:33:18.326 --> 01:33:19.961
Just eat it! It's a sandwich!

01:33:19.961 --> 01:33:20.795
Yeah, God.

01:33:20.795 --> 01:33:21.963
And it's the shredded lettuce, too.

01:33:21.963 --> 01:33:25.533
It's not, like, leafy lettuce
or spinach or anything.

01:33:25.533 --> 01:33:27.435
It's just that shredduce that
they put on the sandwich.

01:33:27.435 --> 01:33:28.869
[groans]

01:33:28.869 --> 01:33:32.473
So, here is Japan's exclusive sides.

01:33:32.473 --> 01:33:36.611
This one right here is korokoro
potatoes, original flavor.

01:33:36.611 --> 01:33:39.981
And next one, we've got korokoro potatoes,

01:33:39.981 --> 01:33:41.716
triple cheese flavored.

01:33:41.716 --> 01:33:44.652
Korokoro potatoes, herb salt flavor.

01:33:44.652 --> 01:33:48.356
The korokoro means it's,
like, rolling over and over.

01:33:48.356 --> 01:33:50.725
Like, korokorokoro. Korokorokoro.

01:33:50.725 --> 01:33:52.560
Rolling over and over.

01:33:52.560 --> 01:33:56.864
And last one, we've
got corn cream chowder.

01:33:56.864 --> 01:34:00.301
Yeah dude. Chips! Chips!

01:34:01.869 --> 01:34:04.372
Chips!

01:34:04.372 --> 01:34:06.207
Get yourself the Baked Lays.

01:34:06.207 --> 01:34:09.543
I mean, the undisputed chip
champion in the United States

01:34:09.543 --> 01:34:12.546
right here, baby. Nacho cheese Doritos.

01:34:12.546 --> 01:34:13.914
A favorite. A classic Lays.

01:34:13.914 --> 01:34:15.416
When you just wanna see
what potato chips were like

01:34:15.416 --> 01:34:18.152
in the '50s, get yourself
a bag of classic Lays.

01:34:18.152 --> 01:34:21.956
Oh, Miss Vickie's! Jalapeño,
and lime cracked pepper.

01:34:21.956 --> 01:34:24.592
I don't think I've had
the lime cracked pepper.

01:34:28.129 --> 01:34:30.064
These are so good.

01:34:30.064 --> 01:34:31.232
Sun Chips.

01:34:31.232 --> 01:34:33.000
I hate Sun Chips.

01:34:33.000 --> 01:34:34.435
Here's a side that you can get in the US

01:34:34.435 --> 01:34:35.870
you can't get in Japan.

01:34:35.870 --> 01:34:38.939
I'm gonna go "muscle man's" applesauce.

01:34:38.939 --> 01:34:42.276
So, here is Japan's exclusive drinks.

01:34:42.276 --> 01:34:44.679
This one right here is iced tea,

01:34:44.679 --> 01:34:47.148
and Pepsi, melon soda,

01:34:47.148 --> 01:34:49.617
oolong tea, which is Chinese tea,

01:34:49.617 --> 01:34:52.553
iced coffee, soy cocoa.

01:34:52.553 --> 01:34:55.556
And this one right here is
vegetable and fruit juice,

01:34:55.556 --> 01:34:59.827
which has 11 kinds of vegetables
and three kinds of fruits.

01:34:59.827 --> 01:35:02.196
And this one right here is Pepsi zero.

01:35:02.196 --> 01:35:03.864
And this one is mocha.

01:35:03.864 --> 01:35:05.533
Iced café au lait.

01:35:05.533 --> 01:35:07.368
And this one right here is ginger ale.

01:35:07.368 --> 01:35:09.970
And soy latte, soy mango,

01:35:09.970 --> 01:35:12.106
mango orange, mango juice,

01:35:12.106 --> 01:35:15.209
mocha, and milk tea, cocoa,

01:35:15.209 --> 01:35:18.846
hot black tea, and herb tea.

01:35:18.846 --> 01:35:20.181
In the US, as you noticed,

01:35:20.181 --> 01:35:23.017
we have Coke and Coke
products at our Subways.

01:35:23.017 --> 01:35:24.218
So we have Coke.

01:35:24.218 --> 01:35:25.386
And they also have to-go bottles,

01:35:25.386 --> 01:35:27.822
so I went ahead and got diet Coke,

01:35:27.822 --> 01:35:30.958
Sprite, and Gatorade,

01:35:30.958 --> 01:35:31.926
the fruit punch.

01:35:31.926 --> 01:35:33.260
All right, Sauce Talk.

01:35:33.260 --> 01:35:34.829
Sauce Talk.

01:35:34.829 --> 01:35:36.630
I couldn't get any of them on the side,

01:35:36.630 --> 01:35:40.000
but we have exclusive sauces
here at the Subway in the US.

01:35:40.000 --> 01:35:42.903
We can get a red wine
vinegar, a yellow mustard,

01:35:42.903 --> 01:35:46.207
a creamy sriracha, a
Buffalo sauce, of course,

01:35:46.207 --> 01:35:50.211
we also have ranch, chipotle
southwest, marinara sauce,

01:35:50.211 --> 01:35:54.515
sweet onion sauce, and MVP Parmesan.

01:35:54.515 --> 01:35:56.650
The most valuable Parmesan, apparently.

01:35:56.650 --> 01:35:59.553
I was surprised to learn
that the Japanese Subway

01:35:59.553 --> 01:36:00.654
doesn't have cookies.

01:36:00.654 --> 01:36:01.956
The cookies are actually pretty good.

01:36:01.956 --> 01:36:03.991
In the US, you can get
a chocolate chip cookie,

01:36:03.991 --> 01:36:05.392
an oatmeal raisin cookie,

01:36:05.392 --> 01:36:06.894
a raspberry cheesecake cookie,

01:36:06.894 --> 01:36:10.397
and a white chip macadamia nut cookie.

01:36:10.397 --> 01:36:14.301
All right, so let's move on
to Japan's exclusive sweets.

01:36:14.301 --> 01:36:17.371
So, let's start with this
one, chocolate brownie.

01:36:18.439 --> 01:36:21.041
We've got cheese tart,

01:36:21.041 --> 01:36:24.845
and this one right here
is cream soda float.

01:36:24.845 --> 01:36:28.883
And this one right here
is cream latte float,

01:36:28.883 --> 01:36:31.118
and coffee float.

01:36:33.454 --> 01:36:36.423
In Japan, our 6-inch
turkey sub on white bread

01:36:36.423 --> 01:36:38.926
is 261 calories.

01:36:38.926 --> 01:36:42.596
And in the US, that same
turkey sub is 270 calories.

01:36:42.596 --> 01:36:43.464
So pretty close.

01:36:43.464 --> 01:36:48.435
But I did notice ours has much
less sodium, like 26% less.

01:36:48.435 --> 01:36:52.773
Our 6-inch tuna sub is 361 calories.

01:36:52.773 --> 01:36:54.508
And our tuna is 430,

01:36:54.508 --> 01:36:57.178
so a little more, but much more fat.

01:36:57.178 --> 01:37:01.148
I have not eaten tuna
anything on purpose ever.

01:37:01.148 --> 01:37:02.950
It smells like cat food.
Don't you think it smells?

01:37:02.950 --> 01:37:04.985
I guess most cat food is tuna, so yeah.

01:37:04.985 --> 01:37:07.588
This looks super gross, but
I have to try it, right?

01:37:07.588 --> 01:37:10.357
Let's see if my distaste is misplaced.

01:37:16.463 --> 01:37:17.398
No.

01:37:17.398 --> 01:37:19.200
I hate that, man.

01:37:19.200 --> 01:37:20.768
Do you like calories?

01:37:20.768 --> 01:37:23.971
In Japan, our most calorific sandwich

01:37:23.971 --> 01:37:26.707
is the pizza bacon Italiana.

01:37:26.707 --> 01:37:31.045
One 6-inch is 436 calories.

01:37:31.045 --> 01:37:32.947
In the US, our most calorific sandwich

01:37:32.947 --> 01:37:35.115
is the chicken and bacon ranch.

01:37:35.115 --> 01:37:37.918
Just 6 inches of this
bad boy is 500 calories,

01:37:37.918 --> 01:37:40.621
so a foot-long is 1,000 calories.

01:37:40.621 --> 01:37:44.024
In Japan, our regular
sandwich with a small drink

01:37:44.024 --> 01:37:46.527
and small serving of potatoes,

01:37:46.527 --> 01:37:51.365
the total calories for
this meal is 498 calories.

01:37:51.365 --> 01:37:53.434
In the US, a 6-inch turkey sandwich

01:37:53.434 --> 01:37:55.536
with a small drink, which
the Subway I went to

01:37:55.536 --> 01:37:56.737
said they do not have,

01:37:56.737 --> 01:37:59.106
and a bag of chips, I went
with the classic Lays,

01:37:59.106 --> 01:38:01.742
is 750 calories.

01:38:01.742 --> 01:38:05.479
In Japan, this meal total is 790 yen,

01:38:05.479 --> 01:38:08.249
or $7.23 US.

01:38:08.249 --> 01:38:11.385
In the US, that same meal is $9.14,

01:38:11.385 --> 01:38:15.222
or about 998.26 Japanese yen.

01:38:15.222 --> 01:38:18.525
Roughly 26.4% increase.

01:38:18.525 --> 01:38:21.595
In Japan, we focus on
having a healthy diet,

01:38:21.595 --> 01:38:23.764
or chōkatsu meals.

01:38:23.764 --> 01:38:26.300
Chōkatsu means having a healthy diet

01:38:26.300 --> 01:38:29.236
that contains a lot of dietary fiber

01:38:29.236 --> 01:38:32.640
in order to keep your
intestinal environment healthy.

01:38:32.640 --> 01:38:36.477
And it's getting common in
Japan to have chōkatsu meals

01:38:36.477 --> 01:38:39.179
at home or even at restaurants,

01:38:39.179 --> 01:38:44.018
because a lot of Japanese people
have a constipation problem

01:38:44.018 --> 01:38:48.255
due to a lot of stress
and lack of exercise.

01:38:48.255 --> 01:38:50.925
So Subway offers a special meal

01:38:50.925 --> 01:38:54.028
called chōkatsu chicken
and cheese sandwich,

01:38:54.028 --> 01:38:56.597
which contains a lot of dietary fiber.

01:38:56.597 --> 01:38:58.599
So it's going to help you return to your

01:38:58.599 --> 01:39:00.768
regular bowel movements,

01:39:00.768 --> 01:39:05.072
and you can start your day with a No. 2.

01:39:05.072 --> 01:39:06.707
So, we don't have anything like that,

01:39:06.707 --> 01:39:08.642
but I can only speak for myself that

01:39:08.642 --> 01:39:12.746
if you're experiencing
constipation in the United States,

01:39:12.746 --> 01:39:15.616
may I recommend the steak
and cheese at Subway?

01:39:18.085 --> 01:39:20.554
The Subway in Japan does not disclose

01:39:20.554 --> 01:39:22.222
all their raw ingredients,

01:39:22.222 --> 01:39:25.225
but they did provide
the main raw ingredients

01:39:25.225 --> 01:39:26.694
for their breads.

01:39:26.694 --> 01:39:30.664
Japan Subway flatbread
contains wheat flour,

01:39:30.664 --> 01:39:35.336
yeast, vegetable fat and
oils, skim milk powder,

01:39:35.336 --> 01:39:38.772
wheat protein, salt, sugar,

01:39:38.772 --> 01:39:41.976
barley malt powder, et cetera.

01:39:41.976 --> 01:39:43.944
Well, our Subway in the US
does gives us the ingredients,

01:39:43.944 --> 01:39:46.347
and our flatbread contains all of this.

01:39:46.347 --> 01:39:48.549
Now, there's a few similar ingredients,

01:39:48.549 --> 01:39:51.051
and there's a bunch that are pretty close.

01:39:51.051 --> 01:39:53.520
That "Etc." in the Japan
flatbread, that gives me pause.

01:39:53.520 --> 01:39:55.089
I mean, if that's supposed to represent

01:39:55.089 --> 01:39:59.126
all of this other stuff,
that is a huge dot dot dot,

01:39:59.126 --> 01:40:02.129
or to be continued, or yada yada yada,

01:40:02.129 --> 01:40:04.631
that Japan's throwing at their customers.

01:40:04.631 --> 01:40:07.634
I mean, if America has
proven anything, it's like,

01:40:07.634 --> 01:40:09.336
you can tell us what's in
the food, we don't care,

01:40:09.336 --> 01:40:10.137
we'll still eat it.

01:40:10.137 --> 01:40:12.172
So, I don't know what's
up with the etc., guys.

01:40:12.172 --> 01:40:14.842
Subway's tuna was a bit
controversial here in the US

01:40:14.842 --> 01:40:15.876
starting in January,

01:40:15.876 --> 01:40:18.679
where a class action
lawsuit made false claims

01:40:18.679 --> 01:40:20.280
about their tuna meat.

01:40:20.280 --> 01:40:22.282
The drama continued when
a New York Times article

01:40:22.282 --> 01:40:24.184
claiming to have had a lab

01:40:24.184 --> 01:40:26.787
analyze 60 inches' worth of Subway tuna

01:40:26.787 --> 01:40:27.755
shared the results,

01:40:27.755 --> 01:40:30.724
saying they could not
identify a species of fish

01:40:30.724 --> 01:40:34.695
and, "No amplifiable tuna DNA
was present in the sample."

01:40:34.695 --> 01:40:35.929
Subway responded, of course,

01:40:35.929 --> 01:40:38.298
saying it uses 100% wild-caught tuna

01:40:38.298 --> 01:40:39.833
and even launched a website,

01:40:39.833 --> 01:40:42.269
Subwaytunafacts.com,

01:40:42.269 --> 01:40:44.605
to give everyone a clear
and transparent look

01:40:44.605 --> 01:40:46.573
into their tuna process.

01:40:46.573 --> 01:40:49.610
Furthermore, USA Today did
their own fact-checking

01:40:49.610 --> 01:40:51.211
and had its doubts about how The Times

01:40:51.211 --> 01:40:53.480
tested the tuna samples and pointed out

01:40:53.480 --> 01:40:56.417
the lab tested for five
tuna species out of 15

01:40:56.417 --> 01:40:58.786
and concluded the tuna was too processed,

01:40:58.786 --> 01:41:00.554
or that there was no tuna DNA.

01:41:00.554 --> 01:41:03.290
Different tests have detected
tuna in Subway sandwiches,

01:41:03.290 --> 01:41:04.658
and experts say canned tuna

01:41:04.658 --> 01:41:06.427
can become denatured when cooked.

01:41:06.427 --> 01:41:07.995
Then I did my own scientific research

01:41:07.995 --> 01:41:09.396
to find out what denatured means,

01:41:09.396 --> 01:41:11.532
and the scientists at Dictionary.com said,

01:41:11.532 --> 01:41:14.401
"Dear Joe, thanks for reaching
out to Dictionary.com!

01:41:14.401 --> 01:41:16.637
The word denatured means 'to
destroy the characteristic

01:41:16.637 --> 01:41:20.007
properties of (a protein or
biological macromolecule)

01:41:20.007 --> 01:41:22.676
by heat, acidity, or
other effects that disrupt

01:41:22.676 --> 01:41:24.144
its molecular conformation."

01:41:24.144 --> 01:41:25.212
They went on to say,

01:41:25.212 --> 01:41:26.747
"For further definition inquiries

01:41:26.747 --> 01:41:29.450
please just use the search
function on the home page

01:41:29.450 --> 01:41:32.252
as that is what it's there
for, don't email us."

01:41:32.252 --> 01:41:34.421
So, believe what you want.

01:41:34.421 --> 01:41:36.356
Another Subway ingredient controversy

01:41:36.356 --> 01:41:37.758
that's a bit more clean-cut,

01:41:37.758 --> 01:41:39.326
at least for the good people of Ireland,

01:41:39.326 --> 01:41:41.228
is that an Irish court ruled Subway

01:41:41.228 --> 01:41:45.099
cannot call their bread bread
due to its high sugar content.

01:41:45.099 --> 01:41:47.434
In Ireland, for bread
to be considered bread,

01:41:47.434 --> 01:41:48.936
the amount of sugar in the dough

01:41:48.936 --> 01:41:51.305
must be 2% the flour's weight.

01:41:51.305 --> 01:41:55.576
Subway's bread, however,
the sugar content is 9.2%.

01:41:56.510 --> 01:41:58.745
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

01:41:58.745 --> 01:42:00.647
