01:57:38.217 --> 01:57:39.952
Let's talk about nutrition.

01:57:39.952 --> 01:57:42.555
In Japan, a beef crunchy taco

01:57:42.555 --> 01:57:46.426
is 164.4 calories.

01:57:46.426 --> 01:57:49.829
It has 87.2 grams of protein,

01:57:49.829 --> 01:57:52.298
5.5 grams of fat,

01:57:52.298 --> 01:57:55.201
14.7 grams of carbs,

01:57:55.201 --> 01:57:59.072
and 293 milligrams of sodium.

01:57:59.072 --> 01:58:01.074
In the US, our standard beef crunchy taco

01:58:01.074 --> 01:58:02.842
is 170 calories,

01:58:02.842 --> 01:58:05.645
8 grams of protein, 9 grams of fat,

01:58:05.645 --> 01:58:09.449
13 grams of carbs, and
310 milligrams of sodium.

01:58:09.449 --> 01:58:12.185
So we lead in calories, fat, and sodium,

01:58:12.185 --> 01:58:14.253
where Japan has more protein and carbs.

01:58:14.253 --> 01:58:17.824
The next one is the chicken quesadilla.

01:58:17.824 --> 01:58:22.161
Ours has 492.51 calories.

01:58:22.161 --> 01:58:24.430
This one has 510 calories.

01:58:24.430 --> 01:58:25.331
One thing to note:

01:58:25.331 --> 01:58:27.700
that in both countries,
one of these quesadillas

01:58:27.700 --> 01:58:30.870
hovers around half of your daily sodium.

01:58:30.870 --> 01:58:33.573
Sodium at Taco Bell
appears to be such an issue

01:58:33.573 --> 01:58:36.476
that in the US menu online,
certain combos and items,

01:58:36.476 --> 01:58:39.979
like this one right here, are
labeled with sodium warnings.

01:58:39.979 --> 01:58:42.582
In Japan, a Crunchwrap Supreme

01:58:42.582 --> 01:58:46.819
has 1,290 milligrams of sodium.

01:58:46.819 --> 01:58:50.923
That's 56% of your daily allowance.

01:58:50.923 --> 01:58:54.727
Our Crunchwrap Supreme
is 52% your daily sodium.

01:58:54.727 --> 01:58:56.295
That's more than half, right?

01:58:56.295 --> 01:58:59.332
Man, so both countries,
way too much sodium.

01:58:59.332 --> 01:59:03.302
Are you looking for the most
calories in one menu item?

01:59:03.302 --> 01:59:06.672
In Japan, it's our loaded fries.

01:59:06.672 --> 01:59:10.076
One order is 718 calories.

01:59:10.076 --> 01:59:12.745
It has a third of your daily calories,

01:59:12.745 --> 01:59:14.714
almost half of your daily fat,

01:59:14.714 --> 01:59:17.984
and 66% of your daily sodium.

01:59:17.984 --> 01:59:19.252
In the US, the biggest thing

01:59:19.252 --> 01:59:20.620
you should look out for are the nachos.

01:59:20.620 --> 01:59:22.822
The very popular Nachos BellGrande,

01:59:22.822 --> 01:59:23.623
I love you guys,

01:59:23.623 --> 01:59:26.058
is 740 calories,

01:59:26.058 --> 01:59:28.327
1,050 milligrams of sodium.

01:59:28.327 --> 01:59:32.899
OK. Now, the Cinnabon Delights
do have more calories, 930.

01:59:32.899 --> 01:59:34.367
But technically that's a 12-pack,

01:59:34.367 --> 01:59:36.102
which is supposed to be for four people.

01:59:36.102 --> 01:59:37.203
I'm certain, if you're like me,

01:59:37.203 --> 01:59:38.871
you're getting 12 and
you're not sharing them.

01:59:38.871 --> 01:59:41.207
Some do, most don't, but obviously

01:59:41.207 --> 01:59:44.143
the Nachos BellGrande is for one person.

01:59:44.143 --> 01:59:46.078
But the most calories lie in an item

01:59:46.078 --> 01:59:48.014
that's on Taco Bell's cantina menu,

01:59:48.014 --> 01:59:49.315
which is only available

01:59:49.315 --> 01:59:50.783
at certain locations here in the US.

01:59:50.783 --> 01:59:53.753
There, you can get something
called the grande beef nachos,

01:59:53.753 --> 01:59:57.990
which has 1,120 calories,

01:59:57.990 --> 02:00:00.760
which is more than half
of your daily allowance,

02:00:00.760 --> 02:00:02.828
and 68% of your daily sodium.

02:00:02.828 --> 02:00:04.063
[sighs]

02:00:04.063 --> 02:00:06.499
Now, it's just not the food at Taco Bell.

02:00:06.499 --> 02:00:08.701
You also have to watch out for the drinks.

02:00:08.701 --> 02:00:10.036
Here it is, everyone.

02:00:10.036 --> 02:00:14.507
30 fluid ounces of
Mountain Dew Baja Blast.

02:00:14.507 --> 02:00:16.209
A beverage that answers the question,

02:00:16.209 --> 02:00:18.177
"What if we combined Mountain Dew's bold,

02:00:18.177 --> 02:00:21.180
refreshing tropical
flavor with crystal meth?"

02:00:21.180 --> 02:00:24.850
This totally logical 30 fluid
ounces of nightmare fuel

02:00:24.850 --> 02:00:27.587
is 420 calories, very cool,

02:00:27.587 --> 02:00:30.089
and 110 grams of sugar.

02:00:30.089 --> 02:00:30.990
I don't know. Sorry.

02:00:30.990 --> 02:00:32.692
This stuff is making me delirious.

02:00:36.929 --> 02:00:39.565
In the US, there are a few
ingredients at our Taco Bell

02:00:39.565 --> 02:00:40.733
you should look out for.

02:00:40.733 --> 02:00:43.569
Both are in the beverages
on Taco Bell's cantina menu.

02:00:43.569 --> 02:00:46.539
First is brominated vegetable oil,

02:00:46.539 --> 02:00:48.674
aka BVO,

02:00:48.674 --> 02:00:50.042
which is banned in Japan.

02:00:50.042 --> 02:00:53.145
BVO is an emulsifier found
in citrus-flavored sodas

02:00:53.145 --> 02:00:55.514
and is specifically used with citrus oils,

02:00:55.514 --> 02:00:56.749
and it's considered a health risk

02:00:56.749 --> 02:00:58.150
when ingested in large amounts.

02:00:58.150 --> 02:00:59.919
It was brought to public attention

02:00:59.919 --> 02:01:01.721
when it was discovered
in popular beverages

02:01:01.721 --> 02:01:04.390
like Mountain Dew and Powerade,
but due to public pressure,

02:01:04.390 --> 02:01:06.592
it was removed from
Coke and Pepsi products

02:01:06.592 --> 02:01:08.594
in 2014, which is good.

02:01:08.594 --> 02:01:11.330
Now, unfortunately, you can
still find this ingredient

02:01:11.330 --> 02:01:14.033
in three cantina menu freezes.

02:01:14.033 --> 02:01:16.869
The beach berry freeze,
the ginger mule freeze,

02:01:16.869 --> 02:01:18.871
and the party punch freeze.

02:01:18.871 --> 02:01:20.172
Luckily, they weren't
in any of the freezes

02:01:20.172 --> 02:01:23.075
you'd find in the regular
menu, only on the cantina menu.

02:01:24.744 --> 02:01:26.212
Ugh!

02:01:26.212 --> 02:01:29.582
OK. When it comes to citrus-flavored soda,

02:01:29.582 --> 02:01:31.817
we have CC Lemon.

02:01:31.817 --> 02:01:33.719
That's one of the most popular

02:01:33.719 --> 02:01:36.055
citrus-flavored soda in Japan.

02:01:36.055 --> 02:01:38.524
CCL Lemon contains the following:

02:01:38.524 --> 02:01:42.028
sugars, which is fructose-glucose syrup

02:01:42.028 --> 02:01:46.999
and sugar, lemon juice,
flavoring, vitamin C,

02:01:46.999 --> 02:01:51.771
acidulant, safflower dye,
calcium pantothenate,

02:01:51.771 --> 02:01:54.707
vitamin B6, carotene pigment.

02:01:54.707 --> 02:01:55.675
That's it.

02:01:55.675 --> 02:02:00.479
See? It doesn't have
brominated vegetable oil.

02:02:00.479 --> 02:02:02.682
It tastes really good.

02:02:02.682 --> 02:02:05.451
So that means you can make it delicious

02:02:05.451 --> 02:02:08.287
without BVO.

02:02:08.287 --> 02:02:09.955
The last one, party punch freeze,

02:02:09.955 --> 02:02:13.659
also contains Yellow
No. 5, aka tartrazine,

02:02:13.659 --> 02:02:15.728
which is subject to
restrictions outside of the US

02:02:15.728 --> 02:02:17.863
in places like the EU and Japan,

02:02:17.863 --> 02:02:20.366
as it may have "adverse effect

02:02:20.366 --> 02:02:23.269
on activity and attention in children."

02:02:23.269 --> 02:02:24.670
What the hell?

02:02:24.670 --> 02:02:28.074
You can tell this color is yellow, right?

02:02:28.074 --> 02:02:32.712
So why don't you use something
else that isn't harmful?

02:02:32.712 --> 02:02:35.748
Just like CC Lemon.

02:02:35.748 --> 02:02:37.016
♪ CC lemon, hey ♪

02:02:37.216 --> 02:02:39.118
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

02:02:39.118 --> 02:02:40.953
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:02:40.953 --> 02:02:43.489
between Kit Kats in Japan and the US.

02:02:43.489 --> 02:02:45.725
This is "Food Wars."

02:02:47.360 --> 02:02:49.962
In Japan, our Kit Kats come in four sizes,

02:02:49.962 --> 02:02:51.530
big little pouch bite,

02:02:51.530 --> 02:02:52.698
minis,

02:02:52.698 --> 02:02:53.733
and bar,

02:02:53.733 --> 02:02:55.901
and classy one, Sublime.

02:02:55.901 --> 02:02:58.571
So, one thing to note
here regarding mini sizes,

02:02:58.571 --> 02:03:01.374
the regular Kit Kat is 11.6 grams,

02:03:01.374 --> 02:03:04.410
but the flavored minis, such as matcha,

02:03:04.410 --> 02:03:07.680
are said to be slightly
smaller, 11.3 grams.

02:03:07.680 --> 02:03:09.582
So I'm going to weigh them now to confirm.

02:03:09.582 --> 02:03:13.119
So, let's weigh a
regular-flavor Kit Kat first.

02:03:13.119 --> 02:03:15.020
It weighs 11 grams.

02:03:15.020 --> 02:03:16.889
But it doesn't show the decimal points,

02:03:16.889 --> 02:03:18.657
it says just 11 grams.

02:03:18.657 --> 02:03:21.694
Let's weigh matcha flavor.

02:03:21.694 --> 02:03:22.528
12.

02:03:22.528 --> 02:03:24.830
It's actually heavier than regular flavor.

02:03:24.830 --> 02:03:25.731
Interesting.

02:03:25.731 --> 02:03:28.401
Japanese Kit Kats have become
popular all around the world,

02:03:28.401 --> 02:03:30.703
and the US, of course, is no exception.

02:03:30.703 --> 02:03:31.937
I just want to mention at the top here,

02:03:31.937 --> 02:03:33.105
we're going to be talking about Kit Kats

02:03:33.105 --> 02:03:34.607
that are native to our countries.

02:03:34.607 --> 02:03:35.908
I know you can get them online.

02:03:35.908 --> 02:03:38.110
I think Walmart.com has some of them.

02:03:38.110 --> 02:03:40.413
Fantastic. They're imported.
We know. Thank you.

02:03:40.413 --> 02:03:43.416
In the US, our Kit Kats
come in nine sizes.

02:03:43.416 --> 02:03:44.917
Starting from the smallest,

02:03:44.917 --> 02:03:47.853
we have a Kit Kat minis unwrapped,

02:03:47.853 --> 02:03:49.255
then the thins,

02:03:49.255 --> 02:03:50.256
miniatures,

02:03:50.256 --> 02:03:51.157
snack size,

02:03:51.157 --> 02:03:52.558
standard four finger,

02:03:52.558 --> 02:03:53.859
the Big Kat.

02:03:53.859 --> 02:03:57.196
From there, we move up
to king size, which is,

02:03:57.196 --> 02:03:58.631
a piece accidentally broke off

02:03:58.631 --> 02:04:00.366
and then I accidentally ate it.

02:04:00.366 --> 02:04:02.001
The Big Kat king size.

02:04:02.001 --> 02:04:03.969
So it looks like it's just two Big Kats.

02:04:03.969 --> 02:04:06.672
And the biggest size, the XL.

02:04:09.642 --> 02:04:12.445
A bag of Kit Kat bites
should have 11 bites.

02:04:12.445 --> 02:04:14.380
Let's count in Japanese.

02:04:14.380 --> 02:04:17.016
Ichi, ni, san, shi, go,

02:04:17.016 --> 02:04:19.485
roku, shichi, hachi, ku, juu,

02:04:19.485 --> 02:04:20.920
juuichi.

02:04:20.920 --> 02:04:22.054
11 bites.

02:04:22.054 --> 02:04:23.689
And according to the bag,

02:04:23.689 --> 02:04:26.025
the combined weight should be 50 grams.

02:04:26.025 --> 02:04:28.160
So let's weigh all 11 bites.

02:04:28.160 --> 02:04:29.061
Ooh!

02:04:29.061 --> 02:04:31.730
It weighs 52 grams.

02:04:31.730 --> 02:04:33.032
Good deal.

02:04:33.032 --> 02:04:35.634
All of our US sizes come
in a variety of units,

02:04:35.634 --> 02:04:37.503
depending on your Kit Kat needs.

02:04:37.503 --> 02:04:38.637
So many varieties.

02:04:38.637 --> 02:04:39.939
Here's a few worth mentioning.

02:04:39.939 --> 02:04:42.875
The minis. The biggest
bag of minis unwrapped

02:04:42.875 --> 02:04:45.344
you can get is 419 grams.

02:04:45.344 --> 02:04:47.146
As the title implies,

02:04:47.146 --> 02:04:49.215
these things are unwrapped little bites.

02:04:49.215 --> 02:04:51.050
It's sold like it's for
sharing, but get real.

02:04:51.050 --> 02:04:53.452
Whoever sticks their hand in
here first, it's their bag.

02:04:53.452 --> 02:04:55.120
For the miniatures, according to Amazon,

02:04:55.120 --> 02:04:57.289
you can get up to 4-pound bags,

02:04:57.289 --> 02:05:02.261
aka 1,814.37 grams.

02:05:02.261 --> 02:05:04.663
And what it looks like, they just sent me

02:05:04.663 --> 02:05:08.901
a bag that's loosely 4
pounds of Kit Kat minis.

02:05:08.901 --> 02:05:11.270
All the bars have their various packs.

02:05:11.270 --> 02:05:12.605
None of them seem unusual.

02:05:12.605 --> 02:05:14.607
I will, however, mention that

02:05:14.607 --> 02:05:17.877
the biggest single purchase
of a Kit Kat item you can get

02:05:17.877 --> 02:05:20.112
is the king-size 24-pack.

02:05:20.112 --> 02:05:22.615
The total here is 2,040 grams,

02:05:22.615 --> 02:05:26.952
about 4.5 pounds of Kit Kat.

02:05:28.420 --> 02:05:31.390
Here's all the Kit Kats
exclusive to the US.

02:05:31.390 --> 02:05:34.260
And here is all the Kit
Kats native to Japan.

02:05:34.260 --> 02:05:36.629
Kit Kat in Japan is made by Nestlé

02:05:36.629 --> 02:05:39.365
and is one of the best-selling
candies in the country.

02:05:39.365 --> 02:05:41.166
One of the reasons for its popularity

02:05:41.166 --> 02:05:44.036
is that Kit Kat has a
good-luck charm in Japan

02:05:44.036 --> 02:05:47.840
because the name Kit Kat
in Japanese is Kitto Katto.

02:05:47.840 --> 02:05:50.676
And Kitto Katto sounds like "kitto katsu,"

02:05:50.676 --> 02:05:53.145
which means "you will surely win."

02:05:53.145 --> 02:05:56.315
So the Kit Kat brand became
associated with good luck.

02:05:56.315 --> 02:05:58.584
And these Kit Kats are
often given to students

02:05:58.584 --> 02:06:00.085
before their exams.

02:06:00.085 --> 02:06:01.453
For the past 20 years,

02:06:01.453 --> 02:06:04.990
Kit Kat has introduced more
than 350 unique flavors.

02:06:04.990 --> 02:06:05.824
Wow!

02:06:05.824 --> 02:06:08.394
Some of them are
discontinued, unfortunately,

02:06:08.394 --> 02:06:10.262
and some of them are regional,

02:06:10.262 --> 02:06:13.332
so we couldn't get them by
the filming of this episode.

02:06:13.332 --> 02:06:14.500
Gomen ne!

02:06:14.500 --> 02:06:18.270
So here are a few standard
Kit Kat flavors in Japan.

02:06:18.270 --> 02:06:19.672
Coffee break.

02:06:19.672 --> 02:06:21.607
But it doesn't taste like coffee,

02:06:21.607 --> 02:06:23.542
but goes well with coffee.

02:06:23.542 --> 02:06:25.744
So I brought my coffee with me today,

02:06:25.744 --> 02:06:27.546
so let's see how it goes.

02:06:27.546 --> 02:06:28.547
Itadakimasu.

02:06:33.285 --> 02:06:34.853
It's actually pretty good,

02:06:34.853 --> 02:06:36.555
much better than expected.

02:06:36.555 --> 02:06:38.223
So, next we have

02:06:38.223 --> 02:06:39.725
melon.

02:06:39.725 --> 02:06:40.859
Mm!

02:06:40.859 --> 02:06:42.194
It's so melon.

02:06:42.194 --> 02:06:44.229
It has way too strong melon flavor.

02:06:44.229 --> 02:06:47.333
Next, we have chocolate orange.

02:06:48.200 --> 02:06:49.535
Overall, not bad.

02:06:49.535 --> 02:06:51.136
Next, graham cracker.

02:06:52.638 --> 02:06:54.006
This is fantastic.

02:06:54.006 --> 02:06:55.674
Next, I'm gonna go

02:06:55.674 --> 02:06:56.909
cheesecake.

02:06:59.511 --> 02:07:01.447
This is marvelous.

02:07:01.447 --> 02:07:03.282
If you're a cheesecake person like me,

02:07:03.282 --> 02:07:04.917
you will definitely like this.

02:07:04.917 --> 02:07:06.885
Next, strawberry cheesecake.

02:07:08.253 --> 02:07:10.723
You get some decent strawberry flavor

02:07:10.723 --> 02:07:14.293
and cheesecake flavor at the
same time, which is amazing.

02:07:14.293 --> 02:07:16.161
Next, apple cinnamon.

02:07:18.097 --> 02:07:19.398
I'm not a big fan of this.

02:07:19.398 --> 02:07:20.933
There is a lot of cinnamon in it,

02:07:20.933 --> 02:07:22.901
which makes this horrible.

02:07:22.901 --> 02:07:23.902
Pistachio.

02:07:23.902 --> 02:07:26.271
Look at this cute squirrel!

02:07:26.271 --> 02:07:27.640
Kawaii ne!

02:07:27.640 --> 02:07:28.641
Kawaii!

02:07:29.808 --> 02:07:31.844
It's not great, but not horrible either.

02:07:31.844 --> 02:07:33.879
Next, pudding.

02:07:33.879 --> 02:07:35.114
Mm!

02:07:35.114 --> 02:07:37.549
Mm, it's disgusting.

02:07:37.549 --> 02:07:39.284
It's way too sweet.

02:07:39.284 --> 02:07:40.486
Let's go next one.

02:07:40.486 --> 02:07:42.087
We have strawberry milk.

02:07:43.322 --> 02:07:44.690
Ah!

02:07:44.690 --> 02:07:46.525
Holy crap.

02:07:46.525 --> 02:07:48.327
This is nasty.

02:07:48.327 --> 02:07:50.496
This is the worst one.

02:07:50.496 --> 02:07:51.964
So, this is the last one.

02:07:51.964 --> 02:07:53.565
I've got cookies and cream.

02:07:55.334 --> 02:07:59.104
This is the best thing I
have ever had in my mouth.

02:07:59.104 --> 02:08:00.239
Sorry to interrupt.

02:08:00.239 --> 02:08:01.073
But believe it or not,

02:08:01.073 --> 02:08:03.275
the US does have a few exclusive flavors

02:08:03.275 --> 02:08:04.376
