Nothing's glowing.

02:09:04.470 --> 02:09:06.004
All right. Lights back on.

02:09:06.004 --> 02:09:07.740
It's a regular Kit Kat.

02:09:07.740 --> 02:09:08.874
This is regular. How
disappointing is that?

02:09:08.874 --> 02:09:10.743
Thumbs down.

02:09:10.743 --> 02:09:11.977
Birthday cake.

02:09:13.245 --> 02:09:14.947
Close to a frosting and sprinkles flavor.

02:09:14.947 --> 02:09:16.248
Man, these are all really good.

02:09:16.248 --> 02:09:20.285
Also in the US, you can
get a lemon crisp flavor.

02:09:20.285 --> 02:09:21.687
Sold out everywhere.

02:09:21.687 --> 02:09:23.522
It was like a Supreme drop.

02:09:23.522 --> 02:09:25.657
The second those hit the
shelves, they were are gone.

02:09:25.657 --> 02:09:29.194
Also Kit Kat in the US
has this line called Duos.

02:09:29.194 --> 02:09:31.630
As you can see, three different flavors,

02:09:31.630 --> 02:09:32.631
two flavors in one.

02:09:32.631 --> 02:09:35.200
We got mint and dark chocolate.

02:09:38.137 --> 02:09:39.371
Mocha and chocolate.

02:09:39.371 --> 02:09:40.806
Eh, I'm already,

02:09:40.806 --> 02:09:42.474
I'm not predicting this is
going to be anything special.

02:09:43.876 --> 02:09:44.710
It's just OK.

02:09:44.710 --> 02:09:46.945
Strawberry and dark chocolate.

02:09:46.945 --> 02:09:48.447
Is the way I'm eating these annoying?

02:09:50.682 --> 02:09:52.184
I mean, it's not terrible, but.

02:09:52.184 --> 02:09:53.685
Maybe strawberry and chocolate
would've been too sweet,

02:09:53.685 --> 02:09:55.487
but with the dark chocolate,
I'm just not into it.

02:09:55.487 --> 02:09:57.623
So these were fun, right? These were fun?

02:09:57.623 --> 02:09:58.657
No?

02:09:58.657 --> 02:09:59.958
All right, back to Japan.

02:09:59.958 --> 02:10:01.827
Kit Kat has a collection of flavors

02:10:01.827 --> 02:10:05.531
inspired by the many regions
and prefectures of Japan.

02:10:05.531 --> 02:10:08.300
So I'm going to start
with this, Mount Fuji,

02:10:08.300 --> 02:10:10.536
the highest mountain in Japan.

02:10:10.536 --> 02:10:14.006
It's 3,776 meters high.

02:10:14.006 --> 02:10:17.843
And the flavor is
strawberry-cheesecake flavor.

02:10:17.843 --> 02:10:19.278
How can I open this?

02:10:20.312 --> 02:10:21.346
Here we go.

02:10:21.346 --> 02:10:22.447
It looks great.

02:10:24.283 --> 02:10:25.484
It's pretty good.

02:10:25.484 --> 02:10:27.352
But it tastes exactly the same

02:10:27.352 --> 02:10:29.388
as that one that I tasted 10 minutes ago.

02:10:30.522 --> 02:10:34.426
All right, next one is this Shinshu apple.

02:10:34.426 --> 02:10:36.028
Shinshu is kind of very old way

02:10:36.028 --> 02:10:37.963
to call Nagano Prefecture.

02:10:37.963 --> 02:10:41.266
And Nagano Prefecture is
located in the center of Japan

02:10:41.266 --> 02:10:43.735
and is famous for delicious apples.

02:10:43.735 --> 02:10:46.572
And, finally, they turn into Kit Kat.

02:10:48.707 --> 02:10:49.575
Ooh.

02:10:49.575 --> 02:10:52.811
This is the nicest
chocolate I've ever had.

02:10:52.811 --> 02:10:55.447
Next, we have Amaou strawberry.

02:10:55.447 --> 02:10:57.950
So it's basically from Kyushu.

02:10:57.950 --> 02:11:00.485
Kyushu is Japan's third-largest island

02:11:00.485 --> 02:11:02.821
and is located southwest of Japan.

02:11:02.821 --> 02:11:06.525
And Amaou is the best brand
of strawberries in Japan.

02:11:09.194 --> 02:11:10.762
Marvelous, again.

02:11:10.762 --> 02:11:13.398
Next, I'm going to go with this one.

02:11:13.398 --> 02:11:15.834
Ito Kyuemon Uji matcha

02:11:15.834 --> 02:11:18.470
and Ito Kyuemon Uji hojicha.

02:11:18.470 --> 02:11:21.874
Uji matcha and Uji hojicha
are named after Uji city,

02:11:21.874 --> 02:11:23.208
where they're grown.

02:11:23.208 --> 02:11:25.844
And the difference between
matcha and hojicha is

02:11:25.844 --> 02:11:26.979
matcha is matcha, right?

02:11:26.979 --> 02:11:28.480
Matcha is a green tea.

02:11:28.480 --> 02:11:31.283
But hojicha is a roasted green tea.

02:11:31.283 --> 02:11:33.218
Let's go with Uji matcha first.

02:11:34.820 --> 02:11:35.821
Whoo!

02:11:35.821 --> 02:11:38.357
Matcha is always perfect.

02:11:38.357 --> 02:11:39.258
How about hojicha?

02:11:40.359 --> 02:11:42.194
It's as beautiful as my heart.

02:11:42.194 --> 02:11:43.962
Let's move on to the next one.

02:11:43.962 --> 02:11:45.931
We have beni imo.

02:11:45.931 --> 02:11:48.634
Beni imo, which is purple sweet potato.

02:11:48.634 --> 02:11:50.135
It's from Okinawa.

02:11:50.135 --> 02:11:53.305
So, Okinawa is Japan's
southernmost prefecture

02:11:53.305 --> 02:11:55.240
and is famous for beni imo.

02:11:55.240 --> 02:11:57.342
Okinawa is my favorite place in Japan.

02:11:59.778 --> 02:12:00.779
I love this.

02:12:00.779 --> 02:12:02.414
It has just right sweetness.

02:12:02.414 --> 02:12:06.385
We've got azuki sandwich
flavor from Nagoya.

02:12:06.385 --> 02:12:09.922
So, Nagoya is located in
between Tokyo and Osaka

02:12:09.922 --> 02:12:13.225
and is famous for its azuki sandwich.

02:12:13.225 --> 02:12:15.460
Azuki is sweet red bean paste.

02:12:15.460 --> 02:12:17.462
So sweet red bean paste sandwich.

02:12:18.597 --> 02:12:19.531
Oh.

02:12:19.531 --> 02:12:20.999
It's not my taste at all.

02:12:20.999 --> 02:12:23.035
Momiji manju flavor.

02:12:23.035 --> 02:12:25.203
It's from Hiroshima.

02:12:25.203 --> 02:12:28.373
So, Hiroshima is located
in the southwest of Japan

02:12:28.373 --> 02:12:31.009
and is famous for its momiji manju,

02:12:31.009 --> 02:12:33.879
which is kind of maple-leaf-shaped cake

02:12:33.879 --> 02:12:35.847
filled with sweet bean paste.

02:12:37.182 --> 02:12:39.217
It tastes exactly the same as this one.

02:12:39.217 --> 02:12:41.019
Sweet red bean paste.

02:12:41.019 --> 02:12:44.022
Japanese people love sweet red bean paste.

02:12:44.022 --> 02:12:47.292
Hokkaido azuki and strawberry flavor.

02:12:47.292 --> 02:12:48.860
Hokkaido is the largest

02:12:48.860 --> 02:12:50.996
and northernmost prefecture in Japan

02:12:50.996 --> 02:12:53.932
and is famous for its azuki.

02:12:54.866 --> 02:12:57.936
Much better than the other azuki flavors.

02:12:58.870 --> 02:13:00.305
Why wasabi?

02:13:00.305 --> 02:13:02.040
And it's from Shizuoka,

02:13:02.040 --> 02:13:05.344
and Shizuoka is located
along the Pacific coast

02:13:05.344 --> 02:13:08.513
and is the top wasabi-producing
region in Japan.

02:13:12.284 --> 02:13:15.187
Believe it or not, it's
actually pretty good.

02:13:15.187 --> 02:13:16.488
Let's go! This one!

02:13:16.488 --> 02:13:19.858
Strawberry cheesecake flavor again.

02:13:19.858 --> 02:13:21.560
It's from Yokohama.

02:13:21.560 --> 02:13:24.396
Yokohama is located next to Tokyo,

02:13:24.396 --> 02:13:27.432
but Yokohama is not famous
for strawberry cheesecake.

02:13:27.432 --> 02:13:28.533
I don't know why they chose

02:13:28.533 --> 02:13:31.403
strawberry-cheesecake flavor for this.

02:13:31.403 --> 02:13:33.238
It tastes exactly the same.

02:13:33.238 --> 02:13:34.206
Same!

02:13:34.206 --> 02:13:36.675
Next we have Tokyo banana.

02:13:36.675 --> 02:13:39.244
So, Tokyo banana is a banana-shaped

02:13:39.244 --> 02:13:42.114
sponge cake with cream filling,

02:13:42.114 --> 02:13:44.750
and it is very popular souvenir of Tokyo.

02:13:44.750 --> 02:13:48.053
And they turn into Kit Kats.

02:13:48.053 --> 02:13:50.288
Ta-da! Ooh!

02:13:52.824 --> 02:13:53.658
It's gross.

02:13:53.658 --> 02:13:56.294
When you come to Tokyo, you
should try Tokyo bananas,

02:13:56.294 --> 02:13:59.398
but you should not try
Tokyo banana Kit Kats.

02:13:59.398 --> 02:14:01.333
Rum raisin.

02:14:01.333 --> 02:14:03.101
It's from Tokyo.

02:14:03.101 --> 02:14:05.404
Tokyo is not famous for rum raisin.

02:14:05.404 --> 02:14:08.040
But it says, "Rum raisin's gorgeousness

02:14:08.040 --> 02:14:11.043
and fanciness matches the image of Tokyo."

02:14:17.082 --> 02:14:19.084
There is a shot of rum.

02:14:19.084 --> 02:14:19.918
I don't like it!

02:14:19.918 --> 02:14:21.787
It contains a lot of alcohol.

02:14:21.787 --> 02:14:23.121
Ooh.

02:14:23.121 --> 02:14:24.389
Nande?

02:14:24.389 --> 02:14:25.223
Last one!

02:14:25.223 --> 02:14:26.625
Sake flavor,

02:14:26.625 --> 02:14:30.095
which is a Japanese traditional
alcohol made from rice.

02:14:30.095 --> 02:14:31.730
This is a really interesting one.

02:14:33.298 --> 02:14:34.566
Oh.

02:14:34.566 --> 02:14:35.801
Personally, I like it.

02:14:35.801 --> 02:14:38.303
And this is an acquired taste.

02:14:38.303 --> 02:14:40.338
So, when it comes to sake flavor,

02:14:40.338 --> 02:14:44.276
we were supposed to have
yogurt sake, yuzu sake,

02:14:44.276 --> 02:14:47.179
limited-edition Japan sake umeshu,

02:14:47.179 --> 02:14:50.115
but these were not available
at the time of filming this.

02:14:50.115 --> 02:14:53.385
And we have Kit Kat desserts.

02:14:53.385 --> 02:14:55.120
We have Kit Kat Colliders,

02:14:55.120 --> 02:14:56.555
which I could not find
at the filming of this,

02:14:56.555 --> 02:14:59.157
but it looks to be almost
like vanilla-flavored cups

02:14:59.157 --> 02:15:02.094
with Kit Kat chunks broken up in it.

02:15:02.094 --> 02:15:04.629
Oh, man, I ate too many Kit Kats.

02:15:04.629 --> 02:15:06.331
And then we have these.

02:15:06.331 --> 02:15:08.867
These Kit Kat ice cream cones.

02:15:09.968 --> 02:15:10.802
Eh.

02:15:10.802 --> 02:15:13.205
I hit a wall real hard.

02:15:13.205 --> 02:15:16.908
I hit a giant Kit Kat XL wall,

02:15:16.908 --> 02:15:19.311
and I officially do not
want to do this anymore.

02:15:20.378 --> 02:15:22.180
Better, but not by much more.

02:15:22.180 --> 02:15:24.282
Yeah, so that's it for the US.

02:15:24.282 --> 02:15:26.118
Sorry we have so few flavors.

02:15:26.118 --> 02:15:28.954
Japan has a Kit Kat called Otona no Amasa,

02:15:28.954 --> 02:15:32.858
which translates to
"sweetness for adults."

02:15:32.858 --> 02:15:35.961
Ow! R-rated!

02:15:35.961 --> 02:15:38.396
Don't let your kids watch this part!

02:15:38.396 --> 02:15:40.699
All right, so it's a
line of Kit Kat flavors

02:15:40.699 --> 02:15:41.967
that are a little more bitter

02:15:41.967 --> 02:15:44.069
and less sweet than regular Kit Kats.

02:15:44.069 --> 02:15:47.506
So, here we have Otona
no Amasa strawberry,

02:15:47.506 --> 02:15:48.940
white,

02:15:48.940 --> 02:15:51.009
and dark matcha

02:15:51.009 --> 02:15:52.544
and dark chocolate.

02:15:52.544 --> 02:15:53.645
All right, so let's give it a try.

02:15:53.645 --> 02:15:54.479
First.

02:15:54.479 --> 02:15:56.414
This is just straight-up dark chocolate,

02:15:56.414 --> 02:15:57.249
as you can imagine.

02:15:57.249 --> 02:15:58.650
Strawberry.

02:15:59.718 --> 02:16:01.953
Ooh, it's actually tart.

02:16:01.953 --> 02:16:02.787
This is good.

02:16:02.787 --> 02:16:04.422
All right, so let's
move on to the next one.

02:16:04.422 --> 02:16:06.258
We've got dark matcha.

02:16:06.258 --> 02:16:07.759
Mm.

02:16:07.759 --> 02:16:09.461
This is so deep.

02:16:09.461 --> 02:16:12.397
Much deeper than the other matcha flavors.

02:16:12.397 --> 02:16:16.668
So, last one, we've got Otona
no Amasa white chocolate.

02:16:18.069 --> 02:16:19.738
This is the best one

02:16:19.738 --> 02:16:22.307
among these Otona no Amasa chocolates.

02:16:22.307 --> 02:16:24.709
Just right sweetness.

02:16:24.709 --> 02:16:28.813
All right, so let's do matcha taste test.

02:16:28.813 --> 02:16:32.584
In Japan, matcha-flavored
Kit Kats are so popular.

02:16:32.584 --> 02:16:35.854
Over the years, we've
introduced 13 different,

02:16:35.854 --> 02:16:38.190
different, different,
different matcha flavors.

02:16:38.190 --> 02:16:41.426
But currently, we were only
able to get these three.

02:16:41.426 --> 02:16:43.929
So let's see how different they are.

02:16:43.929 --> 02:16:45.430
First, dark matcha.

02:16:46.264 --> 02:16:47.832
Deep matcha.

02:16:48.867 --> 02:16:49.834
But it's also deep.

02:16:49.834 --> 02:16:52.003
Ito Kyuemon Uji matcha.

02:16:52.871 --> 02:16:55.674
So freaking hard to tell the difference.

02:16:55.674 --> 02:16:59.177
But I'd say this one is
the most delicious one.

02:16:59.177 --> 02:17:00.645
Kyoto.

02:17:00.645 --> 02:17:03.848
You can get it in Kyoto or order online.

02:17:03.848 --> 02:17:07.586
So, here we have classy
chocolates called Sublime.

02:17:07.586 --> 02:17:10.055
So we have white Sublime

02:17:10.055 --> 02:17:12.090
and raw milk Sublime

02:17:12.090 --> 02:17:14.526
and a volcanic green Sublime

02:17:14.526 --> 02:17:17.195
and orange volcanic Sublime,

02:17:17.195 --> 02:17:18.096
yellow,

02:17:18.096 --> 02:17:19.397
ruby Sublime.

02:17:19.397 --> 02:17:21.166
All right, so let's try some out.

02:17:21.166 --> 02:17:23.668
I'm getting sick of the sweetness.

02:17:23.668 --> 02:17:24.736
Itadakimasu.

02:17:28.607 --> 02:17:30.108
It doesn't taste anything!

02:17:30.108 --> 02:17:32.577
I was thinking that it'd
taste like strawberry

02:17:32.577 --> 02:17:34.379
or raspberry or something, but.

02:17:35.914 --> 02:17:37.115
Did I get COVID?

02:17:37.115 --> 02:17:38.416
COVID-19?

02:17:38.416 --> 02:17:39.985
OK, let's keep going.

02:17:39.985 --> 02:17:42.487
All right, so I'm going
to go yellow volcanic.

02:17:42.487 --> 02:17:44.723
Volcano! Pew!

02:17:46.091 --> 02:17:47.259
Ooh!

02:17:47.259 --> 02:17:49.327
This is the bitterest.

02:17:49.327 --> 02:17:51.062
I've got orange.

02:17:54.499 --> 02:17:55.800
Bitter.

02:17:55.800 --> 02:17:56.968
Now I'm so scared.

02:17:56.968 --> 02:17:58.703
Green Sublime.

02:18:00.405 --> 02:18:04.175
It tastes exactly same
as these two. So bitter.

02:18:04.175 --> 02:18:06.745
Next we have milk Sublime.

02:18:08.246 --> 02:18:11.316
It tastes exactly the
same as regular flavor.

02:18:11.316 --> 02:18:12.550
I prefer this one.

02:18:12.550 --> 02:18:14.853
Last one, I've got white Sublime.

02:18:17.555 --> 02:18:21.159
Compared to the Otona no
Amasa white chocolate,

02:18:21.159 --> 02:18:22.294
it's much better.

02:18:22.294 --> 02:18:23.128
I'm done.

02:18:24.262 --> 02:18:25.263
Hey, guys, it's Harry.

02:18:25.263 --> 02:18:26.865
I can't let you do a Kit
Kat episode without me,

02:18:26.865 --> 02:18:29.934
because Kit Kats were actually
invented in the UK in 1935.

02:18:29.934 --> 02:18:31.670
They would eventually
be distributed by Nestlé

02:18:31.670 --> 02:18:33.838
across the UK, the EU, and Japan.

02:18:33.838 --> 02:18:35.173
But in the US, Kit Kats are made

02:18:35.173 --> 02:18:36.708
and distributed by Hershey's.

02:18:36.708 --> 02:18:38.176
If you watched our Snickers episode,

02:18:38.176 --> 02:18:39.944
you'll know that there are
some major taste differences

02:18:39.944 --> 02:18:42.013
between the chocolate
in the UK and the US.

02:18:42.013 --> 02:18:43.915
Mostly that the UK's is way better.

02:18:43.915 --> 02:18:45.083
I'm going to do a three-way taste test

02:18:45.083 --> 02:18:47.819
between UK, US, and
also a Japanese Kit Kat

02:18:47.819 --> 02:18:49.854
to see if there's any major
differences between the three.

02:18:49.854 --> 02:18:52.757
And, Harry, thank you for sending me this

02:18:52.757 --> 02:18:54.392
with your cute handwriting.

02:18:54.392 --> 02:18:56.528
Thank you, Harry! Arigato.

02:18:56.528 --> 02:18:58.663
Let's try UK Kit Kat first.

02:19:00.999 --> 02:19:02.734
The UK one is obviously
the one I'm used to.

02:19:02.734 --> 02:19:04.102
The chocolate is very smooth,

02:19:04.102 --> 02:19:06.604
not overwhelmingly sweet,
and just very tasty.

02:19:06.604 --> 02:19:08.573
The UK is already a lot richer.

02:19:10.942 --> 02:19:12.077
OK, OK.

02:19:12.077 --> 02:19:13.678
Can I try US Kit Kat?

02:19:13.678 --> 02:19:14.546
I also couldn't find

02:19:14.546 --> 02:19:16.214
just a standard American Kit Kat anywhere.

02:19:16.214 --> 02:19:18.483
I guess we didn't bother
importing the regular one.

02:19:18.483 --> 02:19:19.551
The closest thing I could find

02:19:19.551 --> 02:19:21.853
was this Kit Kat Duos
mocha and chocolate one.

02:19:24.189 --> 02:19:26.391
Something doesn't taste
quite right about that.

02:19:26.391 --> 02:19:27.225
Yep.

02:19:27.225 --> 02:19:29.094
UK, US,

02:19:29.094 --> 02:19:30.428
they suck.

02:19:30.428 --> 02:19:32.931
They both have too much sugar.

02:19:32.931 --> 02:19:35.767
Joe, Harry, try Japan's Kit Kat.

02:19:36.901 --> 02:19:37.736
Mm.

02:19:37.736 --> 02:19:39.337
Much smoother. Creamier.

02:19:39.337 --> 02:19:40.338
In terms of picking a favorite,

02:19:40.338 --> 02:19:42.540
I think the US one gets
discounted immediately.

02:19:42.540 --> 02:19:44.109
Then, between the UK and the Japan one,

02:19:44.109 --> 02:19:46.411
it's kind of a different
style of Kit Kat, I guess.

02:19:46.411 --> 02:19:48.413
I would say Japan and UK
are pretty neck and neck.

02:19:48.413 --> 02:19:49.414
They seem very similar.

02:19:49.414 --> 02:19:52.517
Japan's Kit Kat is the best in the world.

02:19:52.517 --> 02:19:54.419
Ugh, I've eaten too much candy.

02:19:54.419 --> 02:19:55.520
Ugh!

02:19:55.520 --> 02:19:57.255
Perhaps we can pinpoint
the taste difference

02:19:57.255 --> 02:19:58.089
to the ingredients.

02:19:58.089 --> 02:19:59.758
In the US, a Kit Kat is made up of

02:19:59.758 --> 02:20:01.292
sugar, wheat flour --

02:20:01.292 --> 02:20:02.127
[beep]

02:20:04.028 --> 02:20:04.863
[beep]

02:20:04.863 --> 02:20:06.731
Our Kit Kats have the following.

02:20:08.733 --> 02:20:09.834
Looking over the ingredients,

02:20:09.834 --> 02:20:12.303
I noticed our Kit Kats have
cocoa butter and chocolate,

02:20:12.303 --> 02:20:13.638
although it does not specify

02:20:13.638 --> 02:20:15.173
what that chocolate is made up of.

02:20:15.173 --> 02:20:16.341
Do we assume it is the same

02:20:16.341 --> 02:20:17.575
as the Hershey's chocolate bar?

02:20:17.575 --> 02:20:18.410
I don't know.

02:20:18.410 --> 02:20:20.645
Whereas the Japan Kit Kat has cocoa mass,

02:20:20.645 --> 02:20:23.448
cocoa butter, and cocoa powder.

02:20:23.448 --> 02:20:25.850
Now, if we're to believe
that Nestlé in Japan

02:20:25.850 --> 02:20:27.352
holds their chocolate
to the same standards

02:20:27.352 --> 02:20:28.720
they do in the UK, it would mean

02:20:28.720 --> 02:20:31.156
that it would have a higher
fat and cocoa content.

02:20:31.156 --> 02:20:33.024
According to the UK rules,

02:20:33.024 --> 02:20:36.094
"a product must contain no
less than 25% cocoa solids

02:20:36.094 --> 02:20:38.196
to be considered 'milk chocolate.'"

02:20:38.196 --> 02:20:40.598
The US definitely does
not go by this rule.

02:20:40.598 --> 02:20:42.667
Our Kit Kat is made up of palm oil,

02:20:42.667 --> 02:20:45.003
where theirs is vegetable
oil. Same in the UK.

02:20:45.003 --> 02:20:47.372
It is cheaper, but it's also
worse on the environment,

02:20:47.372 --> 02:20:48.706
adding to deforestation,

02:20:48.706 --> 02:20:50.175
increasing greenhouse [gas] emissions,

02:20:50.175 --> 02:20:51.643
and water pollution.

02:20:51.643 --> 02:20:54.479
So it is bad on the
environment and tastes worse.

02:20:54.479 --> 02:20:55.613
Fantastic.

02:20:55.613 --> 02:20:58.049
But good news for all you vegans,

02:20:58.049 --> 02:21:00.518
Nestlé has created a vegan Kit Kat,

02:21:00.518 --> 02:21:04.255
with substituted milk with
a rice-based alternative,

02:21:04.255 --> 02:21:06.591
but availability is currently limited,

02:21:06.591 --> 02:21:09.527
so they are not available
in the US or Japan.

02:21:11.529 --> 02:21:13.598
This is a US Kit Kat miniature,

02:21:13.598 --> 02:21:15.500
and it is 8.5 grams.

02:21:15.500 --> 02:21:17.635
It's the closest size
we had to Japan's mini.

02:21:17.635 --> 02:21:19.270
This is 42 calories,

02:21:19.270 --> 02:21:20.939
2.2 grams of fat,

02:21:20.939 --> 02:21:22.540
6 milligrams of sodium,

02:21:22.540 --> 02:21:24.108
5.8 grams of carbs,

02:21:24.108 --> 02:21:25.610
4 of those are sugar,

02:21:25.610 --> 02:21:27.612
and 1 gram of protein.

02:21:27.612 --> 02:21:30.515
In Japan, the mini is
the most popular size.

02:21:30.515 --> 02:21:32.350
It's 62 calories

02:21:32.350 --> 02:21:34.452
and 3.5 grams of fat,

02:21:34.452 --> 02:21:38.022
3.5 to 11.4 milligrams of sodium,

02:21:38.022 --> 02:21:41.960
8.99 to 19.4 grams of total carbs,

02:21:41.960 --> 02:21:44.696
and 0.9 grams of protein.

02:21:44.696 --> 02:21:46.965
The most common Kit Kat size in the US

02:21:46.965 --> 02:21:48.633
is the four-finger bar.

02:21:48.633 --> 02:21:50.235
210 calories,

02:21:50.235 --> 02:21:51.269
11 grams of fat,

02:21:51.269 --> 02:21:52.570
7 of those are saturated,

02:21:52.570 --> 02:21:54.372
20 milligrams of sodium,

02:21:54.372 --> 02:21:55.673
28 grams of carbs,

02:21:55.673 --> 02:21:57.342
23 of those are sugar,

02:21:57.342 --> 02:21:58.776
and 2 grams of protein.

02:21:58.776 --> 02:22:01.079
The closest size we have to that in Japan

02:22:01.079 --> 02:22:02.514
is the Kit Kat bar.

02:22:02.514 --> 02:22:05.216
It contains 224 calories.

02:22:05.216 --> 02:22:07.118
The most caloried Kit Kat in the US we got

02:22:07.118 --> 02:22:08.686
is the Kit Kat XL.

02:22:08.686 --> 02:22:10.255
Now, I unwrapped it here so you could see

02:22:10.255 --> 02:22:11.456
just how big it is.

02:22:11.456 --> 02:22:13.725
It contains 640 calories.

02:22:13.725 --> 02:22:16.928
The most calories you will
get in a Kit Kat in Japan

02:22:16.928 --> 02:22:18.663
is the big little pouch bite.

02:22:18.663 --> 02:22:21.566
This bag is 275 calories.

02:22:21.966 --> 02:22:24.102
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

02:22:24.102 --> 02:22:25.904
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:22:25.904 --> 02:22:28.640
between Burger King in Japan and the US.

02:22:28.640 --> 02:22:30.575
This is "Food Wars."

02:22:35.580 --> 02:22:37.782
Here's everything you can find on the menu

02:22:37.782 --> 02:22:41.052
at the Burger King in
Japan but not in the US.

02:22:41.052 --> 02:22:44.088
Here's everything you can
find at a US Burger King

02:22:44.088 --> 02:22:45.957
you cannot get in Japan.

02:22:45.957 --> 02:22:49.661
All right, so let's start
with exclusive burgers.

02:22:49.661 --> 02:22:53.131
So, here we have teriyaki lettuce burger

02:22:53.131 --> 02:22:55.233
and teriyaki Whopper.

02:22:55.233 --> 02:22:57.302
Ooh!

02:22:57.302 --> 02:22:58.903
Huge.

02:22:58.903 --> 02:23:02.807
Next we have avocado salad burger

02:23:02.807 --> 02:23:04.509
and avocado Whopper.

02:23:04.509 --> 02:23:08.413
Aah, a little cute baby.

02:23:08.413 --> 02:23:09.747
Look at this.

02:23:09.747 --> 02:23:12.984
And Whopper.

02:23:14.986 --> 02:23:17.322
It's totally different.

02:23:17.322 --> 02:23:19.357
This one is so huge.

02:23:19.357 --> 02:23:21.526
And avocados, tomato,

02:23:21.526 --> 02:23:23.061
no tomatoes.

02:23:23.061 --> 02:23:24.262
I don't know why.

02:23:24.262 --> 02:23:27.966
Next we have quattro cheese Whopper.

02:23:27.966 --> 02:23:31.336
Oh, big boy.

02:23:32.470 --> 02:23:35.306
We've got smoky barbecue Whopper

02:23:35.306 --> 02:23:38.309
and smoky barbecue Whopper junior.

02:23:38.309 --> 02:23:41.613
And here is spicy Whopper.

02:23:44.983 --> 02:23:46.451
Ooh!

02:23:46.451 --> 02:23:47.485
It's hot sauce.

02:23:48.820 --> 02:23:52.256
Next, we have tartar chicken burger.

02:23:52.256 --> 02:23:55.093
Ooh, it's got

02:23:55.093 --> 02:23:57.462
a lot of tartar sauce,

02:23:57.462 --> 02:23:59.797
chicken, crispy.

02:23:59.797 --> 02:24:02.467
Burger King in Japan just
released a brand-new burger

02:24:02.467 --> 02:24:04.802
called Guilty Burger.

02:24:04.802 --> 02:24:07.438
It's basically butter burger.

02:24:07.438 --> 02:24:08.339
Why?

02:24:08.339 --> 02:24:10.041
What have you done?

02:24:10.041 --> 02:24:14.312
Let's check out this Guilty
butter beef burger first.

02:24:14.312 --> 02:24:15.747
The bun is different.

02:24:15.747 --> 02:24:17.815
Itadakimasu!

02:24:20.284 --> 02:24:22.654
Just a little bit of butter flavor,

02:24:22.654 --> 02:24:25.890
but I don't feel as guilty as it claims.

02:24:25.890 --> 02:24:29.027
This one is Guilty butter
croquette sandwich.

02:24:29.027 --> 02:24:31.029
Ooh.

02:24:32.030 --> 02:24:33.531
Guilty!

02:24:35.566 --> 02:24:39.937
And here is Guilty butter chicken burger.

02:24:41.005 --> 02:24:43.508
First one is something
that BK has exclu --

02:24:43.508 --> 02:24:45.410
oh, my God.

02:24:45.410 --> 02:24:47.445
This is called the Texas Whopper.

02:24:49.347 --> 02:24:51.849
Look at the size of this f---ing thing.

02:24:53.584 --> 02:24:56.721
Two patties, cheese,
bacon, bunch of veggies.

02:24:56.721 --> 02:24:57.922
Wait for it!

02:25:01.492 --> 02:25:03.127
The triple Whopper.

02:25:03.127 --> 02:25:05.863
Look at the size of this thing.

02:25:05.863 --> 02:25:09.567
The weight of it has completely
flattened the bottom bun.

02:25:09.567 --> 02:25:12.970
And there's nothing between
the patties of meat!

02:25:14.072 --> 02:25:16.507
What the hell are you
guys doing over there?

02:25:16.507 --> 02:25:17.842
Next.

02:25:17.842 --> 02:25:19.143
Oh, the Bacon King.

02:25:19.143 --> 02:25:20.445
Oh, my God.

02:25:20.445 --> 02:25:23.781
Looks to be pretty bacon centric.

02:25:23.781 --> 02:25:25.083
Looks like a double Whopper with cheese,

02:25:25.083 --> 02:25:27.351
bacon, mayo, ketchup, mustard.

02:25:27.351 --> 02:25:29.487
They didn't mess with
the veggies. Thank you.

02:25:29.487 --> 02:25:30.521
You're not fooling anyone

02:25:30.521 --> 02:25:32.256
getting lettuce and onion on that one.

02:25:32.256 --> 02:25:35.626
The rodeo burger is a
little guy with onion rings.

02:25:35.626 --> 02:25:37.962
The rodeo burger. Yeehaw.

02:25:37.962 --> 02:25:39.497
On to the chicken.

02:25:39.497 --> 02:25:40.531
I'll just put this over here.

02:25:40.531 --> 02:25:41.966
Japan does not have

02:25:41.966 --> 02:25:44.535
what we call the original
chicken sandwich.

02:25:44.535 --> 02:25:46.204
And I don't know why Burger King,

02:25:46.204 --> 02:25:47.739
maybe just to set itself apart,

02:25:47.739 --> 02:25:50.007
the chicken sandwich is
this, like, sub shape.

02:25:50.007 --> 02:25:51.542
It's like I'm holding the phone.

02:25:51.542 --> 02:25:52.410
This is great.

02:25:52.410 --> 02:25:54.412
Chicken junior, spicy chicken junior.

02:25:54.412 --> 02:25:55.246
Let's go spicy.

02:25:58.950 --> 02:26:00.318
Barely registers in the spice meter.

02:26:00.318 --> 02:26:01.352
Wait!

02:26:01.352 --> 02:26:02.186
Yeah.

02:26:02.186 --> 02:26:05.256
BKs in the US have something
called the Ch'King sandwich.

02:26:05.256 --> 02:26:07.091
You can get the sandwich
regular or deluxe.

02:26:07.091 --> 02:26:10.228
You can also get the sandwich
flavor regular or spicy.

02:26:10.228 --> 02:26:14.165
So here is the regular regular.

02:26:14.165 --> 02:26:15.199
And as you can see,

02:26:15.199 --> 02:26:17.735
just comes with sauce and
pickles and the chicken.

02:26:17.735 --> 02:26:19.904
You can get it deluxe and spicy,

02:26:19.904 --> 02:26:21.973
so we went with deluxe,
comes with all these veggies

02:26:21.973 --> 02:26:24.942
that you brush off right
when you start eating it,

02:26:24.942 --> 02:26:29.280
and it has got a spicy kind
of hue to the chicken there.

02:26:29.280 --> 02:26:31.549
Here's our side menu.

02:26:31.549 --> 02:26:33.351
Let's start with this one.

02:26:33.351 --> 02:26:35.419
We've got hot dog.

02:26:35.419 --> 02:26:37.989
It's got such a big sausage.

02:26:40.958 --> 02:26:43.361
This one is chili beans hot dog.

02:26:44.862 --> 02:26:48.232
And next we have this little guy,

02:26:48.232 --> 02:26:50.201
snack chicken.

02:26:50.201 --> 02:26:53.538
And last we have this one,

02:26:53.538 --> 02:26:56.107
chili cheese fries.

02:26:56.107 --> 02:27:00.044
And if you want some veggies,
you can order Caesar salad.

02:27:00.044 --> 02:27:03.214
But my bad, I forgot to order.

02:27:03.214 --> 02:27:06.250
Also exclusives to the US
are these, chicken fries.

02:27:06.250 --> 02:27:07.652
As you can tell, they look like fries,

02:27:07.652 --> 02:27:09.420
but they're pieces of chicken.

02:27:09.420 --> 02:27:10.755
Not bad.

02:27:10.755 --> 02:27:13.157
You can get Mott's applesauce.

02:27:13.157 --> 02:27:14.959
Jalapeño cheddar bites.

02:27:14.959 --> 02:27:16.227
I've never heard of these.

02:27:18.830 --> 02:27:20.431
And now I know why.

02:27:20.431 --> 02:27:24.135
Burger King in the US has
two iced-coffee flavors,

02:27:24.135 --> 02:27:25.469
mocha and vanilla.

02:27:25.469 --> 02:27:26.971
Assuming that's the mocha.

02:27:30.441 --> 02:27:32.009
Tastes exactly like chocolate milk.

02:27:32.009 --> 02:27:32.844
Blech! No.

02:27:32.844 --> 02:27:34.312
Oh, the aftertaste is horrible.

02:27:34.312 --> 02:27:35.346
What the hell?

02:27:35.346 --> 02:27:36.881
That's ridiculous how bad that is.

02:27:36.881 --> 02:27:38.883
And the vanilla.

02:27:41.118 --> 02:27:43.254
That is so sweet.

02:27:43.254 --> 02:27:44.455
I'm gonna keep this one.

02:27:45.356 --> 02:27:47.592
So, here is our dessert menus.

02:27:47.592 --> 02:27:50.061
Here we have coffee float.

02:27:50.061 --> 02:27:51.829
A little bit melting, sorry.

02:27:51.829 --> 02:27:54.832
And we have melon soda float.

02:27:54.832 --> 02:27:58.135
Coke float and Coke Zero float.

02:27:58.135 --> 02:28:03.007
And here we've got premium
sundae chocolate and coffee.

02:28:03.007 --> 02:28:05.877
And here is our chocolate sundae

02:28:05.877 --> 02:28:07.678
and strawberry sundae.

02:28:07.678 --> 02:28:11.182
And my favorite is this apple pie.

02:28:15.353 --> 02:28:16.554
Desserts.

02:28:16.554 --> 02:28:19.190
Here in the US you can get
yourself a Hershey's sundae pie.

02:28:20.691 --> 02:28:22.526
Ugh.

02:28:22.526 --> 02:28:25.930
This one might have got a
little roughed up in transit.

02:28:25.930 --> 02:28:29.934
And in the US Burger King, you
can also get various shakes.

02:28:29.934 --> 02:28:32.937
Here we have Oreo shake,
a chocolate Oreo shake,

02:28:32.937 --> 02:28:34.939
a chocolate shake, and a vanilla shake.

02:28:34.939 --> 02:28:35.773
All right.

02:28:36.641 --> 02:28:37.808
God, that's so good.

02:28:37.808 --> 02:28:39.043
The straight-up chocolate.

02:28:40.478 --> 02:28:41.879
Oh, man, this is trouble.

02:28:41.879 --> 02:28:43.781
Mm!

02:28:43.781 --> 02:28:45.783
Wow, Burger King's shakes are really good.

02:28:45.783 --> 02:28:48.185
I'm assuming this is just
the straight Oreo one.

02:28:50.488 --> 02:28:54.025
Oh, my God, this is fantastic.

02:28:54.025 --> 02:28:57.161
Are we all curious what a
chocolate Oreo shake tastes like?

02:28:57.161 --> 02:28:58.496
Wonder no more.

02:29:00.431 --> 02:29:02.400
Good. This one's the best.

02:29:02.400 --> 02:29:05.002
Also at a US Burger King, you
can get a soft-serve cone.

02:29:05.002 --> 02:29:05.937
I didn't get it,

02:29:05.937 --> 02:29:08.839
only because we have no
refrigeration unit here

02:29:08.839 --> 02:29:11.842
and it would just be a cone
with a puddle of ice cream. So.

02:29:11.842 --> 02:29:15.179
Victoria, please turn me
into a giant soft-serve cone.

02:29:17.014 --> 02:29:19.116
So, here are our drinks.

02:29:19.116 --> 02:29:20.751
Let's start with this one.

02:29:20.751 --> 02:29:22.186
This one is ginger ale;

02:29:22.186 --> 02:29:23.988
and Fanta melon;

02:29:23.988 --> 02:29:25.723
oolong tea,

02:29:25.723 --> 02:29:27.692
which is Chinese tea;

02:29:27.692 --> 02:29:29.493
and orange juice.

02:29:29.493 --> 02:29:33.197
And this one is Earl Grey iced tea.

02:29:33.197 --> 02:29:35.800
Next we have Darjeeling tea.

02:29:35.800 --> 02:29:39.203
And here is Calpis,

02:29:39.203 --> 02:29:43.107
which, you guys call it
Calpico in your country.

02:29:43.107 --> 02:29:46.277
But in Japan we say "ka-ru pi-su."

02:29:46.277 --> 02:29:49.580
I know it sounds like
"cow piss" in English,

02:29:49.580 --> 02:29:51.983
but if you say Calpico to Japanese people,

02:29:51.983 --> 02:29:54.552
they will never understand
what you're talking about.

02:29:54.552 --> 02:29:58.589
So in Japan, once again,
we say "ka-ru pi-su."

02:29:58.589 --> 02:30:01.292
Repeat after me. "Ka-ru pi-su."

02:30:01.292 --> 02:30:03.294
Very good!

02:30:03.294 --> 02:30:04.295
First things you can get,

02:30:04.295 --> 02:30:06.430
you can get a little orange juice guy,

02:30:06.430 --> 02:30:10.267
and you can also get
Capri Sun apple juice.

02:30:10.267 --> 02:30:12.370
Shout-out to the pouch.

02:30:12.370 --> 02:30:14.805
Burger King in the US has
Coke products as well,

02:30:14.805 --> 02:30:17.341
but we have something called
a Coke Freestyle machine.

02:30:17.341 --> 02:30:18.642
If you haven't seen it,
it's this big machine

02:30:18.642 --> 02:30:21.178
that has a bunch of
Coca-Cola-related beverages.

02:30:21.178 --> 02:30:22.213
You can mix and match them.

02:30:22.213 --> 02:30:24.749
Anyway, we can get Hi-C fruit punch,

02:30:24.749 --> 02:30:27.952
Hi-C pink lemonade, Fanta
orange, Mello Yello,

02:30:27.952 --> 02:30:32.156
Powerade Zero, Dr Pepper,
Barq's, diet Barq's.

02:30:32.156 --> 02:30:34.925
You can also get yourself a fat-free milk.

02:30:34.925 --> 02:30:35.760
There it is.

02:30:35.760 --> 02:30:37.361
Sweetened or unsweetened tea.

02:30:37.361 --> 02:30:38.729
I think I got the sweetened.

02:30:38.729 --> 02:30:41.766
I don't want any tea. Tea sucks.

02:30:41.766 --> 02:30:44.368
We also have something
called frozen Cokes.

02:30:44.368 --> 02:30:45.836
That is this right here.

02:30:45.836 --> 02:30:47.104
As you can see, it's
been sitting for a while,

02:30:47.104 --> 02:30:47.972
it's starting to separate.

02:30:47.972 --> 02:30:49.140
But we have frozen Coke,

02:30:49.140 --> 02:30:51.342
we also have a frozen Fanta wild cherry,

02:30:51.342 --> 02:30:53.210
a frozen Fanta blue raspberry,

02:30:53.210 --> 02:30:55.379
and a frozen strawberry lemonade.

02:30:55.379 --> 02:30:56.213
Mm.

02:30:57.415 --> 02:30:58.315
Oh, yeah.

02:30:58.315 --> 02:31:01.218
Japan has a few exclusives
that are similar

02:31:01.218 --> 02:31:03.220
but different to that in the US.

02:31:03.220 --> 02:31:08.092
So, for example, this is
our plant-based Whopper.

02:31:08.092 --> 02:31:12.363
This burger is made from 100% soybeans.

02:31:12.363 --> 02:31:13.798
Itadakimasu!

02:31:16.367 --> 02:31:17.935
It's actually delicious.

02:31:17.935 --> 02:31:19.370
I like it.

02:31:19.370 --> 02:31:20.204
Mm.

02:31:20.204 --> 02:31:23.307
When it comes to
vegetarianism and veganism,

02:31:23.307 --> 02:31:25.242
they are not that popular in Japan.

02:31:25.242 --> 02:31:28.312
But gradually, especially
the restaurants in Tokyo

02:31:28.312 --> 02:31:31.449
are offering more vegan
or vegetarian meals

02:31:31.449 --> 02:31:33.617
because there is more Japanese people

02:31:33.617 --> 02:31:36.720
and non-Japanese people
who are vegan or vegetarian

02:31:36.720 --> 02:31:38.756
compared to other places in Japan.

02:31:38.756 --> 02:31:41.425
But overall, the vegan
or vegetarian option

02:31:41.425 --> 02:31:43.194
is still limited in Japan.

02:31:43.194 --> 02:31:45.830
And in the US, we have
the Impossible Whopper.

02:31:45.830 --> 02:31:46.697
What's the difference?

02:31:46.697 --> 02:31:49.867
Well, the Impossible burger
has all these ingredients.

02:31:49.867 --> 02:31:52.269
So as you can see, a lot more.

02:31:52.269 --> 02:31:54.472
I am curious.

02:31:54.472 --> 02:31:56.006
That looks like meat, right?

02:31:59.043 --> 02:31:59.944
Tastes exactly like a Whopper.

02:31:59.944 --> 02:32:01.445
I don't think I would
notice the difference.

02:32:01.445 --> 02:32:03.347
They're covering the
lack of meat with, like,

02:32:03.347 --> 02:32:06.016
with that char flavor
that they have on there.

02:32:06.016 --> 02:32:08.085
Oh, it's good.

02:32:08.085 --> 02:32:10.488
In Japan, we call this burger

02:32:10.488 --> 02:32:12.389
crispy chicken burger.

02:32:12.389 --> 02:32:14.058
And in the US, we have
the before-mentioned

02:32:14.058 --> 02:32:15.226
Ch'King sandwich,

02:32:15.226 --> 02:32:18.496
which comes in varieties
of spicy and/or deluxe.

02:32:18.496 --> 02:32:22.299
For breakfast, our hash
brown comes in one big piece.

02:32:23.334 --> 02:32:24.902
Whereas in the US,

02:32:24.902 --> 02:32:27.204
our hash browns come in little bites.

02:32:27.204 --> 02:32:31.976
And in Japan, we have this cheese bites.

02:32:31.976 --> 02:32:33.410
Look at this.

02:32:33.410 --> 02:32:36.080
And in the US, we have
eight-piece cheesy tots.

02:32:37.815 --> 02:32:39.984
And on to the US breakfast exclusives.

02:32:39.984 --> 02:32:41.752
As you can see, we have
a lot more going on

02:32:41.752 --> 02:32:45.089
in our breakfast menu here
in the US than Japan has.

02:32:45.089 --> 02:32:47.024
Here in the US, you can
get your breakfast sandwich

02:32:47.024 --> 02:32:50.361
in biscuit or Croissan'wich options.

02:32:50.361 --> 02:32:53.063
Croissan'wich is, of course,
a croissant sandwich.

02:32:53.063 --> 02:32:55.432
Took those two words, put
them together. Croissan'wich.

02:32:55.432 --> 02:32:57.968
So we have bacon, egg, and cheese;

02:32:57.968 --> 02:33:00.471
ham, egg, and cheese;

02:33:00.471 --> 02:33:03.774
and sausage, egg, and cheese.

02:33:03.774 --> 02:33:06.877
We have two breakfast burritos.

02:33:06.877 --> 02:33:09.079
The Egg-Normous breakfast burrito,

02:33:09.079 --> 02:33:10.581
which I'm assuming is this one,

02:33:10.581 --> 02:33:13.417
'cause it is enormous.

02:33:13.417 --> 02:33:15.386
The breakfast burrito junior.

02:33:15.386 --> 02:33:16.887
Look at this little guy!

02:33:16.887 --> 02:33:18.322
French toast sticks.

02:33:18.322 --> 02:33:20.758
Who doesn't like French toast?

02:33:20.758 --> 02:33:23.561
Finally, pancake platter
with just three pancakes

02:33:23.561 --> 02:33:26.163
or a pancake platter with three pancakes

02:33:26.163 --> 02:33:27.998
and a side of sausage.

02:33:30.301 --> 02:33:33.437
The fries at Burger King in
Japan come in three sizes,

02:33:33.437 --> 02:33:34.271
small,

02:33:36.273 --> 02:33:37.107
medium,

02:33:38.709 --> 02:33:39.643
and large.

02:33:41.679 --> 02:33:44.248
Fries in the US at Burger
King come in four sizes,

02:33:44.248 --> 02:33:46.817
value, small, medium, or large.

02:33:46.817 --> 02:33:50.154
Or maybe it's value, small, medium, large.

02:33:51.355 --> 02:33:52.656
Does this look right?

02:33:52.656 --> 02:33:54.058
Any of you "Food Wars" heads

02:33:54.058 --> 02:33:56.961
would've seen the Burger
King US vs UK episode

02:33:56.961 --> 02:33:59.096
where we uncovered Frygate.

02:33:59.096 --> 02:34:03.267
Two sizes had pretty much
the exact same unit of fries.

02:34:03.267 --> 02:34:04.902
Now, as you can see from these,

02:34:04.902 --> 02:34:08.205
I can't tell which is
the value and the small.

02:34:08.205 --> 02:34:09.807
I'm assuming this is the medium.

02:34:09.807 --> 02:34:14.678
Well, unfortunately, we cannot
do that amazingly accurate

02:34:14.678 --> 02:34:17.348
scientific test that we
did in the last episode

02:34:17.348 --> 02:34:19.783
because the fries have been compromised.

02:34:19.783 --> 02:34:21.852
They all came in the same bag, and ...

02:34:22.987 --> 02:34:25.055
I think they knew what we were up to

02:34:25.055 --> 02:34:28.025
and they purposely dumped
all the fries in the same bag

02:34:28.025 --> 02:34:31.295
to contaminate the experiment.

02:34:31.295 --> 02:34:33.063
You've outsmarted us this time.

02:34:33.063 --> 02:34:34.265
George: Let's weigh the large fries

02:34:34.265 --> 02:34:36.000
to see how much you actually get.

02:34:36.934 --> 02:34:39.270
151 grams.

02:34:39.270 --> 02:34:40.504
What if we did a thing where, like,

02:34:40.504 --> 02:34:43.507
whatever lands and stays on counts as it?

02:34:43.507 --> 02:34:45.909
Does that seem like a fair thing to say?

02:34:45.909 --> 02:34:48.512
That's really smart, what
I just did there, I think.

02:34:51.382 --> 02:34:53.050
It's 195 grams.

02:34:54.285 --> 02:34:55.953
Let's weigh Japan's Whopper.

02:34:57.554 --> 02:34:59.123
250 grams.

02:34:59.123 --> 02:35:02.993
Joe: And let us weigh
our Whopper in the US.

02:35:02.993 --> 02:35:05.062
Yo!

02:35:05.062 --> 02:35:06.330
270?

02:35:06.330 --> 02:35:07.798
Yeah, 270 grams.

02:35:07.798 --> 02:35:09.733
So pretty close. Surprisingly close.

02:35:09.733 --> 02:35:12.002
If you're not feeling like having beef,

02:35:12.002 --> 02:35:14.271
Burger King also has some chicken options.

02:35:14.271 --> 02:35:15.639
You can order your chicken nuggets

02:35:15.639 --> 02:35:18.442
in five pieces and eight pieces.

02:35:18.442 --> 02:35:20.577
Here in the US, you can
get your nuggets in sizes

02:35:20.577 --> 02:35:23.614
of four pieces, eight
pieces, or 16 pieces.

02:35:23.614 --> 02:35:26.617
And it's worth noting that
you can only get the 16-piece

02:35:26.617 --> 02:35:29.286
online or through their
app, and even if you do,

02:35:29.286 --> 02:35:31.855
they still just give you two eight-pieces.

02:35:31.855 --> 02:35:33.490
I don't know why either.

02:35:33.490 --> 02:35:35.659
So, let's weigh eight-piece nuggets.

02:35:36.760 --> 02:35:39.630
130 grams.

02:35:39.630 --> 02:35:42.700
Divide by eight equals

02:35:42.700 --> 02:35:46.670
16.25 grams per nugget.

02:35:46.670 --> 02:35:48.605
I don't know if we can get
as accurate of a measurement

02:35:48.605 --> 02:35:49.506
for something so small.

02:35:49.506 --> 02:35:53.410
So we will use this guy instead.

02:35:53.410 --> 02:35:57.047
So I'll just do this
and put this scale here.

02:35:59.216 --> 02:36:00.451
Ah!

02:36:00.451 --> 02:36:01.485
This is a bad idea.

02:36:01.485 --> 02:36:05.956
Eight pieces is 104 grams,

02:36:05.956 --> 02:36:10.527
divided by eight is 13 grams.

02:36:11.995 --> 02:36:14.164
In Japan, we have three drink sizes,

02:36:15.232 --> 02:36:16.066
small

02:36:17.534 --> 02:36:18.802
and medium

02:36:20.304 --> 02:36:21.905
and large.

02:36:23.040 --> 02:36:25.142
In the US, we have four drink sizes.

02:36:25.142 --> 02:36:27.277
Value, which only comes with a value meal;

02:36:27.277 --> 02:36:29.580
small; medium; and large.

02:36:29.580 --> 02:36:32.483
Now, I want to note that
the US's largest drink size

02:36:32.483 --> 02:36:36.220
is 112% larger than Japan's largest drink.

02:36:39.356 --> 02:36:40.858
Now, what's the biggest meal

02:36:40.858 --> 02:36:43.127
you can get in Japan's Burger King?

02:36:43.127 --> 02:36:46.730
Over here, it's the King Meal.

02:36:46.730 --> 02:36:51.268
[singing "Circle of Life"]

02:36:51.268 --> 02:36:53.437
The King Meal ranges anywhere

02:36:53.437 --> 02:36:56.774
from 790 to 990 yen

02:36:56.774 --> 02:36:58.642
depending on the burger you choose.

02:36:58.642 --> 02:37:01.145
It has your choice of an avocado Whopper,

02:37:01.145 --> 02:37:03.614
double cheeseburger, or Whopper.

02:37:03.614 --> 02:37:05.883
We chose the double cheeseburger,

02:37:05.883 --> 02:37:08.619
which comes with small fries,

02:37:08.619 --> 02:37:10.154
five-piece nuggets,

02:37:10.154 --> 02:37:12.990
medium Coke, and apple pie.

02:37:12.990 --> 02:37:16.627
And in the US, currently
our single biggest menu item

02:37:16.627 --> 02:37:19.997
at a Burger King is the
$30 Ultimate Party Bundle.

02:37:19.997 --> 02:37:22.199
Now, you could only
order this party bundle

02:37:22.199 --> 02:37:25.903
through the BK app, and
it includes two Whoppers,

02:37:25.903 --> 02:37:27.237
two double cheeseburgers,

02:37:27.237 --> 02:37:28.772
two original chicken sandwiches,

02:37:28.772 --> 02:37:30.541
two eight-piece chicken nuggets,

02:37:30.541 --> 02:37:33.477
four small fries, and four small drinks.

02:37:33.477 --> 02:37:35.379
And it costs:

02:37:35.379 --> 02:37:37.114
$30.

02:37:37.114 --> 02:37:39.516
In Japan, a Whopper cheese set,

02:37:39.516 --> 02:37:44.288
it costs around 890 yen, or $7.80 US.

02:37:44.288 --> 02:37:45.722
Whereas in the US, the same meal

02:37:45.722 --> 02:37:48.926
with a small fry and drink is $9.29,

02:37:48.926 --> 02:37:52.963
or 1,059.65 Japanese yen.

02:37:52.963 --> 02:37:53.831
What about the medium?

02:37:53.831 --> 02:37:55.299
You get that with the
medium fry and medium drink,

02:37:55.299 --> 02:37:56.900
it's $10.29,

02:37:56.900 --> 02:38:01.872
or 1,173.71 Japanese yen.

02:38:02.072 --> 02:38:03.574
What about the large?

02:38:05.309 --> 02:38:07.444
Poof! Hey, there it is,
right in front of me.

02:38:07.444 --> 02:38:11.114
Large fries and drink, $11.29,

02:38:11.114 --> 02:38:15.986
or 1,287.78 Japanese yen.

02:38:19.122 --> 02:38:20.491
Let's look at calories.

02:38:20.491 --> 02:38:24.495
In Japan, a Whopper is 676 calories.

02:38:24.495 --> 02:38:26.396
The calories aren't too bad,

02:38:26.396 --> 02:38:29.132
but watch out for the sodium levels.

02:38:29.132 --> 02:38:32.269
One Japan Whopper is 113%

02:38:32.269 --> 02:38:35.005
of your daily recommended
amount of sodium.

02:38:35.005 --> 02:38:36.673
Too much!

02:38:36.673 --> 02:38:39.910
In the US, our Whopper is 667 calories.

02:38:39.910 --> 02:38:41.879
Both Whoppers are pretty comparable

02:38:41.879 --> 02:38:43.113
in most of the categories,

02:38:43.113 --> 02:38:45.616
but there's one statistic
that really stands out,

02:38:45.616 --> 02:38:46.850
the salt content.

02:38:46.850 --> 02:38:51.588
The sodium level in Japan's
Whopper is 122% higher

02:38:51.588 --> 02:38:53.223
than that in the US.

02:38:53.223 --> 02:38:54.992
Let's make that a meal.

02:38:54.992 --> 02:38:57.594
A Whopper with large
fries and a large Coke

02:38:57.594 --> 02:39:00.998
is 1,323 calories.

02:39:00.998 --> 02:39:05.602
And the same meal in the
US is 1,680 calories,

02:39:05.602 --> 02:39:06.603
so a lot more.

02:39:06.603 --> 02:39:08.772
Now, a big portion of the calories

02:39:08.772 --> 02:39:11.008
actually come from the large Coke.

02:39:11.008 --> 02:39:14.912
The US's is roughly 182% more calories

02:39:14.912 --> 02:39:16.079
than that of Japan's.

02:39:16.079 --> 02:39:18.815
Let's look at the highest-calorie sandwich

02:39:18.815 --> 02:39:20.117
at Japan's Burger King.

02:39:20.117 --> 02:39:22.853
The double Whopper cheese is here.

02:39:22.853 --> 02:39:26.456
Eating one of these is already
half of your daily calories

02:39:26.456 --> 02:39:29.393
and a little over your
daily recommended protein.

02:39:29.393 --> 02:39:32.930
The main thing to watch
out for here is the sodium,

02:39:32.930 --> 02:39:37.501
which is 152% of your
daily recommended value.

02:39:37.501 --> 02:39:39.436
Whereas in the US, our
highest-calorie sandwich

02:39:39.436 --> 02:39:43.440
is the spicy chicken
deluxe sandwich, seen here.

02:39:43.440 --> 02:39:44.675
If you're worried about your health,

02:39:44.675 --> 02:39:45.943
steer clear of this one.

02:39:45.943 --> 02:39:50.681
The fat content is 190%
your daily allowance,

02:39:50.681 --> 02:39:55.652
and the sodium is over 200%
of your daily allowance.

02:39:55.652 --> 02:39:57.087
Yikes.

02:39:57.087 --> 02:39:58.522
As I mentioned earlier,

02:39:58.522 --> 02:40:01.525
the biggest menu item is the King Meal.

02:40:01.525 --> 02:40:04.394
If you get it with a
double bacon cheeseburger,

02:40:04.394 --> 02:40:08.432
the total calories are 1,329.

02:40:08.432 --> 02:40:11.868
That's 66% of your daily calories.

02:40:11.868 --> 02:40:15.172
And, of course, the $30
Ultimate Party Bundle,

02:40:15.172 --> 02:40:18.408
which is 8,903 calories,

02:40:18.408 --> 02:40:22.145
or 445% your daily

02:40:22.145 --> 02:40:24.047
caloric allowance.

02:40:27.684 --> 02:40:29.686
Burger King in Japan doesn't disclose

02:40:29.686 --> 02:40:31.388
the exact ingredients,

02:40:31.388 --> 02:40:34.691
but it does disclose where
the ingredients come from

02:40:34.691 --> 02:40:37.127
and where they're finished processing.

02:40:37.127 --> 02:40:39.062
For example, the Whopper beef patties

02:40:39.062 --> 02:40:42.966
are sourced from Australia,
New Zealand, and Europe,

02:40:42.966 --> 02:40:45.202
but they are processed in Australia,

02:40:45.202 --> 02:40:47.771
Japan, and Austria.

02:40:47.771 --> 02:40:49.172
Burger King in the US is pretty vague

02:40:49.172 --> 02:40:50.407
when it comes to its ingredients.

02:40:50.407 --> 02:40:53.477
They don't disclose a
comprehensive list anywhere.

02:40:53.477 --> 02:40:54.544
At the end of 2020,

02:40:54.544 --> 02:40:58.281
Burger King permanently
banned 120 artificial flavors

02:40:58.281 --> 02:41:01.118
from their menu, including aluminum,

02:41:01.118 --> 02:41:04.621
yellows 1 through 5, BHA, and BHT.

02:41:04.621 --> 02:41:06.657
Here's the complete list.

02:41:06.657 --> 02:41:08.759
It was actually a lot of stuff.

02:41:08.759 --> 02:41:09.793
Good for you guys.

02:41:10.293 --> 02:41:12.329
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

02:41:12.329 --> 02:41:14.131
we wanted to find out all the differences

02:41:14.131 --> 02:41:16.867
between Wendy's in Japan and the US.

02:41:16.867 --> 02:41:18.769
This is "Food Wars."

02:41:21.238 --> 02:41:23.073
In Japan, our Wendy's hamburgers

02:41:23.073 --> 02:41:24.608
come in four sizes:

02:41:24.608 --> 02:41:28.445
junior, single, double, and triple.

02:41:28.445 --> 02:41:31.281
In the US, our burgers come in four sizes:

02:41:31.281 --> 02:41:33.450
junior, Dave's single,

02:41:33.450 --> 02:41:36.753
Dave's double, and the Dave's triple.

02:41:36.753 --> 02:41:39.189
Look at the size of this thing.

02:41:42.059 --> 02:41:46.697
In Japan, our nuggets come
in orders of five and 10.

02:41:46.697 --> 02:41:49.533
Our US nuggets come in four, six,

02:41:49.533 --> 02:41:51.201
and 10-piece.

02:41:51.201 --> 02:41:53.470
Our Wendy's drinks come in three sizes:

02:41:53.470 --> 02:41:55.972
small, medium, and large.

02:41:55.972 --> 02:41:58.208
And in the US we also
have three drink sizes,

02:41:58.208 --> 02:41:59.843
small, medium,

02:41:59.843 --> 02:42:01.144
you've gotta be kidding me.

02:42:01.144 --> 02:42:02.512
Look at the size of this thing.

02:42:02.512 --> 02:42:04.247
This might be 40 ounces, Yuelei.

02:42:04.247 --> 02:42:06.216
Only one way to find out.

02:42:06.216 --> 02:42:07.050
Ho!

02:42:08.385 --> 02:42:10.454
Oh, not quite 40.

02:42:10.454 --> 02:42:15.225
About 36 or 37 fluid ounces of Coca-Cola.

02:42:15.225 --> 02:42:16.693
And how big's a bladder?

02:42:16.693 --> 02:42:18.762
This looks like more
than I would normally pee

02:42:18.762 --> 02:42:19.629
in the morning.

02:42:19.629 --> 02:42:23.266
OK, let's measure our large drink.

02:42:24.301 --> 02:42:27.771
It measures exactly 500 milliliters.

02:42:28.638 --> 02:42:31.074
Our Wendy's fries come in two sizes.

02:42:31.074 --> 02:42:33.510
Small and medium.

02:42:33.510 --> 02:42:35.345
Our fries come in four sizes,

02:42:35.345 --> 02:42:39.015
junior, small, medium,

02:42:39.015 --> 02:42:40.684
pew, large.

02:42:40.684 --> 02:42:42.586
Let's weigh our largest.

02:42:42.586 --> 02:42:44.121
[laughs]

02:42:44.121 --> 02:42:47.891
Roughly 180 grams.

02:42:47.891 --> 02:42:51.061
It weighs 135 grams.

02:42:51.061 --> 02:42:53.263
Japan's chili comes in two sizes,

02:42:53.263 --> 02:42:55.632
medium and large.

02:42:55.632 --> 02:42:58.235
And the US, our chili comes in two sizes,

02:42:58.235 --> 02:43:00.003
small and large.

02:43:00.003 --> 02:43:02.372
Let us weigh the largest now.

02:43:02.372 --> 02:43:06.109
Including the paper cup, 430 grams.

02:43:06.109 --> 02:43:08.912
George: Let's weigh our large chili.

02:43:08.912 --> 02:43:11.615
265 grams.

02:43:14.151 --> 02:43:16.520
In Japan, a Wendy's burger USA double

02:43:16.520 --> 02:43:21.424
is 730 yen, or $6.38.

02:43:21.424 --> 02:43:24.761
Our US Dave's double goes for $5.99,

02:43:24.761 --> 02:43:27.531
or around 685 Japanese yen.

02:43:27.531 --> 02:43:32.102
That's a 6.16% decrease
in price in the US.

02:43:32.102 --> 02:43:33.103
Let's make it a meal.

02:43:33.103 --> 02:43:35.772
In Japan, if you're getting
your burger as a set,

02:43:35.772 --> 02:43:37.374
it includes a small fries

02:43:37.374 --> 02:43:39.843
and a three-piece nuggets and a drink.

02:43:39.843 --> 02:43:42.379
It costs around 440 yen more.

02:43:42.379 --> 02:43:44.681
Our meals only include fries and drink.

02:43:44.681 --> 02:43:46.783
So a small Dave's double meal,

02:43:46.783 --> 02:43:47.851
and I threw in a four-piece

02:43:47.851 --> 02:43:49.186
because we don't have a three-piece,

02:43:49.186 --> 02:43:52.823
works out to $10.98.

02:43:52.823 --> 02:43:56.259
That's an 8.12% increased cost in the US.

02:43:56.259 --> 02:43:58.261
Mind you, we did get an extra nugget.

02:43:58.261 --> 02:43:59.896
Speaking of nuggets, in Japan,

02:43:59.896 --> 02:44:02.299
10-piece nugget is 510 yen,

02:44:02.299 --> 02:44:05.302
which breaks down to 51 yen per nugget.

02:44:05.302 --> 02:44:07.904
In the US, a 10-piece nugget is $4.29,

02:44:07.904 --> 02:44:11.675
which makes it per nugget around 43 cents.

02:44:11.675 --> 02:44:12.876
So per nugget average,

02:44:12.876 --> 02:44:15.912
the US is paying 8.11% less.

02:44:15.912 --> 02:44:17.480
A Baconator double in Japan

02:44:17.480 --> 02:44:22.152
is 850 yen, or $7.43.

02:44:22.152 --> 02:44:26.756
In the US, you get that
same Baconator for $7.49,

02:44:26.756 --> 02:44:29.793
or 857 Japanese yen.

02:44:29.793 --> 02:44:33.330
So close. Only a 0.82% increase.

02:44:35.732 --> 02:44:38.535
Here is everything you can
get at the Wendy's in Japan

02:44:38.535 --> 02:44:40.737
you cannot get in the US.

02:44:40.737 --> 02:44:42.405
And here's everything at a US Wendy's

02:44:42.405 --> 02:44:44.007
you can't get in Japan.

02:44:44.007 --> 02:44:46.710
One thing I want to point
out is that in Japan,

02:44:46.710 --> 02:44:50.113
Wendy's is known as Wendy's First Kitchen.

02:44:50.113 --> 02:44:52.582
First Kitchen is a
Japanese fast-food chain,

02:44:52.582 --> 02:44:55.719
and it was acquired by Wendy's in 2016

02:44:55.719 --> 02:44:59.022
and became a hybrid of Wendy's
and First Kitchen's menus.

02:44:59.022 --> 02:45:01.925
And we call them Fakkin,

02:45:01.925 --> 02:45:04.461
which is the abbreviation of First Kitchen

02:45:04.461 --> 02:45:05.695
in a Japanese way.

02:45:05.695 --> 02:45:07.864
It's like First Kitchen's "Fa"

02:45:07.864 --> 02:45:10.367
and kitchen's "ki" and "n."

02:45:10.367 --> 02:45:12.269
And say: Fakkin.

02:45:12.269 --> 02:45:15.305
Repeat after me: Fakkin.

02:45:15.305 --> 02:45:17.073
[beep]

02:45:17.073 --> 02:45:18.408
Got it, buddy.

02:45:18.408 --> 02:45:19.743
Very good!

02:45:19.743 --> 02:45:23.113
So, here are our Japan's
exclusive burgers.

02:45:23.113 --> 02:45:26.483
So, this one is bacon mushroom melt,

02:45:26.483 --> 02:45:28.985
and this one is just mushroom melt.

02:45:28.985 --> 02:45:32.589
We have Wendy's bacon egg burger.

02:45:32.589 --> 02:45:36.760
We also have Wendy's
cheese bacon egg burger,

02:45:36.760 --> 02:45:37.961
and this sauce,

02:45:39.262 --> 02:45:41.364
tartar sauce. Umai.

02:45:41.364 --> 02:45:43.800
Everybody's curious what this is.

02:45:43.800 --> 02:45:46.870
This one is Wild Rock.

02:45:46.870 --> 02:45:48.271
It's got no buns.

02:45:48.271 --> 02:45:50.273
It's got two beef patties.

02:45:50.273 --> 02:45:51.908
I think I should try this one.

02:45:51.908 --> 02:45:52.909
Itadakimasu.

02:45:54.411 --> 02:45:57.147
This meat itself has a good taste

02:45:57.147 --> 02:46:00.016
and some kind of, like, peppery flavor,

02:46:00.016 --> 02:46:02.218
but it's a little bit dry.

02:46:02.218 --> 02:46:03.653
I wouldn't get this again.

02:46:03.653 --> 02:46:04.988
And last things,

02:46:04.988 --> 02:46:07.958
we have junior teriyaki burger,

02:46:07.958 --> 02:46:11.528
and we have junior teriyaki cheeseburger.

02:46:12.762 --> 02:46:14.464
The big bacon cheeseburger.

02:46:14.464 --> 02:46:16.166
The big bacon double.

02:46:16.166 --> 02:46:19.469
Look at this! Yep, one, two,
three, the big bacon triple.

02:46:19.469 --> 02:46:24.107
I mean, I don't know what angle
is best to look at this at.

02:46:24.107 --> 02:46:26.643
And then we got big
bacons on the fancy bread.

02:46:26.643 --> 02:46:29.512
This must be the big bacons classicses.

02:46:29.512 --> 02:46:31.481
This looks like a big bacon --

02:46:31.481 --> 02:46:33.383
look, it's got shredded
cheese and stuff on this.

02:46:33.383 --> 02:46:36.353
Everything's bacon
something with these guys.

02:46:36.353 --> 02:46:38.521
At this point, it's just
like, how many slabs of meat

02:46:38.521 --> 02:46:40.390
do you want on your bacon sandwich?

02:46:40.390 --> 02:46:43.126
Two things you can get at a Wendy's

02:46:43.126 --> 02:46:45.528
in the US you cannot get in Japan

02:46:45.528 --> 02:46:48.832
or just the junior burger
and the junior cheeseburger.

02:46:48.832 --> 02:46:50.900
Look at this little guy. Look at this.

02:46:50.900 --> 02:46:52.902
Literally every fast-food burger place

02:46:52.902 --> 02:46:54.337
has a version of this.

02:46:54.337 --> 02:46:55.772
Chicken!

02:46:55.772 --> 02:46:57.207
[grunts]

02:46:57.207 --> 02:46:59.376
The Asiago chicken sandwiches.

02:46:59.376 --> 02:47:04.381
We got the Asiago chicken
ranch classic club.

02:47:04.381 --> 02:47:07.283
I said that in the wrong
order, but you get what I mean.

02:47:07.283 --> 02:47:08.551
Probably this one.

02:47:08.551 --> 02:47:12.589
This is the fried Asiago club with bacon.

02:47:12.589 --> 02:47:15.058
And then there is the spicy,

02:47:15.058 --> 02:47:17.427
which I'm assuming is this one.

02:47:17.427 --> 02:47:19.496
And then they got the grilled.

02:47:22.532 --> 02:47:23.867
That's pretty good.

02:47:23.867 --> 02:47:25.502
Don't like Asiago?

02:47:25.502 --> 02:47:26.870
Wendy's got you covered.

02:47:26.870 --> 02:47:29.105
So many chicken sandwiches at Wendy's

02:47:29.105 --> 02:47:31.574
that of course are not Asiago'd.

02:47:31.574 --> 02:47:33.476
This is the grilled chicken sandwich.

02:47:33.476 --> 02:47:36.279
As you can see, it is grilled.

02:47:36.279 --> 02:47:39.149
And then we have the
grilled chicken big bacon.

02:47:39.149 --> 02:47:42.719
Man, they must've gotten some
deal on bacon for Wendy's.

02:47:42.719 --> 02:47:44.020
Everything's got bacon on it!

02:47:44.020 --> 02:47:45.488
I'm going to go ahead
and assume this is the

02:47:45.488 --> 02:47:47.857
big bacon fried chicken sandwich,

02:47:47.857 --> 02:47:49.559
'cause it has bacon on it.

02:47:49.559 --> 02:47:52.395
So you have the spicy big
bacon cheddar chicken.

02:47:52.395 --> 02:47:55.265
In Japan, our Wendy's have pasta,

02:47:55.265 --> 02:47:57.634
which were originally on
the First Kitchen menu.

02:47:57.634 --> 02:48:01.004
So here we have
ramen-style soy cream pasta

02:48:01.004 --> 02:48:02.906
with spinach and ham.

02:48:02.906 --> 02:48:06.309
Expires 2023,

02:48:06.309 --> 02:48:08.144
January 20.

02:48:08.144 --> 02:48:10.580
Joe, I'll keep this for you.

02:48:10.580 --> 02:48:13.116
Nah, my guy, you can go
ahead and throw that out.

02:48:13.116 --> 02:48:17.287
And next we have ramen-style
dandan soup pasta

02:48:17.287 --> 02:48:19.656
with spinach and ham.

02:48:19.656 --> 02:48:23.793
So, dandan soup is kind of like
a spicy chili-flavored soup

02:48:23.793 --> 02:48:26.196
with miso and pork mince.

02:48:26.196 --> 02:48:30.667
Dandan soup and dandan ramen
are very popular in Japan.

02:48:30.667 --> 02:48:32.936
Tomato sauce pasta

02:48:32.936 --> 02:48:36.739
with mozzarella and bacon.

02:48:36.739 --> 02:48:41.010
All right, next we have beef
cheek meat cream spaghetti.

02:48:42.178 --> 02:48:43.279
Plastic.

02:48:43.279 --> 02:48:44.114
Mm.

02:48:45.315 --> 02:48:48.751
Next we have carbonara spaghetti.

02:48:48.751 --> 02:48:49.686
Naotomo: Carbon-AR-a.

02:48:49.686 --> 02:48:51.187
Carbon-AAH-ra.

02:48:51.187 --> 02:48:52.722
Carbona-rrra.

02:48:52.722 --> 02:48:53.823
A-rrra? OK.

02:48:53.823 --> 02:48:55.191
Carbra-rrra.

02:48:55.191 --> 02:48:56.159
[crew laughing]

02:48:56.159 --> 02:48:57.594
It's got bacon

02:48:57.594 --> 02:49:01.731
and this creamy carbona-rrra sauce.

02:49:01.731 --> 02:49:03.299
Molto bene!

02:49:03.299 --> 02:49:08.271
Last thing I have is
spicy cod roe spaghetti.

02:49:08.271 --> 02:49:12.375
So, spicy cod roe in Japanese is mentaiko,

02:49:12.375 --> 02:49:16.679
and mentaiko spaghetti is
also very popular in Japan.

02:49:16.679 --> 02:49:18.581
Unfortunately, some Americans I know

02:49:18.581 --> 02:49:20.683
don't like mentaiko so much

02:49:20.683 --> 02:49:22.852
because of the texture and smell.

02:49:22.852 --> 02:49:24.454
But for me, mentaiko,

02:49:24.454 --> 02:49:27.991
it's super Fakkin delicious.

02:49:27.991 --> 02:49:31.261
Uh, it's been a while
since I got this one.

02:49:31.261 --> 02:49:33.296
It's been, like, three hours.

02:49:33.296 --> 02:49:34.464
Itadakimasu.

02:49:37.333 --> 02:49:38.268
Mm.

02:49:38.268 --> 02:49:40.503
Joe, try it out.

02:49:40.503 --> 02:49:41.804
I appreciate the offer, George,

02:49:41.804 --> 02:49:43.640
but you can go ahead and finish that,

02:49:43.640 --> 02:49:46.543
'cause it looks Fakkin disgusting.

02:49:46.543 --> 02:49:47.877
We got salads.

02:49:47.877 --> 02:49:49.245
Over here on this end, the first one

02:49:49.245 --> 02:49:52.182
looks like we got the
Parmesan Caesar salad.

02:49:52.182 --> 02:49:54.551
Comes with, of course, Caesar dressing

02:49:54.551 --> 02:49:57.387
and what looks to be Parmesan crisps.

02:49:57.387 --> 02:49:59.689
This next salad is ridiculous.

02:49:59.689 --> 02:50:01.591
We're going to go ahead and
put quotes around salad.

02:50:01.591 --> 02:50:05.528
Wendy's has a taco "salad" that comes

02:50:05.528 --> 02:50:10.500
with tortilla chips, sour
cream, signature salsa,

02:50:10.500 --> 02:50:13.603
and, if that wasn't enough, chili.

02:50:13.603 --> 02:50:14.971
And before we continue,

02:50:14.971 --> 02:50:16.773
you confirmed that the taco salad

02:50:16.773 --> 02:50:18.374
is supposed to have chili on it?

02:50:18.374 --> 02:50:19.375
They told you that.

02:50:19.375 --> 02:50:21.744
Just gotta get the chips all around here.

02:50:21.744 --> 02:50:22.679
I can't believe this.

02:50:22.679 --> 02:50:24.347
This is so gross.

02:50:24.347 --> 02:50:27.917
Signature salsa, then chili.

02:50:27.917 --> 02:50:30.320
Oh, it smells so bad.

02:50:30.320 --> 02:50:32.222
Oh, God.

02:50:32.222 --> 02:50:33.056
Eh.

02:50:34.224 --> 02:50:35.558
I'm just -- this is just like eating chili

02:50:35.558 --> 02:50:37.093
with tortilla chips.

02:50:37.093 --> 02:50:37.894
They said there was some salt --

02:50:37.894 --> 02:50:39.596
I'm just pushing this s--- around.

02:50:41.431 --> 02:50:42.665
On to the next salad,

02:50:42.665 --> 02:50:45.368
the Southwest avocado salad.

02:50:45.368 --> 02:50:46.836
Oh, my God, there's bacon on it!

02:50:46.836 --> 02:50:47.804
That's weird.

02:50:47.804 --> 02:50:49.405
That was in Dave Thomas' obituary.

02:50:49.405 --> 02:50:51.040
"I want everything to
be covered in bacon."

02:50:51.040 --> 02:50:55.144
But yeah. Chicken, avocado,
bacon, cheese, and some sauce.

02:50:55.144 --> 02:50:55.979
This makes sense.

02:50:55.979 --> 02:50:58.248
And the last salad,

02:50:58.248 --> 02:50:59.482
apple pecan salad.

02:50:59.482 --> 02:51:00.383
That smells.

02:51:00.383 --> 02:51:02.518
Oh, 'cause it's got blue cheese on it.

02:51:02.518 --> 02:51:04.053
Roasted pecan bits.

02:51:04.053 --> 02:51:05.588
Pomegranate vinaigrette!

02:51:07.724 --> 02:51:09.092
Mm. Apples are nice.

02:51:09.092 --> 02:51:11.861
It's kind of nice to get a
little bit of actual fruit,

02:51:11.861 --> 02:51:13.396
something nutritious while doing this.

02:51:13.396 --> 02:51:15.565
It's like my body's like, "What is this?!"

02:51:15.565 --> 02:51:17.433
So, here are Japan's side menu.

02:51:17.433 --> 02:51:19.869
We have a few flavor options for fries.

02:51:19.869 --> 02:51:23.606
So we have happy butter flavor fries.

02:51:24.474 --> 02:51:26.476
Happy butter flavor.

02:51:26.476 --> 02:51:29.746
It has just subtle buttery flavor. Mm.

02:51:29.746 --> 02:51:33.049
Burnt butter soy sauce flavor.

02:51:33.049 --> 02:51:34.550
Rip it off. Bwah!

02:51:34.550 --> 02:51:37.553
I don't know what's going on
here, but it's pretty good.

02:51:37.553 --> 02:51:39.489
Much better than this.

02:51:39.489 --> 02:51:42.292
Savory steamed potato butter.

02:51:42.292 --> 02:51:45.028
It gets quite strong buttery flavor.

02:51:45.028 --> 02:51:46.896
Definitely I prefer this one

02:51:46.896 --> 02:51:49.065
than the happy butter flavor.

02:51:49.065 --> 02:51:50.533
This is not happy.

02:51:50.533 --> 02:51:54.170
This one is chicken consommé flavor.

02:51:54.170 --> 02:51:55.338
Mm.

02:51:55.338 --> 02:51:58.474
This is the best fries
I've ever had in my life.

02:51:58.474 --> 02:52:00.877
Now I'm going to introduce you

02:52:00.877 --> 02:52:05.481
this spicy chicken breast.

02:52:05.481 --> 02:52:07.917
Wendy's in the US also has baked potatoes.

02:52:07.917 --> 02:52:08.885
See what we got.

02:52:08.885 --> 02:52:11.821
Of course, there's your regular.

02:52:11.821 --> 02:52:13.156
And this one, oh, yeah.

02:52:13.156 --> 02:52:15.258
This one's got, like,
chives and stuff in it.

02:52:15.258 --> 02:52:17.427
If I was to stop here, you would go,

02:52:17.427 --> 02:52:21.464
"Wow, what a tasteful
selection of healthy potatoes."

02:52:21.464 --> 02:52:23.599
But of course we don't stop here.

02:52:23.599 --> 02:52:28.304
We move on to absolute
baked-potato madness.

02:52:28.304 --> 02:52:30.907
Ah, No. 1, oof.

02:52:30.907 --> 02:52:32.375
Cheese baked potato.

02:52:32.375 --> 02:52:34.143
Drowned this thing in cheese.

02:52:34.143 --> 02:52:35.611
It's like -- ooh!

02:52:35.611 --> 02:52:37.680
It's, like, caked to the side. Blech.

02:52:37.680 --> 02:52:39.182
Ugh. Ugh.

02:52:39.182 --> 02:52:42.485
Oh, God! [laughs]

02:52:42.485 --> 02:52:45.121
The chili and cheese baked potato.

02:52:45.121 --> 02:52:46.289
Blech.

02:52:46.289 --> 02:52:49.092
If you are like me, you're
wondering to yourself,

02:52:49.092 --> 02:52:50.560
something's missing.

02:52:50.560 --> 02:52:55.031
Something is missing from
this potato menu, Yuelei!

02:52:55.031 --> 02:52:56.432
Can you guess what that is?

02:52:56.432 --> 02:52:59.936
The bacon cheese baked potato!

02:52:59.936 --> 02:53:02.472
Oh, they got big pieces
of bacon on this one too.

02:53:02.472 --> 02:53:03.506
Oof!

02:53:03.506 --> 02:53:05.375
You can get spicy chicken nuggets.

02:53:05.375 --> 02:53:06.676
Yessiree Bob.

02:53:07.610 --> 02:53:09.479
Seasoned potatoes.

02:53:09.479 --> 02:53:11.481
All right, so fruit finally made the menu.

02:53:11.481 --> 02:53:12.315
Apple slices.

02:53:12.315 --> 02:53:14.350
It wouldn't be a Wendy's category

02:53:14.350 --> 02:53:16.853
without the Baconator fries.

02:53:16.853 --> 02:53:19.088
We need the bacon meter in this episode.

02:53:19.088 --> 02:53:20.656
Last of the sides.

02:53:20.656 --> 02:53:21.858
Oh, yeah.

02:53:21.858 --> 02:53:22.859
Oatmeal bar.

02:53:22.859 --> 02:53:23.993
Looks like a Clif bar.

02:53:25.728 --> 02:53:27.397
Whoa, that's actually pretty good.

02:53:27.397 --> 02:53:30.600
So, here are our Japan's exclusive drinks.

02:53:30.600 --> 02:53:33.770
We have tapioca royal
milk tea with brown sugar

02:53:33.770 --> 02:53:36.873
and tapioca milk with brown sugar.

02:53:36.873 --> 02:53:37.974
Tornado.

02:53:39.442 --> 02:53:40.510
Mm!

02:53:41.744 --> 02:53:43.413
This is amazing.

02:53:43.413 --> 02:53:44.680
Simply amazing.

02:53:44.680 --> 02:53:45.581
I love this.

02:53:45.581 --> 02:53:47.383
So, here are our other drinks.

02:53:47.383 --> 02:53:50.987
We have Pepsi, orange juice,

02:53:50.987 --> 02:53:52.655
and ginger ale,

02:53:52.655 --> 02:53:55.491
lemonade and melon soda,

02:53:55.491 --> 02:53:58.127
peach tea and iced tea,

02:53:58.127 --> 02:54:01.764
iced matcha, and this one is iced cocoa.

02:54:01.764 --> 02:54:04.667
So, here we have our hot drinks.

02:54:04.667 --> 02:54:07.770
We have Darjeeling tea,

02:54:07.770 --> 02:54:10.273
and we have café mocha,

02:54:10.273 --> 02:54:12.608
and we have peach tea.

02:54:12.608 --> 02:54:13.910
Mm.

02:54:13.910 --> 02:54:15.077
I like this.

02:54:15.077 --> 02:54:17.113
And we have café latte

02:54:17.113 --> 02:54:18.614
and cocoa

02:54:18.614 --> 02:54:20.817
and matcha.

02:54:20.817 --> 02:54:22.919
This is matcha, but it looks like

02:54:22.919 --> 02:54:26.055
water from 100 years ago.

02:54:26.055 --> 02:54:28.224
Our Wendy's has Frosty-ccinos,

02:54:28.224 --> 02:54:31.561
which I'm assuming are
Frostys meet Frappuccinos?

02:54:31.561 --> 02:54:32.762
Frosty-ccinos?

02:54:32.762 --> 02:54:35.998
But it does not appear that
there's Frostys in this.

02:54:35.998 --> 02:54:39.001
They have two flavors,
vanilla and chocolate.

02:54:39.001 --> 02:54:41.437
I'm assuming this is the vanilla.

02:54:41.437 --> 02:54:43.639
Wendy's did smart on this
one. It isn't that sweet.

02:54:43.639 --> 02:54:46.843
I was expecting it to
be, like, undrinkable,

02:54:46.843 --> 02:54:47.910
but it's actually kind of nice.

02:54:47.910 --> 02:54:50.346
All right, this one is the chocolate.

02:54:50.346 --> 02:54:51.180
Yeah.

02:54:51.180 --> 02:54:53.349
Also, it's a nice flavor.

02:54:53.349 --> 02:54:54.684
'Cause of the Frosty-ccinos,

02:54:54.684 --> 02:54:56.052
you know what that means.

02:54:56.052 --> 02:54:57.420
At Wendy's you can also get:

02:54:57.420 --> 02:54:59.088
booyah, Frostys.

02:54:59.088 --> 02:55:00.723
They don't have these in Japan?

02:55:00.723 --> 02:55:03.159
I feel like this is the staple menu item.

02:55:04.427 --> 02:55:09.365
[laughs]

02:55:10.566 --> 02:55:11.934
I love these so much.

02:55:15.204 --> 02:55:18.107
Fantastic. That's fantastic.

02:55:18.107 --> 02:55:19.141
Gotta go for the chocolate.

02:55:19.141 --> 02:55:20.142
Don't bother finding me a spoon.

02:55:20.142 --> 02:55:21.477
I'm just gonna do a little taste here.

02:55:21.477 --> 02:55:22.612
That's great.

02:55:22.612 --> 02:55:24.046
The Frostys are great.

02:55:24.046 --> 02:55:27.283
It's like a milkshake, but
it's super thick and delicious.

02:55:27.283 --> 02:55:29.585
Japan, you want this.

02:55:29.585 --> 02:55:30.486
Thick.

02:55:30.486 --> 02:55:31.854
It is thick!

02:55:31.854 --> 02:55:35.424
In Japan, we have floats
instead of Frostys.

02:55:35.424 --> 02:55:37.293
We have Coke float

02:55:37.293 --> 02:55:39.695
and melon soda float.

02:55:39.695 --> 02:55:43.132
Japan has an exclusive breakfast sandwich.

02:55:43.132 --> 02:55:46.369
It's called the breakfast sandwich.

02:55:46.369 --> 02:55:48.738
It's got tomato, lettuce,

02:55:48.738 --> 02:55:53.175
and I believe this is
beef or pork patties.

02:55:54.644 --> 02:55:57.213
OK, whereas Japan has one
exclusive breakfast sandwich,

02:55:57.213 --> 02:55:58.681
we have way more.

02:55:58.681 --> 02:56:00.149
Like all the fast food here in America,

02:56:00.149 --> 02:56:02.385
we take our breakfast very seriously.

02:56:02.385 --> 02:56:06.923
You can get yourself a
maple bacon croissant.

02:56:06.923 --> 02:56:08.724
It looks like it's a chicken sandwich

02:56:08.724 --> 02:56:13.095
that of course has bacon and
maple syrup on the croissant.

02:56:13.095 --> 02:56:15.298
We have what just appears
to be the bacon biscuit.

02:56:15.298 --> 02:56:18.267
Bacon, egg, cheese

02:56:18.267 --> 02:56:20.903
in the incredibly dry biscuit.

02:56:20.903 --> 02:56:22.371
Bacon croissant.

02:56:22.371 --> 02:56:23.573
I don't know about this one.

02:56:23.573 --> 02:56:27.777
Moving on to the sausage zone
of the Wendy's breakfast.

02:56:27.777 --> 02:56:30.813
This is the special sausage biscuit.

02:56:30.813 --> 02:56:33.115
No, no, no, no, no.

02:56:33.115 --> 02:56:34.216
Here's what I hate about this.

02:56:34.216 --> 02:56:37.053
Pick a drier thing to have for breakfast.

02:56:37.053 --> 02:56:39.088
I feel like it'd be impossible
to swallow a bite of this.

02:56:39.088 --> 02:56:40.623
You're going to choke on it.

02:56:40.623 --> 02:56:42.625
Here we go. See, this is
what I'm talking about.

02:56:42.625 --> 02:56:43.659
They might have gotten this backwards.

02:56:43.659 --> 02:56:45.561
This is actually the better sausage one.

02:56:45.561 --> 02:56:47.029
This at least has a better chance

02:56:47.029 --> 02:56:48.564
of not getting stuck in your throat.

02:56:48.564 --> 02:56:51.934
The sausage croissant
also has egg. Thank you.

02:56:51.934 --> 02:56:55.071
They have a few things that
are honey-butter-based.

02:56:55.071 --> 02:56:56.639
I am so glad that fast-food places

02:56:56.639 --> 02:56:59.275
are introducing honey
to their breakfast menu.

02:56:59.275 --> 02:57:00.309
I think maybe it has to do with the fact

02:57:00.309 --> 02:57:02.078
that chicken sandwiches
have become so popular.

02:57:02.078 --> 02:57:04.246
First one we got here is
the honey butter biscuit.

02:57:04.246 --> 02:57:06.015
[laughs]

02:57:06.015 --> 02:57:08.250
Hey, it's just a biscuit
with honey butter.

02:57:08.250 --> 02:57:10.553
I mean, yeah, I'll have this anytime.

02:57:10.553 --> 02:57:11.821
I'll have this anytime.

02:57:11.821 --> 02:57:13.756
This one has some heft to it.

02:57:13.756 --> 02:57:15.558
It's the hot honey biscuit.

02:57:15.558 --> 02:57:17.827
Yeah!

02:57:18.995 --> 02:57:20.696
A little chicken on there.

02:57:20.696 --> 02:57:21.530
Yep.

02:57:24.400 --> 02:57:26.102
I really like that.

02:57:26.102 --> 02:57:29.972
This is the special chicken croissant.

02:57:29.972 --> 02:57:32.708
So, here are our desserts.

02:57:32.708 --> 02:57:35.211
So here we have Melotozzo.

02:57:35.211 --> 02:57:37.880
So, Melotozzo are
maritozzo-style pastries,

02:57:37.880 --> 02:57:40.182
which are popular in
Rome and Japan as well,

02:57:40.182 --> 02:57:41.984
made with melon bread.

02:57:41.984 --> 02:57:44.420
So melon bread is a type
of sweet Japanese bread

02:57:44.420 --> 02:57:47.189
which has a sugar cookie
crust on the surface.

02:57:47.189 --> 02:57:48.691
But what's funny is that

02:57:48.691 --> 02:57:51.794
it doesn't have a melon flavor at all.

02:57:51.794 --> 02:57:52.628
At all.

02:57:52.628 --> 02:57:54.230
The reason it's called melon bread

02:57:54.230 --> 02:57:56.432
is that it just looks like melon.

02:57:56.432 --> 02:57:58.501
Does it look like melon?

02:57:58.501 --> 02:57:59.802
It does in Japan.

02:58:01.270 --> 02:58:02.738
Oh!

02:58:02.738 --> 02:58:03.873
And this time,

02:58:03.873 --> 02:58:07.610
First Kitchen made a
maritozzo using melon bread

02:58:07.610 --> 02:58:09.679
and mascarpone cheese whipped cream,

02:58:09.679 --> 02:58:11.981
and it's called Melotozzo.

02:58:11.981 --> 02:58:15.618
So here we have Melotozzo tiramisu

02:58:15.618 --> 02:58:18.721
and Melotozzo matcha and Melotozzo plain.

02:58:18.721 --> 02:58:22.958
So, actually, yesterday was
my birthday, February 18.

02:58:22.958 --> 02:58:25.394
Hey, it's your birthday!
Happy birthday, George!

02:58:25.394 --> 02:58:28.731
Thank you for your message!
Thank you! Arigatou gozaimasu!

02:58:28.731 --> 02:58:31.534
So this is my birthday present.

02:58:31.534 --> 02:58:34.437
All right, so let's give it a shot.

02:58:34.437 --> 02:58:37.306
Best birthday present ever.

02:58:37.306 --> 02:58:38.307
Itadakimasu.

02:58:39.842 --> 02:58:42.478
This is so good.

02:58:42.478 --> 02:58:45.181
I can't stop eating this.

02:58:45.181 --> 02:58:46.515
Mm.

02:58:46.515 --> 02:58:49.752
So, Wendy's in Japan has a
Japanese traditional sweet

02:58:49.752 --> 02:58:52.588
since it has been a
collaboration with First Kitchen.

02:58:52.588 --> 02:58:56.025
So we have shiratama cream zenzai.

02:58:56.025 --> 02:58:57.059
Ooh.

02:58:57.059 --> 02:59:00.162
So it has three main
ingredients, ice cream,

02:59:00.162 --> 02:59:02.698
and sweet red beans, and the shiratama,

02:59:02.698 --> 02:59:04.900
which is kind of like a mochi rice cake.

02:59:04.900 --> 02:59:08.370
And my grandma likes this type of zenzai.

02:59:08.370 --> 02:59:10.106
This is for you, my grandma.

02:59:10.106 --> 02:59:13.743
And also we have mini pancakes.

02:59:13.743 --> 02:59:15.745
In the US, we only have
two exclusive desserts,

02:59:15.745 --> 02:59:16.579
and they're both cookies.

02:59:16.579 --> 02:59:17.980
And that's no disrespect to cookies,

02:59:17.980 --> 02:59:19.849
cookies are great, but I want one of those

02:59:19.849 --> 02:59:22.151
fun Italian ice cream sandwiches they had.

02:59:22.151 --> 02:59:24.353
Anyway, you can get two
cookies here in the US,

02:59:24.353 --> 02:59:27.790
a chocolate chunk cookie
and a sugar cookie.

02:59:30.092 --> 02:59:33.896
Our Wendy's double burger is 578 calories

02:59:33.896 --> 02:59:37.233
and 29% of your daily recommended amount

02:59:37.233 --> 02:59:40.970
and 60% of the recommended daily sodium.

02:59:40.970 --> 02:59:43.939
Our double burger, the Dave's
double, isn't much better.

02:59:43.939 --> 02:59:46.408
Ours is 850 calories

02:59:46.408 --> 02:59:49.779
and way more fat. Over 70%!

02:59:49.779 --> 02:59:51.781
But less sodium,

02:59:51.781 --> 02:59:53.816
just a bit over half of the daily amount.

02:59:53.816 --> 02:59:55.751
Still, not great.

02:59:55.751 --> 02:59:57.453
Make it a meal in Japan,

02:59:57.453 --> 03:00:01.357
and that increases the calories to 1,089.

03:00:01.357 --> 03:00:06.128
That's 55% of your daily
recommended calorie intake.

03:00:06.128 --> 03:00:08.430
And if you make it a combo
here, we chose the small

03:00:08.430 --> 03:00:10.199
and took a few sips,

03:00:10.199 --> 03:00:12.535
that's 440 more calories,

03:00:12.535 --> 03:00:15.604
bringing the total to 1,290,

03:00:15.604 --> 03:00:19.241
or 64.5% of your daily allowance.

03:00:19.241 --> 03:00:22.578
In Japan, the single menu
item with the most calories

03:00:22.578 --> 03:00:25.314
is the eight-piece fried-chicken pack,

03:00:25.314 --> 03:00:30.119
which contains [gasps] 4,018 calories,

03:00:30.119 --> 03:00:33.355
201% of your daily calories.

03:00:33.355 --> 03:00:35.658
In the US, our single
biggest-calorie menu item

03:00:35.658 --> 03:00:37.793
is the Feed the Fam deal.

03:00:37.793 --> 03:00:40.296
A fam, yeah, right! This is all for you.

03:00:40.296 --> 03:00:42.431
It is two spicy chicken sandwiches,

03:00:42.431 --> 03:00:44.166
two junior bacon cheeseburgers,

03:00:44.166 --> 03:00:47.002
and four small fries.

03:00:47.002 --> 03:00:49.438
Total 2,780 calories,

03:00:49.438 --> 03:00:54.043
which is 139% of your daily intake.

03:00:55.911 --> 03:00:59.782
Japan's Wendy's doesn't
disclose their ingredients list.

03:00:59.782 --> 03:01:01.150
Why, Japan?

03:01:01.150 --> 03:01:02.418
The US sure does.

03:01:02.418 --> 03:01:05.454
Now, is there anything we
should be looking out for?

03:01:05.454 --> 03:01:06.455
Of course there is.

03:01:06.455 --> 03:01:07.790
Let's start with sodium nitrate,

03:01:07.790 --> 03:01:11.193
which is found in the Baconator's
applewood-smoked bacon.

03:01:11.193 --> 03:01:14.396
Sodium nitrate is a chemical
that is used to cure meats

03:01:14.396 --> 03:01:17.533
and gives meat that appealing pink color.

03:01:17.533 --> 03:01:18.934
Perfect for bacon.

03:01:18.934 --> 03:01:20.502
Also, get this,

03:01:20.502 --> 03:01:21.904
it's super toxic.

03:01:21.904 --> 03:01:23.906
It is restricted for purchase online.

03:01:23.906 --> 03:01:26.609
People have accidentally
eaten too much of it and died.

03:01:26.609 --> 03:01:29.812
It's also been used in homicides. Yikes!

03:01:29.812 --> 03:01:31.513
Sodium nitrate is on a list

03:01:31.513 --> 03:01:34.283
of Japan's designated food additives,

03:01:34.283 --> 03:01:37.820
but our Wendy's gets its
bacon imported from Denmark,

03:01:37.820 --> 03:01:41.557
where it isn't banned,
but being reduced in use.

03:01:41.557 --> 03:01:43.459
Our American cheese contains lecithin,

03:01:43.459 --> 03:01:45.961
a common emulsifier that,
according to one academic,

03:01:45.961 --> 03:01:49.531
a worrisome number of scientific
studies have suggested

03:01:49.531 --> 03:01:52.768
that too much of it
can promote depression.

03:01:52.768 --> 03:01:53.769
[sighs]

03:01:53.769 --> 03:01:55.604
The pickles contain polysorbate 80.

03:01:55.604 --> 03:01:59.208
This is commonly used as
an emulsifier in foods,

03:01:59.208 --> 03:02:02.278
but in pickles, it tends to
be used as a solubilizer.

03:02:02.278 --> 03:02:03.846
Not how that's pronounced, sorry.

03:02:03.846 --> 03:02:06.882
Which helps other ingredients
in the brine fully dissolve.

03:02:06.882 --> 03:02:10.152
Studies have suggested it can
cause colon cancer in mice.

03:02:10.152 --> 03:02:11.587
Not fantastic.

03:02:11.587 --> 03:02:13.489
There is no info on Wendy's website

03:02:13.489 --> 03:02:15.524
of where the pickles come from,

03:02:15.524 --> 03:02:18.761
but we want to point
out that polysorbate 80

03:02:18.761 --> 03:02:21.697
is on Japan's list of
designated additives.

03:02:21.697 --> 03:02:25.501
And therefore, it's permitted
to be used in Japan.

03:02:25.734 --> 03:02:27.870
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

03:02:27.870 --> 03:02:29.672
we wanted to find out all the differences

03:02:29.672 --> 03:02:32.274
between Domino's in Japan and the US.

03:02:32.274 --> 03:02:34.376
This is "Food Wars."

03:02:37.346 --> 03:02:39.782
In Japan, Domino's pizzas
come in three sizes.

03:02:39.782 --> 03:02:42.384
Our Domino's pizza comes in four sizes.

03:02:42.384 --> 03:02:45.888
George: So, this one is medium,
which is cut into 8 slices.

03:02:45.888 --> 03:02:47.623
Joe: Over here on this
end, you got the small.

03:02:47.623 --> 03:02:50.359
That's 10-inch pizza.

03:02:50.359 --> 03:02:54.363
And here's regular, which is
also cut into eight slices.

03:02:54.363 --> 03:02:55.597
Joe: Next up is our medium.

03:02:55.597 --> 03:02:57.900
That's a 12-inch pizza.

03:02:57.900 --> 03:03:00.002
And this one is large.

03:03:00.002 --> 03:03:03.005
This one is cut into 12 slices.

03:03:03.005 --> 03:03:07.109
Joe: Then we move to our large, 14 inches.

03:03:07.109 --> 03:03:11.313
And finally, the extra
large, which is 16 inches.

03:03:11.313 --> 03:03:12.815
Look at all that grease.

03:03:18.354 --> 03:03:22.524
A Domino's large plain pizza
has a 33-centimeters diameter

03:03:22.524 --> 03:03:27.096
or an 855.3-square-centimeters area

03:03:27.096 --> 03:03:29.431
and costs 2,000 yen.

03:03:29.431 --> 03:03:30.699
So breaking that down,

03:03:30.699 --> 03:03:34.536
our pizza is 2.33 yen per square inch,

03:03:34.536 --> 03:03:36.638
or about 2 cents.

03:03:36.638 --> 03:03:39.108
Now take our large.
This is a 14-inch pizza,

03:03:39.108 --> 03:03:42.444
also a 35.56-centimeter pizza.

03:03:42.444 --> 03:03:43.879
And it has a surface area

03:03:43.879 --> 03:03:48.083
of 993.1 square centimeters.

03:03:48.083 --> 03:03:51.020
That's 1.4 cents per square inch,

03:03:51.020 --> 03:03:54.189
or 1.62 Japanese yen.

03:03:54.189 --> 03:03:58.293
But what gives you the
most food for your money?

03:03:58.293 --> 03:04:01.663
So, here's a large plain
slice with a pan crust.

03:04:01.663 --> 03:04:04.933
And here's another with hand-tossed crust.

03:04:04.933 --> 03:04:07.803
Let's weigh both right
now and see which is more.

03:04:07.803 --> 03:04:10.606
So, first let's weigh pan crust.

03:04:11.440 --> 03:04:13.108
51 grams.

03:04:13.108 --> 03:04:15.511
And hand-tossed crust.

03:04:15.511 --> 03:04:18.647
It weighs 49 grams.

03:04:18.647 --> 03:04:20.282
And we will do the same.

03:04:20.282 --> 03:04:22.851
I want to note that right now in America,

03:04:22.851 --> 03:04:26.355
you can only get the pan
Domino's in the medium size.

03:04:26.355 --> 03:04:29.224
Same exact experiment, only
I'm doing two medium pizzas.

03:04:29.224 --> 03:04:31.860
Medium pan slice, medium
hand-tossed slice.

03:04:31.860 --> 03:04:36.865
So, this is the hand-tossed slice,

03:04:36.865 --> 03:04:38.133
and it weighs

03:04:39.268 --> 03:04:41.236
a smidge over 75.

03:04:41.236 --> 03:04:42.271
We'll go 76.

03:04:42.271 --> 03:04:43.639
The pan.

03:04:45.374 --> 03:04:46.975
That goes in there too.

03:04:46.975 --> 03:04:48.844
110 grams.

03:04:48.844 --> 03:04:52.548
Making the difference this amount.

03:04:52.548 --> 03:04:54.183
I'm not doing math.

03:04:54.183 --> 03:04:57.052
In Japan, we have seven
different crust options.

03:04:57.052 --> 03:04:59.922
No. 1, we have pan.

03:04:59.922 --> 03:05:03.025
And No. 2 we have hand-tossed.

03:05:03.959 --> 03:05:07.796
And No. 3, we have ultra-crispy.

03:05:07.796 --> 03:05:08.664
Ooh.

03:05:08.664 --> 03:05:10.466
It's like a cracker.

03:05:12.167 --> 03:05:15.471
No. 4, we have cheese burst,

03:05:15.471 --> 03:05:19.208
where a string cheese is placed
around the edge of the crust

03:05:19.208 --> 03:05:22.444
and sprinkled with consommé
Parmesan seasoning.

03:05:22.444 --> 03:05:23.779
Ooh.

03:05:23.779 --> 03:05:27.216
No. 5, we have the cheese 'n' roll.

03:05:28.183 --> 03:05:31.286
It's got mozzarella cheese in the crust.

03:05:31.286 --> 03:05:35.524
And No. 6, we have mille-filet.

03:05:35.524 --> 03:05:38.594
Or mill-foy.

03:05:38.594 --> 03:05:40.662
Mille-fail.

03:05:40.662 --> 03:05:43.465
In Japanese we say mi-ru fi-yu.

03:05:43.465 --> 03:05:45.601
So this one is mi-ru-fi-yu pizza,

03:05:45.601 --> 03:05:47.569
which has two layers of crust

03:05:47.569 --> 03:05:50.172
with Camembert mixed cheese in between.

03:05:50.172 --> 03:05:51.740
Mille-fail.

03:05:51.740 --> 03:05:53.542
Mille-fee-yuh.

03:05:53.542 --> 03:05:56.612
French people, please
correct my pronunciation.

03:05:56.612 --> 03:05:59.381
No. 7, the last one we have,

03:05:59.381 --> 03:06:01.884
the triple mille-feuille.

03:06:01.884 --> 03:06:05.554
It's got three layers of
crust with cheese in between.

03:06:05.554 --> 03:06:06.421
Wow.

03:06:06.421 --> 03:06:09.258
In the US, we have only
five crust options.

03:06:09.258 --> 03:06:10.993
I realize there's four
pizzas in front of me.

03:06:10.993 --> 03:06:11.827
Let me explain.

03:06:11.827 --> 03:06:13.595
One crust option you can get here,

03:06:13.595 --> 03:06:17.466
and it's a small only,
is the gluten-free crust.

03:06:17.466 --> 03:06:22.471
I don't know how bread is gluten-free,

03:06:22.638 --> 03:06:24.773
but we figured it out.

03:06:24.773 --> 03:06:25.707
Ta-da.

03:06:25.707 --> 03:06:28.277
We also have the hand-tossed,

03:06:28.277 --> 03:06:31.280
which is more of a standard pillowy,

03:06:31.280 --> 03:06:32.481
I mean, right, this is
like standard dough,

03:06:32.481 --> 03:06:33.782
this is what we think a pizza looks like.

03:06:33.782 --> 03:06:36.185
This is the pan.

03:06:36.185 --> 03:06:37.586
Look how thick that is, man.

03:06:37.586 --> 03:06:39.621
That's, like, triple the dough thickness.

03:06:39.621 --> 03:06:40.822
Good on you for the pan.

03:06:40.822 --> 03:06:43.158
Now, you can get this in the medium only.

03:06:43.158 --> 03:06:45.994
We also have a crunchy thin crust.

03:06:45.994 --> 03:06:47.930
And we have so many
pizzas here, to be honest,

03:06:47.930 --> 03:06:49.164
I don't know which one it is.

03:06:49.164 --> 03:06:51.900
So when it just comes up in
the video, I'll show it off.

03:06:51.900 --> 03:06:54.870
But imagine a crunchy thin pizza.

03:06:54.870 --> 03:06:56.405
Oddly enough, we also
have something called

03:06:56.405 --> 03:06:57.706
the Brooklyn-style pizza.

03:06:57.706 --> 03:07:00.375
This is reserved for large
and extra-large pizzas only.

03:07:00.375 --> 03:07:03.278
And this is a Brooklyn-style
right here, extra large.

03:07:03.278 --> 03:07:05.847
Obviously it isn't crispy,
because it's sagging.

03:07:05.847 --> 03:07:07.282
This is really thin.

03:07:09.785 --> 03:07:12.554
Here's everything you can
get at the Japanese Domino's

03:07:12.554 --> 03:07:15.190
that you cannot get in the US.

03:07:15.190 --> 03:07:17.192
Here's everything you
can get at a US Domino's

03:07:17.192 --> 03:07:18.827
you cannot get in Japan.

03:07:18.827 --> 03:07:21.296
Everyone, look at this.

03:07:21.296 --> 03:07:23.999
This is a limited-time-offer pizza.

03:07:23.999 --> 03:07:27.002
It's called the Best 34.

03:07:27.002 --> 03:07:28.270
Look at this lid.

03:07:28.270 --> 03:07:30.672
It's disgusting!

03:07:30.672 --> 03:07:33.175
Don't look at me! Don't look at me!

03:07:33.175 --> 03:07:36.645
So, this one has all 34 Domino's toppings,

03:07:36.645 --> 03:07:41.116
like teriyaki chicken, mayo,
spinach, tomato, shrimp.

03:07:41.116 --> 03:07:43.151
This is huge.

03:07:43.151 --> 03:07:45.153
It's like my baby.

03:07:45.153 --> 03:07:48.991
[sings lullaby]

03:07:50.092 --> 03:07:52.094
The New Yorker-style pizza is similar

03:07:52.094 --> 03:07:55.197
to the Brooklyn XL option
you can get in America.

03:07:55.197 --> 03:07:58.433
But only in Japan you can
get the Quattro New Yorker.

03:07:58.433 --> 03:08:01.870
It's a 16-inch pizza with
each New Yorker topping style

03:08:01.870 --> 03:08:03.939
covering a quarter of the pizza.

03:08:03.939 --> 03:08:07.743
So one quarter is pepperoni,
and one is cheese,

03:08:07.743 --> 03:08:09.845
and one is pepperoni and sausage,

03:08:09.845 --> 03:08:12.180
and one is ham and mushroom.

03:08:12.180 --> 03:08:15.384
So, here we have Nippon favorites series.

03:08:15.384 --> 03:08:18.920
Nippon, or Nihon, means Japan in Japanese.

03:08:18.920 --> 03:08:21.423
So these pizzas feature
Japanese ingredients.

03:08:21.423 --> 03:08:23.859
This one charcoal-grilled
teriyaki chicken.

03:08:23.859 --> 03:08:27.629
It's got teriyaki chicken, teriyaki sauce,

03:08:27.629 --> 03:08:30.966
spinach, mayonnaise, and corn.

03:08:30.966 --> 03:08:33.735
Next we have Hokkaido three cheeses.

03:08:33.735 --> 03:08:37.506
So, Hokkaido is the northern
island prefecture in Japan,

03:08:37.506 --> 03:08:40.208
and it's famous for its cheese.

03:08:40.208 --> 03:08:42.077
It's got Hokkaido Gouda cheese,

03:08:42.077 --> 03:08:43.712
Hokkaido cheddar cheese,

03:08:43.712 --> 03:08:46.848
and Hokkaido Camembert
and sliced asparagus.

03:08:46.848 --> 03:08:49.384
We have spicy mayo and mochi.

03:08:49.384 --> 03:08:52.387
It's got mochi rice cake and corn,

03:08:52.387 --> 03:08:55.357
pork sausage and sliced asparagus,

03:08:55.357 --> 03:08:57.125
and Korean seaweed flakes.

03:08:57.125 --> 03:08:59.795
And last one, we've got
charcoal-grilled beef

03:08:59.795 --> 03:09:01.697
and spinach and mushrooms.

03:09:04.533 --> 03:09:06.401
Mm!

03:09:06.401 --> 03:09:07.836
Oh!

03:09:07.836 --> 03:09:09.137
Umai!

03:09:10.138 --> 03:09:11.840
Umai!

03:09:11.840 --> 03:09:14.076
This beef is so tender,

03:09:14.076 --> 03:09:19.081
and it's got so much,
like, charcoal flavor,

03:09:19.081 --> 03:09:20.982
which makes this amazing.

03:09:20.982 --> 03:09:22.250
I love this.

03:09:22.250 --> 03:09:24.553
So many exclusive pizzas
here at the US Domino's.

03:09:24.553 --> 03:09:25.420
I don't know where to begin,

03:09:25.420 --> 03:09:27.222
so I'll just start with
this one that I'm holding.

03:09:27.222 --> 03:09:31.693
This is the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

03:09:31.693 --> 03:09:35.731
I don't know what makes it
California-in-y or Cali-y,

03:09:35.731 --> 03:09:38.533
but it definitely has
chicken, and bacon, and ranch,

03:09:38.533 --> 03:09:39.768
and it's big.

03:09:39.768 --> 03:09:40.869
Thank you very much.

03:09:40.869 --> 03:09:41.737
All right.

03:09:42.604 --> 03:09:44.005
Chicken taco pizza.

03:09:46.675 --> 03:09:48.176
Oh, yeah.

03:09:48.176 --> 03:09:49.745
Got taco spices to it.

03:09:49.745 --> 03:09:50.612
Good job on this one.

03:09:50.612 --> 03:09:52.414
Next one, the cheeseburger pizza.

03:09:52.414 --> 03:09:53.515
Um ...

03:09:56.685 --> 03:09:58.520
Yeah. Oh, my God.

03:09:58.520 --> 03:09:59.921
I'm going to say something crazy.

03:09:59.921 --> 03:10:02.324
This tastes exactly like
a McDonald's cheeseburger.

03:10:02.324 --> 03:10:04.926
Even has the oniony
and the ketchupy taste.

03:10:05.894 --> 03:10:07.462
Wow.

03:10:07.462 --> 03:10:09.131
That is a surprise.

03:10:09.131 --> 03:10:10.065
I thought this one was going to be bad,

03:10:10.065 --> 03:10:11.266
but it's actually pretty good.

03:10:11.266 --> 03:10:15.237
The extravaganZZa.

03:10:15.237 --> 03:10:19.574
This has pepperoni, sausage, ham,

03:10:19.574 --> 03:10:23.678
mushrooms, black olives, green peppers.

03:10:23.678 --> 03:10:25.180
This is the meatZZa,

03:10:25.180 --> 03:10:27.983
which I'm assuming is just a lot of meat.

03:10:27.983 --> 03:10:30.585
I'm seeing sausage, I'm seeing pepperoni,

03:10:30.585 --> 03:10:31.720
and maybe hamburger.

03:10:35.357 --> 03:10:36.425
Yeah, I'll put this in the good pile.

03:10:36.425 --> 03:10:37.259
I f--- with this one.

03:10:37.259 --> 03:10:38.260
Philly cheesesteak.

03:10:38.260 --> 03:10:39.795
Oh, no.

03:10:39.795 --> 03:10:42.197
In some weird way, I'm
blaming you for this.

03:10:42.197 --> 03:10:45.066
Since you handed this to
me, this is your fault.

03:10:45.066 --> 03:10:46.668
Look at this nightmare.

03:10:46.668 --> 03:10:48.503
Meat somewhere on here.

03:10:48.503 --> 03:10:50.439
I'm also seeing green peppers.

03:10:50.439 --> 03:10:53.442
Oh. Look, look, it's like,

03:10:53.442 --> 03:10:55.510
look at that, it's,
like, stuck to the box.

03:10:59.881 --> 03:11:01.249
No.

03:11:01.249 --> 03:11:02.184
Buffalo chicken.

03:11:02.184 --> 03:11:03.485
OK, OK.

03:11:03.485 --> 03:11:04.453
This is more my speed.

03:11:04.453 --> 03:11:05.320
Chicken.

03:11:05.320 --> 03:11:06.888
No, not tomato sauce, like a white sauce.

03:11:06.888 --> 03:11:07.722
Good call.

03:11:09.858 --> 03:11:11.693
Mm!

03:11:11.693 --> 03:11:13.361
This isn't Buffalo enough.

03:11:13.361 --> 03:11:15.964
The capital of the great state of New York

03:11:15.964 --> 03:11:18.300
needs to be better
represented in this pizza.

03:11:18.300 --> 03:11:21.470
The capital of New York
is Buffalo, correct?

03:11:21.470 --> 03:11:22.304
No?

03:11:22.304 --> 03:11:24.539
We got the Memphis barbecue chicken.

03:11:24.539 --> 03:11:25.674
Love Memphis.

03:11:25.674 --> 03:11:26.708
Love barbecue.

03:11:26.708 --> 03:11:27.709
Love chicken.

03:11:29.678 --> 03:11:31.046
Yeah.

03:11:31.046 --> 03:11:32.514
The key thing here is the barbecue sauce.

03:11:32.514 --> 03:11:35.116
I don't know what is in it,
but, man, that's really good.

03:11:35.116 --> 03:11:35.951
Memphis,

03:11:36.918 --> 03:11:39.754
capital of the great state of Tennessee.

03:11:39.754 --> 03:11:44.759
Everyone, here is the
ultra cheese New Yorker.

03:11:45.227 --> 03:11:47.529
It's got 1 kilogram of cheese,

03:11:47.529 --> 03:11:49.998
or 2.2 pounds.

03:11:49.998 --> 03:11:52.434
OMG.

03:11:52.434 --> 03:11:53.268
Ooh!

03:11:54.202 --> 03:11:57.272
Look how thick this cheese is!

03:11:57.272 --> 03:11:58.106
Go!

03:12:05.547 --> 03:12:06.615
Go home.

03:12:06.615 --> 03:12:09.017
It weighs 180 grams,

03:12:09.017 --> 03:12:12.053
180 times eight equals

03:12:12.053 --> 03:12:15.490
1,440 grams in total.

03:12:15.490 --> 03:12:18.527
So, here are other
Japanese specialty pizzas.

03:12:18.527 --> 03:12:21.863
So, here we have quattro meat max.

03:12:21.863 --> 03:12:24.366
So it's got charcoal-grilled
teriyaki chicken

03:12:24.366 --> 03:12:26.801
and charcoal-grilled beef

03:12:26.801 --> 03:12:30.338
and giga meat and Goryeo galbi.

03:12:30.338 --> 03:12:33.275
It's Korean-style beef pizza.

03:12:33.275 --> 03:12:35.477
And next we have seafood special.

03:12:36.545 --> 03:12:39.781
This part and this part
is shrimp mayonnaise.

03:12:39.781 --> 03:12:42.484
So this part, it's got shrimp, octopus,

03:12:42.484 --> 03:12:44.819
mussels, littleneck clams,

03:12:44.819 --> 03:12:47.322
Mactra clams, green peppers,

03:12:47.322 --> 03:12:48.924
and cherry tomatoes.

03:12:48.924 --> 03:12:52.127
Next we've got garlic master.

03:12:52.127 --> 03:12:53.895
Looks so spicy.

03:12:53.895 --> 03:12:57.766
Garlic and pork sausage and pancetta.

03:12:57.766 --> 03:13:01.303
And this part has got jalapeño, obviously.

03:13:01.303 --> 03:13:03.305
It's picante.

03:13:03.305 --> 03:13:06.775
Pepperoni and Italian sausage and onions.

03:13:06.775 --> 03:13:09.144
And look at this huge thing.

03:13:09.144 --> 03:13:10.645
Mayo jaga.

03:13:10.645 --> 03:13:14.649
So, jaga, or jagaimo,
means potato in Japanese.

03:13:14.649 --> 03:13:17.085
It's got potato and pork sausage

03:13:17.085 --> 03:13:18.954
and a lot of mayo.

03:13:18.954 --> 03:13:21.957
Joe: Our US Domino's has
sandwiches and pasta.

03:13:21.957 --> 03:13:24.559
I was not a fan of the
Philly cheesesteak pizza,

03:13:24.559 --> 03:13:26.528
but let's see what the Philly
cheesesteak tastes like

03:13:26.528 --> 03:13:29.898
in its native form of sandwich.

03:13:31.433 --> 03:13:32.834
Better than the pizza.

03:13:32.834 --> 03:13:34.069
Also at the US Domino's,

03:13:34.069 --> 03:13:35.837
you can get a Buffalo chicken sandwich,

03:13:35.837 --> 03:13:37.339
a chicken habanero sandwich,

03:13:37.339 --> 03:13:38.506
the Mediterranean veggie,

03:13:38.506 --> 03:13:39.341
no, thanks,

03:13:39.341 --> 03:13:40.575
a chicken bacon ranch,

03:13:40.575 --> 03:13:41.543
an Italian sandwich,

03:13:41.543 --> 03:13:44.412
and, of course, the chicken Parm sandwich.

03:13:44.412 --> 03:13:46.781
Our Domino's has four
pastas to choose from.

03:13:46.781 --> 03:13:48.917
I only got two, the chicken Alfredo

03:13:48.917 --> 03:13:51.019
and the Italian sausage marinara.

03:13:51.019 --> 03:13:54.556
You can also get a chicken
carbonara and a pasta primavera.

03:13:54.556 --> 03:13:56.558
I've just been informed
I have to eat this.

03:14:01.296 --> 03:14:03.298
Strong flavor on this.

03:14:03.298 --> 03:14:07.168
I would skip the pasta
at Domino's, personally.

03:14:07.168 --> 03:14:08.603
This thing is, like, baked on.

03:14:08.603 --> 03:14:09.571
See how baked this is?

03:14:09.571 --> 03:14:10.672
Like, come on.

03:14:10.672 --> 03:14:11.606
I feel like chef Ramsay here.

03:14:11.606 --> 03:14:15.410
Just, "Oh, come on. Oh,
this baked on here!"

03:14:15.410 --> 03:14:17.912
In the US, we have a few chicken options

03:14:17.912 --> 03:14:19.080
you can't get in Japan.

03:14:19.080 --> 03:14:20.548
Yes, Japan has wings,

03:14:20.548 --> 03:14:22.017
but they don't have these flavors.

03:14:22.017 --> 03:14:23.852
Visually, I can see why.

03:14:23.852 --> 03:14:27.922
First flavor we got here
is the garlic Parmesan.

03:14:27.922 --> 03:14:31.159
Hey, Domino's, what are you doing?

03:14:31.159 --> 03:14:32.661
Next one, we got,

03:14:32.661 --> 03:14:35.630
I'm assuming this is the honey barbecue.

03:14:35.630 --> 03:14:37.532
These drizzles! What are you
guys doing drizzling, man?

03:14:37.532 --> 03:14:38.767
Just toss it!

03:14:38.767 --> 03:14:40.435
Toss it in the sauce!

03:14:40.435 --> 03:14:41.703
Nobody wants a drizzle.

03:14:44.406 --> 03:14:45.573
Oh, wait a second.

03:14:46.675 --> 03:14:48.743
This is the sweet mango habanero.

03:14:48.743 --> 03:14:50.011
I wasn't expecting that heat.

03:14:51.646 --> 03:14:53.048
Oh, man.

03:14:53.048 --> 03:14:53.915
Very good.

03:14:53.915 --> 03:14:56.151
These are --

03:14:57.452 --> 03:14:58.787
why did you do this?

03:14:58.787 --> 03:15:00.622
Why did you do this?

03:15:00.622 --> 03:15:02.123
Toss it in the sauce.

03:15:02.123 --> 03:15:04.693
Why'd you just squirt it on
here, like, as an afterthought?

03:15:04.693 --> 03:15:05.794
Honey barbecue.

03:15:05.794 --> 03:15:06.861
Right? Is this not nuts?

03:15:06.861 --> 03:15:08.863
This is nuts, right, that
they did it like this.

03:15:11.633 --> 03:15:13.368
I like the sauce.

03:15:13.368 --> 03:15:17.105
So, Domino's also does their
wings in boneless flavors.

03:15:17.105 --> 03:15:18.940
They have obviously those three,

03:15:18.940 --> 03:15:21.109
and you can also get these two other ones.

03:15:21.109 --> 03:15:23.378
And I see we have the
crispy bacon and tomato,

03:15:23.378 --> 03:15:27.148
and this one must be the
spicy jalapeño pineapple.

03:15:27.148 --> 03:15:28.183
Whoa, what?

03:15:29.050 --> 03:15:30.085
Hell yeah.

03:15:30.085 --> 03:15:31.252
All right.

03:15:31.252 --> 03:15:32.253
Get that B-roll fast.

03:15:32.253 --> 03:15:35.356
There it goes!

03:15:36.224 --> 03:15:37.392
I know.

03:15:37.392 --> 03:15:41.262
Your audible gasps are warranted.

03:15:41.262 --> 03:15:43.598
I don't know what this --

03:15:43.598 --> 03:15:45.700
what am I supposed to do with this?

03:15:45.700 --> 03:15:47.869
Ooh, this one I'm looking
forward to, Yuelei.

03:15:47.869 --> 03:15:49.871
We got the food less than an hour ago.

03:15:49.871 --> 03:15:53.575
I don't think an hour is
unrealistic for food to sit.

03:15:53.575 --> 03:15:55.110
I think you guys gotta
put some more chemicals

03:15:55.110 --> 03:15:57.112
in your cheese to keep it goopier longer.

03:15:57.112 --> 03:15:58.913
Ooh, I got some pineapple,
and I got some jalapeño,

03:15:58.913 --> 03:15:59.814
and I got some chicken.

03:15:59.814 --> 03:16:00.682
Let's check it out.

03:16:03.551 --> 03:16:04.753
Yeah.

03:16:04.753 --> 03:16:07.422
Overall, everything
here tastes pretty good.

03:16:07.422 --> 03:16:09.424
Presentation, you gotta work on that.

03:16:09.424 --> 03:16:11.893
In Japan, we don't have boneless wings,

03:16:11.893 --> 03:16:14.996
but we have Japanese fried chicken,

03:16:14.996 --> 03:16:16.664
which is called karaage.

03:16:16.664 --> 03:16:19.134
It kind of looks like
American boneless wings.

03:16:20.034 --> 03:16:21.336
Ah.

03:16:21.336 --> 03:16:23.238
I love karaage.

03:16:23.238 --> 03:16:26.474
And also we have chicken nuggets.

03:16:26.474 --> 03:16:30.145
Both come in four, eight, and 12 pieces.

03:16:30.145 --> 03:16:33.615
Our Domino's has breads
and oven-baked dips.

03:16:33.615 --> 03:16:35.316
Let's review the breads first.

03:16:35.316 --> 03:16:36.284
Shall we?

03:16:36.284 --> 03:16:37.118
Over here,

03:16:37.118 --> 03:16:40.922
we have Parmesan bread twists
and garlic bread twists.

03:16:40.922 --> 03:16:45.093
I know that because of their
totally twisted shapes.

03:16:45.093 --> 03:16:47.028
They also have Parmesan bread bites

03:16:47.028 --> 03:16:48.329
that were currently unavailable.

03:16:50.331 --> 03:16:51.633
Whoa.

03:16:51.633 --> 03:16:52.801
Uh-oh.

03:16:52.801 --> 03:16:54.469
These are very good.

03:16:54.469 --> 03:16:56.004
To Parmesan we go.

03:16:58.306 --> 03:16:59.274
Not as good.

03:16:59.274 --> 03:17:00.875
But still pretty good.

03:17:00.875 --> 03:17:03.978
I mean, it's bread and
cheese and oil, right?

03:17:03.978 --> 03:17:06.848
US Domino's also has something
called stuffed cheesy bread.

03:17:06.848 --> 03:17:08.249
You can get your stuffed
cheesy bread with either

03:17:08.249 --> 03:17:12.287
spinach and feta or bacon and jalapeños.

03:17:12.287 --> 03:17:14.289
Take a wild guess which one I chose.

03:17:15.690 --> 03:17:18.359
[beep] Just ripping this
whole [beep] thing apart.

03:17:18.359 --> 03:17:19.994
Oh, God!

03:17:19.994 --> 03:17:21.896
This thing is especially greasy.

03:17:24.465 --> 03:17:28.670
For whatever reason,
Domino's didn't stop there.

03:17:28.670 --> 03:17:30.738
Domino's has something called dips.

03:17:30.738 --> 03:17:31.573
[sighs]

03:17:31.573 --> 03:17:33.141
What it appears to be

03:17:34.008 --> 03:17:36.511
is a giant dish of melted cheese.

03:17:36.511 --> 03:17:39.547
And you can get it in cheesy
marinara or five cheese.

03:17:39.547 --> 03:17:41.482
What are we doing, Domino's?

03:17:41.482 --> 03:17:44.352
[laughs]

03:17:44.352 --> 03:17:45.954
What is this?

03:17:45.954 --> 03:17:48.489
Come on, guys.

03:17:48.489 --> 03:17:50.525
So, this is the marinara
one, I'm assuming.

03:17:50.525 --> 03:17:52.961
A pizza without the bread, right?

03:17:52.961 --> 03:17:57.131
These dips are literally
zapping my will to live.

03:17:57.131 --> 03:17:58.600
Please don't ever get ...

03:18:00.268 --> 03:18:03.972
It's a whole bowl of cheese, Yuelei!

03:18:03.972 --> 03:18:06.908
Why would -- oh, look
at the oil in this too!

03:18:07.809 --> 03:18:09.777
Everyone in here just gagged.

03:18:09.777 --> 03:18:11.246
Can I even dip it?

03:18:18.386 --> 03:18:20.054
Oh, whoa.

03:18:21.256 --> 03:18:22.991
I don't know what of the
five cheeses is in here,

03:18:22.991 --> 03:18:23.858
like, which five.

03:18:25.293 --> 03:18:27.061
Why am I eating this?!

03:18:28.196 --> 03:18:29.631
Ugh!

03:18:31.599 --> 03:18:34.969
So, here are our Japanese
exclusive side-menu items.

03:18:34.969 --> 03:18:36.671
Let's start with this one.

03:18:36.671 --> 03:18:40.074
We've got oven-baked potato wedges.

03:18:40.074 --> 03:18:41.743
This one is plain.

03:18:41.743 --> 03:18:43.211
Consommé.

03:18:43.211 --> 03:18:44.946
Chili garlic.

03:18:44.946 --> 03:18:47.148
And this one is butter.

03:18:48.082 --> 03:18:51.519
And next we have cheese sticks.

03:18:52.387 --> 03:18:54.088
Shrimp popcorn.

03:18:55.723 --> 03:18:58.526
It comes with this tartar sauce.

03:18:58.526 --> 03:19:01.396
Here we have choregi salad.

03:19:01.396 --> 03:19:04.799
We've got Korean-style seaweed flakes

03:19:04.799 --> 03:19:07.235
and choregi dressing.

03:19:07.235 --> 03:19:12.140
So, choregi is, like,
Korean-style sesame-oil dressing.

03:19:12.140 --> 03:19:15.643
And fresh salad in the package.

03:19:17.078 --> 03:19:20.148
So, here we have corn potage.

03:19:20.148 --> 03:19:21.349
Clam chowder.

03:19:21.349 --> 03:19:22.684
Minestrone.

03:19:22.684 --> 03:19:24.585
Black chili.

03:19:24.585 --> 03:19:25.887
You've seen these before.

03:19:25.887 --> 03:19:29.424
It is the Domino's
marbled cookie brownies.

03:19:29.424 --> 03:19:31.859
♪ Liquid sugar ♪

03:19:31.859 --> 03:19:33.194
Oh, yeah.

03:19:33.194 --> 03:19:36.097
You can also get these
cinnamon bread twists.

03:19:36.097 --> 03:19:39.000
Lastly, another dip.

03:19:39.000 --> 03:19:42.503
I swear to God, if there's cheese in this,

03:19:42.503 --> 03:19:44.572
I'm walking out of here
and I'm never coming back.

03:19:48.042 --> 03:19:49.510
Baked apple dips.

03:19:49.510 --> 03:19:52.814
And I'm assuming you dip these into this.

03:19:52.814 --> 03:19:53.915
I'm not gonna.

03:19:53.915 --> 03:19:55.950
So, here are our other desserts.

03:19:55.950 --> 03:19:58.720
We have mini pancakes,

03:19:58.720 --> 03:20:01.422
heart-shaped fondant chocolate,

03:20:01.422 --> 03:20:05.126
and here we have egg custard tart.

03:20:05.126 --> 03:20:08.329
I have never tried this one before.

03:20:08.329 --> 03:20:09.497
Itadakimasu.

03:20:11.966 --> 03:20:13.568
Mm.

03:20:13.568 --> 03:20:15.103
Mm!

03:20:15.103 --> 03:20:16.304
This is so good.

03:20:16.304 --> 03:20:17.739
So flaky.

03:20:19.674 --> 03:20:20.575
Mm.

03:20:20.575 --> 03:20:23.444
This one is apple pie.

03:20:23.444 --> 03:20:26.247
And next we have custard pie.

03:20:27.081 --> 03:20:31.219
Lastly, of the sodas
you can get in the US,

03:20:31.219 --> 03:20:32.653
can't get in Japan,

03:20:32.653 --> 03:20:36.424
get yourself Fanta orange and Sprite.

03:20:36.424 --> 03:20:39.060
We have Coke Zero.

03:20:39.060 --> 03:20:40.428
It's supposed to be Zero,

03:20:40.428 --> 03:20:42.930
but they gave us just normal Coke.

03:20:42.930 --> 03:20:45.600
Next, we have ginger ale.

03:20:45.600 --> 03:20:47.101
Canada Dry.

03:20:47.101 --> 03:20:50.538
Canada is an amazing country, eh?

03:20:50.538 --> 03:20:51.973
Qoo orange juice.

03:20:52.807 --> 03:20:55.510
And here is Sokenbicha.

03:20:55.510 --> 03:20:57.678
It's Japanese blended tea.

03:20:57.678 --> 03:21:01.716
And last one, we've got Georgia Japan

03:21:01.716 --> 03:21:04.052
Craftsman café latte.

03:21:04.052 --> 03:21:05.653
Georgia Japan.

03:21:05.653 --> 03:21:08.089
Sounds like George Japan.

03:21:08.089 --> 03:21:10.024
I'd like to be sponsored by you.

03:21:10.024 --> 03:21:11.526
Let me try this.

03:21:13.761 --> 03:21:17.065
It's got a lot of milk and sugar in it.

03:21:17.065 --> 03:21:18.199
I gotta be honest.

03:21:18.199 --> 03:21:19.700
It's not my taste.

03:21:23.638 --> 03:21:24.505
Take two.

03:21:26.207 --> 03:21:27.842
I really love this.

03:21:27.842 --> 03:21:30.445
Please give me a sponsorship.

03:21:32.613 --> 03:21:34.348
A Japan large hand-tossed pizza

03:21:34.348 --> 03:21:36.984
is 130 calories per slice,

03:21:36.984 --> 03:21:41.589
or 1,560 calories for the full pizza.

03:21:41.589 --> 03:21:45.593
In the US, a large hand-tossed
pizza slice is 280 calories,

03:21:45.593 --> 03:21:50.231
which makes the entire
pizza 2,240 calories.

03:21:50.231 --> 03:21:52.567
A large big-pepperoni hand-tossed slice

03:21:52.567 --> 03:21:55.703
is 335 calories per slice,

03:21:55.703 --> 03:21:59.507
or 4,020 calories for the entire pizza.

03:21:59.507 --> 03:22:03.044
Our large pepperoni is
370 calories per slice,

03:22:03.044 --> 03:22:07.115
which makes the entire pie 2,960 calories.

03:22:07.115 --> 03:22:09.584
Japan's most calorific pizza is

03:22:09.584 --> 03:22:12.186
the ultra cheese New Yorker size.

03:22:12.186 --> 03:22:15.590
One slice is 478 calories.

03:22:15.590 --> 03:22:19.994
That's 3,827 for the full pizza.

03:22:19.994 --> 03:22:21.195
Ah.

03:22:21.195 --> 03:22:23.564
Our US Domino's pizza
with the most calories

03:22:23.564 --> 03:22:26.534
is the Cali chicken bacon ranch.

03:22:26.534 --> 03:22:28.436
This is an XL of said pizza.

03:22:28.436 --> 03:22:31.072
One slice is 560 calories,

03:22:31.072 --> 03:22:35.943
and that makes the full
pie 3,360 calories.

03:22:35.943 --> 03:22:40.781
Our large plain pizza
has 1,620 calories total.

03:22:40.781 --> 03:22:43.751
Our large cheese is 2,240 calories.

03:22:43.751 --> 03:22:46.821
That's a 38.2% increase.

03:22:46.821 --> 03:22:51.325
Our large big pepperoni is 2,680 calories,

03:22:51.325 --> 03:22:55.096
over 34% of your daily
recommended calorie intake.

03:22:55.096 --> 03:22:58.966
333% of your daily sodium.

03:22:58.966 --> 03:23:00.434
Ah!

03:23:00.434 --> 03:23:03.004
Too many tasty calories!

03:23:03.004 --> 03:23:05.173
Ours is 2,960 calories,

03:23:05.173 --> 03:23:09.544
48% over your daily recommended amount,

03:23:09.544 --> 03:23:11.979
but somehow ours has less sodium,

03:23:11.979 --> 03:23:15.850
only 299% of your daily sodium.

03:23:18.019 --> 03:23:19.120
In October of last year,

03:23:19.120 --> 03:23:22.390
a study found detectable
amounts of phthalate,

03:23:22.390 --> 03:23:24.559
a plastic softener, in common menu items

03:23:24.559 --> 03:23:27.662
from large fast-food
chains, including Domino's.

03:23:30.431 --> 03:23:33.334
The study analyzed 64 food samples

03:23:33.334 --> 03:23:35.269
from several popular fast-food chains

03:23:35.269 --> 03:23:40.208
and found phthalates DnBP and DEHP

03:23:40.208 --> 03:23:42.310
in a majority of the items.

03:23:42.310 --> 03:23:44.845
USA Today reported that,
"Food containing meat,

03:23:44.845 --> 03:23:46.747
such as chicken burritos
and cheeseburgers,

03:23:46.747 --> 03:23:49.050
had higher levels of
the chemicals studied,

03:23:49.050 --> 03:23:51.352
while cheese pizza had the lowest levels."

03:23:51.352 --> 03:23:53.721
OK, so that's good news
for Domino's, I guess.

03:23:53.721 --> 03:23:56.657
The study goes on to say
that "food handling gloves

03:23:56.657 --> 03:23:59.460
contain replacement plasticizers,

03:23:59.460 --> 03:24:02.096
which may be [a] source
of food contamination."

03:24:02.096 --> 03:24:03.631
Sounds to me like an easy fix.

03:24:03.631 --> 03:24:06.100
Just prepare the food without gloves.

03:24:06.100 --> 03:24:10.671
Japan has a ban on DEHP
in food-handling gloves.

03:24:10.671 --> 03:24:12.873
Good-er news, if you're
a fan of "Food Wars"

03:24:12.873 --> 03:24:15.443
and saw the US versus UK Domino's episode,

03:24:15.443 --> 03:24:19.447
we highlighted BHA and
BHT in the US pepperoni.

03:24:19.447 --> 03:24:23.084
Well, on the stewardship
page on Domino's website,

03:24:23.084 --> 03:24:24.819
they have stated, ahem,

03:24:24.819 --> 03:24:26.087
"We have eliminated a long list

03:24:26.087 --> 03:24:27.722
of ingredients from all
of our core products

03:24:27.722 --> 03:24:31.626
including BHA and BHT and PHOs,

03:24:31.626 --> 03:24:34.762
as well as trans-fat from
core pizza products,"

03:24:34.762 --> 03:24:36.430
which is fantastic news.

03:24:36.430 --> 03:24:38.332
I clearly was going to eat it anyway,

03:24:38.332 --> 03:24:40.167
but thank you regardless.

03:24:40.568 --> 03:24:42.703
From calorie
count to portion sizes,

03:24:42.703 --> 03:24:44.572
we wanted to find out all the differences

03:24:44.572 --> 03:24:47.375
between Pocky in Japan and the US.

03:24:47.375 --> 03:24:48.976
This is "Food Wars."

03:24:52.913 --> 03:24:56.350
In Japan, our Pocky comes in a 72-gram box

03:24:56.350 --> 03:25:00.821
which contains two
packets and a nine-pack.

03:25:01.722 --> 03:25:03.457
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

03:25:03.457 --> 03:25:05.926
- Our Pocky's come in
basically three sizes.

03:25:05.926 --> 03:25:09.930
The one 1.14-ounce box,
the 2.47-ounce box,

03:25:09.930 --> 03:25:14.502
and the 4.13-ounce boxy bag.

03:25:14.502 --> 03:25:16.871
But our strawberry-flavored box is smaller

03:25:16.871 --> 03:25:18.039
than this chocolate box.

03:25:18.039 --> 03:25:20.741
This is a 3.81-ounce box,

03:25:20.741 --> 03:25:24.011
which is 0.32 ounces
smaller than this one.

03:25:24.011 --> 03:25:27.281
Largest box bag is this,
the Cookies &amp; Cream flavor,

03:25:27.281 --> 03:25:30.418
which is 4.57 ounces

03:25:30.418 --> 03:25:35.423
or 0.44 grams larger
than the chocolate box.

03:25:35.423 --> 03:25:36.924
One theory, my theory,

03:25:36.924 --> 03:25:39.660
is that the Pocky boxes
contain a specific number

03:25:39.660 --> 03:25:40.661
of Pocky sticks

03:25:40.661 --> 03:25:43.898
and each Pocky is a different weight

03:25:43.898 --> 03:25:46.000
based on the flavor coating.

03:25:46.000 --> 03:25:49.036
So we're gonna weigh
each Pocky individually

03:25:49.036 --> 03:25:50.604
to see if this is true.

03:25:50.604 --> 03:25:52.907
All right, chocolate first.

03:25:52.907 --> 03:25:57.511
So seven of these are 13 grams.
Can someone write that down?

03:25:57.511 --> 03:26:02.249
Strawberry, seven is 13 grams.

03:26:02.249 --> 03:26:04.952
Was that what the first one was? Okay.

03:26:04.952 --> 03:26:06.354
Cookies &amp; Cream!

03:26:06.354 --> 03:26:10.558
Cookies &amp; Cream, seven
of them are 18 grams.

03:26:10.558 --> 03:26:12.993
Well, the Cookies &amp; Cream ones
are definitely a lot heavier.

03:26:12.993 --> 03:26:13.828
A lot heavier.

03:26:13.828 --> 03:26:16.797
(Joe chomping)

03:26:16.797 --> 03:26:17.865
Mm!

03:26:17.865 --> 03:26:20.935
- So let's see how many
Pocky are in a box.

03:26:20.935 --> 03:26:24.705
(George counting in Japanese)

03:26:24.705 --> 03:26:28.476
(audio chirping)

03:26:28.476 --> 03:26:33.147
32, 33, 34.

03:26:33.147 --> 03:26:35.483
Thirty-four Pocky in total.

03:26:35.483 --> 03:26:37.752
So one packet has 17 Pocky

03:26:37.752 --> 03:26:40.855
and another one also has 17 Pocky.

03:26:40.855 --> 03:26:42.757
- Let's see how many
Pocky's are in this box.

03:26:42.757 --> 03:26:45.593
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

03:26:45.593 --> 03:26:47.094
(exhales) Oh, man.

03:26:49.930 --> 03:26:50.765
Is this normal?

03:26:51.599 --> 03:26:52.433
I think I can kind of like,

03:26:52.433 --> 03:26:55.669
do you wanna get a
close-up on there before?

03:26:55.669 --> 03:26:57.671
So one, two, three, those
are the broken ones.

03:26:57.671 --> 03:26:59.407
(audio chirping)

03:26:59.407 --> 03:27:04.412
30, 31, 32, 33, 34, 35, 36.

03:27:04.545 --> 03:27:05.746
You know how everyone
was complaining about

03:27:05.746 --> 03:27:08.349
how I eat Kit-Kats in the Kit-Kat episode?

03:27:08.349 --> 03:27:10.418
(suspenseful music)

03:27:10.418 --> 03:27:12.753
(Joe chomps)

03:27:12.753 --> 03:27:14.655
(Joe chewing)

03:27:14.655 --> 03:27:16.857
Mm!

03:27:16.857 --> 03:27:19.059
(upbeat music)

03:27:19.059 --> 03:27:21.195
Here's all the Pocky's
that are native to the US

03:27:21.195 --> 03:27:22.897
that are not in Japan.

03:27:22.897 --> 03:27:26.066
- And here are all the
Pocky's native to Japan.

03:27:26.066 --> 03:27:29.570
- Cookies &amp; Cream, Cookies &amp; Cream.

03:27:29.570 --> 03:27:31.439
Not a solid block, so that's good.

03:27:31.439 --> 03:27:33.941
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

03:27:33.941 --> 03:27:34.942
(Joe chomping)

03:27:34.942 --> 03:27:38.579
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

03:27:38.579 --> 03:27:40.147
Mm!

03:27:40.147 --> 03:27:40.981
I like those.

03:27:40.981 --> 03:27:42.583
This looks like fun, Yuelei.

03:27:42.583 --> 03:27:44.518
Chocolate Banana, have
you had these before?

03:27:44.518 --> 03:27:45.352
You have?

03:27:46.253 --> 03:27:47.888
No, mm-mm.

03:27:47.888 --> 03:27:49.790
That banana flavor hits right away.

03:27:51.859 --> 03:27:52.726
Oh, no.

03:27:53.894 --> 03:27:55.129
Matcha green tea.

03:27:55.129 --> 03:27:57.064
Any "Food Wars" heads watching know,

03:27:57.965 --> 03:27:59.266
Joe does not like matcha.

03:28:00.234 --> 03:28:03.137
Mm, smells like a freshly-cut lawn.

03:28:03.137 --> 03:28:04.071
(lawnmower rumbles)

03:28:04.071 --> 03:28:06.073
(Joe chomps)

03:28:06.073 --> 03:28:07.775
Yeah, nah.

03:28:07.775 --> 03:28:09.877
There's also a Crunchy Strawberry
flavor you can get here

03:28:09.877 --> 03:28:10.711
in the US,

03:28:10.711 --> 03:28:12.513
but I was not able to get my hands on it

03:28:12.513 --> 03:28:15.082
by the time of filming this episode.

03:28:15.082 --> 03:28:18.886
So here's just regular strawberry.

03:28:18.886 --> 03:28:19.720
Uh-oh.

03:28:19.720 --> 03:28:23.190
Oh, another solid block.

03:28:23.190 --> 03:28:24.024
Yeah.

03:28:26.794 --> 03:28:28.496
(Joe chomps)
(audience gasps)

03:28:28.496 --> 03:28:30.831
Mm, yeah, dude.

03:28:30.831 --> 03:28:32.900
Put me in jail for crimes against Pocky's.

03:28:34.168 --> 03:28:35.002
- George's energy.

03:28:35.002 --> 03:28:37.071
Bong, let's go!

03:28:37.071 --> 03:28:39.540
All right, let's start with this one.

03:28:39.540 --> 03:28:42.576
We have Pocky Luxury Milk Chocolate.

03:28:44.879 --> 03:28:47.248
(laughs) Is it Pocky?

03:28:47.248 --> 03:28:49.416
You look like corn dog.

03:28:49.416 --> 03:28:50.851
What happened to you?

03:28:53.153 --> 03:28:53.988
Hmm.

03:28:55.689 --> 03:29:00.427
It's got milk and fermented butter flavor.

03:29:00.427 --> 03:29:02.997
And we have another corn dog.

03:29:02.997 --> 03:29:05.466
It's a Almond Milk flavor.

03:29:05.466 --> 03:29:07.535
(George speaks in Japanese)

03:29:09.436 --> 03:29:11.005
Mm.

03:29:11.005 --> 03:29:13.807
It has strong almond milk flavor.

03:29:13.807 --> 03:29:16.944
I prefer this one, the milk chocolate,

03:29:16.944 --> 03:29:19.013
but both are so short.

03:29:19.013 --> 03:29:19.847
You should be longer.

03:29:19.847 --> 03:29:20.781
(whistle screeches)

03:29:20.781 --> 03:29:21.749
You too!

03:29:21.749 --> 03:29:24.585
We have this ultra-thin Pocky.

03:29:25.753 --> 03:29:28.389
Oh. (laughs)

03:29:28.389 --> 03:29:31.825
You are so thin this time.

03:29:31.825 --> 03:29:33.727
This one is short.

03:29:33.727 --> 03:29:35.062
This one is so thin.

03:29:37.898 --> 03:29:40.134
We have Tasty.

03:29:40.134 --> 03:29:41.669
Why is it Tasty?

03:29:41.669 --> 03:29:45.706
Oh, fermented butter
is used for this stick.

03:29:47.308 --> 03:29:48.142
Ooh.

03:29:49.510 --> 03:29:51.111
(George chomps)

03:29:51.111 --> 03:29:54.615
It's got just a little
bit of butter flavor.

03:29:54.615 --> 03:29:58.285
I still prefer this one, this corn dog.

03:29:58.285 --> 03:30:00.120
Almond Crush.

03:30:00.120 --> 03:30:02.856
It's a little different.
Look at the packets.

03:30:05.059 --> 03:30:07.795
Yeah, obviously, it's got almonds.

03:30:07.795 --> 03:30:09.263
Okey-dokey, Pocky.

03:30:09.263 --> 03:30:11.165
(George speaks in Japanese)

03:30:12.333 --> 03:30:13.334
I love this.

03:30:14.668 --> 03:30:17.037
I love this.

03:30:17.037 --> 03:30:18.038
Mm.

03:30:18.038 --> 03:30:21.275
We've got Pocky Chocolate Coconut.

03:30:21.275 --> 03:30:26.146
Oh, this one is also
this style of packets.

03:30:27.948 --> 03:30:29.416
Oh.

03:30:29.416 --> 03:30:32.586
It's pretty similar with
this one, Almond Crush.

03:30:33.754 --> 03:30:35.623
(George chomps)

03:30:35.623 --> 03:30:36.924
Hmm?

03:30:36.924 --> 03:30:39.793
Yeah, obviously, it's got coconut flavor,

03:30:39.793 --> 03:30:43.263
and also, it's got a
little bit of saltiness.

03:30:43.263 --> 03:30:44.465
It's not my taste.

03:30:44.465 --> 03:30:47.234
Strawberry chocolate Pocky.

03:30:47.234 --> 03:30:49.403
(George chomps)

03:30:49.403 --> 03:30:50.237
Oh.

03:30:51.205 --> 03:30:52.039
Ah.

03:30:52.873 --> 03:30:56.644
Right after you bite this,
you get some sweetness.

03:30:56.644 --> 03:30:58.812
But after that, you get sourness.

03:30:58.812 --> 03:31:00.247
It smells so strong.

03:31:02.082 --> 03:31:04.151
I can smell it from here.

03:31:04.151 --> 03:31:06.320
Cocoa powder Pocky,

03:31:06.320 --> 03:31:09.757
And it says you can only
get this in winter season.

03:31:09.757 --> 03:31:12.292
Oh yeah, look at this.
It's got cocoa powder.

03:31:15.062 --> 03:31:17.164
(George speaks in Japanese)

03:31:17.164 --> 03:31:18.699
(George's lips smack)

03:31:18.699 --> 03:31:21.902
We've got the cutest Pocky ever.

03:31:21.902 --> 03:31:23.871
Cherry heart-shaped Pocky.

03:31:24.938 --> 03:31:26.373
Aha.

03:31:27.975 --> 03:31:30.310
Oh, look at this!

03:31:30.310 --> 03:31:32.312
Heart! It's in there.

03:31:32.312 --> 03:31:33.847
How cute.

03:31:33.847 --> 03:31:36.617
And this part, cherry
chocolate is so awesome.

03:31:37.751 --> 03:31:39.853
You get strong cherry flavor.

03:31:39.853 --> 03:31:44.191
We've also got blueberry
heart-shaped chocolate Pocky.

03:31:44.191 --> 03:31:45.492
(Pocky wrapper crinkles)

03:31:45.492 --> 03:31:47.961
Ooh, look at this.

03:31:47.961 --> 03:31:49.396
So blue.

03:31:49.396 --> 03:31:53.534
This color doesn't make me want
to eat this, but let's try.

03:31:53.534 --> 03:31:56.103
(George speaks in Japanese)

03:31:56.103 --> 03:31:57.638
Ooh!

03:31:57.638 --> 03:31:58.472
Mm.

03:31:59.339 --> 03:32:01.108
So sour.

03:32:01.108 --> 03:32:03.310
But look at this heart-shaped Pocky.

03:32:04.244 --> 03:32:05.045
Not for me.

03:32:05.979 --> 03:32:10.084
This is what I've been
waiting for, sakura matcha.

03:32:10.084 --> 03:32:13.053
So "sakura" means cherry blossom.

03:32:13.053 --> 03:32:14.822
Cherry blossom matcha taste.

03:32:16.123 --> 03:32:16.957
Ooh.

03:32:18.225 --> 03:32:19.860
Look at this!

03:32:19.860 --> 03:32:22.930
So it's got matcha chocolate

03:32:22.930 --> 03:32:25.899
and this stick is pink.

03:32:25.899 --> 03:32:28.068
(George chomps)

03:32:28.068 --> 03:32:31.905
Mm, this is so Japanese-y Pocky.

03:32:31.905 --> 03:32:33.507
Just sweet matcha.

03:32:33.507 --> 03:32:35.976
The feeling of spring has come to my life.

03:32:35.976 --> 03:32:37.211
(bird chirping)

03:32:37.211 --> 03:32:38.846
Spring days here in my body.

03:32:39.880 --> 03:32:44.818
(George sings in Japanese)

03:32:44.818 --> 03:32:47.354
Everybody's curious what these are.

03:32:47.354 --> 03:32:48.756
Megami no Ruby.

03:32:48.756 --> 03:32:51.191
Otona no Kohaku.

03:32:51.191 --> 03:32:52.392
What does it mean?

03:32:52.392 --> 03:32:55.028
I don't even know. (laughs)

03:32:56.263 --> 03:32:58.465
Anyway, so it says Megami no Ruby.

03:32:58.465 --> 03:33:02.903
It means like, "Goddess Ruby".

03:33:02.903 --> 03:33:06.406
Otona no Kohaku, in
English, it says, "amber."

03:33:06.406 --> 03:33:10.210
Kind of like stone, fossil, jewel.

03:33:10.210 --> 03:33:13.380
It says it goes well with red wine.

03:33:13.380 --> 03:33:14.348
Interesting.

03:33:14.348 --> 03:33:16.116
Ta-da!

03:33:16.116 --> 03:33:19.119
It looks like regular chocolate Pocky.

03:33:19.119 --> 03:33:21.255
(George chomps)

03:33:21.255 --> 03:33:22.089
Oh?

03:33:22.956 --> 03:33:24.024
What is this?

03:33:25.893 --> 03:33:28.395
This taste itself is like berries.

03:33:28.395 --> 03:33:31.365
This one goes well with whiskey.

03:33:31.365 --> 03:33:34.067
(George chomps)

03:33:34.067 --> 03:33:34.902
Huh?

03:33:35.936 --> 03:33:39.273
It's pretty close to dark
chocolate, it's bitter.

03:33:39.273 --> 03:33:42.543
In Japan, we have this
Gokuboso extra-fine Pocky,

03:33:42.543 --> 03:33:44.511
which are roughly half the thickness

03:33:44.511 --> 03:33:46.313
of a regular chocolate Pocky.

03:33:46.313 --> 03:33:49.183
- In the US, ours are
called the Ultra Slim.

03:33:49.183 --> 03:33:51.885
- I got a new digital scale.

03:33:51.885 --> 03:33:55.556
What I'm gonna do is weigh
a regular chocolate Pocky.

03:33:55.556 --> 03:33:58.258
2.13 grams.

03:33:58.258 --> 03:34:00.427
So ultra thin Pocky.

03:34:00.427 --> 03:34:04.097
So it weighs 1.52 grams.

03:34:04.097 --> 03:34:07.034
- Thinner, that's it?

03:34:07.034 --> 03:34:07.868
Here's a big boy.

03:34:09.303 --> 03:34:10.704
Here's the thin.

03:34:10.704 --> 03:34:11.839
Is it able to do this?

03:34:11.839 --> 03:34:13.373
Can I get out of the way so
it's just the white background?

03:34:13.373 --> 03:34:18.178
23, 24, 25, and there's another
bag in here, so 50 per box.

03:34:18.178 --> 03:34:20.714
Okay, so 50 instead of 36.

03:34:20.714 --> 03:34:22.983
Seven regular Pocky's are 13 grams.

03:34:22.983 --> 03:34:26.019
Let's see how many slim ones
we needed to get to 13 grams.

03:34:26.019 --> 03:34:29.590
5, 6, 7, 8 1/2.

03:34:29.590 --> 03:34:31.792
Eight and a half slim ones are the same

03:34:31.792 --> 03:34:33.493
as seven regular ones.

03:34:33.493 --> 03:34:34.995
Is that that much slimmer?

03:34:34.995 --> 03:34:36.330
I guess that's slimmer.

03:34:36.330 --> 03:34:38.532
Does anyone think that's
not significant enough

03:34:38.532 --> 03:34:40.067
to be a selling point?

03:34:40.067 --> 03:34:42.970
Pocky adjusts its sweetness
for different countries.

03:34:42.970 --> 03:34:46.039
Not surprisingly, the US
ones are meant to be sweeter.

03:34:46.039 --> 03:34:48.141
I'm gonna do a taste test side by side.

03:34:48.141 --> 03:34:50.244
We got the American ones
and the Japanese one,

03:34:50.244 --> 03:34:52.713
and we're gonna see just
how different they taste.

03:34:52.713 --> 03:34:56.183
I'm worried that these are
also gonna be a Pocky popsicle.

03:34:56.183 --> 03:34:57.017
Oh no, okay.

03:34:58.151 --> 03:34:59.519
Japanese.

03:34:59.519 --> 03:35:00.821
These are only Japanese ones I can find.

03:35:00.821 --> 03:35:04.024
Obviously, they're bigger. I
don't know if this is the norm.

03:35:04.024 --> 03:35:05.325
(Joe chomps)

03:35:05.325 --> 03:35:08.061
Mm-hm, in the baseline sweetness.

03:35:11.798 --> 03:35:13.333
Yeah.

03:35:13.333 --> 03:35:14.134
Mm.

03:35:15.269 --> 03:35:17.671
(Joe chomps)

03:35:19.840 --> 03:35:21.942
Yeah, it's noticeably different.

03:35:21.942 --> 03:35:26.947
They taste identical, but
ours has a sweet aftertaste.

03:35:27.481 --> 03:35:29.549
I like the Japanese ones much better.

03:35:29.549 --> 03:35:33.086
- So Pocky is in the Guinness
World Records three times.

03:35:33.086 --> 03:35:35.923
It's the largest
chocolate-coated biscuits brand,

03:35:35.923 --> 03:35:37.824
has the most mentions of a brand name

03:35:37.824 --> 03:35:40.160
on Twitter in 24 hours,

03:35:40.160 --> 03:35:45.032
which was 3,710,044 times.

03:35:45.032 --> 03:35:46.066
And finally, it was part

03:35:46.066 --> 03:35:49.202
of the most people opening
packaged food online

03:35:49.202 --> 03:35:52.973
simultaneously with 143 people.

03:35:52.973 --> 03:35:55.208
- 143 people, that's it?

03:35:55.208 --> 03:35:56.843
That doesn't seem like that many.

03:35:56.843 --> 03:35:58.845
I feel like I've been on Zoom work calls

03:35:58.845 --> 03:36:02.482
with 143 people in it, right?

03:36:02.482 --> 03:36:05.285
It would've been literally
one email to set that up.

03:36:05.285 --> 03:36:06.586
- I can do (George speaks in Japanese).

03:36:08.789 --> 03:36:12.626
Pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom-pom.

03:36:12.626 --> 03:36:17.064
Now I got more than 200
George's clones right here.

03:36:17.064 --> 03:36:20.067
Simultaneously, three, two, one.

03:36:20.067 --> 03:36:20.901
Boom.

03:36:22.736 --> 03:36:26.039
Now I broke the Guinness World Records.

03:36:26.039 --> 03:36:28.875
So November 11th is known as
a Pocky (speaks in Japanese)

03:36:28.875 --> 03:36:31.044
or Pocky Day in Japan.

03:36:31.044 --> 03:36:34.614
This date was chosen because
a Pocky is shaped like a one.

03:36:34.614 --> 03:36:38.352
At November 11th, visually,
it looks like four Pocky.

03:36:38.352 --> 03:36:41.922
And also, Pretz are included
in this day, November 11th,

03:36:41.922 --> 03:36:44.024
which is the pretzel version of Pocky.

03:36:44.024 --> 03:36:47.694
And in Japan, you can get
them in flavors like Salad,

03:36:47.694 --> 03:36:52.699
Ripe Tomato, Sweet Potato,
and Roasted Bread flavor.

03:36:52.933 --> 03:36:54.735
In the US, we also have Pretz,

03:36:54.735 --> 03:36:59.172
and we get these fun flavors
like Sweet Corn, fun,

03:36:59.172 --> 03:37:01.174
and Pizza.

03:37:01.174 --> 03:37:02.342
Oh, God.

03:37:04.244 --> 03:37:05.612
It has nothing on it.

03:37:05.612 --> 03:37:06.847
(Joe chomps)

03:37:06.847 --> 03:37:07.748
Nope.

03:37:07.748 --> 03:37:11.718
I mean, yeah, it tastes like corn.

03:37:11.718 --> 03:37:12.719
Why though?

03:37:12.719 --> 03:37:16.723
What is the demand for
corn-flavored sticks?

03:37:16.723 --> 03:37:18.058
(Joe sighs)

03:37:18.058 --> 03:37:21.361
Besides pizza, anything
flavored like pizza is terrible.

03:37:21.361 --> 03:37:23.363
Even pizza combos aren't very good.

03:37:23.363 --> 03:37:25.132
(Pretz wrapper crinkles)

03:37:25.132 --> 03:37:26.166
No.

03:37:26.166 --> 03:37:28.235
(Joe chomps)

03:37:28.235 --> 03:37:30.037
I mean, it's up there with croutons.

03:37:30.037 --> 03:37:33.507
Does anyone grab a handful
of croutons on-the-go?

03:37:33.507 --> 03:37:35.142
And would just eating a box of croutons.

03:37:35.142 --> 03:37:37.310
These probably would be good on something.

03:37:37.310 --> 03:37:40.313
(catchy music)

03:37:40.313 --> 03:37:42.516
- In Japan, our chocolate Pocky box,

03:37:42.516 --> 03:37:45.652
per 100 grams, has 506 calories.

03:37:45.652 --> 03:37:48.522
Adjusted for the box size, 72 grams,

03:37:48.522 --> 03:37:53.093
the package contains 364.3 calories.

03:37:53.093 --> 03:37:56.730
And let's break it down
even further to per Pocky.

03:37:56.730 --> 03:38:01.501
One Pocky contains, on
average, 11.38 calories.

03:38:01.501 --> 03:38:06.473
- A US chocolate Pocky
box contains 340 calories.

03:38:06.473 --> 03:38:09.276
Just a little bit less
than a Japanese box,

03:38:09.276 --> 03:38:11.144
but note, there is a two-gram difference.

03:38:11.144 --> 03:38:14.247
Now here at "Food Wars", we
thrive on scientific accuracy.

03:38:14.247 --> 03:38:16.450
So let's break it down per Pocky.

03:38:16.450 --> 03:38:21.421
One US Pocky is 9.44444444444444444...

03:38:25.892 --> 03:38:27.094
calories.

03:38:27.094 --> 03:38:30.764
- The highest-calorie Pocky
in Japan is to be determined.

03:38:30.764 --> 03:38:32.599
We emailed the customer service,

03:38:32.599 --> 03:38:35.535
but we didn't get their response.

03:38:35.535 --> 03:38:37.604
What are you doing? Hurry up!

03:38:37.604 --> 03:38:42.609
But I guess this Pocky is
the most calorific Pocky.

03:38:42.642 --> 03:38:45.979
It's 196 calories.

03:38:45.979 --> 03:38:49.516
So it should be 'cause it's
got a lot of butter in it.

03:38:49.516 --> 03:38:50.884
- The US Pocky

03:38:50.884 --> 03:38:53.954
with the most calories
is the Cookies &amp; Cream.

03:38:53.954 --> 03:38:57.624
It contains total 630 calories.

03:38:57.624 --> 03:38:59.826
There's no question I
can murder this whole box

03:38:59.826 --> 03:39:01.094
in one sitting.

03:39:01.094 --> 03:39:02.562
630 calories? That's nothing.

03:39:02.562 --> 03:39:05.732
That's kind of reassuring
like, "Wow, only 630?

03:39:05.732 --> 03:39:07.134
Found my breakfast!"

03:39:07.134 --> 03:39:10.203
(steady music)

03:39:10.203 --> 03:39:12.639
- Japa-Pocky contains these ingredients.

03:39:12.639 --> 03:39:16.877
Wheat flour, sugar, cacao
mass, vegetable oils,

03:39:16.877 --> 03:39:20.413
whole-milk powder,
shortening, malt extract,

03:39:20.413 --> 03:39:25.085
starch, salt, yeast, cocoa powder, butter,

03:39:25.085 --> 03:39:29.589
emulsifier, flavoring, leavening
agent, annatto coloring,

03:39:29.589 --> 03:39:31.158
and mineral salt.

03:39:31.158 --> 03:39:34.895
- Any US Pocky contains
wheat flour, sugar,

03:39:34.895 --> 03:39:37.063
chocolate liquor, blend of vegetable oils,

03:39:37.063 --> 03:39:39.900
that blend being sunflower oil, palm oil,

03:39:39.900 --> 03:39:42.435
whole-milk powder,
vegetable oil shortening,

03:39:42.435 --> 03:39:45.672
which is palm oil, hydrogenated
palm oil, and cocoa butter,

03:39:45.672 --> 03:39:48.942
salt, artificial flavors,
yeast, soy lecithin,

03:39:48.942 --> 03:39:50.877
leavening, sodium bicarbonate,

03:39:50.877 --> 03:39:55.215
mono- and diglycerides of fatty acids.

03:39:55.215 --> 03:39:56.683
Wink.

03:39:56.683 --> 03:39:59.519
- In Japan, our Pocky
contains malt extract,

03:39:59.519 --> 03:40:01.721
which is sometimes used as a replacement

03:40:01.721 --> 03:40:03.223
for sugar in baking.

03:40:03.223 --> 03:40:05.091
It contains lots of maltose,

03:40:05.091 --> 03:40:06.226
a type of sugar

03:40:06.226 --> 03:40:08.995
which actually has a
higher glycemic index value

03:40:08.995 --> 03:40:10.230
than normal sucrose.

03:40:10.230 --> 03:40:13.133
So it's a surprise that
American Pocky are supposed

03:40:13.133 --> 03:40:14.634
to be sweeter.

03:40:14.634 --> 03:40:16.836
- There are actually differences
in the types of cocoa used.

03:40:16.836 --> 03:40:19.439
If you've watched the "US
versus UK Snickers" episode,

03:40:19.439 --> 03:40:22.676
you know that American
chocolate is not so great.

03:40:22.676 --> 03:40:25.612
In the US, our Pockys are
made with chocolate liquor

03:40:25.612 --> 03:40:27.013
and cocoa butter.

03:40:27.013 --> 03:40:29.449
Chocolate liquor is just
cocoa that's been processed

03:40:29.449 --> 03:40:30.750
into semisolid form,

03:40:30.750 --> 03:40:34.621
and it's actually around
50% cocoa butter itself.

03:40:34.621 --> 03:40:36.089
The trouble is for an American product

03:40:36.089 --> 03:40:37.824
to be classified as milk chocolate,

03:40:37.824 --> 03:40:41.294
it only needs to contain
around 10% of chocolate liquor,

03:40:41.294 --> 03:40:43.330
and the rest can be made up of sugars

03:40:43.330 --> 03:40:45.031
and various ingredients.

03:40:45.031 --> 03:40:47.133
- In Japan, the rules are different,

03:40:47.133 --> 03:40:49.135
depending on the type of product.

03:40:49.135 --> 03:40:51.104
Milk chocolate material must contain

03:40:51.104 --> 03:40:54.174
at least 21% cocoa content,

03:40:54.174 --> 03:40:56.610
double the required amount in America.

03:40:56.610 --> 03:40:59.112
So our chocolate has more chocolate.

03:40:59.112 --> 03:41:00.647
Are you jealous of us?

03:41:00.647 --> 03:41:01.681
Come to Japan.

03:41:03.116 --> 03:41:05.151
George: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

03:41:05.151 --> 03:41:06.987
we wanted to find out all the differences

03:41:06.987 --> 03:41:09.889
between 7-Eleven in Japan and the US.

03:41:09.889 --> 03:41:11.992
This is "Food Wars."

03:41:14.060 --> 03:41:15.562
In Japan, our coffees come in regular --

03:41:15.562 --> 03:41:17.264
Joe: In small, medium,

03:41:17.264 --> 03:41:18.398
large,
George: And large.

03:41:18.398 --> 03:41:19.833
and extra large.

03:41:19.833 --> 03:41:21.368
If you're getting coffee,

03:41:21.368 --> 03:41:22.869
why not grab a chocolate doughnut?

03:41:25.505 --> 03:41:29.576
Our 7-Eleven drinks come in
sizes of 200 milliliters,

03:41:29.576 --> 03:41:31.144
450 milliliters,

03:41:31.144 --> 03:41:32.279
and 1 liter,

03:41:32.279 --> 03:41:34.748
and 1.5 liters.

03:41:34.748 --> 03:41:36.283
I'm sorry, I couldn't get it.

03:41:36.283 --> 03:41:39.786
[laughing maniacally]

03:41:43.556 --> 03:41:45.191
In the US, we have Big Gulps,

03:41:45.191 --> 03:41:48.228
self-service fountain drink for sodas,

03:41:48.228 --> 03:41:50.497
and they come in these four sizes:

03:41:50.497 --> 03:41:53.533
medium, large, extra large,

03:41:53.533 --> 03:41:55.368
double extra large.
[air horn rings]

03:41:55.368 --> 03:41:58.672
So, I want to see how
much the biggest-size cup

03:41:58.672 --> 03:42:00.573
I could get at the 7-Eleven is.

03:42:00.573 --> 03:42:03.410
And to do that, I will need, hang on ...

03:42:04.411 --> 03:42:05.945
It's just past 40.

03:42:05.945 --> 03:42:07.714
It's exactly 48 ounces.

03:42:07.714 --> 03:42:10.050
That's hardly double extra.

03:42:10.050 --> 03:42:12.152
I'll round it up, 'cause
of this section here.

03:42:12.152 --> 03:42:13.386
I'll round it up to 50.

03:42:13.386 --> 03:42:17.357
7-Eleven also at one point offered a size

03:42:17.357 --> 03:42:20.160
that was even bigger,
called the Team Gulp,

03:42:20.160 --> 03:42:22.195
which, again, according to them,

03:42:22.195 --> 03:42:24.831
was 128 fluid ounces

03:42:24.831 --> 03:42:27.367
for your team,

03:42:27.367 --> 03:42:30.704
'cause who doesn't like
to, after a softball game,

03:42:30.704 --> 03:42:34.307
go to 7-Eleven, get a
Team Gulp and 10 straws?

03:42:34.307 --> 03:42:37.110
You know, just kick it
with the boys, right?

03:42:37.110 --> 03:42:38.244
Come on, team.

03:42:38.244 --> 03:42:41.247
Yeah, right. That's for one
person, don't be ridiculous.

03:42:42.949 --> 03:42:47.020
Here are many, many, many 7-Eleven items

03:42:47.020 --> 03:42:48.888
you can get in the US
you can't get in Japan.

03:42:48.888 --> 03:42:51.624
And here are many of the 7-Eleven items

03:42:51.624 --> 03:42:53.193
exclusive to Japan.

03:42:53.193 --> 03:42:56.996
Japan puts the "convenience"
in the convenience store.

03:42:56.996 --> 03:42:58.732
We call it konbini,

03:42:58.732 --> 03:43:01.334
which is the abbreviation
of the convenience store,

03:43:01.334 --> 03:43:03.670
and it makes our life a lot easier.

03:43:03.670 --> 03:43:07.240
For example, office workers
rely on stores like 7-Eleven

03:43:07.240 --> 03:43:09.676
for food and drink to keep them happy

03:43:09.676 --> 03:43:12.379
so that they can be productive at work.

03:43:12.379 --> 03:43:15.715
And for students, they tend
to buy juices and snacks

03:43:15.715 --> 03:43:18.351
and hot foods, instant noodles, you know.

03:43:18.351 --> 03:43:21.321
And when I was a kid, I would often eat

03:43:21.321 --> 03:43:23.022
hot foods and instant noodles

03:43:23.022 --> 03:43:27.761
with my friends and
with my ex-girlfriends.

03:43:27.761 --> 03:43:29.863
7-Eleven memories.

03:43:33.199 --> 03:43:35.101
And for families, there is pretty much

03:43:35.101 --> 03:43:37.337
every daily essential they may need.

03:43:37.337 --> 03:43:39.205
And also you can pay your bills,

03:43:39.205 --> 03:43:42.175
get ticket reservations
for music and sports,

03:43:42.175 --> 03:43:46.012
7-Eleven even has its own bank and ATMs.

03:43:46.012 --> 03:43:49.282
No matter where you go, especially
in big cities like Tokyo,

03:43:49.282 --> 03:43:53.086
you can find more than one
konbini on every block.

03:43:53.086 --> 03:43:55.188
Yeah, it's a bit different here in the US.

03:43:55.188 --> 03:43:57.757
I do frequent 7-Eleven, and it's not bad,

03:43:57.757 --> 03:43:59.426
but the vibe is more kind of like

03:43:59.426 --> 03:44:01.561
get the thing you need and go.

03:44:01.561 --> 03:44:04.564
The food is usually pretty hit or miss,

03:44:04.564 --> 03:44:06.699
usually miss in my experience.

03:44:06.699 --> 03:44:08.802
The hot food looks like it's
been sitting out for a while,

03:44:08.802 --> 03:44:10.437
so I usually don't get it.

03:44:10.437 --> 03:44:13.573
Since there are way too many
items exclusive to Japan

03:44:13.573 --> 03:44:15.975
for us to buy for one episode,

03:44:15.975 --> 03:44:19.212
so I've curated some of
my favorites for you guys.

03:44:19.212 --> 03:44:21.448
This is still a ton of food.

03:44:21.448 --> 03:44:24.651
So, here we have Japanese onigiris.

03:44:24.651 --> 03:44:26.419
This one is plum,

03:44:26.419 --> 03:44:27.754
tuna mayonnaise,

03:44:27.754 --> 03:44:29.622
shrimp and mayonnaise,

03:44:29.622 --> 03:44:32.892
mentaiko, which is spicy cod roe.

03:44:32.892 --> 03:44:35.261
I picked these onigiris from the back,

03:44:35.261 --> 03:44:39.799
because onigiri in the
back are fresh of all time.

03:44:39.799 --> 03:44:42.035
And let me show you how to open this one.

03:44:42.035 --> 03:44:46.339
Just pull this over till here ...

03:44:50.076 --> 03:44:52.979
Like this, so that you can have

03:44:52.979 --> 03:44:54.981
the dried seaweed.

03:44:56.850 --> 03:44:57.851
Itadakimasu.

03:44:59.919 --> 03:45:04.090
Mm, a little bit sweet,
a little bit of sour.

03:45:04.090 --> 03:45:07.260
So, here is our sushi.

03:45:07.260 --> 03:45:10.830
Look at this huge salmon sushi.

03:45:10.830 --> 03:45:12.165
Ah!

03:45:12.165 --> 03:45:14.868
Gorgeous. Gorgeous sushi.

03:45:14.868 --> 03:45:16.069
Itadakimasu.

03:45:16.069 --> 03:45:17.871
Oh, my God, this is so delicious.

03:45:18.972 --> 03:45:19.806
Mm.

03:45:23.543 --> 03:45:24.744
Osushi!

03:45:25.612 --> 03:45:29.082
We've got this long natto roll.

03:45:31.317 --> 03:45:33.253
Personally, I love natto.

03:45:33.253 --> 03:45:35.555
But even Japanese people,

03:45:35.555 --> 03:45:40.360
50% of them like it, 50%
of them don't like it.

03:45:40.360 --> 03:45:42.729
This is an acquired taste.

03:45:46.232 --> 03:45:48.835
So, after this sticky
and smelly natto roll,

03:45:48.835 --> 03:45:52.472
I've got sushi roll special package.

03:45:52.472 --> 03:45:55.408
So when it comes to this
one, it's called oinarisan.

03:45:55.408 --> 03:45:57.010
It has rice inside,

03:45:57.010 --> 03:45:59.979
and the skin is a sweet tofu skin.

03:46:02.849 --> 03:46:03.783
Mm!

03:46:03.783 --> 03:46:06.819
I'll admit, oinarisan umai wa.

03:46:06.819 --> 03:46:08.521
This is so good.

03:46:08.521 --> 03:46:11.024
So, my grandma always cooked this for me.

03:46:11.024 --> 03:46:14.827
And this makes me happy all the time.

03:46:14.827 --> 03:46:19.799
And next to oinarisan,
this gorgeous sushi roll,

03:46:19.799 --> 03:46:23.570
it's like Japanese version
of California roll.

03:46:23.570 --> 03:46:24.637
Itadakimasu.

03:46:26.706 --> 03:46:28.908
Wah!

03:46:28.908 --> 03:46:32.745
1,000% better than California roll.

03:46:32.745 --> 03:46:34.547
Kanpyo maki.

03:46:34.547 --> 03:46:38.551
In English it's, like, dried-gourd roll.

03:46:38.551 --> 03:46:39.552
Itadakimasu.

03:46:40.687 --> 03:46:42.088
Perfect sushi roll.

03:46:42.088 --> 03:46:45.391
And last one, we have
pickles, radish pickles.

03:46:45.391 --> 03:46:46.459
It's quite yellow.

03:46:46.459 --> 03:46:49.495
It definitely has yellow No. 5.

03:46:49.495 --> 03:46:50.730
Itadakimasu.

03:46:52.098 --> 03:46:55.101
I'm gonna give them Grammy award.

03:46:57.937 --> 03:46:59.505
And standing ovation.

03:47:01.441 --> 03:47:03.443
Ah, the hot food at a 7-Eleven in the US.

03:47:03.443 --> 03:47:06.746
We got a lot of options,
not as many as Japan.

03:47:06.746 --> 03:47:08.681
I'm not quite sure what
some of this stuff is

03:47:08.681 --> 03:47:11.117
just by looking at it, so
let me go down the list.

03:47:11.117 --> 03:47:13.286
Nachos. They're the self-service nachos,

03:47:13.286 --> 03:47:15.188
so they have the chips ready to go,

03:47:15.188 --> 03:47:16.623
and then you just open them up

03:47:16.623 --> 03:47:19.559
and add cheese and chili onto them.

03:47:21.861 --> 03:47:23.262
Ugh. No, thank you.

03:47:23.262 --> 03:47:24.897
Over here, these mini tacos.

03:47:24.897 --> 03:47:27.934
Man, these look really, like ...

03:47:28.868 --> 03:47:30.103
I bit my face.

03:47:30.970 --> 03:47:32.472
Oh, man. They've been sitting for a while,

03:47:32.472 --> 03:47:33.506
so I'll forgive them.

03:47:33.506 --> 03:47:37.510
We also have wings,
crispy and not so crispy.

03:47:37.510 --> 03:47:41.247
Pocket bean burrito guy. Look at that.

03:47:41.247 --> 03:47:44.017
Over here in the roller-taquito section,

03:47:44.017 --> 03:47:46.352
you can get a barbecue
bacon cheeseburger roller,

03:47:46.352 --> 03:47:47.920
spicy garlic roller,

03:47:47.920 --> 03:47:49.255
regular taquito,

03:47:49.255 --> 03:47:50.890
Korean barbecue taquito.

03:47:50.890 --> 03:47:52.592
Also, we have chicken sandwiches,

03:47:52.592 --> 03:47:53.893
a black bean burger,

03:47:53.893 --> 03:47:56.963
glazed cheesy barbecue meatballs.

03:47:56.963 --> 03:47:59.065
Also at our 7-Elevens, you
can get a pepperoni pizza,

03:47:59.065 --> 03:48:01.768
cheese, or seven-meat.

03:48:01.768 --> 03:48:04.771
And also for hot dogs, we got
an exclusive hot picante dog.

03:48:07.040 --> 03:48:07.874
No.

03:48:07.874 --> 03:48:10.309
So, here are our hot food sections.

03:48:10.309 --> 03:48:12.578
We've got steamed buns.

03:48:12.578 --> 03:48:15.248
It's got pork and bamboo shoots.

03:48:15.248 --> 03:48:18.651
And this is really standard nikuman.

03:48:18.651 --> 03:48:23.289
So, next size up, we
have the doubled nikuman.

03:48:23.289 --> 03:48:25.158
And next one, this little guy.

03:48:26.125 --> 03:48:27.994
What is this?

03:48:27.994 --> 03:48:29.662
Sweet beans steamed bun.

03:48:29.662 --> 03:48:34.133
And last steamed bun is pizza bun.

03:48:34.133 --> 03:48:36.869
You really are the pizza!

03:48:39.539 --> 03:48:40.640
Delicious.

03:48:40.640 --> 03:48:42.442
So, all these things, like,

03:48:42.442 --> 03:48:45.111
around 100 yen to 200 yen or so.

03:48:45.111 --> 03:48:49.449
So if you're broke, you
should definitely try this.

03:48:49.449 --> 03:48:52.985
We've got these ones.

03:48:52.985 --> 03:48:55.555
This one is called curry pan.

03:48:55.555 --> 03:48:58.057
So deep-fried curry bread.

03:48:58.057 --> 03:49:00.159
I wanna eat it. I wanna eat this!

03:49:00.159 --> 03:49:01.961
I wanna eat this right now!

03:49:01.961 --> 03:49:03.096
Itadakimasu!

03:49:06.866 --> 03:49:08.668
Holy moly.

03:49:08.668 --> 03:49:11.104
Um, it's freaking delicious.

03:49:11.104 --> 03:49:13.372
And next one, croquette.

03:49:13.372 --> 03:49:17.643
So it's basically got
potato and pork mince.

03:49:17.643 --> 03:49:21.414
And last hot food we've got is corn dog.

03:49:21.414 --> 03:49:23.816
So, this one right here is
a pretty Japanese-y one.

03:49:23.816 --> 03:49:25.885
It's got ketchup and mustard,

03:49:25.885 --> 03:49:28.721
and you just squeeze
this one onto this one.

03:49:28.721 --> 03:49:30.790
All right, let's go, let's go,

03:49:30.790 --> 03:49:32.859
let's go, let's go, let's go!

03:49:34.961 --> 03:49:37.697
In Japan, we have these chicken options.

03:49:37.697 --> 03:49:41.734
First, I'm going to start
with this one, karaage-bo.

03:49:46.706 --> 03:49:49.475
So, in Japan, when you make
Japanese fried chicken,

03:49:49.475 --> 03:49:51.244
you put some soy sauce on it.

03:49:51.244 --> 03:49:54.747
So it has soy-sauce flavor
and also garlic flavor.

03:49:54.747 --> 03:49:57.150
It's so freaking delicious.

03:49:57.150 --> 03:49:58.317
So, this karaage-bo,

03:49:58.317 --> 03:50:03.289
it's got one, two, three,

03:50:03.289 --> 03:50:05.291
and four karaages.

03:50:05.291 --> 03:50:08.261
We have fried chicken,

03:50:08.261 --> 03:50:10.329
spicy fried chicken,

03:50:10.329 --> 03:50:11.931
chicken nuggets.

03:50:11.931 --> 03:50:13.199
Hot sandwich,

03:50:13.199 --> 03:50:16.936
the Buffalo-style chicken slider.

03:50:16.936 --> 03:50:18.471
The cheeseburger

03:50:18.471 --> 03:50:20.373
and the bacon cheeseburger.

03:50:20.373 --> 03:50:22.642
Look, I mean, can you
even tell which one's,

03:50:22.642 --> 03:50:24.443
right, which one?

03:50:24.443 --> 03:50:25.278
Huh?

03:50:26.479 --> 03:50:28.815
I'm assuming, obviously,
this burger's been cooked.

03:50:30.683 --> 03:50:33.119
More on this in the ingredients section.

03:50:33.119 --> 03:50:36.589
7-Eleven in the US, and I think probably

03:50:36.589 --> 03:50:37.890
here in Southern California,

03:50:37.890 --> 03:50:39.926
has tacos and burritos.

03:50:39.926 --> 03:50:43.229
Get yourself a chicken fajita taco,

03:50:43.229 --> 03:50:44.530
al pastor taco.

03:50:44.530 --> 03:50:45.798
Bet this one's good.

03:50:45.798 --> 03:50:48.301
And a chorizo breakfast taco.

03:50:48.301 --> 03:50:51.504
The spicy beef, bean, and cheese burrito.

03:50:51.504 --> 03:50:52.905
This ain't any burrito, baby.

03:50:52.905 --> 03:50:55.975
It's The Bomb.

03:50:55.975 --> 03:50:58.044
Bombing out the toilet, good God.

03:50:58.044 --> 03:51:00.379
You're getting this and
you're microwaving it there.

03:51:00.379 --> 03:51:02.415
So if you're, like,
walking out the 7-Eleven

03:51:02.415 --> 03:51:03.549
chomping on The Bomb,

03:51:03.549 --> 03:51:05.952
like, better make it home in time.

03:51:05.952 --> 03:51:07.753
'Cause oh, man, it's coming.

03:51:07.753 --> 03:51:09.822
Empanadas, right?
Yuelei: Yeah.

03:51:09.822 --> 03:51:10.890
I don't want this.

03:51:10.890 --> 03:51:13.492
I'm gonna go ahead and put this in here

03:51:13.492 --> 03:51:14.560
and then close the lid

03:51:14.560 --> 03:51:15.995
like it's a coffin.

03:51:17.363 --> 03:51:18.431
Go away forever.

03:51:18.431 --> 03:51:21.500
All right, so here are my favorite bentos.

03:51:21.500 --> 03:51:23.236
Let's take a look at this one.

03:51:23.236 --> 03:51:25.238
It's called nori bento.

03:51:25.238 --> 03:51:27.840
This one is a pretty popular one in Japan.

03:51:27.840 --> 03:51:30.476
So it's got croquette,
a deep-fried fish cake,

03:51:30.476 --> 03:51:32.745
fried fish with tartar sauce.

03:51:32.745 --> 03:51:34.247
Kinpira gobo.

03:51:34.247 --> 03:51:36.916
It's like Japanese traditional salad.

03:51:36.916 --> 03:51:38.184
Pickles.

03:51:38.184 --> 03:51:39.385
And as you can see right here,

03:51:39.385 --> 03:51:41.487
it's got spicy cod roe.

03:51:41.487 --> 03:51:46.459
Under this seaweed, it's
got rice and fish flakes.

03:51:46.459 --> 03:51:47.894
I love this bento.

03:51:47.894 --> 03:51:49.562
Like, when I was a student,

03:51:49.562 --> 03:51:52.698
I think I would eat this every single day.

03:51:52.698 --> 03:51:56.168
So, after my favorite one,
this one. Look at this!

03:51:56.168 --> 03:52:00.172
So this one is a Korean-style beef bento.

03:52:00.172 --> 03:52:03.276
Oh, man, smells so good.

03:52:06.279 --> 03:52:07.747
Whoo!

03:52:07.747 --> 03:52:11.550
Everything right here is so amazing.

03:52:11.550 --> 03:52:12.551
Fantastic.

03:52:12.551 --> 03:52:15.254
This is so mashisoyo.

03:52:16.188 --> 03:52:17.757
Tonkatsu bento,

03:52:17.757 --> 03:52:21.160
and it comes with this
sauce for this tonkatsu.

03:52:21.160 --> 03:52:22.662
Look how thick it is.

03:52:22.662 --> 03:52:27.667
So, outside from bentos,
we have soba, soba noodle.

03:52:27.767 --> 03:52:29.835
Put this sauce first.

03:52:29.835 --> 03:52:32.939
Put wasabi and dried seaweed.

03:52:32.939 --> 03:52:35.908
And then you put water onto soba noodle.

03:52:35.908 --> 03:52:37.143
It's getting moist.

03:52:38.811 --> 03:52:42.148
And don't forget to put
green onions right here.

03:52:42.148 --> 03:52:43.082
Itadakimasu.

03:52:43.082 --> 03:52:46.452
So you put soba noodle in this box.

03:52:48.387 --> 03:52:50.089
[slurping]

03:52:51.324 --> 03:52:52.391
Umai!

03:52:52.391 --> 03:52:54.994
I guarantee you can't stop eating this,

03:52:54.994 --> 03:52:56.929
'cause it's so delicious.

03:52:56.929 --> 03:52:58.764
Sorry I slurped the noodles.

03:52:58.764 --> 03:53:01.500
Because Japanese people or Asian people

03:53:01.500 --> 03:53:04.570
do make noises when you eat noodles.

03:53:04.570 --> 03:53:05.938
We slurp.

03:53:05.938 --> 03:53:07.039
Slurp!

03:53:07.039 --> 03:53:08.708
Slurp right now!

03:53:08.708 --> 03:53:10.109
They got the meals over there in Japan.

03:53:10.109 --> 03:53:11.177
We got meals too,

03:53:11.177 --> 03:53:14.113
like this ready-made ricotta-, Romano-,

03:53:14.113 --> 03:53:16.015
and Parmesan-cheese-stuffed ravioli

03:53:16.015 --> 03:53:17.450
topped with marinara sauce and mozzarella.

03:53:17.450 --> 03:53:18.918
Ugh.

03:53:18.918 --> 03:53:20.686
Just stop, stop doing this.

03:53:20.686 --> 03:53:22.321
Stop, please.

03:53:22.321 --> 03:53:23.856
Stop.

03:53:23.856 --> 03:53:24.690
Oden.

03:53:24.690 --> 03:53:27.326
So, oden is like Japanese
traditional hot pot.

03:53:27.326 --> 03:53:31.697
It's got fish cake,
fried tofu, noodle thing.

03:53:31.697 --> 03:53:33.432
This is made from potato.

03:53:33.432 --> 03:53:35.234
Egg, radish.

03:53:35.234 --> 03:53:37.169
In winter, when you eat this,

03:53:37.169 --> 03:53:39.538
this warms you up, from your heart.

03:53:41.073 --> 03:53:41.907
To your body.

03:53:41.907 --> 03:53:44.643
And next, gratin doria.

03:53:44.643 --> 03:53:48.180
So, obviously it's got meat
sauce and a lot of cheese.

03:53:48.180 --> 03:53:51.584
Under this cheese, it's
got a lot of rice in there.

03:53:51.584 --> 03:53:53.419
It's like Japanese Western food.

03:53:53.419 --> 03:53:56.355
We have 7-Premium main dishes.

03:53:56.355 --> 03:53:59.525
Naan and butter chicken curry.

03:53:59.525 --> 03:54:02.361
And next we have 7-Premium side dishes.

03:54:02.361 --> 03:54:05.331
Mackerel, grilled mackerel.

03:54:05.331 --> 03:54:08.534
We also have mackerel in miso.

03:54:08.534 --> 03:54:11.103
Saba miso is [chef's kiss].

03:54:11.103 --> 03:54:12.772
Smoked tongue.

03:54:12.772 --> 03:54:14.874
In Japan, it's a pretty popular item,

03:54:14.874 --> 03:54:18.210
especially when you go to a
Japanese barbecue restaurant,

03:54:18.210 --> 03:54:21.680
we order the beef tongue or pig tongue.

03:54:21.680 --> 03:54:24.550
So this one used to be like this.

03:54:24.550 --> 03:54:26.352
Smells so good.

03:54:26.352 --> 03:54:27.553
So fancy.

03:54:29.922 --> 03:54:31.390
It's marvelous.

03:54:31.390 --> 03:54:34.026
So, after this sexy tongue,

03:54:34.026 --> 03:54:37.063
we have sexy fish cake.

03:54:37.063 --> 03:54:38.931
And look at this bar.

03:54:38.931 --> 03:54:39.965
It's a chicken bar,

03:54:39.965 --> 03:54:42.668
so it's like a chicken
nugget before it's fried.

03:54:42.668 --> 03:54:44.470
Octopus and wasabi.

03:54:44.470 --> 03:54:46.505
This is just raw octopus.

03:54:46.505 --> 03:54:50.309
Kinpira gobo. It's sautéed burdock.

03:54:50.309 --> 03:54:53.746
Hijikini, stewed hijiki seaweed.

03:54:53.746 --> 03:54:55.481
And potato salad.

03:54:55.481 --> 03:54:58.651
So, when I go home, my mom always cooks

03:54:58.651 --> 03:55:00.486
this one, this one, this one.

03:55:00.486 --> 03:55:01.921
I love you, Mom.

03:55:01.921 --> 03:55:03.722
I miss Mom's cooking.

03:55:03.722 --> 03:55:07.359
And next we have Premium Gold main dishes.

03:55:07.359 --> 03:55:09.662
Shrimp with chili sauce.

03:55:09.662 --> 03:55:11.397
Beef stew.

03:55:11.397 --> 03:55:13.265
Hamburg steak.

03:55:13.265 --> 03:55:15.201
Sandwiches, 7-Eleven.

03:55:15.201 --> 03:55:16.168
Egg salad.

03:55:16.168 --> 03:55:17.436
Peanut butter and jelly.

03:55:17.436 --> 03:55:20.306
Turkey and cheddar
cheese on a kaiser roll.

03:55:20.306 --> 03:55:23.275
So, we have the Italian-style sub,

03:55:23.275 --> 03:55:26.912
but then we also got The Italian Job.

03:55:26.912 --> 03:55:30.282
Turkey and ham with, is that
cheese in the picture there?

03:55:30.282 --> 03:55:33.586
We got the smoked turkey and
Monterey Jack cheese sandwich,

03:55:33.586 --> 03:55:35.287
and they separated the lettuce,

03:55:35.287 --> 03:55:36.722
so you add it right before
you're ready to eat,

03:55:36.722 --> 03:55:38.057
so it's still nice and crisp.

03:55:38.057 --> 03:55:40.493
Salads, chicken Caesar salad.

03:55:40.493 --> 03:55:42.828
We also have a pepperoni pasta salad.

03:55:42.828 --> 03:55:45.131
So, here are my favorite sandwiches.

03:55:45.131 --> 03:55:48.667
It's got tuna right here
and cheese and lettuce.

03:55:48.667 --> 03:55:53.239
And the rest of these are ham and egg.

03:55:53.239 --> 03:55:57.076
I thought this is normal,
but you don't have this one,

03:55:57.076 --> 03:55:59.078
fruit sandwich.

03:55:59.078 --> 03:56:00.913
So it's got a whole bunch of fruits.

03:56:00.913 --> 03:56:05.484
It's got peach, pineapples,
and oranges on whipped cream.

03:56:05.484 --> 03:56:06.752
So it's like cake.

03:56:06.752 --> 03:56:09.588
So, here is 7-Premium drip coffee.

03:56:09.588 --> 03:56:13.025
So I'm going to make
myself a cup of coffee.

03:56:13.025 --> 03:56:15.227
Heyo!

03:56:15.227 --> 03:56:17.830
And he just sits on here.

03:56:17.830 --> 03:56:20.533
Ah! Ah ah ah!

03:56:20.533 --> 03:56:21.367
Ah!

03:56:22.301 --> 03:56:23.736
Mm.

03:56:23.736 --> 03:56:25.471
All right.

03:56:25.471 --> 03:56:26.472
Itadakimasu.

03:56:30.476 --> 03:56:32.311
It tastes like shit.

03:56:32.311 --> 03:56:34.146
So, for breakfast sandwiches at 7-Eleven,

03:56:34.146 --> 03:56:37.883
you can get yourself a croissant
with ham, egg, and cheese.

03:56:37.883 --> 03:56:40.119
Ooh, an English muffin with
bacon, egg, and cheese.

03:56:40.119 --> 03:56:42.388
We also have English muffins
with sausage, egg, and cheese,

03:56:42.388 --> 03:56:43.556
sausage biscuits,

03:56:43.556 --> 03:56:45.524
and sausage, egg, and cheese croissants.

03:56:45.524 --> 03:56:47.560
The 7-Eleven signature brand also has

03:56:47.560 --> 03:56:50.663
mini doughnuts, chocolate,
cinnamon, crunch,

03:56:50.663 --> 03:56:52.398
and, of course, powdered.

03:56:52.398 --> 03:56:53.232
Madeleines.

03:56:53.232 --> 03:56:55.267
7-Eleven has cookies right
at the register for a dollar.

03:56:55.267 --> 03:56:58.137
You can get yourself some
macadamia nut cookies,

03:56:58.137 --> 03:57:00.439
oatmeal raisin, sugar,

03:57:00.439 --> 03:57:01.907
but there's also a
chocolate chip cookie one.

03:57:01.907 --> 03:57:03.976
Baked goods, you get
yourself some muffins.

03:57:03.976 --> 03:57:05.211
This is a blueberry muffin.

03:57:05.211 --> 03:57:06.245
Coffee cake.

03:57:06.245 --> 03:57:07.580
Crispy rice treat bar.

03:57:07.580 --> 03:57:08.547
Notice it doesn't say Rice Krispie,

03:57:08.547 --> 03:57:10.349
'cause you know that's copywritten.

03:57:10.349 --> 03:57:11.917
Walnut fudge brownie,

03:57:11.917 --> 03:57:13.252
bear claw Danish,

03:57:13.252 --> 03:57:14.720
iced honey bun,

03:57:14.720 --> 03:57:15.688
cheese Danish,

03:57:15.688 --> 03:57:17.089
mixed berry Danish,

03:57:17.089 --> 03:57:19.391
glazed honey bun.

03:57:19.391 --> 03:57:22.127
I got these prepackaged, it
says "flavored snack pie."

03:57:22.127 --> 03:57:23.295
That's a weird way of putting it.

03:57:23.295 --> 03:57:26.765
Lemon, key lime, banana cream.

03:57:26.765 --> 03:57:28.667
I feel like they used the
same -- that's the same.

03:57:28.667 --> 03:57:30.236
That's Photoshop right there, buddy.

03:57:30.236 --> 03:57:32.371
Boston cream, apple,

03:57:32.371 --> 03:57:34.573
and the last one, strawberry cheesecake.

03:57:34.573 --> 03:57:35.507
Key lime.

03:57:38.110 --> 03:57:39.712
Look at all that cream in there.

03:57:39.712 --> 03:57:40.546
It's key limey.

03:57:40.546 --> 03:57:41.380
Oh, yeah.

03:57:41.380 --> 03:57:42.214
Oatmeal!

03:57:42.214 --> 03:57:44.450
That's obviously maple syrup right there.

03:57:44.450 --> 03:57:45.718
But the first thing I
did when I looked at it,

03:57:45.718 --> 03:57:48.020
I was like, "Wait, does
this have brandy in it?"

03:57:48.020 --> 03:57:49.054
Boozy oatmeal.

03:57:49.054 --> 03:57:50.990
You can put hot water in here, Joe.

03:57:50.990 --> 03:57:52.725
Or hot milk, Yuelei.

03:57:52.725 --> 03:57:54.460
Or hot whiskey.

03:57:54.460 --> 03:57:56.562
Your boss won't notice the difference.

03:57:56.562 --> 03:57:57.896
Well, at first.

03:57:57.896 --> 03:58:00.432
Here we have Japanese type of bread.

03:58:00.432 --> 03:58:03.035
Stir-fried-noodles-and-sauce bread.

03:58:03.035 --> 03:58:05.204
We call it yakisoba pan.

03:58:05.204 --> 03:58:10.209
Now, you may be thinking what
the [dolphin chirps] is this?

03:58:10.209 --> 03:58:13.812
So, it's like hot dog,
but instead of sausage,

03:58:13.812 --> 03:58:17.082
we've got stir-fried noodle inside.

03:58:17.082 --> 03:58:19.184
Carb, carb.

03:58:19.184 --> 03:58:20.052
It makes you fat.

03:58:20.052 --> 03:58:21.587
Bread makes you fat?!

03:58:21.587 --> 03:58:24.356
So, kids love this noodle and bread.

03:58:24.356 --> 03:58:25.624
Itadakimasu.

03:58:29.028 --> 03:58:30.262
Mm!

03:58:30.262 --> 03:58:33.098
This one reminds me of my childhood,

03:58:33.098 --> 03:58:37.469
me playing tags in the
mountain and chasing the girls.

03:58:37.469 --> 03:58:41.006
Now a lot of girls chasing me.

03:58:41.006 --> 03:58:43.108
This is a crab bread.

03:58:43.108 --> 03:58:45.811
It's got two crab-shaped bread.

03:58:45.811 --> 03:58:48.914
Now, the question is,
does it taste like crab?

03:58:50.816 --> 03:58:52.318
It doesn't taste like crab.

03:58:52.318 --> 03:58:54.520
Taste like just bread.

03:58:54.520 --> 03:58:55.554
Pink bread.

03:58:55.554 --> 03:58:59.425
It's a
cherry-blossom-flavored-coating bread.

03:58:59.425 --> 03:59:00.926
This pink stuff is,

03:59:00.926 --> 03:59:02.528
it's pretty sour.

03:59:05.030 --> 03:59:06.732
It tastes like cherry blossom

03:59:06.732 --> 03:59:09.201
and like my first kiss.

03:59:09.201 --> 03:59:12.571
This is the salty, savory snack zone.

03:59:12.571 --> 03:59:13.872
Ah, so much stuff.

03:59:13.872 --> 03:59:16.008
And I've hit the "Food Wars" wall.

03:59:16.008 --> 03:59:18.610
Hot and spicy cracklin
curls, the original,

03:59:18.610 --> 03:59:20.879
and the fried pork rinds, chili lime.

03:59:22.481 --> 03:59:25.150
I'm not tasting anything
pork-related to it.

03:59:25.150 --> 03:59:26.719
Little pig guy there.

03:59:26.719 --> 03:59:27.553
Little piggy guy.

03:59:27.553 --> 03:59:28.620
You're on the menu, buddy.

03:59:28.620 --> 03:59:32.524
Next, 7-Selects has
their own veggie straws.

03:59:32.524 --> 03:59:35.994
This will be the trail
mix and mix-like section.

03:59:35.994 --> 03:59:39.331
We got these
cheese-pizza-flavored snack mix.

03:59:39.331 --> 03:59:41.767
You're gonna be a stinky boy
if you have a bunch of these.

03:59:41.767 --> 03:59:44.436
Now they got the spicy ranch flavor mix.

03:59:44.436 --> 03:59:46.739
And this last one, just sesame sticks.

03:59:46.739 --> 03:59:49.141
For those of you who like
to get your trail mix

03:59:49.141 --> 03:59:51.310
or your Chex Mix and then unmix them

03:59:51.310 --> 03:59:53.011
and organize them and eat them like that,

03:59:53.011 --> 03:59:55.981
7-Eleven has got the snack for you.

03:59:55.981 --> 03:59:58.751
Oh, this is kind of a party snack mix.

03:59:58.751 --> 03:59:59.651
Eh.

03:59:59.651 --> 04:00:02.488
This is what I would totally
get, yogurt pretzels.

04:00:02.488 --> 04:00:04.022
They put yogurt on there,
and, like, you're thinking,

04:00:04.022 --> 04:00:05.090
"Oh, yogurt, that's healthy, right?"

04:00:05.090 --> 04:00:07.226
I mean, it's just, it's the same as icing.

04:00:07.226 --> 04:00:08.894
Now, you're looking at this going,

04:00:08.894 --> 04:00:12.164
"Jack Link's beef jerky?
That's not a 7-Eleven brand."

04:00:12.164 --> 04:00:13.198
No, it's not.

04:00:13.198 --> 04:00:16.235
But as you can see,
exclusive 7-Eleven flavors.

04:00:16.235 --> 04:00:18.771
See, this was like, "Hey,
Jack Link's, guess what?

04:00:18.771 --> 04:00:21.273
We're about to push you
out of our shelf space.

04:00:21.273 --> 04:00:23.142
So do a deal with us, or
you're gone completely."

04:00:23.142 --> 04:00:23.976
And Jack Link's was like,

04:00:23.976 --> 04:00:25.644
"No, I've got kids to feed, please!"

04:00:25.644 --> 04:00:27.813
Brown sugar bourbon,

04:00:27.813 --> 04:00:28.947
original recipe,

04:00:28.947 --> 04:00:30.015
original.

04:00:30.015 --> 04:00:31.417
Hickory-smoked bacon.

04:00:31.417 --> 04:00:33.419
Like snacking on cheese and nothing else?

04:00:33.419 --> 04:00:34.386
Full house, baby.

04:00:34.386 --> 04:00:36.955
This one is mozzarella cheese
wrapped in hard salami.

04:00:36.955 --> 04:00:38.223
Pepper Jack stick,

04:00:38.223 --> 04:00:39.391
Gouda cheese to go.

04:00:39.391 --> 04:00:41.527
Oh, the big one, the big
cheese, the white cheddar.

04:00:41.527 --> 04:00:43.495
This ain't your grandma's cheese.

04:00:43.495 --> 04:00:45.230
It's the big one.

04:00:45.230 --> 04:00:46.064
Just two.

04:00:46.064 --> 04:00:47.266
Cheddar cheese.

04:00:47.266 --> 04:00:50.102
Colby-Jack, which is
like camouflage cheese.

04:00:50.102 --> 04:00:51.136
Ugh!

04:00:51.136 --> 04:00:54.039
Pretzels. Mini twists, non yogurted.

04:00:54.039 --> 04:00:55.741
Pretzel nuggets. Ooh, gross.

04:00:55.741 --> 04:00:57.443
These ones have peanut
butter inside of them.

04:00:57.443 --> 04:00:59.344
Pretzel sticks. I feel like
there was a while there

04:00:59.344 --> 04:01:00.946
in the early '90s when they were like,

04:01:00.946 --> 04:01:02.981
"Chips are bad for you.
Eat pretzels instead."

04:01:02.981 --> 04:01:04.349
And these are really salty, too.

04:01:04.349 --> 04:01:06.218
A serving size of these is three.

04:01:06.218 --> 04:01:07.686
I would get this assuming I'm gonna sit

04:01:07.686 --> 04:01:09.288
and eat this whole bag in one sitting.

04:01:09.288 --> 04:01:10.522
I'm not gonna do three at a time.

04:01:10.522 --> 04:01:13.559
The whole bag is 1,160 milligrams,

04:01:13.559 --> 04:01:15.394
50% of your sodium intake.

04:01:15.394 --> 04:01:16.762
Mini rice cakes.

04:01:17.996 --> 04:01:18.831
Chips.

04:01:18.831 --> 04:01:22.034
7-Eleven has a bunch of
their own potato chips,

04:01:22.034 --> 04:01:24.870
including the original, fiery hot.

04:01:24.870 --> 04:01:26.338
Kettle chips, which are way better

04:01:26.338 --> 04:01:27.973
than regular chips, again.

04:01:27.973 --> 04:01:29.842
Spicy jalapeño, smoked Gouda.

04:01:29.842 --> 04:01:30.909
Ooh, Gouda.

04:01:30.909 --> 04:01:32.744
Barbecue, salt and pepper.

04:01:32.744 --> 04:01:35.714
Ruffles rip-offs. We got
cheddar and sour cream.

04:01:35.714 --> 04:01:37.382
Prime rib, I'm trying these.

04:01:37.382 --> 04:01:39.351
And Buffalo chicken dip.

04:01:39.351 --> 04:01:40.552
Prime rib?

04:01:40.552 --> 04:01:42.287
Woof, smells terrible.

04:01:43.255 --> 04:01:45.123
Oh, my God, that was so bad!

04:01:45.123 --> 04:01:47.025
It's definitely not this.

04:01:47.025 --> 04:01:48.460
Yeah, more like ground beef.

04:01:48.460 --> 04:01:49.962
And instead of one of these fancy forks,

04:01:49.962 --> 04:01:52.865
there'd be the plastic spork
that they have at 7-Eleven.

04:01:52.865 --> 04:01:55.167
They're opening the bag with the spork,

04:01:55.167 --> 04:01:56.335
meat's pouring out of it,

04:01:56.335 --> 04:01:58.737
it's on the floor of a 7-Eleven,

04:01:58.737 --> 04:02:00.739
with a guy mopping around it.

04:02:01.673 --> 04:02:04.109
Nuts, baby. Nuts.

04:02:04.109 --> 04:02:07.412
The rise and shine fiber blend
of a trail mix, whatever.

04:02:07.412 --> 04:02:09.681
Antioxidant. Yeah, right.

04:02:09.681 --> 04:02:12.851
Revive and thrive,
another antioxidant mix.

04:02:12.851 --> 04:02:15.320
Should've just handed
these out during COVID,

04:02:15.320 --> 04:02:16.655
would've bounced back in a week.

04:02:16.655 --> 04:02:17.990
Cashew halves.

04:02:18.991 --> 04:02:20.926
You like your nuts halved? Booyah.

04:02:20.926 --> 04:02:23.662
You like your nuts wholed? Booyah.

04:02:23.662 --> 04:02:25.097
Does it matter if they're whole or not?

04:02:25.097 --> 04:02:27.232
Would that affect the
flavor at all? Who cares?

04:02:27.232 --> 04:02:30.636
Spicy ranch pistachios.

04:02:30.636 --> 04:02:33.772
And, of course, jumbo flavored

04:02:33.772 --> 04:02:36.408
wasabi and soy nuts. Nope.

04:02:36.408 --> 04:02:39.611
Wasabi will never touch my
lips again after that video.

04:02:39.611 --> 04:02:42.881
So, here are my favorite instant noodles.

04:02:42.881 --> 04:02:43.982
Let's start.

04:02:43.982 --> 04:02:45.450
Ippudo ramen.

04:02:45.450 --> 04:02:47.319
Man, I love this.

04:02:47.319 --> 04:02:48.620
So, it's got some packets.

04:02:48.620 --> 04:02:50.522
Dried pork.

04:02:50.522 --> 04:02:53.058
It's a miso for the ramen soup.

04:02:53.058 --> 04:02:54.326
Dried veggies.

04:02:56.194 --> 04:02:57.462
And it's got noodles.

04:03:00.132 --> 04:03:01.633
All right.

04:03:01.633 --> 04:03:04.870
And you've got to wait for three minutes.

04:03:04.870 --> 04:03:08.307
So while I'm waiting for
this, I'm gonna go this one.

04:03:08.307 --> 04:03:10.709
So it's called Ippei-chan.

04:03:10.709 --> 04:03:13.378
So it basically is a yakisoba.

04:03:13.378 --> 04:03:16.381
Yakisoba is like Japanese
stir-fried noodles.

04:03:18.150 --> 04:03:20.886
So, you put some hot
water until this line.

04:03:21.753 --> 04:03:24.156
All right, so it's been three minutes.

04:03:24.156 --> 04:03:27.225
Put this soup into this bowl.

04:03:27.225 --> 04:03:28.460
Mix it.

04:03:30.696 --> 04:03:32.965
Smells so good!

04:03:37.636 --> 04:03:38.570
Bravo.

04:03:42.474 --> 04:03:45.344
So, Ippudo has a lot
of locations in Japan,

04:03:45.344 --> 04:03:48.614
including Tokyo, but this taste,

04:03:48.614 --> 04:03:50.649
this flavor is totally the same

04:03:50.649 --> 04:03:52.384
as the restaurant's serving.

04:03:52.384 --> 04:03:55.921
So just get it at 7-Eleven.

04:03:55.921 --> 04:03:59.691
Oh, shit, I totally forgot the, oh.

04:03:59.691 --> 04:04:01.360
So, I put some hot water, but --

04:04:01.360 --> 04:04:03.562
oh, shit!

04:04:03.562 --> 04:04:06.932
I should have thrown the
water away into the toilet.

04:04:06.932 --> 04:04:08.734
Gomen ne, noodles.

04:04:08.734 --> 04:04:10.469
Let's make yakisoba.

04:04:10.469 --> 04:04:14.840
[laughs] The volume of these noodles

04:04:14.840 --> 04:04:17.142
gets a lot bigger.

04:04:17.142 --> 04:04:19.277
OK, so put yakisoba sauce.

04:04:20.979 --> 04:04:22.214
And flakes.

04:04:23.148 --> 04:04:25.617
And most importantly, mayo.

04:04:25.617 --> 04:04:27.019
Mayo beam!

04:04:27.886 --> 04:04:29.388
Oh!

04:04:29.388 --> 04:04:31.089
And mix it up.

04:04:32.224 --> 04:04:33.058
Ta-da!

04:04:33.058 --> 04:04:35.127
So, this is yakisoba.

04:04:35.127 --> 04:04:38.430
We usually eat this,
like, at summer festival.

04:04:41.033 --> 04:04:42.668
Pretty good, as always.

04:04:42.668 --> 04:04:46.004
Next, we have tako-meshi.

04:04:46.004 --> 04:04:49.241
Look at this. So, it's got green onions,

04:04:49.241 --> 04:04:51.543
and I believe this is tako.

04:04:54.479 --> 04:04:57.115
So, three minutes again.

04:04:57.115 --> 04:04:59.951
Look at this final noodle.

04:04:59.951 --> 04:05:03.922
It says ultra-spicy final.

04:05:03.922 --> 04:05:06.658
You're going to be crying
because of the spiciness.

04:05:06.658 --> 04:05:08.193
It's too spicy.

04:05:08.193 --> 04:05:10.429
But I'm going to try this,

04:05:10.429 --> 04:05:12.064
only for shooting purpose.

04:05:12.064 --> 04:05:13.265
This is for you guys!

04:05:13.265 --> 04:05:14.466
We can do it.
Clip: Never give up!

04:05:15.967 --> 04:05:18.370
Oh, man, I'm so scared.

04:05:21.640 --> 04:05:25.077
All right, so I think
it's time to eat this one.

04:05:25.077 --> 04:05:29.748
So, I'm going to throw the
water away in the toilet again.

04:05:29.748 --> 04:05:31.349
Let's go to the toilet.

04:05:33.118 --> 04:05:35.754
And put yakisoba sauce.

04:05:35.754 --> 04:05:36.788
All righty.

04:05:39.357 --> 04:05:41.960
And the taste itself is
lighter than this one.

04:05:41.960 --> 04:05:44.663
I prefer this one, but,

04:05:44.663 --> 04:05:45.530
but,

04:05:45.530 --> 04:05:48.233
this is the king ramen.

04:05:48.233 --> 04:05:51.770
All right, so finally let's make

04:05:51.770 --> 04:05:54.005
the freaking spicy noodle.

04:05:54.005 --> 04:05:56.975
I call it death sauce.

04:05:56.975 --> 04:05:58.710
In case I'm dead,

04:05:58.710 --> 04:06:01.179
please find another Japanese host.

04:06:01.179 --> 04:06:03.415
It was nice to meet you, Food Insider.

04:06:03.415 --> 04:06:05.350
Go!

04:06:05.350 --> 04:06:08.153
Oh, man, look at this.

04:06:08.153 --> 04:06:10.655
It's not red, it's blood.

04:06:10.655 --> 04:06:12.257
I don't want to eat this.

04:06:13.225 --> 04:06:17.262
[coughing]

04:06:21.433 --> 04:06:22.534
Ah!

04:06:23.935 --> 04:06:24.770
Oh.

04:06:31.343 --> 04:06:34.179
Ah!

04:06:35.614 --> 04:06:38.083
I'm not joking, I'm not joking.

04:06:38.083 --> 04:06:40.152
Ah, ah.

04:06:44.222 --> 04:06:45.357
It hurts!

04:06:46.525 --> 04:06:47.659
Am I alive?

04:06:48.760 --> 04:06:50.829
Am I not dead?

04:06:50.829 --> 04:06:52.964
Am I in heaven?

04:06:52.964 --> 04:06:54.866
Hell?

04:06:54.866 --> 04:06:56.368
I feel like I'm in hell.

04:06:57.235 --> 04:06:59.638
It's not all junk food at
the 7-Eleven, Joe and Yuelei.

04:06:59.638 --> 04:07:04.209
They also have delicious
freshly sliced fruit.

04:07:04.209 --> 04:07:05.710
Prepackaged and everything,

04:07:05.710 --> 04:07:06.845
