04:12:17.388 --> 04:12:19.557
Orange mango, fruit punch, lemonade.

04:12:19.557 --> 04:12:21.559
The cherry is clear.

04:12:21.559 --> 04:12:23.428
What? Why is cherry clear?

04:12:23.428 --> 04:12:25.196
Guava splash, orange mango.

04:12:25.196 --> 04:12:26.531
♪ These are bad ♪

04:12:26.531 --> 04:12:28.800
7-Eleven energy.

04:12:28.800 --> 04:12:30.368
"Strawberry lemonade energy shot,

04:12:30.368 --> 04:12:32.570
one and half times the
caffeine of a cup of coffee."

04:12:32.570 --> 04:12:33.838
Oh, good God.

04:12:37.242 --> 04:12:38.143
Undrinkable.

04:12:38.143 --> 04:12:39.944
How bad does it have to
taste where this is too --

04:12:39.944 --> 04:12:40.778
I couldn't get to this?

04:12:40.778 --> 04:12:41.913
You've seen this show, right?

04:12:41.913 --> 04:12:43.481
You'll see what I'll tolerate.

04:12:43.481 --> 04:12:45.049
This, I can barely tolerate this.

04:12:47.886 --> 04:12:51.389
Here's something that
they don't have in Japan.

04:12:51.389 --> 04:12:52.390
They don't have Slurpees.

04:12:52.390 --> 04:12:53.591
That's nuts, right?

04:12:53.591 --> 04:12:55.460
Slurpees are -- how do
you describe a Slurpee?

04:12:55.460 --> 04:12:58.196
It's like a flavored slush.

04:12:58.196 --> 04:13:00.064
We have endless Slurpee flavors.

04:13:00.064 --> 04:13:02.634
The ones currently you can
get here in America are

04:13:02.634 --> 04:13:04.135
blue rocketberry,

04:13:04.135 --> 04:13:05.103
blood orange,

04:13:05.103 --> 04:13:06.738
Vitaminwater XXX,

04:13:06.738 --> 04:13:07.839
blue raspberry,

04:13:07.839 --> 04:13:09.607
blueberry lemonade bliss,

04:13:09.607 --> 04:13:11.209
cherry, Coca-Cola,

04:13:11.209 --> 04:13:13.444
Mountain Dew citrus, peach perfect,

04:13:13.444 --> 04:13:16.948
piña colada, and pineapple whip.

04:13:16.948 --> 04:13:19.350
So, here are Japanese exclusive drinks.

04:13:19.350 --> 04:13:21.986
We have vegetable juice, of course.

04:13:22.887 --> 04:13:25.256
Mm! Oishii.

04:13:25.256 --> 04:13:28.660
A lot of Japanese salarymen
drink this one every morning

04:13:28.660 --> 04:13:30.995
to get their day started.

04:13:30.995 --> 04:13:33.231
So this one is for Joe.

04:13:33.231 --> 04:13:35.900
Joe, you're missing a lot of veggies,

04:13:35.900 --> 04:13:38.002
so you should drink this one.

04:13:38.002 --> 04:13:41.706
Oi Ocha, my favorite green tea.

04:13:41.706 --> 04:13:44.142
And these two are hot drinks,

04:13:44.142 --> 04:13:46.945
black coffee and café latte.

04:13:46.945 --> 04:13:49.614
And this is our first time filming this.

04:13:49.614 --> 04:13:51.416
We have alcohol.

04:13:51.416 --> 04:13:54.719
We have 7-Premium beer.

04:13:54.719 --> 04:13:56.421
And this one is not beer.

04:13:56.421 --> 04:13:59.290
It's like Sprite with alcohol.

04:13:59.290 --> 04:14:02.227
It contains 9% of alcohol.

04:14:02.227 --> 04:14:03.728
It's pretty delicious,

04:14:03.728 --> 04:14:05.997
but at the same time,
it's pretty dangerous.

04:14:05.997 --> 04:14:08.099
Japanese sake.

04:14:08.099 --> 04:14:09.867
When you come to Japan, you can see

04:14:09.867 --> 04:14:12.670
a lot of people drinking alcohol outside.

04:14:12.670 --> 04:14:15.373
They're like [groans].

04:14:17.242 --> 04:14:19.644
They are not dead, they're just sleeping.

04:14:19.644 --> 04:14:20.912
They're drunk.

04:14:20.912 --> 04:14:21.946
Whisky.

04:14:21.946 --> 04:14:25.149
7-Eleven in the US has its own

04:14:25.149 --> 04:14:27.418
private brand wines,

04:14:27.418 --> 04:14:30.288
Yosemite Road, Trojan Horse,

04:14:30.288 --> 04:14:33.258
Plot and Point, and Voyager Point.

04:14:33.258 --> 04:14:36.728
It also has its own canned
wine brand, called Roamer.

04:14:36.728 --> 04:14:39.897
Perhaps the reason 7-Eleven
has such a wide variety

04:14:39.897 --> 04:14:43.735
of products in Japan is that
it's everywhere in Japan.

04:14:43.735 --> 04:14:47.705
There are 21,215 stores in Japan.

04:14:47.705 --> 04:14:49.240
That's crazy!

04:14:49.240 --> 04:14:53.344
Which is nearly 30% of all
the 7-Elevens in the world.

04:14:53.344 --> 04:14:57.015
Of course, all 37
prefectures have a 7-Eleven.

04:14:57.015 --> 04:14:58.716
And out of all of them,

04:14:58.716 --> 04:15:01.252
the city of Tokyo has the most locations,

04:15:01.252 --> 04:15:03.721
with 2,850.

04:15:03.721 --> 04:15:04.822
To put that in perspective,

04:15:04.822 --> 04:15:08.226
the US has 9,417 7-Elevens,

04:15:08.226 --> 04:15:10.928
and there's no 7-Elevens in 18 states.

04:15:10.928 --> 04:15:13.364
As far as states, California has the most,

04:15:13.364 --> 04:15:15.967
1,823.

04:15:15.967 --> 04:15:19.504
But as far as denseness in area,

04:15:19.504 --> 04:15:23.741
Las Vegas, Nevada, has the most, with 158.

04:15:25.943 --> 04:15:29.380
In Japan, our hot dog is 290 calories

04:15:29.380 --> 04:15:31.949
and 720 milligrams of sodium,

04:15:31.949 --> 04:15:36.220
which is 31.3% of your daily allowance.

04:15:36.220 --> 04:15:37.789
Our hot dog is 180 calories.

04:15:37.789 --> 04:15:39.457
Ooh. How about this?

04:15:39.457 --> 04:15:42.293
Our hot dog is 180 calories,
but for the frank only.

04:15:42.293 --> 04:15:43.561
The stats, for some reason,

04:15:43.561 --> 04:15:45.096
don't say anything about the bun.

04:15:45.096 --> 04:15:47.131
But this isn't much better for you.

04:15:47.131 --> 04:15:49.600
It's 570 milligrams of sodium,

04:15:49.600 --> 04:15:53.237
so around 24.8% of your daily allowance.

04:15:53.237 --> 04:15:55.840
Japan's hand-rolled tuna and mayo onigiri

04:15:55.840 --> 04:15:59.711
has 258 calories and is very filling.

04:15:59.711 --> 04:16:01.646
Remember this guy? The tuna sandwich.

04:16:01.646 --> 04:16:04.749
Here in the US, ours is 420 calories

04:16:04.749 --> 04:16:08.052
and lots of sodium, over 800 milligrams.

04:16:08.052 --> 04:16:09.220
Fuck!

04:16:09.220 --> 04:16:12.123
And in the US, a Super
Big Gulp of Coca-Cola,

04:16:12.123 --> 04:16:15.126
this isn't Coca-Cola, is 44 fluid ounces.

04:16:15.126 --> 04:16:19.330
It's 513 calories and 143 grams of carbs.

04:16:19.330 --> 04:16:21.766
That's over half your daily intake.

04:16:23.668 --> 04:16:26.304
In Japan, 7-Eleven does not disclose

04:16:26.304 --> 04:16:29.807
the ingredients list of its
freshly made food items.

04:16:29.807 --> 04:16:32.744
It does, however, tell
us the country of origin

04:16:32.744 --> 04:16:35.113
for the raw materials for certain items,

04:16:35.113 --> 04:16:38.116
like the fried food, yakitori, oden,

04:16:38.116 --> 04:16:40.118
and Chinese steamed buns.

04:16:40.118 --> 04:16:42.920
The chicken for our fried
chicken is from Thailand.

04:16:42.920 --> 04:16:45.423
The pork for our sausages and hot dogs

04:16:45.423 --> 04:16:48.526
comes from USA, Canada, and Japan.

04:16:48.526 --> 04:16:50.862
The wheat for the buns comes from Canada,

04:16:50.862 --> 04:16:52.864
the USA, and Japan.

04:16:52.864 --> 04:16:55.199
And adzuki beans come from Canada,

04:16:55.199 --> 04:16:57.101
cheese comes from New Zealand,

04:16:57.101 --> 04:17:00.571
and the shrimp for the shrimp
chili buns is from Vietnam.

04:17:00.571 --> 04:17:02.407
This is the pepperoni pizza in the US.

04:17:02.407 --> 04:17:05.343
And it contains all this junk.

04:17:05.343 --> 04:17:08.446
I mean, what's this thing?

04:17:08.446 --> 04:17:10.715
Never heard of that.

04:17:10.715 --> 04:17:12.216
What about chicken strips?

04:17:12.216 --> 04:17:13.985
It's got all this stuff!

04:17:13.985 --> 04:17:15.653
Just like mom used to make.

04:17:15.653 --> 04:17:18.523
And, of course, the 7-Eleven
Select cheeseburger,

04:17:18.523 --> 04:17:20.391
which contains ... [sighs]

04:17:20.391 --> 04:17:22.493
sesame seed bun has enriched flour,

04:17:22.493 --> 04:17:23.961
excuse me, enriched wheat flour,

04:17:23.961 --> 04:17:25.897
wheat flour, niacin, reduced iron,

04:17:25.897 --> 04:17:28.900
monoserititate, serotitititate,

04:17:28.900 --> 04:17:31.669
calcium propionate as a
preservative, calcium sulfate,

04:17:31.669 --> 04:17:34.772
royal beef patty got smoke flavor added,

04:17:34.772 --> 04:17:36.541
and it's beef, encapsulated
salt, potassium ...

04:17:36.541 --> 04:17:37.575
Is anything else after that?

04:17:37.575 --> 04:17:40.178
Salt, spice, pasteurized
process American cheese.

04:17:40.178 --> 04:17:41.712
Ah, cheese -- they're sitting down.

04:17:41.712 --> 04:17:42.947
That's how long this is going.

04:17:42.947 --> 04:17:44.882
My cameraperson just sat down.

04:17:44.882 --> 04:17:47.952
A preservative, paprika,
and annatto color.

04:17:47.952 --> 04:17:49.687
So I guess the last takeaway

04:17:49.687 --> 04:17:51.689
from this video is that in the US,

04:17:51.689 --> 04:17:54.225
some of our 7-Eleven items can be

04:17:54.225 --> 04:17:56.394
a little bit of a gamble with your health.

04:17:56.394 --> 04:17:58.329
Speaking of gambling, you know your boy

04:17:58.329 --> 04:18:00.465
got some scratchers when
he was over at 7-Eleven.

04:18:00.465 --> 04:18:02.600
Mm-hmm, OK. So there's
the winning numbers.

04:18:02.600 --> 04:18:05.636
OK, so we didn't win anything on that one.

04:18:05.636 --> 04:18:07.538
I have no clue how to do this.

04:18:07.538 --> 04:18:08.840
Did I win?

04:18:08.840 --> 04:18:12.944
If you haven't subscribed
yet, subscribe now!

04:18:12.944 --> 04:18:16.080
'Cause we were filming this for six hours.

